window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4801,"title":"Chapter 4801: Chapter 4800: THE Weaver of Existence I","paragraphs":["THE Secretive Eon simply stated how he wasn’t the only one to have killed an Absolute.","Noah reevaluated her again.","He wanted to ask who she collapsed but...he left it alone as her words did catch his interest.","The vacuum where THE Weavers had died, where an incandescent beam of pure Depth had smashed into him, had continued to increase in Immensity. The hemorrhaging authority of a collapsed Absolute was still flowing, still seeking its rightful destination.","And just as she said it was about time...","Something began to form within that vacuum in THE Palaestra!","He looked at Eon calmly.","She smiled back at him, her gaze stretching out across the Stoa of Dogmata as if she could perceive everything occurring in that distant Arena.","\"I counted you out and thought you were not ready.\"","Her voice came measured and wise, holding the weight of someone who had learned to accept when they were wrong.","\" Killing an Absolute is a sign as any on whether you are ready or not.\"","She tilted her head thoughtfully.","\" Depending on what you can take from what made them an Absolute... you may even have your answers.\"","Her smile grew warmer.","\" Have fun with THE Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers.\"","She began to drift backward, settling into a comfortable position in the air.","\" Rarely do such things form. Rarely... do Absolutes die.\"","Her eyes held something that might have been nostalgia.","\" Only the killer has access to it. If that wasn’t the case, everyone would swarm toward the grave of THE Weavers like vultures to carrion.\"","She waved her hand dismissively.","\" So enjoy it, big guy. You are deserving of it.\"","Her tone shifted slightly, becoming more serious.","\" Just make sure that the chaos you caused doesn’t affect my Disciple. You still have to bring her out.\"","Her eyes sharpened.","\" She comes out, we can get started on our mutual work.\"","...!","After she said this, she sat down comfortably.","As if absolutely nothing had changed.","As if what had just occurred would not change anything of her plans.","As if the first death of an Absolute since THE Fallout was merely a minor development in whatever grand design she was weaving.","Noah calmly looked at her.","He wondered.","Just what had changed from his actions?","And what... would be the response from THE Living Paradox?","THE Weavers had been his instruments. His weapons. His eyes and ears across Observable Existence. They had served him since before THE Fallout, cutting and weaving fates according to his design.","And now they were gone.","Permanently.","Would THE Living Paradox retaliate immediately?","Would he send more of the forces of THE Loom?","Would he come himself?","Noah held no fear for the future or what would come.","He had killed an Absolute.","Whatever consequences arose from that action, he would face them as he had faced everything else.","With Mana. With The First Tongue. With foundations that exceeded even THE Creature.","He focused on what was finishing forming in THE Palaestra where THE Weavers had died.","And it truly seemed like killing an Absolute was a grand affair.","A mausoleum-looking structure formed before him, visible even from this great distance through his connection to the vacuum that had created it.","---","In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","In THE Palaestra.","Glossikos and the other three Strategoi were immeasurably silent.","They watched the structure that formed where THE Weavers had collapsed.","They saw the emergence of THE Absolute Existential Palace!","Something that would now forever exist in the middle of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","Because the tomb of an Absolute... did not perish.","It would remain here as a monument to what had occurred. A reminder that in this place, on this day, an Absolute had fallen. Visitors would come from across Observable Existence to see it. Scholars would study it. Legends would be told about it.","And the only one who could enter and raid the tomb of its contents was the killer.","The Palace manifested as an impossible structure that existed in multiple states simultaneously.","It was both ancient and unbuilt.","Both magnificent and ruined.","Both a temple to fate and a tomb for those who tried to control it.","Its walls were woven from golden threads that stretched into infinity. The threads caught light that shouldn’t have existed in this space, refracting it into patterns that spoke of destinies cut and woven across eons.","Three towers rose from the structure, representing the three bodies of THE Weavers. Each one leaned toward the others as if in eternal conversation, their angles defying normal architecture. They would never touch, but they would never separate. Frozen in the moment of reaching for each other forever.","Gates made from massive golden scissors marked the entrance. They were frozen mid-cut, their blades positioned as if about to sever something impossibly important. To enter was to pass between those blades. To accept the symbolism of what THE Weavers had been.","The entire structure floated in a void filled with severed threads drifting like Existential debris. Remnants of fates that THE Weavers had cut. Destinies that had been altered or ended at their whim. Now they floated aimlessly, no longer guided by the hands that had manipulated them.","THE Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers!","Osmont had watched it emerge calmly.","The brilliant beam of light being absorbed by him stemmed from it, connecting him to the Palace through bonds that could not be severed. He was its master now. Its only visitor. The sole inheritor of everything THE Weavers had accumulated across their impossibly long existence.","Moments later...","WAP!","He took a step toward it and disappeared!","Swallowed by the Palace that called only to him.","Off to the side, the gaze of Paradoxos was heavy.","Both faces wore identical expressions of cold fury as they watched the killer of their faction’s Absolute vanish into a treasure trove they could never access.","\" THE Four continue to do whatever THE Four want to do.\"","Their voice came bitter and resigned.","\" Regardless of the consequences.\"","...!","The words echoed across the ruined Palaestra.","Glossikos remained silent, her eyes completely still.","Ontikos... the multicolored flames around him had dimmed, as if whoever had been watching through his eyes had seen enough!"]},{"number":4802,"title":"Chapter 4802: Chapter 4801: THE Weaver of Existence II","paragraphs":["|Domain Entry Confirmed|","| You have entered THE Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers.|","|Palace Name: The Loom of Ended Threads|","|This is a place that only you have access to.|","|Only you alone can enter.|","|Due to the power of an Absolute that made up this domain in their death, the concept of time barely passes within this space for now.|","|Take what is yours.|","|Become what they could not stop you from becoming.|","These were the words that Noah saw as soon as he entered the construct that rose up from the decimation of THE Weavers.","A vast hall stretched before him where golden threads hung from a ceiling that could not be seen.","The threads descended endlessly, some thick as ropes, others thin as spider silk. They swayed gently despite the absence of wind, each one pulsing with faint light that spoke of lives touched and altered. Some threads were frayed at the ends where they had been cut. Others remained intact but dulled, as if the fates they represented had simply... ended.","The hall extended in all directions beyond what normal perception could track. It was not merely large. It was conceptually vast. A space that contained the accumulated work of an Absolute across eons of existence.","|Location Identified|","| You have arrived in the Treasury of Severed Fates.|","|Each thread represents a fate that THE Weavers cut during their existence.|","|Countless destinies, ended or altered at their whim.|","|Emperors who should have risen, struck down before their time.|","|Civilizations that should have flourished, unraveled before they could bloom.|","|Loves that should have lasted, severed before they could begin.|","|All of it hangs here.|","|All of it is now yours to witness.|","The atmosphere pressed against Noah with weight that transcended physical sensation.","The sound of scissors cutting echoed constantly, though no source could be found.","Snip. Snip. Snip .","The rhythm was relentless, the phantom labor of THE Weavers continuing even after their collapse. As if the Palace remembered their work and could not stop performing it.","Threads of light drifted through corridors that branched off from the main hall. Remnants of fates that were being woven at the moment of death. They floated aimlessly now, incomplete destinies that would never be finished.","The air smelled of aged parchment and copper.","The scent of blood and destiny intertwined.","Noah walked through this place calmly.","His steps rang out against a floor made from crystallized fate-thread, each footfall sending ripples of golden light spreading outward. The sound echoed through the vast space, announcing his presence to a Palace that already knew he was there.","His gaze went toward floating items at the very center of this place.","They hovered before a massive doorway that seemed to lead to another chamber entirely. The items radiated power that made the surrounding threads tremble in response. They were the tools of an Absolute. The weapons of beings who had shaped fate across Observable Existence.","And now they waited for their new master.","|Loot Assessment Complete|","| You have obtained the following items that you can freely grasp and take into your existence as the victor over the collapsed Absolute:|","|Primary Items:|","| The Golden Scissors of Fate (Three Sets)|","|Classification: Absolute-tier Artifacts|","|Description: The signature weapons of THE Weavers. Each set can cut through anything, including Declarations, Ways, and even aspects of reality itself. One set per body they possessed.|","|Special Capability: Combined, they can sever connections between an entity and their Claim. This includes severing an Absolute from their authority over Observable Existence, but that is impossibly hard.|","|Warning: Wielding requires sufficient Depth to bear their weight. Current assessment: Partial utilization possible.|","|THE Axiom of Absolute Denial (Almost Complete)|","|Classification: Nearly Complete Axiom|","|Description: A weapon Paradoxos lent to THE Weavers before the battle. Missing only a few fragments to achieve wholeness.|","|Current Capability: Can deny anything the wielder wishes, though with limitations due to incompleteness. Denial strength scales with wielder’s Depth.|","|Full Capability (if completed): Absolute invincibility against anything below full Absolute Depth. Complete denial of any attack, Declaration, or reality alteration directed at the wielder. Denial of Embodiments...|","|Note: Fragments required for completion are scattered across Observable Existence. Locations unknown.|","|The Musing of Observable Existence|","|Classification: Absolute-tier Intelligence Artifact|","|Description: A woven map of all fates THE Weavers had touched across their existence. Shows connections between beings, events, and destinies across Observable Existence.|","|Capability: Can be used to understand the web of causality. Can track beings across dimensional boundaries through their fate-threads.|","|Warning: The map is vast. Full comprehension requires extensive study.|","| The Thread of THE Living Paradox|","|Classification: Connection Artifact|","|Description: A single golden thread that connects to THE Living Paradox himself. THE Weavers maintained this connection as proof of their servitude.|","|Warning: This thread is a two-way connection. Claiming it may alert THE Living Paradox to your location and status. Handle with extreme caution.|","| The Loom of Minor Destinies|","|Classification: Fate Manipulation Tool|","|Description: A smaller loom used for manipulating fates of lesser beings. Can alter the destiny of anyone below Absolute Depth.|","|Requirement: Requires thread harvested from the target’s existence to function. Thread must be obtained through direct contact or combat.|","|Secondary Items:|","|Countless spools of fate-thread harvested from collapsed beings across eons.|","|Scissors of various sizes for different scales of destiny manipulation.|","|Preserved \"knots\" representing pivotal moments THE Weavers prevented from occurring.|","|A collection of \"unraveled\" Ways, taken from entities they collapsed before you.|","...!","The prompts were abundant.","But Noah kept his gaze forward as he took his steps lightly to arrive before the objects radiating heart-shaking power.","Now, he had seen a lot of treasures and loot over the many months and years.","But some loot you looked at and you simply felt your heart skip a beat.","He felt this way toward the Golden Scissors that floated in triplicate, their blades gleaming with light that seemed to cut the very air around them.","He felt this way toward THE Axiom of Absolute Denial.","The almost complete Axiom appeared as a crystalline construct of impossible geometry. It was simultaneously a sphere and a cube and shapes that had no names. Its surface was obsidian threaded with gold, and within its depths, the concept of DENIAL swirled in patterns that hurt to observe directly.","Where fragments were missing, the structure showed gaps that looked like wounds in reality itself. Incomplete. Hungry. Waiting to be whole.","Noah waved his hand.","Power surged from his existence as he collected every single one of the secondary items. Spools of fate-thread flowed into his foundations. Scissors of various sizes disappeared into his Grimoire. Knots and unraveled Ways merged with his Civilization. All the other loot apart from the Thread of THE Living Paradox","But the Golden Scissors and the almost complete Axiom resisted his collection.","They acknowledged his victory.","But they did not yet acknowledge his capability to wield them.","Noah reached out to grasp THE Axiom of Absolute Denial directly.","The moment his fingers touched its surface...","Even with how heavy and vast he was at this very moment, this Axiom still felt unfathomably heavy to pick up and utilize.","It was like trying to lift a mountain with fingers meant for feathers.","It was like grasping at concepts too large for his current foundations to contain.","The Axiom was telling him that his Depth was still a ways off.","But he knew that this would not be the case for long.","He was still absorbing the Absolute Depth of the collapsed Weavers. His foundations were still rising. His Weight was still increasing.","Soon.","But even though he was looking at loot that caused his heart to skip a beat, this was actually not the main thing that he was looking for in this place.","Not after he had talked to THE Secretive Eon.","When an Absolute died, Existence mourned.","He knew the sheer absurdity of power that Absolutes wielded. Even though none of them held a Claim to the Oldest Paradox like THE Four did, their Claim was the very Civilization that they took from THE Surface Depth all the way to THE Absolute Depth.","It quite literally permeated across Observable Existence.","He seemed to have underestimated just how intricate this connection with Absolutes was.","So at this moment, he left the dazzling floating loot remaining in this room.","He proceeded even further in.","Pushing past the golden doorway, he arrived in another place.","That loot was completely his and would remain there. As his Depth rose, he would return to grasp all of it and study its utilizations.","The new place he arrived into was even more wondrous than the last.","|Location Identified|","| You have arrived in the Throne of Woven Closure.|","|This place is both the grandest and saddest domain within the Palace.|","|It represents the very Civilization that THE Weavers stood for.|","|They held a mixture of Paradox within them, but the core of their path was Fate.|","|As Absolutes, THE Weavers had the Weavings of their fates integrated across Observable Existence.|","|To the extent that they were even interlinked with Logos and Philologies relating to fates and destinies.|","|They were not merely powerful beings.|","|They were part of how Existence understood the concept of Fate itself.|","HUUM!"]},{"number":4803,"title":"Chapter 4803: Chapter 4802: THE Weaver of Existence III","paragraphs":["The prompts at this time felt heavy and filled with a sense of weight that Noah could not explain.","They continued.","|Unique Weavings of Information Received|","|The Palace is revealing information relating to the Weavings of an Absolute.|","|The information presents itself as such:|","|THE Weavers were Absolutes that integrated their Civilization across the Weavings of Observable Existence relating to Fate.|","|Their collapse is unwinding countless fates and possibilities.|","|This action is generating a net increase in entropy and chaos across Observable Existence.|","| Unknown musings of Corrupted Growths and Malformed Authorities related to fates, paradox, destiny, fortune, and much more were passively being cleared and purified by the authority of THE Weavers.|","| This contributed to the stability of Observable Existence.|","|This is only the basal surface effect that can be discerned right now.|","|With the loss of an Absolute losing their established function...|","|Once it is lost, it is nearly impossible for it to be established again.|","|The killer of an Absolute has their own Way and Civilization.|","|They cannot replace that which they have killed.|","|This is the tragedy of Absolute collapse.|","|This is why Existence mourns.|","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed as he read all of this.","He looked over into the room.","A throne sat at the center.","But it was not a single throne.","It was three seats fused into one, representing the unity of THE Weavers’ existence. The three components leaned toward each other as if in eternal conversation, frozen in the moment of reaching for connection that could never be completed.","Golden threads extended from the throne in all directions.","They connected to every other part of the Palace. To the Treasury of Severed Fates. To the floating loot. To the very walls and ceiling and floor. Everything in this domain was linked to this throne.","Because this throne was THE Weavers.","And THE Weavers were this throne.","|The Tragedy of Absolute Collapse|","|Observe the throne before you.|","|It sits empty.|","|Desolate.|","|Filled with a sense of sadness that transcends normal emotion.|","|This is the tragedy of the human condition extended to Existential scale.|","|When a mortal dies, their family mourns.|","|When an Absolute dies, Existence itself mourns.|","|Because something irreplaceable has been lost.|","|THE Weavers contributed to the function of Observable Existence.|","|That contribution is now gone.|","|The fates they managed are now unmanaged.|","|The corruptions they purified will now spread.|","|The stability they provided will now decay.|","|This is a loss that can never be recovered.|","|Unless...|","|Unless something is capable of sitting upon this throne.|","|Unless something can accept what THE Weavers stood for.|","|Unless something can fill the void they left behind.|","|Only then would the tragedy of the collapse of an Absolute be cleared.|","|Only then would Existence stop mourning.|","Noah looked at these prompts with quiet silence.","His entire figure continued blazing with prismatic blue-gold waves of light.","He remembered the words of THE Secretive Eon.","She had said that when she collapsed an Absolute, she replaced them.","If this was truly an issue...","Would the tragedy of the collapse of THE Weavers truly be a tragedy?","Or would it be a transformation?","Noah walked toward the thrones in the distance.","The golden threads all around reached out toward him.","With hope.","Immense hope of possibility.","They stretched from their fixed positions, straining toward this being who had entered their domain. They did not reach with malice or desperation. They reached with the same instinct that plants reach toward sunlight.","Because he represented continuation.","Because he represented the possibility that their purpose might not end.","Noah proceeded ahead.","The golden threads latched onto his body.","And where they touched him, they turned blue-gold.","The color of The First Tongue.","The color of Mana.","The color of what he represented.","A symphony began to play in the surroundings.","It started soft, barely perceptible. Notes of loss and longing. But as he walked closer to the throne, it grew. Swelling with harmonies that spoke of ancient purpose and desperate hope.","And behind the thrones...","Illusory figures of THE Weavers appeared.","They had no consciousness.","No cognition.","They were merely echoes. Remnants of what had been. Shadows cast by beings whose light had been extinguished.","But they did not look shrewd and despotic as they had in life.","Their skin was fair. Their hair was golden. Their bodies were wrapped in white-gold robes that flowed like destiny itself.","And they began to sing.","Hymns of immense sacredness and glory poured from their throats. Songs that spoke of purpose and duty and the weight of managing fate for all of Observable Existence.","They sang for what they had been.","They sang for what might still be.","They sang for the one who walked toward their throne.","Noah only spared them a glance as he was calm and unmoved.","Then he proceeded to sit down with the absolute authority of someone claiming what was rightfully his, lowering himself onto the throne of THE Weavers with deliberate weight that made the entire Palace tremble in recognition of its new master.","His back pressed against the throne with the casual dominance of a king who had conquered everything worth conquering, his arms resting on the armrests as if they had been carved specifically for his hands to claim. His legs spread slightly in the posture of someone who owned the very ground beneath them, his chin lifted and his eyes blazing with the light of The First Tongue itself.","He sat like Tyranny given form.","At the moment he sat down, Noah truly and fully felt the full weight of the Depth and Civilization of THE Weavers flow toward him.","Countless golden threads now latched onto him from all directions!","They connected to his arms, his legs, his chest, his head! They wove themselves into his existence! They integrated their purpose into his foundations!","The hymns of the illusory manifestations of THE Weavers above became even heavier!","The symphony swelled to a crescendo that shook the very fabric of the Palace!","And at this moment, Noah spoke.","\" All Ways and Civilizations at some point, before differentiation, before specialization... were Mana.\"","His voice carried across the throne room with weight that silenced even the hymns.","\" Were The First Tongue.\"","His eyes blazed brighter.","\" Others may contribute a net loss to Existence when they collapse Absolutes.\"","His smile became something vast and terrible.","\" But every Absolute I collapse... I will take on their Immensity and purpose over Observable Existence.\"","...!","BOOM!","Brilliant golden light shone all around!","The threads that had been connecting to him blazed with incandescent radiance!","The hymns transformed from mourning to celebration!","And in the next moment, in dazzling golden letters that burned themselves into the very air of the Palace...","| THE Weaver of Existence seeks to make his emergence through The First Tongue|"]},{"number":4804,"title":"Chapter 4804: Chapter 4803: THE Weaver of Existence IV","paragraphs":["In his vision, there were countless strings of gold permeated over everything.","They covered so much and were so extensive that they may have overwhelmed him, stretching across distances that his perception had never been able to grasp before. They wove through the air itself, through the walls of the Palace, through the very fabric of reality in patterns so dense and intricate that a lesser being would have been lost in their complexity.","But his gaze turned heavy and imperious moments later.","He looked at these strings and broke them down to Mana!","And all that he could see became strings and dots of Mana covering everything.","The golden threads transformed before his perception, their essence revealed as what they had always truly been at the most fundamental level. Fate was not separate from Mana. Fate was not separate from The First Tongue. It was merely a differentiation, a specialization, a path that Mana had taken when THE Weavers had shaped it according to their will.","And now that will was his.","The strings flowed out of the tomb he was in and stretched out across THE Palaestra, weaving through the ruined Arena where he had collapsed THE Weavers just moments before. They spread across the lands of the Glossarians and Existentialists and all others, touching every faction within this domain with tendrils of fate that now answered to a new master.","They spread across all of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment and even outside to the Stoa of Dogmata.","The threads of Mana, or really, the threads of fate as Mana, flowed and touched his other body sitting near THE Secretive Eon.","His body there shone in recognition!","The strings flowed in the region near THE Secretive Eon as there seemed to be a heavy barrier around her preventing any strings from coming near, an absolute wall of darkness and secrecy that even fate itself could not penetrate.","But shockingly, her eyes flashed sharply!","She looked up and around at the permeating strings nearby as if she could see them, her gaze becoming stern as she turned over to his body there and asked with a voice that carried weight beyond its casual tone.","\" What are you doing?\"","...!","And Noah allowed these threads to spin and spread even faster and more thoroughly!","They left THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap entirely!","They spilled into The Wastes of THE Fallout!","And here, the strings felt unbound chaos and corruption pressing against them from all sides. The Wastes were a nightmare of twisted reality where THE Living Paradox’s actions had scarred Existence itself. The threads encountered resistance, felt the weight of entropy and madness that permeated this region.","But they permeated across it still.","They spread with the inevitability of fate itself, because fate did not discriminate between the pure and the corrupted. Fate touched all things. Fate connected all things. And now, the glimmer of fate followed even corrupted fates all around.","Noah felt his perception expand in an unfathomable manner.","Where before he could see his immediate surroundings, now he could perceive threads stretching across distances that would take eons to travel. Where before he understood only what was directly before him, now he sensed connections and causalities that spanned a vast distance of Observable Existence. Not thr entirety...that was not possible for the current him.","|The Inheritance of Paradoxical Fate|","|The Civilization of THE Weavers was that of Paradoxical Fate, and its Weavings have been received by you and The First Tongue.|","|Mana can differentiate and specialize into anything.|","|This is the truth that has always been.|","|This is the truth that you are now embodying.|","|At this moment, Mana has fully accepted the Way and Depth of THE Weavers and transformed it into a Derivative Civilization under your authority.|","|The First Tongue has gone further to streamline your existence.|","|It officially places the Civilization of Hunger as a Derivative Civilization under you.|","|The musings of THE Weavers have been interpreted and specialized.|","| They have become the Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate.|","|They have fully settled in your existence.|","|Through them, Mana has become interlinked and connected with Fate in a way that was never possible before.|","|The depth and immensity of who you are has risen.|","| You have gained the distinction of THE Weaver of Existence.|","BOOM!","The sensation was a unique one.","As if the sensation of Mana, of The First Tongue he had always been trying to be more in tune with, was becoming clearer. The boundaries between his perception and the fundamental language of reality were thinning. The walls that had separated his understanding from the true nature of Existence were crumbling.","The endless musings of fate stretching out everywhere were now bound under him, and through them, he could perceive The First Tongue that also faced corruption from THE Fallout even easier than before. The threads of fate acted like conduits, like pathways that let him feel the pulse of language across Observable Existence.","And in doing so, he felt immense.","He felt grand.","He felt threads of countless blue-gold stretching out across interminable distances, each one a connection, each one a fate, each one a piece of the vast weaving that now answered to his authority!","|The Throne of Fate Has Been Claimed|","| THE Weaver of Existence has successfully grasped an Absolute Throne that had been integrated and carrying out work across Observable Existence.|","|Though collapsed, this Absolute Throne, this Civilization, has been inherited and is being transformed.|","| THE Weaver of Existence looks upon the complex and corrupted Weavings of Observable Existence.|","|All that which relates to him and is fated for him is being perceived and observed.|","|Fate Connections Detected:|","| The Disciple of THE Secretive Eon has been located in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.|","|She resides in a region between the territories of Existence and Chaos.|","|The location of THE Fisherman, Ains, has been grasped.|","|He drifts through The Wastes of THE Fallout, his fate-thread corrupted but still connected to your Civilization.|","|The locations of others across The Wastes of THE Fallout connected to Mana or Hunger have been observed.|","|They call out through fate-threads that stretch across impossible distances.|","|The pained and Mutated Inevitabilities across The Wastes have been observed.|","| Through them, multiple Shelters of THE Loom have their locations uncovered.|","|Their fates are intertwined with corruption, but corruption does not hide fate from THE Weaver of Existence.|","|The Fates of countless pained Mutated Inevitabilities call out to you.|","|The Fates of those connected to your Civilization call out to you.|","| You perceive. You understand. You see.|","BOOM!","Noah felt as if he was groggily waking up from an unfathomably heavy slumber.","Or rather, as if his vision was waking up.","His eyes had been closed all his life, and now they were finally opening. His perception had been limited to a tiny corner of Existence, and now it was spreading across distances that defied comprehension.","And he could see.","Oh, he could see.","He could see THE Secretive Eon’s Disciple, her fate-thread burning with the light of Existence that she had always admired. He could see Ains, THE Fisherman, drifting through corruption with a fate that stubbornly refused to end. He could see followers of his Civilization scattered across The Wastes, their fates crying out for rescue.","He could see the Shelters of THE Loom, hidden bases where THE Living Paradox’s forces were. He could see the Mutated Inevitabilities that had once been something else, their fates twisted by corruption but still readable to one who now held the authority to read fates.","At this moment, THE Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers illuminated with brilliant golden light!","The radiance blazed outward from the structure that had risen from the vacuum of THE Weavers’ collapse. It was not merely bright. It was meaningful. It was a declaration that burned itself across the fabric of reality.","The four Absolutes nearby frowned with heaviness at seeing this light!","Glossikos’s eyes rustled with agitation that she could not contain. Paradoxos’s four eyes widened with expressions that contradicted each other in their intensity. Khaotikos stopped grinning entirely, his features settling into something that looked almost like concern. Ontikos, the one who never moved, shifted on his throne of uncarved marble.","A golden pillar of light shot out from the Palace!","It stretched out across Existence itself!","Not as the obsidian-gold pillar that had announced THE Weavers’ death, but as something different entirely. Something that carried a different message. Something that made the Absolutes watching feel their foundations pulse.","They knew what this light represented.","They knew what it displayed.","The collapse of an Absolute.","But at the same time, the light was saying something else. Something that should not have been possible.","It said...","The Weavers may have been collapsed, but their work lives on!","Their Civilization lives on!","Their contribution to Observable Existence has not been lost!","Glossikos’s obsidian-blue eyes widened to impossible degrees as she whispered words that carried across the ruined Palaestra.","\"Well...fuck.\"","Golden threads that had been unraveling since THE Weavers’ death began to stabilize.","The entropy that had been spreading, the chaos that had been growing, the corruptions that had begun to spread without THE Weavers to contain them... began to slow.","Because someone had claimed the Throne.","Because someone had accepted the responsibility.","Because THE Weaver of Existence now looked upon the complex and corrupted Weavings of Observable Existence with eyes that could perceive what THE Weavers had once perceived.","What had THE Genesis Monarch done?","What had he done?!","Inside the Palace, Noah sat upon the Throne of Woven Closure with threads of blue-gold fate streaming from his existence in all directions.","His eyes blazed with light that was both Mana and Fate intertwined as he looked like a sacred abomination that was just getting started!"]},{"number":4805,"title":"Chapter 4805: Chapter 4804: Everything I","paragraphs":["Why was it so hard to replace an Absolute?","THE Civilizational Scale of Existence, or THE Level One Scale of Existence, held entities whose Ways held a level of differentiation.","Someone following the Civilization of Elemental, at THE Fundamental Depth more often than not, could also expand their existence to encompass the Way of Fire or the Way of Air. They could branch out, diversify, build subsidiary paths that complemented their main journey.","But ultimately, if and when they attained Absolute, it would be with their singular Civilization of Elemental.","If they were profound enough, they would have Fire or Air as Derivative Civilizations that remained at Fundamental Depth, while their main Elemental Civilization stayed at Absolute Depth.","They had to embody that Civilization absolutely in order to be an Absolute, after all.","The word itself implied totality.","Complete dedication to a single path.","Now the question came which asked... can an Absolute not have two Civilizations at Absolute?","They had such a complex weight of their Depth. Surely, such a thing may be possible?","The answer to this was a very, very difficult one.","And it was why the statement was made that replacing an Absolute was nigh impossible!","To replace an Absolute, one would have to take on their Civilization at the Absolute level. But if one already had their own Civilization at Absolute, the two would conflict.","Two Absolute Civilizations in one being?","It may be considered fundamentally impossible.","But of course, as always, there were exceptions.","At this moment, Noah chose to be one particular exception as he remained attuned in that state where he was seeing a great deal of things.","|THE Weaver of Existence feels a tug from the musing of Undifferentiated Fate.|","|This tug resonates with all Principles related to Fate across Observable Existence.|","|The connection is not complete.|","|The perception is not total.|","|But glimpses are available.|","The Principles related to Fate.","At such words, Noah followed the sensation of that tug.","He felt the glimmer of Principles that looked like countless lines permeating out across different portions of Observable Existence. They were like veins carrying the lifeblood of causality, like roots of a tree so vast that its branches touched every corner of reality.","He felt as if he was sensing portions of them here and there, never a full picture, and never did he even come close to perceiving every single Principle nor even how they permeated across Observable Existence.","That was too distant of a thought.","That level of perception would require Depth far beyond what he currently held.","He only saw glimpses.","And at this moment, he saw scenes of...","Something unique.","Something that made even his hardened existence pause.","It was...corruption.","Malformed Authorities clustered around Principles related to Fate like parasites feeding on a host. They appeared as foam or seaweed, green and obsidian intertwined in patterns that spoke of wrongness made manifest. They clung to Philologies relating to Fate with desperate hunger, their forms pulsing with stolen authority that they were slowly corrupting into something twisted.","Corrupted Growths spread across the surface of pure concepts like mold spreading across bread. They were everywhere he looked, clustering most densely around the Weavings that THE Weavers had once maintained. Without their caretakers, these growths were propagating at rates that would have terrified anyone who understood what they were seeing.","And they seemed unfathomably abundant!","For every pure thread of Fate he perceived, there were dozens of corrupted masses trying to consume it. For every clean Philology, there were hundreds of Malformed Authorities attempting to twist its meaning. The scale of corruption was beyond anything he had anticipated.","This was what THE Weavers had been managing?","As he saw this...","|Unique Information Obtained|","| Observable Existence is so vast that most Absolutes still do not know its true vastness, but it is incomprehensibly stable.|","|This stability was not achieved normally.|","|In nature, all of Existence leans toward entropy and chaos.|","|Without intervention, reality would collapse into formless disorder.|","| The Origin of Corruption|","|Across Observable Existence, countless things mutate and go wrong with every passing moment.|","| Ways collapse. Civilizations fail. Existence Malforms. Beings die. Concepts degrade.|","|As a product of these failed, collapsed, or malformed Weavings of Existence, corruption manifests.|","|This corruption takes the form of Malformed Authorities or Corrupted Growths.|","|These manifestations naturally have a tendency to converge around that which is pure in order to continue the process of degradation.|","|They feed on purity. They spread through contact. They transform order into chaos.|","| The Role of Depth|","|As natural processes of corruption, entities with sufficient Depth can destroy and purify these Corrupted Growths with an exertion of their power.|","|This transforms them back to Pure Civilizational Authority that flows back into Observable Existence to further contribute to its stability.|","|The higher the Depth, the more efficiently this purification occurs.|","| The Role of Absolutes|","|With the existence of Absolutes, nearly all Malformed Authorities converge toward them or the Weavings related to them.|","|This is because Absolutes represent the purest expressions of their Civilizations.|","|Corruption is drawn to purity like moths to flame.|","|Passively, THE Weavers would routinely send their authority out to cleanse the Malformed Authorities or Corrupted Growths that were byproducts of collapsed Existence, collapsed Ways, and all forms of malformation across Observable Existence.|","|This was not a conscious effort.|","|It was as natural as breathing.|","|Their very existence performed this function simply by being what they were.|","|If left unattended, established Weavings of Existence can become malformed.|","|Malformations lead to instability.|","|Instability leads to collapse.|","|Some forms of instabilities and malformations previously observed are:|","|Living Collapses and Mutated Inevitabilities.|","|The Wastes of THE Fallout: An entire region of Observable Existence transformed into concentrated instability through deliberate action.|","|Even with THE Fallout, even with endless corruption spread across Existence, Observable Existence still remains unfathomably stable.|","|By no other reason other than the fact that...|","| Absolutes exist.|","|For Absolutes, cleansing Corrupted Growths before they propagate is something easy.|","|It requires minimal effort and provides benefits in the form of Pure Civilizational Authority reclaimed.|","|It is why Absolutes passively maintain the stability of all Observable Existence simply through the natural expression of their power.|","|This is the function you have inherited.|","| This is the responsibility that now falls upon THE Weaver of Existence, yet another musing and capability of an Absolute, even though you are far from Absolute.|","BOOM!","The information he received was heavy.","Malformed Living. Corrupted Growths. Living Collapses. Mutated Inevitabilities. The Wastes of THE Fallout.","Two of these were natural consequences of entropy in an existence that tended toward chaos.","The other three...","Were all in one way or another related to Paradox!","Living Collapses.","Mutated Inevitabilities.","The Wastes of THE Fallout were the direct result of THE Living Paradox’s actions during THE Change.","Noah sat on the Throne of Woven Closure with threads of blue-gold fate streaming from his existence in all directions!","And his singular thought in all this after learning what he learned was...shouldn’t THE Primordial Chaos be the scariest fucker out there?"]},{"number":4806,"title":"Chapter 4806: Chapter 4805: Everything II","paragraphs":["With all this knowledge regarding Chaos and Entropy and malformations, it all pointed to signs of Chaos truly being the most powerful.","But...there seemed to be more information he needed to obtain to better grasp this as he moved his thoughts elsewhere.","As THE Weaver of Existenc, he had many names, but he truly was a farmer at heart.","The task Absolutes had of purifying Existence and increasing its continued stability while they benefited from it was an act of cultivation and harvesting he would no doubt enjoy. It was not so different from tending fields or nurturing crops. You removed the weeds. You fed the soil. You reaped the rewards.","The scale was simply different.","Where a farmer might tend to acres, he would tend to portions of Observable Existence itself.","But as he received waves and waves of information, one singular ideology became abundantly clear.","Absolutes were a critical and glorious source of Weavings that Observable Existence very much loved. Otherwise, why would it mourn for the collapse of an Absolute? Why would the fabric of reality itself tremble when one of them ceased to be?","It was because Absolutes gave back.","Their very existence was a net positive for all of Observable Existence.","And now Noah understood why THE Secretive Eon had spoken of replacement rather than mere collapse. Why she had emphasized that when she killed an Absolute, nothing was lost.","Because if you killed an Absolute without replacing them, you robbed Observable Existence of one of its caretakers.","You created a wound that would never heal.","But at this point...","Noah sat upon the Throne of THE Weavers.","No.","The Throne of THE Weaver of Existence.","It was his now.","The three seats fused into one supported his weight with the recognition of legitimate inheritance. The golden threads that extended from it in all directions had turned blue-gold where they connected to his existence. The illusory figures of THE Weavers behind him continued their hymns, but the songs had shifted from mourning to something that sounded almost like welcome.","He tapped his finger on the armrest thoughtfully.","His body was surrounded by countless golden strings that pulsed with the rhythm of fate itself. Through them, he could see the endless waves of Corrupted Growths surrounding the many lines of Principles related to Fate. Green and obsidian parasites clustering around pure concepts, feeding on them, slowly transforming order into chaos.","He could express his Formless Depth upon them and purify them.","It would be simple enough.","But...","\" I have claimed The First Tongue.\"","HUUM!","His voice boomed like a grand king making a command rather than a request.","The Palace trembled in response. The golden threads vibrated with recognition of his authority. The hymns behind him swelled with anticipation.","\"I wish to observe and purify Malformed Authorities, Corrupted Growths... that permeate all across The First Tongue.\"","BOOM!","Blue-gold light erupted from him!","It mixed with the pillar of golden light representing the inheritance of THE Weavers, creating a radiance that was both Fate and Language intertwined. His Immensity. His Formless Depth. His continued absorption of the Depth of an Absolute.","He exerted all of it!","|THE Weaver of Existence seeks to observe the interactions of Observable Existence where all of The First Tongue permeates, and this is a lofty goal. Even THE Weavers, Absolutes who had existed since before THE Fallout, could only barely glimpse and perceive all the Principles relating to Fate among other things for them to cleanse Existence through.|","| But THE Weavers did not lay a Claim over The First Tongue, as they were limited to their domain of Fate, and you are not so limited.|","|Due to your current Depth and Immensity, paired with the access you gained by collapsing an Absolute, an unknown percentage of THE First Tongue and how it interacts with Observable Existence is free for observation and manipulation at the most basic degree.|","|The percentage is small compared to the totality, but it is vast compared to what any non-Absolute has ever perceived.|","|Open your eyes, THE Weaver of Existence, and see what you have claimed.|","BOOM!","The moment such a prompt came, Noah’s eyes pulsed with light!","He saw everything become covered in blue-gold brilliance.","Everything!","In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, The First Tongue permeated through every faction’s territory like an invisible ocean that all beings swam through without knowing. The Glossarians naturally had denser concentrations, but even the Paradoxians and Chaosites and Existentialists utilized language. Even they spoke. Even they wrote. Even they thought in words that were derivatives of The First Tongue.","In THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap, The First Tongue filtered through the ancient Primordial Realm with threads that connected to secrets older than most Absolutes. The Nexus Point between Primordial Realms blazed with concentrated linguistic authority where fundamental truths about Existence had first been spoken into being.","In the nearby Wastes of THE Fallout, even corruption could not erase The First Tongue. It persisted through the chaos, words of power that had survived THE Living Paradox’s attempt to reshape reality. Corrupted, yes. Twisted, certainly. But still present. Still readable to one who had laid claim to their authority.","All of it had The First Tongue permeating across it!","He saw how The First Tongue, how Mana, filtered through the gaps of Weavings of everything like an endless blue-gold sea!","It was not merely present.","It was fundamental.","It wove through the components of the other three Weavings of the Oldest Paradox of Existence in ways that were both complementary and essential.","Where Paradox twisted reality, The First Tongue provided the framework for that twisting. Where Chaos disrupted order, The First Tongue gave names to that disruption. Where Existence simply was, The First Tongue described what that being meant.","The First Tongue touched all of them.","He perceived all lines of Principles nearby, golden threads of Fate and silver threads of other concepts and crimson threads of yet others, all of them surrounded by the blue-gold sea of linguistic authority. He even sensed all of THE Infiniverse, his own Early Veiled Shore where his Civilization grew and flourished.","He felt portions of Muspelheim, the Primordial Realm of fire where Skoll had originated. He touched the edges of the Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature himself, that vast domain where the most powerful of THE Four had built his Belly of Existence.","And moments later, Noah could also perceive the countless Corrupted Growths hugging different areas of this sea like parasites or weeds.","They were everywhere.","But not evenly distributed.","Some areas were fairly empty of them, the blue-gold sea running clean and pure as if they had recently been cleansed. These regions sparkled with stability that spoke of diligent maintenance.","Other areas were more filled with corruption, green-obsidian masses clustering around linguistic concepts and slowly transforming their meanings. These areas had not been cleansed in a while, or corruption was propagating at higher frequencies due to instability in the underlying Weavings.","Noah observed the patterns with the calculating eye of a farmer assessing his fields.","The regions most infected with Corrupted Growths were concentrated primarily in two areas.","Paradox.","And Existence!"]},{"number":4807,"title":"Chapter 4807: Chapter 4806: Everything III","paragraphs":["The Weavings related to THE Living Paradox were absolutely crawling with corruption. It made sense given what Noah now understood.","THE Living Paradox spread instability through his very actions. His changes to reality created byproducts of malformation that naturally accumulated around anything connected to him.","The Weavings related to THE Creature were also surprisingly infected.","But Chaos...","Chaos was actually relatively clean.","It did not make sense!","Was THE Primordial Chaos more diligent than even Paradox and THE Creature?","The being who represented disorder and entropy was somehow maintaining his domain with more care than those who represented existence and contradiction?","Noah filed this information away for later contemplation. There was something there. Some insight into the nature of THE Primordial Chaos that contradicted his apparent philosophy. Some secret hidden in the cleanliness of Chaos that spoke of intentions not yet revealed.","But for now, he had work to do.","Noah perceived all of this before he shook his head and focused.","In the next moment, he began forming a Logos with his Seals of Absolute Tongue.","The Seals that were branded across his skin blazed with incandescent light. They rotated around his form, aligning themselves according to principles that transcended normal linguistic construction. Letters combined. Sounds merged. Meaning crystallized.","A word formed.","A word of power.","A word that carried the authority of THE Weaver of Existence, THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons.","CLEANSE!","BOOOM!","He did not need to use it like this.","He could have just utilized his Depth and expressed it to press down on all the Corrupted Growths he saw. It would have been efficient. It would have been effective. It would have accomplished the same goal with less expenditure of authority.","But he did it because he could.","He did it because he wanted to see what would happen when The First Tongue itself commanded corruption to cease.","He did it because he was a farmer, and a farmer took pride in the tools of his trade.","In the next moment, a blinding blue-gold light permeated over everything Noah had the visibility to see!","It spread like dawn breaking across an endless horizon!","It washed over THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, touching every corner of that vast domain where four philosophical factions competed for supremacy.","It spread through THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","It spread into the nearby Wastes, pushing back against corruption that had seemed eternal. For just a moment, for just a breath, some regions of the Wastes of THE Fallout became slightly less chaotic. Slightly more stable. Slightly more like what they had been before THE Living Paradox had scarred reality itself.","And as soon as his cleansing light passed over it, all the countless Corrupted Growths across different regions of Observable Existence that he could see and grasp trembled!","They shriveled!","The green-obsidian masses that had been feeding on purity found themselves facing authority that transcended their parasitic existence. They could not resist. They could not flee. They could only transform.","They turned into pure white-gold light!","The corruption that had been feeding on The First Tongue was converted back into Pure Civilizational Authority that then sank and permeated into the surrounding Observable Existence. What had been poison became medicine. What had been degradation became nourishment. What had been entropy became stability.","All the lines representing golden threads of Principles related to Fate became clean.","All the endless blue-gold seas permeating over everything that Noah saw became free of any Corrupted Growths.","And as this cleansing finished, the affected regions seemed to shine even more brightly!","The First Tongue ran cleaner through Weavings that had been partially clogged with corruption. Principles pulsed with renewed vigor now that parasites no longer fed upon them. Nearby Existence itself seemed to breathe easier in the regions that Noah had touched.","And as this action finished...","BOOM !","Noah felt a loud boom in his mind and existence!","A heavy and unfathomable thing emerged within him!","It was not Depth. It was not Weight. It was not any of the conventional measurements of power that he had grown accustomed to tracking.","It was something else entirely.","Something that felt like concentrated wonder from Observable Existence itself.","|Purification Complete|","|You have cleansed a significant portion of Existence and contributed to the net positive stability of Observable Existence, and this contribution has been recognized.|","|Finally, for the first time in your existence, you are a significant contributing member of Civilization, of Observable Existence, as before this moment you only took and harvested and consumed and grew through the collapse of others, which is not wrong since it is how the strong become stronger, but it is not the only way.|","|The grander the contributors of Observable Existence are, the grander Observable Existence is, and vice versa, because Observable Existence is vast and seemingly endless but it does not exist by itself as it is not a passive backdrop against which events unfold, but rather a living musing woven from the contributions of all who exist within it.|","|Those within it decide just how immense they are, and as a result, how immense Observable Existence itself becomes.|","|You have decided to be immense, and Observable Existence has thus become enen more immense.|","...!","The prompts were heavy, but Noah only gave them a glance.","His attention was focused on what was emerging in his existence.","He looked inward, toward THE Organ of Civilization where his Ways and Depths were housed. Where his Civilizations of Mana and Hunger flowed through. Where the newly inherited Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate had begun flowing.","And there, forming among these foundations, was something new.","It looked like a cluster of mobius strips wrapping around each other endlessly, surfaces that had no true beginning or end, edges that connected to themselves in impossible geometries. It pulsed with light that was simultaneously all colors and no color. It hummed with a frequency that resonated with the very fabric of Observable Existence.","And it was fucking heavy.","Fat and heavy!"]},{"number":4808,"title":"Chapter 4808: Chapter 4807: Everything IV","paragraphs":["Even just perceiving it made Noah’s foundations tremble with the effort of containing its weight. It pressed against the boundaries of his existence as if testing whether he was worthy of housing it!","| Absolute Everything Formed|","|You have cleansed a large portion of Existence and formed your first genuine Absolute Everything of your existence, which represents the currency of Absolutes and marks your first step on a path that only Absolutes can walk.|","|An Absolute Everything is condensed potential that can be utilized in ways that normal authority cannot, as where lesser beings accumulate Depth and Weight and Civilizational Authority, Absolutes accumulate Absolute Everythings that are formed through an expression of their own power, or when an Absolute contributes significantly to Observable Existence in ways that lesser beings cannot.|","|Purifying corruption, stabilizing Weavings, and maintaining the fabric of reality itself are all actions that generate Absolute Everythings due to the net positive gained from such actions.|","| Absolute Everything Properties and Utilizations|","|Depth Elevation: Absolute Everythings can be consumed to directly elevate Depth without the need for conventional advancement, as where a normal being must accumulate authority over eons to reach Absolute, one who possesses sufficient Absolute Everythings can simply forge an unquestionable Foundation to act as a stairway to Absolute by converting this currency into pure Depth.|","|Axiom Utilization: Absolute Everythings can serve as fuel for Axioms, and where THE Axiom of Absolute Denial currently resists your usage due to insufficient Depth, feeding it an Absolute Everything would allow temporary activation regardless of your classification, with the more complete the Axiom, the more Absolute Everythings required for full utilization.|","|Artifact Nurturing: Absolute-tier Artifacts like the Golden Scissors of Fate require Absolute Everythings to reach their full potential when wielded by non-Absolutes, as an Absolute Everything fed to such an artifact creates a temporary bond that allows usage and even forging of similar items.|","|Existence Manipulation: Absolute Everythings can be expended to perform actions that would normally require Absolute Depth, allowing for Embodiments and other forms of expressions.|","|Absolutes maintain Observable Existence with such diligence because they are not being altruistic but rather gaining Absolute Everythings through large cleansings of Corrupted Growths.|","|The gap between Absolutes and non-Absolutes is not merely one of Depth but one of access, as Absolutes have access to Absolute Everythings while non-Absolutes do not, at least until now.|","|You, THE Weaver of Existence, have bridged that gap by forming your first Absolute Everything without being an Absolute yourself, accessing the currency that fuels the most powerful beings in Observable Existence while still being below their classification.|","...!","Noah stared at the cluster of mobius strips rotating within his existence.","His first Absolute Everything.","It was something unique to feel as around the same time that he was analyzing the cluster of mobius strips within his existence, another set of prompts came down with information that made his foundations pulse with recognition.","|Absolute Depth Absorption Complete|","|The recoverable Depth of an Absolute has been fully absorbed and distributed across your recovered Fundamental Depth foundation, or really, within your Formless Depth that defies conventional classification.|","|Although it may be inaccurate due to the limited data available on the foundations of THE Four during their earlier stages, it has been estimated that devouring the recoverable Depth of an Absolute like THE Weavers has reinforced your Fundamental Depth weight and immensity to be approximately 25% comparable to that of THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos when they crossed this stage.|","|Little information is available regarding the foundations of THE Four, but it seems that the foundations built by these beings sought to make up for all the deficiencies of weight in their prior Depths before they took a step to become Absolutes with unquestionable foundations.|","|They spent eons at Fundamental Depth, building weight that would support their eventual ascension.|","|You have achieved 25% of that weight in a fraction of the time through the consumption of an Absolute.|","|Civilizational Status|","| Primary Civilization: THE Primordial Civilization of Mana(THE First Tongue)|","|Classification: Formless Depth (unplaceable within conventional categories)|","|Status: Primary vessel for all authority, containing foundations that exceed THE Creature at Surface and Intermediate classifications while approaching meaningful comparison at Fundamental|","| Derivative Civilization: Hunger|","|Classification: THE Fundamental Depth|","|Status: Fully integrated, contributing to Perpetual Harvest and consumption-based advancement|","| Derivative Civilization: Undifferentiated Fate|","|Classification: THE Fundamental Depth|","|Status: Newly inherited from THE Weavers, provides access to fate perception and manipulation across Observable Existence|","| Derivative Civilization: Elemental|","|Classification: Pre-THE|","|Status: (Will you continue your encroachment on your most hated enemy in existence?)|","...!","The vibrant pressure around him calmed.","He remained on the throne as he was still receiving waves of information from different sources, but at this moment, he raised his hand and clenched his fist as...","BZZT!","A terrifying pressure emanated from him!","It radiated outward from his existence with weight that would have crushed any Fundamental Depth entity into paste. It pressed against the walls of THE Absolute Existential Palace with authority that made even this domain of a dead Absolute tremble slightly.","He could clearly feel that it was as oppressive as, if not a bit more oppressive than, the Half-Step Absolute Depth of THE Living Spirit!","More immense and grand than someone who was Half-Step Absolute!","|Comparative Assessment Confirmed|","|Your current Depth and Weight exceeds the Half-Step Absolute classification as demonstrated by THE Living Spirit and similar entities, and if you were to meet THE Living Spirit again, you could potentially curb stomp him without utilizing any Axioms or special artifacts. It may be time to say hi to THE Living Concept.|","|You have devoured an Absolute, and this simple action alone will make it extremely hard to find any enemy below Absolute Depth capable of going against you.|","|At most, Half-Step Absolutes, depending on who they are and what type of treasures or Axiom fragments they carry, could give you a challenge, but even then, your Formless Depth and the foundations you have built that exceed THE Creature at multiple classifications would provide advantages that most Half-Step Absolutes simply cannot overcome.|","| You are no longer prey for anything below Absolute.|","The affirmation was a grand one as Noah gave a light nod while looking at another distant door.","The Tomb of THE Weavers had many things as he sensed that what remained were her memories locked in the Memory Sanctum, but he would come back for these later as right now, he wanted to do a few things.","So he rose up from the throne as golden strings followed him like loyal pets seeking their master’s attention.","But his eyes flashed with authority.","The strings dimmed and disappeared completely, retreating back into the fabric of the Palace to await his return.","The Tomb of THE Weavers could be considered half cleared with many things still in it, including the Golden Scissors of Fate and THE Axiom of Absolute Denial that still resisted his grasp, but it was still his treasury as he would come back to it when his Depth rose further.","For now...","He took a step and disappeared.","HUUM!","He could sense the fates and Mana of all those connected with him, threads of blue-gold that stretched across distances and told him exactly where his people were and what state they were in.","He appeared in the shattered stands of THE Palaestra, right behind Ul’moreth and Lumivara and Skoll who remained where they were, but at this moment, the heavy and interminable auras of Absolutes shockingly pressed around them!","The situation had changed since he had entered the Tomb.","The visage of Paradoxos shockingly floated a distance away from his followers, their dual form radiating menace that would have crushed any Fundamental Depth entity into submission. Four eyes burned with fury that had not diminished since watching Noah collapse their faction’s Absolute.","And Glossikos, this dazzling Dryad, stood in front of Ul’moreth and Lumivara with an imperious expression, her eyes pulsing.","When Noah appeared beside Ul’moreth and Lumivara, both Absolutes gave glances to him that he completely ignored as he got down on one knee and began to play with an excited Skoll who saw his Master return!","The massive dog’s tail wagged with enthusiasm that seemed entirely out of place given the tension filling the air. His neon flames brightened. His tongue lolled out in pure canine joy.","While Noah rubbed his ears and scratched behind his head...","\"I wonder what the great Strategoi of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment would be gracing their presence for little things like us.\"","His voice came casual and unbothered, as if he was not surrounded by beings who could reshape reality with a thought.","\"Is there anything we can help you with?\"","HUUM!","He did not even gaze at them.","He spoke while playing with his dog as the Absolutes turned over with shining eyes!","The way they looked at him had changed completely!"]},{"number":4809,"title":"Chapter 4809: Chapter 4808: Vast and Full of Terrors! I","paragraphs":["Noah knew the full scope of his power as he did not delude himself into thinking that just because he killed an Absolute, he held the power to stand against another.","He didn’t have the raw power to do that, no.","But there were always musings of Existence that made things complicated for even Absolutes to move at times.","What he did with THE Weavers was a trick that one could say would be nigh impossible to repeat again, as all Absolutes now knew the result of trying to claim what they could not back.","No Absolute would be foolish enough to grasp his Heart after witnessing what had occurred. No Absolute would attempt to claim The First Tongue without knowing they possessed the Infinities required to bear its weight.","That particular trap had been sprung.","It would not work twice.","And also...","THE Agora of Primordial Judgment was a domain with its own rulings, and its Absolutes could not move against him freely.","There were protocols and challenges and rights that protected those who had earned standing within this place.","So he continued moving with the same Immensity and grandness his entire existence emanated, even though he knew that the Absolutes here may not be as powerless as they appeared!","So he asked how he could help them.","And a voice boomed out.","\" You are grand.\"","The words came from Paradoxos, both faces speaking in rare unison with weight that pressed against everyone present.","\" By all accounts you are deserving of the standing among THE Four purely from what you did here today.\"","A pause that felt like it lasted an eternity.","\" But you... are not fully there.\"","...!","The booming voice of Paradoxos echoed out grandly as Noah finally raised his head to glance at this being.","An ugly and grand fucker he was with his two faces that contradicted each other even while saying the same words. Half obsidian, half gold, the division line between them constantly shifting as if reality itself could not decide which half should dominate.","Noah looked at this being, and then at Glossikos who stood between him and Paradoxos.","Had she finally come to a decision and stuck to it?","Because he had seen her greed for his Heart and Claim when he took it out during the battle. He had seen how she had nearly broken through the Arena’s barriers to reach for what he was offering. He had seen the hunger in those obsidian-blue eyes.","And yet here she stood, positioned between him and Paradoxos as if protecting him.","He looked between the two of them as Paradoxos continued with a voice that carried the weight of someone accustomed to being obeyed.","\" THE Weavers took something from me that was not theirs. As the one to have claimed their Tomb, you should have obtained it.\"","Four eyes fixed on Noah with intensity that would have crushed lesser beings into immediate compliance.","\" THE Axiom of Absolute Denial. I wish to have this back.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he looked over to Paradoxos!","When he used the Lens of Civilization on this being, it returned absolutely nothing useful as this entity was genuinely at the Absolute Depth, beyond the ability of his current perception to accurately assess!","And yet even against him, Noah tilted his head with casual dismissiveness and said with a voice that held no trace of the deference one might expect when addressing an Absolute.","\" Oh? So you gave THE Weavers an Axiom that wasn’t theirs before the battle just to guarantee my collapse? Whatever did I do to you to deserve that treatment?\"","He spoke casually as he rose up from where he had been playing with Skoll to meet the gaze of Paradoxos, his posture radiating the confidence of someone who had just collapsed an Absolute and felt no need to bow before another!","Paradoxos looked at him calmly, four eyes unblinking, before speaking simply.","\" The Axiom of Absolute Denial. The one asking for it back is not me.\"","HUUM!","...!","The one asking for it back wasn’t Paradoxos.","As the only one who could have the support of another Absolute like Paradoxos, the only one who could demand such things through intermediaries bound to THE Agora, the only one whose request would make a Strategos act as a messenger...","Had to be a single being.","THE Living Paradox.","Noah smiled at the sheer idea alone that he had stolen something belonging to one of THE Four, something that THE Living Paradox had lent to THE Weavers specifically to guarantee their victory against him, and he smiled even wider as he said with cheerful defiance that bordered on mockery.","\" Even if THE Creature stood where you stand and demanded such a thing from me, I would still say no.\"","His voice moved across the ruined Palaestra with weight that made his words feel like Declarations rather than mere statements.","\" And regardless, Existence is so vast and filled with wonders that we should not place importance on items so much. Do not worry about a mere Axiom, O Great Strategos\"","He paused, letting the dismissal settle.","\" And. ..\"","He looked toward Glossikos as he said with innocent curiosity that fooled absolutely no one.","\"I seem to remember that you all hate THE Four with a passion. Why would you be listening to THE Living Paradox so astutely?\"","BOOM!","He said such words with calmness as both Absolutes here silently stared at him, and he could feel the distant gazes of the Strategoi of Existentialists and Chaos observing from their thrones far above.","At this moment, both sides seemed to be only looking at each other with heavy tension that made the air itself grow thick with unspoken threats and calculations!","Paradoxos stood representing the interests of THE Living Paradox, seeking to reclaim what had been lost.","Glossikos stood representing... what exactly? Her own interests? The interests of The First Tongue? Or simply the desire to spite the very beings who had bound her to this place for eons?","The silence stretched.","Until ultimately...","\" Hold your existence and connections steadfast.\"","Paradoxos spoke with a voice that held a warning wrapped in the guise of advice.","\" For Existence is vast and full of terrors, and things can always change so... rapidly.\"","Both faces smiled with expressions that contradicted each other yet somehow conveyed the same menace.","\" Just look at THE Weavers as an example.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":4810,"title":"Chapter 4810: Chapter 4809: Vast and Full of Terrors! II","paragraphs":["After he said such words, he looked toward Glossikos as if he was disappointed in her choice to stand where she stood, and he disappeared with a flash of obsidian-gold light that left afterimages burned into the air!","A heavy silence settled in the destroyed Palaestra.","Noah looked toward Glossikos who turned to him with a calm gaze that seemed to be hiding many things beneath its composed surface.","He did not trust this bitch at all.","She was an Absolute who had spent eons failing to claim what he had claimed. She was a being who had shown naked greed for his Heart when he offered it to THE Weavers. She was someone whose motivations remained unclear even after everything that had occurred.","But she was a follower of The First Tongue and wanted everything about it, so until she made her allegiances clear, there were still many things he could do with her.","And at this moment...","\" Hey, I need to make a visit to the lands of Existentialists in this place.\"","...!","He spoke such words calmly as if he didn’t even want to discuss THE Weavers or the Axiom or the implicit threat that Paradoxos had just delivered on behalf of THE Living Paradox!","He wanted to get a move on his objectives as things were moving around far too quickly, and all of it was mainly due to him and his actions across existence since arriving in THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","But as he held the Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate under him, he now sensed many more things across Existence.","Threads of fate that he could perceive and follow.","Connections that had been invisible before but now blazed with clarity.","And the Disciple of THE Secretive Eon was one he could grab right now and complete this objective!","—","Around the same time.","In Alfheimr.","THE Primordial Chaos walked through the crystalline forests of Alfheimr with the ease of someone who owned everything and nothing simultaneously.","The glory of his form shifting constantly as THE Living Emotive floated beside him and THE Living Elemental trailed behind with the caution of someone who knew he was in dangerous company.","THE Primordial Chaos looked up at the obsidian gold pillar that still had not faded above as if it was reminding him of long forgotten memories.","Emotive blinked as she looked at him and said...","\" Scary old man, what are you thinking about right now with such a brutal gaze?\"","THE Primordial Chaos did not turn to her as he replied calmly.","\"I was remembering an Absolute I collapsed long ago, during the Infinite Unfurling.\"","BOOM!","Emotive’s emotions had been cycling through boredom and mild interest, but her eyes now shone brighlty as she came closer as if she was ready to listen, and Elemental remained silent.","\" His name was THE Solitary Extreme.\"","Chaos’s shifting features settled into something almost nostalgic.","\" He was magnificent in ways that most Absolutes could only dream of being. He burned brighter than any constellation of lesser beings, fueled entirely by his own foundations, beholden to nothing and connected to none. He did not share his authority. He did not receive support from others. He simply burned, alone and magnificent, because burning alone was what THE Solitary Extreme had always done.\"","The crystalline trees around them seemed to lean in, as if even the realm of Alfheimr wanted to hear this tale.","\" And when I came for him, THE Solitary Extreme collapsed into himself as it was not even a grand battle, and I had even gone there to give him a choice.\"","Chaos’s voice grew heavier with each word.","\" No other Absolute felt his death approaching in time to intervene. No other power dimmed itself to come to his aid. The vast expanse of Observable Existence simply watched as I consumed something that had touched nothing beyond itself.\"","He paused, letting the weight of the memory settle.","\" Other Absolutes I have faced over the eons, they had connections. They had threads tying their fates to beings who would cross Existence to stand beside them. They had networks of Ways that supported and elevated each other when crisis arrived. Those Absolutes were harder to collapse. Some remain uncollapsed to this day precisely because I could never catch them truly alone. Osmont, when I met him, had many that wanted to stand by his side in Ginnungagap. He was not isolated, and he moved from the grasp of Temporal and others smoothly.\"","His smile became something vast and knowing.","\" But THE Solitary Extreme believed that isolation was strength. Because solitude felt safer.\"","Chaos turned to look at both Emotive and Elemental with eyes that held depths of accumulated eons.","\" There is a particular pride in standing alone that many mistake for power. The pride of saying that everything one has achieved came from within, that no hand lifted them, that no thread tied their fate to another.\"","His voice dropped to something that resonated with the very fabric of Alfheimr itself.","\"It is the pride of THE Solitary Extreme, burning bright and burning fast and burning toward an ending that no one came to prevent.\"","\" An Absolute who burns in constellation with others may shine less brilliantly in isolation, but they burn longer, reach further, and when enemies come for them, the threads they have woven become shields that solitary brilliance can never provide. And yet THE Weaver, with all her connections, perished alone, while other Absolutes were even observing. So truly...what is The Way? Isolation, or connections?\"","Elemental listened silently.","And Emotive yawned as if she had lost interest and was bored.","A moment later, she blinked and turned her head sharply as she looked toward a certain direction with eyes that suddenly blazed with genuine interest.","\" No fucking way...\"","...!","\"Oh, I wasn’t talking about your boring ass story.\"","She waved her hand dismissively at Chaos while her attention remained locked on whatever she had sensed.","\"I seem to have found something unbelievable over there.\"","...!","THE Primordial Chaos remained calm as he looked at Emotive and what she had sensed, his shifting features betraying nothing of the fact that this was something he had already observed the moment he arrived in Alfheimr.","THE Living Emotive was staring into the far distance, her attention locked onto a grand citadel filled with life and activity that blazed against the serene beauty of the Primordial Realm.","And within that citadel, THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger had just arrived."]},{"number":4811,"title":"Chapter 4811: Chapter 4810: A Meeting in Alfheimr! I","paragraphs":["The Citadel of Yggdrasil’s Echo rose from the heart of Alfheimr like a living testament to the majesty of Existence itself.","The walls were woven from luminescent vines that had been cultivating since before The Infinite Unfurling, their leaves shimmering with colors that existed only in this Primordial Realm.","Bridges of solidified starlight connected the various towers, and waterfalls of liquid Mana cascaded from floating gardens that orbited the central structure like devoted moons around a radiant sun.","The inhabitants of this place were beings of breathtaking beauty and terrible power.","Ljósálfar, natives of Alfheimr, moved through the corridors with grace that transcended physical movement, their forms composed of light given flesh and purpose.","Some had wings of crystalline energy. Others bore antlers that branched into configurations that mapped the very Weavings of Existence. All of them radiated the unmistakable signature of THE Creature’s domain, beings who had been shaped by the authority of Existence itself across countless eons.","This was the realm where THE Creature had first risen.","This was the birthplace of the most powerful of THE Four.","And today, this citadel welcomed home one of its most beloved daughters.","THE Living Origin stood at the center of the Grand Processional Hall, surrounded by lifeforms who looked upon her with reverence that transcended mere respect.","THE First Hunger stood behind her with solemn vigilance, his crimson-obsidian eyes scanning the gathered crowd.","Multiple THE Surface Depth entities floated in the outer rings of the gathering, their presence adding weight to the ceremonial atmosphere. Intermediate Depth beings occupied the middle tiers, their authority contributing to the layered Immensity that filled the hall.","And circling closest to Origin herself, eight Fundamental Depth entities gazed upon her with eyes that held memories stretching back to ages she had nearly forgotten.","\" Ljósmóðir returns!\"","The cry went up from countless throats.","\" The Mother of Light walks among us once more!\"","Ljósmóðir.","It was a distinction that Origin had earned in ages past, when she had helped THE Creature learn of the foundations of what Alfheimr would become. She had been his companion then!","The procession swelled around her with joy that felt almost painful after so long in isolation.","Ljósálfar reached out to touch her robes as she passed, seeking connection with one they had mourned as lost.","The eight Fundamental Depth entities began to sing hymns of welcome.","And for just a moment, Origin allowed herself to feel something like peace.","Peace.","And yet...peace never did last long, did it?","BOOM!","The skies above quaked!","The crystalline spires of the citadel trembled!","The hymns of welcome died in throats that suddenly forgot how to produce sound!","Three figures descended from above.","THE Primordial Chaos came first, his form shifting constantly as reality itself seemed unable to decide what shape should contain him. His presence alone was enough to silence everything within the citadel, the sheer weight of his Absolute Depth pressing down on all present like the hand of something that had existed since before differentiation.","His gaze was calm and distant as if all of this had nothing to do with him, as if he was merely passing through on his way to matters of actual importance.","THE Living Emotive floated beside him, her body crackling with emotions that cycled faster than expressions could form, joy and malice and curiosity and hunger all competing for dominance across her features.","THE Living Elemental trailed behind them, his form shrouded by Phonemes of Fire, Air, Earth, and Water.","But moments after arriving, the calm and distant gaze of THE Primordial Chaos changed.","He frowned.","His shifting features settled into something focused as he looked at Origin, sensing something on her being that interested him.","Origin and Hunger looked up with heavy gazes at this moment as they observed the new entrants.","The eyes of Origin actually only glanced at Chaos before they locked onto Emotive.","And in the next moment, Emotive smiled brilliantly toward THE Living Origin with an expression that held joy and menace in equal measure.","Her figure moved forward like a flicker of light!","The power of an Absolute crashed down immensely!","All lifeforms nearby had color draining from their faces as they were all forced to kneel under pressure that transcended anything they had ever experienced. The Ljósálfar collapsed. The Surface Depth entities buckled. The Intermediate Depth beings fell to their knees with expressions of terror. Even the eight Fundamental Depth entities, ancient beings who had existed since before THE Fallout, found themselves pressing against the ground with effort that strained their very foundations.","And shockingly, even THE First Hunger trembled!","His crimson-obsidian flames blazed desperately as he sought to prevent being forced to kneel, his pride as one who had devoured Folds refusing to allow him to bow before anyone.","Emotive came before Origin with an utterly smiling expression.","And in the next moment...","\" Haha, Origin! I thought you collapsed and were forgotten, but here you are!\"","...!","After she said this, Emotive actually jumped forward and embraced Origin, wrapping her arms around the being she had not seen in eons and giving her a hug as if they were long-time friends reuniting after a brief separation!","She did all of this as in contrast, everything and everyone around her was shaking from her horrific pressure that continued to press down without mercy or restraint.","But in the next moment, with a calm wave from the hand of THE Primordial Chaos above, all of this pressure faded.","Chaos looked toward Emotive and said with a voice that carried absolute authority.","\" Behave.\"","HUUM!","The pressure emerging from her immediately faded as Emotive pouted with an expression that cycled through irritation and amusement.","But she kept her gaze on Origin, who was staring at her coldly and without any emotions warming her white-gold eyes.","Emotive let go of her embrace as she looked over Origin up and down with a smile that evaluated and judged and found entertainment in what she observed.","\" Man, so much has changed since I last saw you. A bit more fat here and there, but still so gorgeous...\"","Her voice dripped with honeyed venom.","\" You seem to be a bit weak as... who knew I would be among those to become an Absolute before the great Living Origin?\"","She tilted her head with mock sympathy.","\"I mean, I can sense your Depth fluctuating as this is...\"","She breathed in deeply as if she smelled something from Origin.","And she smiled even wider after.","\" Oh, that’s definitely the smell of THE Creature. Did he give you a little bit of something something after all this time?\"","Her emotions cycled through delight and mockery.","\" But one can only be given so much, as for Absolute, it ultimately has to be yourself... ah, no worries.\"","She paused as her prismatic eyes narrowed.","\" But why do I also smell a uniqueness of The First Tongue within you?\"","Her smile became something sharp.","\" Is it... true that you jumped ship? Is it true that you went to... THE Youngest making waves?\"","Her voice dropped to something almost intimate.","\" Osmont?\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4812,"title":"Chapter 4812: Chapter 4811: A Meeting in Alfheimr! II","paragraphs":["She asked as her eyes burned with a dangerous light, her smile never leaving her features as she was acting as if she was gossiping with a long-term friend about inconsequential matters.","And yet Origin looked at Emotive with clear distaste as she said with a voice that could have frozen the waterfalls of liquid Mana flowing throughout the citadel.","\" Who I associate with is none of your concern.\"","...!","Her words were chilly as Emotive smiled even more brilliantly.","She came ever closer as she wrapped her hands around Origin once more, leaning in to whisper in her ear with a breath that carried the weight of countless chaotic emotions.","\" How is Osmont? Is he as... grand as THE Creature? Is that why he made you jump ship?\"","Her whisper held manic intensity.","\" I’ve been... ecstatic to meet him, you know. Could you introduce us?\"","Her grip tightened slightly.","\" You always have this way of picking the good ones first, and the rest of us can only meet them later...\"","...!","Her words were filled with manic emotions as Origin calmly took Emotive’s hands off her body and distanced herself while moving to stand beside a solemn First Hunger.","Her gaze remained heavy as she looked at Emotive and then at THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Elemental above.","\" What do you want?\"","What did they want?","Or in this case, what did Emotive want, because somehow, as always, she was moving things along with her chaotic interference.","\" What do I want? Oh, I want many things in Existence. So many. I want...!\"","Before she could finish her words, Emotive stopped.","At this moment, THE Primordial Chaos landed down beside them.","A unique air of power radiated from him that cut off everything and everyone.","It even pressed down on Emotive as if to say... enough of your antics, a true power is here.","...!","Emotive’s gaze flickered as her eyes flashed with humiliation, but Chaos seemed serious at this time as even she could not step out of line!","Because as much as she loved to break boundaries and play, THE Primordial Chaos was still one of THE Four!","They were all Absolutes, but THE Primordial Chaos could likely crush her and Elemental with the same thumb he pressed down with.","They were absolutely not in the same category.","At this moment, Chaos walked over and looked at Origin and Hunger with a serene gaze that held depths of calculation behind its apparent calm.","\" As if we are back in Ginnungagap again in that pivotal moment.\"","His voice carried nostalgia that seemed almost genuine.","\" How unique.\"","He paused.","\" But when it comes to what I want... it is actually the same as always.\"","His shifting features settled into something almost kind.","\" I want a choice.\"","He tilted his head as he studied Origin more closely.","\"I didn’t expect it until I looked closely at you, but... you can reach out to THE Youngest, can’t you?\"","His smile became something that made even Emotive grow still.","\"I wish to give you the choice to call him over. I feel like a conversation is long overdue.\"","BOOM!","The gaze of THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger became heavy.","A conversation?","Nothing with an Absolute was ever just... a conversation!","—","Noah sat on an enlarged Skoll who now looked like a very good dog of large size as he entered what was known as The Ousia in the Middle City, Meso Polis , where mainly Lochagoi resided.","The Ousia was a grand domain that Existentialists gathered around, and it looked like an ancient structure fused with Existence itself.","Pillars of living stone rose toward artificial skies that shifted with the breathing of the realm. Gardens of conceptual flowers bloomed in patterns that spoke of truths about being and becoming. Pools of liquid Existence reflected not images but essences, showing those who gazed into them glimpses of what they truly were beneath their surface forms.","At this moment, Noah was looking at a figure of a fairy-like existence who sat atop a small mountain surrounded by multicolored sacred herbs.","There were multiple such mountains like this surrounding The Ousia where many Existentialists cultivated, beings so attuned to nature and Existence that they did not even go to THE Palaestra for the battle that just took place.","They cared nothing for the politics of factions or the drama of challenges. They simply existed, cultivating their understanding of being itself.","But here was... The Disciple of THE Secretive Eon.","Nyx.","She was a bit different from the image he sas before, but she was...serene, her form composed of twilight given flesh and purpose. Her skin held the color of the moment between day and night, that liminal space where neither sun nor stars held dominion.","Her hair flowed like shadows learning to dance, dark and luminous simultaneously. Her wings were currently retracted, folded into her back as if they had never existed, but the spaces where they would emerge shimmered with potential.","Her gaze was solid and unchanging as if she was truly trying to blend in with the surrounding Existence, becoming one with the sacred herbs and conceptual flowers and pools of liquid being that surrounded her cultivation spot.","Her master had said this entity was a fan of THE Creature, someone who idolized Existence itself and had traveled to THE Agora of Primordial Judgment specifically to be closer to his domain.","She was also an entity who could cross levels of power, sitting at THE Intermediate Depth but holding power at THE Fundamental Depth through foundations that defied conventional classification.","Noah looked at her calmly.","This being opened her eyes and blinked as she looked at him before she saw the graceful visage of Glossikos floating nearby.","She quickly grew astonished as she rose up and nodded respectfully with deference that spoke of genuine reverence for the Strategoi.","\"To what do I owe the honor of having the great Strategos, Glossikos, come to my humble self?\"","She asked such a question toward Glossikos as Noah looked at her calmly and said with directness that cut through any pretense of ceremony.","\" An Absolute just fell in THE Palaestra. This didn’t interest you enough to come see?\"","This being came to look at Noah calmly with twilight eyes that held depths of philosophical certainty as she said with a voice like the quiet moment before dawn.","\"Absolutes rise. Absolutes fall. It has nothing to do with me as it is the nature of Existence.\"","She said such words with such calm detachment that Noah gazed at her silently for a moment before he said with pragmatic urgency that had no patience for philosophical musings.","\" Okay. Your Master sent me to get you. And I actually don’t have the time right now, so let’s do this quickly.\"","He said such words calmly because his existence perceived the Immensity of an Absolute near his Absolute Seal of Quintessence that he had given to Origin!","The Seal was akin to an extension of himself as it allowed him to know where she and Tor were, and he could theoretically do a few things with it as at this time, he felt the familiar, suffocating aura of none other than...","THE Primordial Chaos.","So within Alfheimr, THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger were for one reason or another coming across Chaos.","Why would THE Primordial Chaos be in the home of THE Creature?","There were many questions, but as always, Existence continued to move however it wished.","The only thing he could do was move alongside it to see how he could navigate it with all the terrifying monsters out there.","Nyx raised her brows at his words as she said with the calm certainty of someone who understood reality.","\"Only a Polemarch can exit THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, and with the agreement and permission of two Strategoi at that. And I am finding this place very beneficial as...\"","Before she could even finish her words, Noah turned over to Glossikos and said with authority that expected compliance rather than requested it.","\"I have an overabundance of contributions. I would like to transfer a sufficient amount to Nyx here, to Ul’moreth, and to my dog here to give them sufficient ranking.\"","...!"]},{"number":4813,"title":"Chapter 4813: Chapter 4812: Usage of Absolute Everything! I","paragraphs":["He said such words gloriously as Glossikos raised her brows with an expression that mixed surprise with calculation.","\" Even if rules are bent to make them all Polemarchs, you would need my permission and another. I don’t believe Paradoxos, Khaotikos, or Ontikos would particularly be feeling generous...\"","Glossikos paused as her eyes flashed with surprise.","And Noah looked at her as the musings of Undifferentiated Fate burned in his eyes. He had planned to reach out to Ontikos as with his relation to THE Creature, he did not expect any problems there!","But had Ontikos already reached out to Glossikos even before he asked?","He only thought of this as a moment later, Glossikos spoke with a unique expression that held layers of meaning Noah could not fully parse.","\" Well, it seems this is an action supported by many moving parts. A Strategos has reached out and stated that they will approve this departure.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes squinted as in the next moment, Glossikos began to move her hands with authority that reshaped the rules of this domain according to her will.","The numbers on Noah’s toga went down rapidly while on Ul’moreth, Skoll, and Nyx, their numbers rose higher and higher as contributions flowed from his account to theirs.","Until their togas transformed to match Polemarchs!","Lumivara was the only one unchanged as Noah wanted to keep her with him here to elevate her Depth some more through the opportunities this place provided.","As for Noah, his toga still remained that of a Polemarch as he had done far too much in the short period of time in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, with his latest action being winning a debate and collapsing an Absolute. Even after transferring enough contributions to elevate three beings to Polemarch status, he still had more than enough to maintain his own rank.","As he watched all this happen, Glossikos grandly said in the next moment with finality that carried the weight of law.","\" It is done. I can send them out of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment at any time.\"","Noah nodded at these words as his senses flickered. Undifferentiated Fate told him that he was thinking wrong about something.","So he asked to be sure.","\" Who was the other Strategos to give their approval for their departure?\"","Glossikos turned to him after this question.","Her immensely deep obsidian-blue eyes bore into his with Immensity and calmness as she said with weight that made Noah’s foundations pulse with recognition.","\" Strategos Khaotikos.\"","BOOM!","...!","It was not Ontikos, related to Existence, but Khaotikos who stepped in without even being asked.","Chaos!","Noah’s eyes squinted as he also recalled the cleanliness of the Weavings of Chaos when it came to Malformations surrounding them.","When he closed his eyes to sense what only Absolutes could sense, he could see those weed-like corruptions already forming silently around all Weavings, especially Paradox and Existence as these two seemed to be holding immense waves of corruption that spread and propagated without adequate cleansing at much faster rates.","But barely any Corrupted Growths formed around Weavings of Chaos, and when they did, Noah saw them disappearing soon after into golden threads that further stabilized Existence.","THE Primordial Chaos was diligent in ways that his philosophy of disorder should have contradicted.","There was a lot to be learned regarding how everything worked out.","At this moment, Noah gave a light nod as he said with command that expected immediate execution.","\" Send them out.\"","Glossikos looked at him silently before a moment later, she clenched her fist with authority that transcended normal space.","A reluctant Nyx, Ul’moreth, and Skoll disappeared!","Only Glossikos and Lumivara remained nearby as Lumivara came closer toward Noah with a happy smile, almost as if she was reminded of when they had been alone and crossing the Infinite Unfurling together before everything had become so complicated.","As for Noah, his gaze was on the Stoa of Dogmata where at this moment, Ul’moreth, Nyx, and Skoll appeared outside THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","The moment they did, Noah exerted his power across the Stoa of Dogmata through the threads of fate and Mana that connected him to everything he claimed authority over.","He brought them to the region where his other body stood a distance away from THE Secretive Eon!","---","THE Secretive Eon looked over with raised brows as she saw her Disciple appear with a look of reluctance that instantly changed the moment Nyx recognized who she was seeing.","Nyx took a step to appear beside her master and knelt down with deference that spoke of genuine devotion as she said with a voice filled with regret and submission.","\" This unworthy disciple apologizes to Master for any trouble she has caused.\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon looked at her Disciple with sharp eyes that evaluated and judged, but she didn’t reply.","Instead, she looked over to Noah.","But at this moment, Noah was not looking at her!","He was gazing at Ul’moreth as he evaluated his Teacher’s immense waves of power that were no longer suppressed by THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","Ul’moreth stood at Half-Step Absolute Depth.","His time in THE Belly of Existence over the eons had been utilized grandly, building foundations that approached the threshold of true Absolute classification. His countless hairs swayed with authority that pressed against the boundaries of what non-Absolutes could achieve.","At this moment, Noah thought of many possibilities as within his existence, an Absolute Everything buzzed with potential utilizations.","He asked Ul’moreth with a voice that held calculation and hope intertwined.","\" Old man, how is your foundation after all these eons? What would you need to tip you over from Half-Step Absolute to... Absolute?\"","...!","There were many things happening as Existence was full of possibilities.","Right now, he was looking at the possibility of the emergence of an Absolute under his faction.","The choices were Ul’moreth, Origin, or potentially others.","And at this moment, after gaining Undifferentiated Fate and having access to observing where those connected to him were through threads of causality that stretched across Observable Existence...","He had already sent another body across The Wastes toward THE Fisherman who had given up everything for him in Ginnungagap!","And he looked at Ul’moreth as he wondered...of the Usage of his Absolute Everything!"]},{"number":4814,"title":"Chapter 4814: Chapter 4813: The Enemy Unseen I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the old hairy man in front of him as he searched for an answer regarding the possibilities of what he could do.","He knew that THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Paradox did everything that they could when they arrived at THE Fundamental Depth to build their foundation before they became Absolutes.","It was so ridiculous to the point that even though he just devoured the recoverable Depth of an Absolute, he only gained a bit over twenty-five percent of the comparable Immensity of foundation when looking at THE Creature and others like him.","Those beings had spent eons at Fundamental Depth, accumulating weight that would support their eventual ascension with foundations so unshakeable that nothing could threaten their position once they crossed that final threshold.","So he knew that even though he had an Absolute Everything, his utilization of it would only increase a percentage of his foundation, and whether that was ten percent or twenty percent may not be too significant of a difference in the grand scheme of his own advancement.","But an Absolute under his faction... that was something entirely different!","That was a force multiplier that could change the dynamics of everything he was trying to accomplish.","Ul’moreth looked at him as even within those waves of countless hairs, Noah saw a brilliant Ginnu Lifeform who smiled at him with warmth.","\"I couldn’t rise as an Absolute in THE Belly of Existence even after eons passed because of a suppression that pressed down on all of us who sought to advance beyond what THE Creature deemed appropriate.\"","His voice carried weight that spoke of frustrations accumulated across ages.","\" You left me and Ains your Sparks. Your Way. Haha, if you did not exist, maybe we would have claimed The First Tongue by now.\"","He chuckled with genuine amusement.","\" But we advanced through your authority instead. I forged my foundation using what you provided. I wish I had been patient enough to remain at Fundamental and not jump to Half-Step Absolute as this actually set me back in certain ways, but even here, I need to just take... a step.\"","His expression grew contemplative.","\" But the single step can sometimes feel like the entire span of Observable Existence.\"","...!","A step.","Ul’moreth was a grand entity. Perfect Speaker of The First Tongue. His power, potential, and immensity was no less if not grander than some of THE Living Existences in The Infinite Unfurling.","Noah stroked the head of a happy Skoll as he listened to this and said with casual confidence that belied the significance of what he was about to offer.","\" Alright. I have something, maybe it can help you take that step.\"","...!","Noah closed his eyes.","Within his existence, he reached for the cluster of mobius strips that had formed from his cleansing of Observable Existence, that first genuine Absolute Everything that marked his entry into the currency of beings who shaped reality itself.","A glorious blue-gold cluster of mobius strips floated out of his head!","Its aura was so heavy and dense that reality itself seemed to bend around its presence, and shockingly, it radiated a glimmer of Absolute authority that made everything nearby tremble with recognition of what they were perceiving!","Absolute!","Something that carried the essence of what Absolutes accumulated through their contributions to Observable Existence!","It emerged from Noah as a shocked hairy hand of Ul’moreth rose to grasp it with reverence that spoke of understanding exactly what he was being offered!","In the distance, THE Secretive Eon and Nyx turned over with shining eyes.","Eon even seemed to have a pondering look as she locked her gaze onto Noah with intensity that evaluated and calculated and found new depths of interest in what this being was capable of producing!","Noah didn’t pay attention to any of the gazes as he said with casualness that masked how much he truly hoped this would work.","\" See if it’s possible. If it is, great. If it’s not... that’s also okay. No pressure.\"","...!","Well, he didn’t say it, but there was a little bit of pressure!","Ul’moreth grasped the Absolute Everything solemnly as he nodded, and it disappeared into his body as he sat down in a meditative position with countless hairs settling around him like a cocoon of accumulated authority.","Noah was about to turn toward THE Secretive Eon to see how things would progress from here, because the aura of THE Primordial Chaos was in Alfheimr, and she had said that Chaos was the first target among THE Four before they would be targeting Jotunheim!","But as he did so, his Weavings buzzed as he received a message through his Derivative Civilization of Hunger and Undifferentiated Fate!","| Hey big guy, I don’t know if you can hear this, but THE Primordial Chaos has for some reason decided to be in Alfheimr when Origin is here looking for THE Creature.|","|The bitch Emotive and Elemental are here as well.|","|Chaos says he wants to talk to you, but Origin won’t activate the Seal you gave her because she likely does not want to embroil you in whatever is happening here.|","|But hey, you are one of THE Four.|","|There’s half a chance that THE Creature is watching all of this and will intervene, but just in case he is being an ass, there is you.|","...!","The message was a heavy one, and it stemmed from THE First Hunger!","Emotive, Elemental, and THE Primordial Chaos were moving together in Alfheimr.","The sentence alone was ridiculous as shouldn’t Emotive and Elemental be moving with Paradox?","They were part of THE Loom. They served THE Living Paradox. They had been instruments of his designs.","But what was this?","Why were they walking alongside THE Primordial Chaos as if they were old companions taking a stroll through one of the most ancient Primordial Realms in existence?","His eyes moved with Immensity as he needed an answer and solution at this moment.","He was inclined to speak to Eon about this, to tell her that her target was in Alfheimr right now and they could set off there immediately. After all, she had said THE Primordial Chaos was the first among THE Four that she planned to collapse and replace. If he was in Alfheimr, if he was near beings connected to Noah’s Civilization...","But his intuition was buzzing.","He didn’t know why, but it made him take a pause and close his eyes.","THE Weaver of Existence closed his eyes as he asked his very Civilizations how to proceed, reaching inward toward the foundations that had been built across his journey through Observable Existence.","Moments later...","| You already know.|","His Civilizations only affirmed his intuition as he sighed internally and made a silent Thesis!","| Where my Seal is, I can have a sliver of my consciousness appear.|","BOOM!"]},{"number":4815,"title":"Chapter 4815: Chapter 4814: The Enemy Unseen II","paragraphs":["Chaos wanted to talk?","He would talk.","After all, much of what he saw and came to learn from THE Weavers’ death made him very curious about Chaos.","Why did THE Secretive Eon target him first among THE Four?","And what explained how different Chaos was from the other Aspects as he was seeing through his newly gained perception?","The cleanliness of the Weavings of Chaos. The diligence with which Corrupted Growths were purified around his domain. The contradiction between his philosophy of disorder and his apparent dedication to maintaining stability.","When there were a number of questions, it was always good to get answers from the source!","So he closed his eyes as a part of his consciousness began to buzz and sought to impose itself countless gigaparsecs away, inside a Primordial Realm!","---","In Alfheimr.","The standoff between THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger had settled into a heavy silence that pressed against everyone present with weight that made breathing difficult.","Chaos stood with his form shifting constantly, his presence alone enough to make the crystalline trees of Alfheimr tremble with recognition of what they were hosting. Behind Origin, the natives of this realm, the Ljósálfar who had welcomed her home with such joy moments before, shakily stood up as if they would die for her without hesitation.","Their light-woven forms flickered with determination that transcended their fear.","They would stand beside their Ljósmóðir even against one of THE Four.","Even if it meant their complete and utter collapse.","And yet, uniquely, THE Primordial Chaos was looking at them with a calm gaze that held no malice, no threat, no intention of violence. He did not make any move after telling Origin to reach out toward THE Youngest.","He simply waited.","Origin shook her head resolutely.","\" As I said before, it is not happening.\"","Her voice came firm despite the pressure pressing down on her from an entity who could crush her with a thought.","\" The musings of THE Creature are here. Can you all not talk amongst each other? Is that not why you are here to begin with?\"","She actually spoke in such a way against a terrifying Absolute who could crush other Absolutes, much less someone like her who had not yet grasped the level of Absolute!","And once more, THE Primordial Chaos did not reply to her.","He only looked within her existence as if he could sense something there, something uniquely different from everything else that Origin represented. His shifting features settled into focused attention as he studied whatever he was perceiving.","And shockingly, a moment later, a brilliant blue-gold light began to shine from the hip of THE Living Origin!","What looked like a medallion flowed out of her existence and began to spin in the air of its own accord!","It was a glorious Absolute Seal of Quintessence!","From the back, THE Living Emotive laughed with delight that cycled through her features.","\" Haha, no way, right? Osmont himse...\"","\"Hush.\"","BOOM!","The booming voice of THE Primordial Chaos echoed out with a sense of finality at this moment, as if he was giving the last warning that he would be giving today to Emotive.","Her mouth did not even finish moving as she quieted down, the light in her gaze flickering with humiliation and barely contained rage as she looked at what was happening silently.","The Seal spun with increasing intensity, blue-gold light radiating outward in patterns that spoke of authority being channeled across impossible distances.","Moments later, an illusory visage of none other than Noah appeared beside THE Living Origin!","Origin turned to Hunger as her eyes squinted sharply with accusation, but he looked at the figure of Noah with innocent confusion, as if he had done absolutely nothing to bring this about.","And Noah fully formed as he looked around this landscape.","Alfheimr.","Yet another Primordial Realm that was not even a possibility for many to know across Observable Existence, unless you had the power to truly perceive the ancient domains where THE Four had first risen.","The crystalline forests stretched in all directions. The floating islands cascaded with waterfalls of liquid Mana. The sky shifted between aurora and starlight.","And now at this moment, somehow, those who had backed his Way and who came here for their own purposes had met with a party that contained one of THE Four alongside THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive.","The moment his illusory consciousness arrived here, Noah gave a glance to the terrifying visage of THE Primordial Chaos.","Looking at this being was like staring into the heart of disorder itself given form. His features never settled. His outline never stabilized. He was simultaneously many possibilities and no possibilities, the very concept of chaos made manifest.","And yet Chaos looked back at him with something that might have been respect.","Thereafter, Noah gave a glance to Emotive.","She was beautiful in the way that a storm was beautiful, her features cycling through emotions faster than normal perception could track. Joy and malice and curiosity and hunger all competed for dominance across her expression.","Her authority felt like layers of manic energy that were waiting to erupt, that actually wanted to erupt at this very moment, and yet she didn’t seem able to, as if she was being held back by something more powerful than her desire for chaos.","He barely heard the word \"hush\" when he entered that stemmed from THE Primordial Chaos.","It seemed other Absolutes, even with all their power, could be put in line by a single word from a truly powerful Absolute.","After he looked at THE Living Emotive, he turned his head toward THE Living Elemental.","This was the man who did what no man should do to another.","This was the man who put a burning curse on him that forced him to separate from his women for such a long...","Well, it actually wasn’t that long, but still!","The one he marked to be his greatest enemy in existence, purely from that single simple action.","THE Living Elemental.","He looked at this being and the first thing that he did after he arrived in this place was smile toward him.","A smile.","But the smile was brutal and heavy, and it held immense waves of meaning. It was like he was silently communicating that he had just taken down an Absolute and Elemental was his number one target coming up next.","...!","The figure of THE Living Elemental hardened his expression as he retained his majesty and glory, keeping his face straight as he said nothing in response to the silent threat being delivered.","And then Noah returned his gaze back to THE Primordial Chaos.","In the distant past when he met this being before, Chaos had been full of smiles while presenting his choices. He had seemed playful. Amused. As if everything was entertainment for his enjoyment.","And yet right now he seemed unfathomably serious as he looked at Noah straight and said with weight that pressed against everyone present.","\" Why don’t the rest of you find something to do? The adults have to talk for a bit.\"","BOOM!","Woah.","The adults?","The words that THE Primordial Chaos said were extremely heavy and demeaning to all others here as he considered THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive, and THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger to be mere children!","And he didn’t differentiate between either of them.","The only one he gave any sense of respect to was Noah since he was in the same rank as him.","One of THE Four!","It was an astonishing scene as the moment THE Primordial Chaos said this, THE Living Elemental was the first to move back and actually leave this area without even looking back.","He simply turned and disappeared into the crystalline forests of Alfheimr as if he had received a command that could not be disobeyed.","Noah could already sense the hesitation of THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger behind him as he raised his hands and said with casual authority that expected compliance.","\"Go. It shouldn’t be anything too crazy.\"","...!"]},{"number":4816,"title":"Chapter 4816: Chapter 4815: The Enemy Unseen III","paragraphs":["He said this calmly as after all, he was considered the leader that the two of them had backed. He had to at least be capable of standing up for them when they called for him.","So in a shockingly short amount of time, this entire area that was filled with hymns and grace of the natives of Alfheimr cleared.","THE Living Emotive disappeared with a pout that promised future mischief.","Origin and Hunger retreated with the Ljósálfar who had been willing to die for their Ljósmóðir.","Until only THE Primordial Chaos and Noah remained!","THE Primordial Chaos looked over Noah’s illustrious figure again and again as Noah gazed back at the being he could not fully understand at all.","After a moment, Chaos spoke with a voice that held weight beyond its casual tone.","\"It seems that it was good that you escaped from my grasp and the grasp of Temporal in Ginnungagap. Everything is as it should be...\"","He paused.","\" Well, except when it isn’t.\"","His shifting features settled into something almost kind.","\" Youngest, do you want to see something interesting?\"","...!","Noah looked at this being who began talking with him like this as his eyes squinted and he replied with caution wrapped in casual interest.","\"I live to see interesting things. But I wonder if it would fit my definition of interesting.\"","\"Oh, you will definitely find it interesting...\"","As he said such words, THE Primordial Chaos waved his hand.","Between him and Noah, a massive illusory screen appeared, conjured from authority that reshaped the air itself into a viewing portal.","On this illusory screen, it showed a vast and ancient-looking citadel of a civilization.","The endless expanse of ancient structures stretched across frozen landscapes that seemed to go on forever. Black ice formed the foundations of towers that rose toward skies crackling with perpetual lightning. Glaciers the size of continents groaned beneath constructions that had been built by beings of impossible scale.","And there were the auras of billions upon billions of lifeforms in this endlessly vast civilization.","Chaos Giants moved through the citadel with grace that belied their massive forms. Their skin was the color of storms and obsidian. Their eyes burned with the light of dying stars. They were chaos incarnate, descendants of forces that had existed since before differentiation.","Among these billions, there were thousands of giants at Pre-THE classification, their power impressive but not yet having crossed the threshold into true Depth.","There were hundreds at THE Surface Depth, their authority beginning to press against reality itself.","There were dozens at THE Intermediate Depth, beings whose Ways had begun to truly shape the Existence around them.","There were ten at THE Fundamental Depth, entities whose power could collapse civilizations with a thought.","And there were three Half-Step Absolutes!","It was such a glorious scene of a civilization, showing musings of Chaos permeating throughout every corner and crevice.","And yet the Chaos was unique.","It felt very calm and ordered.","It was truly paradoxical to see.","Noah looked at the scene before him as he frowned for a moment because something felt off.","Something that made his foundations buzz with unease that he could not immediately identify.","Opposite him, THE Primordial Chaos spoke with a voice that held weight beyond its casual observation.","\"A grand landscape, is it not? This is Jotunheim. One of my homes.\"","He paused.","\" But I can already see that you can see something off. Are you able to point it out?\"","THE Primordial Chaos asked such a question as Noah looked at the ongoing scenery of this grand and glorious civilization.","He studied the billions of giants going about their existence.","He observed the structures and the authority and the Ways that permeated through everything.","And he quickly said with certainty that carried unease.","\" Why is it so quiet? And why... are all of them so still?\"","...!","They could feel and hear the hums of authority that were permeating all across this vast civilization.","Noah could even feel the flow of The First Tongue that was permeating across the vastness of this location, even through just this illusory scene.","And yet of the billions of giants that were here...","Not a single one said a word to the other.","The illusory screen showed the shocking scene that portrayed how nearly all of them were seated in meditative positions across different regions of this vast civilization. The glimmer of the Way of Chaos moved around them in slow, methodical patterns. Noah could sense small but tiny elevations of the Depths of many of those there, as if they were cultivating with perfect efficiency.","But there was no conversation.","No argument, no interactions, nothing.","No chaos at all.","In a realm dedicated to disorder, there was only silence and stillness and order that should not have existed.","Opposite him, the figure of THE Primordial Chaos nodded and solemnly said with weight that made the air itself grow heavy.","\"I have been under attack these last few hours since THE Fallout began, and the enemy is an extremely terrifying one.\"","BOOM!","His shifting features settled into something that looked almost like concern.","\" Even though THE Living Paradox and THE Creature began this war, I am the only one currently under assault. And it is an enemy that even I could not have predicted.\"","As he began saying all of this, Noah felt a foreboding sensation as the more he studied the vast civilization within Jotunheim, the more unsettling it felt.","The giants sat in perfect rows.","Their cultivation was synchronized.","Their breathing was identical.","Everything about them screamed uniformity in a realm that should have celebrated diversity and disorder.","THE Primordial Chaos continued with heavy and solemn words as he also looked at the scenery of what would have been his civilization.","\" With the emergence of THE Fallout, one would expect the increased level of chaos and corruption to possibly cause the emergence of horrific mutations of Existence. Many of us predicted that Corrupted Growths and Malformed Authorities would exponentially increase and begin causing issues if they weren’t properly taken care of, or even the rise of terrifying Lifeforms based on Corruption.\"","He paused.","\" And we were right in some sense.\"","His voice grew darker.","\" But what did arise... is something that not even I could have imagined.\"","The giants in the illusory screen continued their silent cultivation, their movements so perfectly synchronized that they looked like extensions of a single will.","\" An invisible enemy.\"","Chaos’s shifting features flickered with something that might have been frustration.","\" Even I did not perceive them until they had overpowered more than half of Jotunheim.\"","He gestured toward the citadel displayed before them.","\" This citadel that you see before you is one of those that has been fully overpowered by that enemy.\"","...!"]},{"number":4817,"title":"Chapter 4817: Chapter 4816: The Enemy Unseen IV","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes widened as he studied the billions of giants more closely.","\"I noticed it first when those who backed and followed my Way of Chaos seemingly began to disappear one after another, as if they were pulling back their backing.\"","Chaos’s voice carried the weight of memory.","\" Do you want to know what I initially saw when I went to investigate?\"","He didn’t wait for an answer.","\" This was a few hours ago.\"","THE Primordial Chaos waved his hand, and another illusory screen appeared beside the first.","This one displayed the same vast citadel of a civilization that Noah was just looking at on the other screen.","But it shockingly showed things decimated, as if a war was occurring!","The giants seemed divided on two sides as they were fighting each other with authority that shook the very foundations of Jotunheim!","One side was shockingly efficient and silent while they attacked. Their movements were precise and coordinated. Their usage of the Way of Chaos was grander and more controlled than anything Noah had ever seen. They fought without roaring. They advanced without hesitation.","The other side was roaring orders and fighting with everything they had. They utilized chaos in the traditional sense, wild and unpredictable and desperate. They threw Declarations and Theses and raw authority at their attackers with abandon.","Half-Step Absolutes clashed with power that cracked the black ice beneath them!","THE Fundamental Depth entities traded blows that would have collapsed lesser civilizations!","THE Intermediate and Surface Depth beings fought in numbers that should have made this a battle lasting eons!","And yet, with just the passage of seconds...","The less efficient side, the side that had been roaring orders and fighting with everything they had...","Brought their hands down silently.","No more assertions or impositions or Declarations or anything flew around.","Nobody fought anymore.","Everybody stopped fighting.","An immense, eerie quiet spread over the entire civilization!","The giants then began to move as if they had not just been fighting, their Ways of Chaos moving with perfect synchronization as they began to repair the citadel around them. They fixed what had been destroyed. They cleaned what had been bloodied. They restored what had been damaged.","As if nothing had happened.","As if the battle had never occurred.","As if they had always been on the same side.","Noah’s face became heavy as THE Primordial Chaos explained with a voice that held the weight of someone describing a nightmare that had become reality.","\" The enemy that has been encroaching upon my Way is one that is extremely lethal in their attacks, and their method of action seems to be a silent spread into all Depths and Civilizations without you even knowing it.\"","He gestured toward the now-peaceful citadel on the first screen.","\" All these billions who were followers of my Way of Chaos... they effectively died and were collapsed without even knowing it.\"","The giants continued their synchronized cultivation, their faces serene and empty.","\" What remains of them should be husks, and yet everything seems as is.\"","Chaos’s voice grew darker still.","\" Them throwing attacks or expressing their Way is a diversion. They are like an infection where just by being near those infected, it may seem like you are fighting them, but the authority that you breathe, the Phonemes of The First Tongue that you use, the very Way and Civilization that you are utilizing across your existence... could already be infected by whatever this is.\"","Noah watched as the giants in the illusory screen moved in perfect unison to purify a cluster of Corrupted Growths that had formed nearby.","\" Before you know it, things simply turn dark. Who you were disappears, and something else replaces you.\"","THE Primordial Chaos paused to let the weight of his words settle.","\" What is even more terrifying is that whatever this invisible enemy is...they have no body for us to be attacking. Even I do not know what to target.\"","The giants finished their purification and returned to their cultivation positions.","\" And after the takeover of all of these existences, they operate as if everything is normal. They have been very astute with my Way as I sense them purifying Chaos constantly and taking care of Corrupted Growths.\"","Noah understood now why the Weavings of Chaos had been so clean when he observed them.","It wasn’t because THE Primordial Chaos was more diligent.","It was because something else was maintaining his domain.","Something that had replaced his followers.","Something that was pretending to be them while spreading further.","...!","Noah’s face became more and more grave as he heard the things that THE Primordial Chaos was saying.","THE Primordial Chaos continued with the finality of someone delivering a verdict.","\" The only headway that I have managed to make is that somehow... the only identity I have been able to uncover that is connected to this that I visibly feel a threat towards...\"","His shifting features settled into something deadly serious.","\" Is THE Secretive Eon.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with light as his illusory visage focused on THE Primordial Chaos!","His foundations trembled.","His heart beat with weight that pressed against his existence.","DUM! DUM! DUM!","The beat of his heart was heavy! His Seals buzzed and as if their hairs stood on end with alarm!","THE Secretive Eon.","The being who had proposed collapsing THE Four together.","The being who said she wanted to replace them rather than merely kill them.","The being whose Disciple he had just retrieved.","The being he had left sitting near his other body moments ago.","\"I will warn the other two, but THE Four of us will have to be vigilant against THE Secretive Eon.\"","Chaos’s voice carried absolute certainty.","\"I reached out to you first since you are the weakest among us and you might not even feel anything. Because this enemy could truly overcome you without even a fight, your consciousness simply erased while those around you don’t know any better.\"","His shifting features held something that might have been concern.","\"As one of THE Four, you should have a unique sense or intuition. If you even sense your existence feeling a tingly sense of alarm, if you ever feel like something is a bit off, run.\"","He leaned closer.","\"If you are close with THE Creature, be around with him for a little bit. If you have any level of trust in me, you can even bring your main body here.\"","His voice dropped to something almost gentle.","\" The moment you sense or hear anything about the Weavings of THE Secretive Eon, run. Because if she is even near you, you may lose yourself soon after before you know. You may already be dead.\"","THE Primordial Chaos straightened.","\"I thought that you would be the one they targeted first since you are the weakest. And whatever this enemy is... if they got their hands on The First Tongue, things would become unfathomably harder for all of us with such a thing under their control.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s mind buzzed.","The beat of his heart was heavy!","He remembered Eon’s words.","She planned to collapse THE Primordial Chaos and others, and Chaos was her first target as she said she would replace him.","She would replace him.","And she would do the same with THE Living Paradox, with THE Creature.","And then she said him!","She had said this!","She had openly told him her plans!"]},{"number":4818,"title":"Chapter 4818: Chapter 4817: The Enemy Unseen V","paragraphs":["In Observable Existence, there is an emotion called terror.","Many beings believe across their lives that they have experienced it, that they have truly known what it means to feel fear press against their foundations and make their very Ways tremble with the weight of what they are perceiving.","They believe this because they have faced enemies stronger than themselves, because they have stared into the eyes of those who could collapse them with a thought, because they have stood at the edge of oblivion and felt the void reaching back toward them with hungry intent.","But truly, nobody has felt true fear.","True fear is not the recognition that something can destroy you, because destruction is merely an ending, a transition from existence to non-existence that carries a certain finality that the mind can comprehend and accept.","True fear is the recognition that something can replace you.","That something can wear your face and speak with your voice and utilize your Way and live your life while you are gone in ways that no one will ever notice.","That the you that you have spent your entire existence building and protecting and nurturing can simply... cease, while something else continues in your place as if nothing has changed at all.","The Absolutes who have existed since The Infinite Unfurling whisper among themselves about enemies that kill, about threats that collapse, about dangers that end.","But they do not speak of the enemy that replaces!","---","The first thing that Noah did after receiving such disastrous information from THE Primordial Chaos was not to panic.","Panic was for those who had no options.","Panic was for those who could not act.","He had options. He could act. And so instead of surrendering to fear, he began looking at other possibilities right away as to what the enemy that THE Primordial Chaos was talking about could be.","His thoughts instantly shifted to THE Great Usurper.","Eckert.","The very same friend who had been scattered across Transcendent Spirit Folds after being destroyed by Duke Veil-Render.","The being who had been slowly spreading across folds like a virus that turned destruction into opportunity.","If anyone could spread invisibly and replace beings without detection...","If anyone had the capability to infect civilizations from within...","With this Existence being connected to him through threads of fate and Mana that transcended normal distance, Noah erupted with all his might!","His twenty-seven Seals buzzed with terrifying brilliance!","He pulled upon his Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate, stopping any other processes he held to focus solely on one target!","Eckert!","BOOM!","THE Primordial Chaos had stopped speaking as he sensed this light variation of Weavings in Noah’s gaze after his words.","His shifting features settled into something curious as he asked with weight that expected answers.","\" Youngest, do you know something?\"","Noah’s eyes blazed with blue-gold intensity as threads of fate stretched across impossible distances, seeking connections that would confirm or deny his suspicions.","\"I am checking on something. Just hold on one second.\"","His voice came stern and focused.","Very soon, detailed prompts bloomed in front of Noah’s eyes with information that made his foundations pulse with recognition.","|THE Weaver of Existence pulls upon one of his deepest connections across Observable Existence.|","|THE Great Usurper, Eckert, has been observed to be slowly spreading threads of his existence across The Wastes of THE Fallout.|","|No threads of his existence can be sensed elsewhere.|","|His expansion remains contained within the corrupted regions where he was scattered.|","|No infiltration of Primordial Realms detected.|","|No connection to the infection spreading through THE Primordial Chaos’s domain has been established.|","BOOM!","The prompts were horrendous ones to hear!","It wasn’t Eckert.","Which meant the enemy was something else entirely.","Noah’s gaze further shifted, and he spent even more of his terrifying Immensity and foundation to focus on the connection with Eckert, utilizing and allowing the expenditure of every ounce of weight and Immensity of his existence as he sent a message across the corrupted Weavings of Observable Existence!","| Hey, are you okay? Have you moved from The Wastes of THE Fallout to any Primordial Realms? Do you know anything of the movements of THE Primordial Chaos?|","...!","He sent such words as a message across corrupted Weavings of Existence, something that should have been impossible before, but now with his Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate threading connections across Observable Existence...","| Woah, big guy! You’re alive? Of course you would be. Primordial Realms? What are those? I’ve just acclimated to fusing with a fragment of an Axiom...|","BOOM!","\"...\"","Noah breathed heavily.","It wasn’t Eckert.","It wasn’t Eckert.","THE Great Usurper was still contained within The Wastes, still spreading slowly, still unaware of even what Primordial Realms were.","Which meant the invisible enemy spreading through Jotunheim, the infection replacing beings across THE Primordial Chaos’s domain, the threat that made one of THE Four speak with caution and concern...","Was something else entirely.","Or someone else.","Noah’s expression became heavy.","In front of him, THE Primordial Chaos squinted and began to rise with caution that seemed entirely out of place for an entity of his power.","\" Youngest...\"","His shifting features flickered with something that looked almost like alarm.","\" You wouldn’t have happened to already come across THE Secretive Eon, right?\"","...!","The musings of Chaos began to rumble and seethe around THE Primordial Chaos!","Shockingly, he moved back from Noah even though Noah was merely an illusory body, as if he was being overly cautious that in the case Noah had already met THE Secretive Eon, he may already be compromised!","The crystalline trees of Alfheimr trembled as reality itself responded to the caution of one of THE Four!","Noah looked at THE Primordial Chaos.","What monstrosity was moving in the undercurrents of Observable Existence to make one of THE Four this cautious?","What enemy could spread invisibly through the domain of an Absolute without being detected until half of everything was already lost?","What threat could make THE Primordial Chaos, a being who had built foundations that let him stand among THE Four, retreat from even an illusory projection out of caution of contamination?","And if Noah truly was staring at the culprit at this very moment while being less than a mile away from her...","He needed to move.","And to move quickly!","Anything an Absolute like THE Primordial Chaos was cautious of...","What could it do against him?!"]},{"number":4819,"title":"Chapter 4819: Chapter 4818: THE Glorious Evolution I","paragraphs":["Understanding, followed by drastic action.","This was what Noah followed, but he still acted first because he had to think about others and not just himself.","So in the Stoa of Dogmata, the figures of Ul’moreth and Skoll disappeared with a flash of blue-gold brilliance as Noah sent them far across The Wastes, toward where another body of his was heading toward Ains!","He remained in this space alone.","He remained under the calm gaze of THE Secretive Eon and her Disciple, Nyx!","His gaze was calm.","Frankly, depending on what was true and what was false, this could potentially be an extremely perilous moment. In what THE Primordial Chaos described, there was a terrifying level of lethality for the enemy he mentioned.","It seemed that Noah had not considered just how terrifying Eckert could be if his capability was amplified to ridiculous degrees, but if the enemy that THE Primordial Chaos spoke of could infect entities of any Depth without them even knowing...","If THE Secretive Eon was truly connected to this...","How horrific would it be if Noah’s consciousness simply shut down without his say so, and something else took his place?","He wouldn’t even be able to reverse time to a previous Anchor Point, and even if he did, something else would be returning.","But at this point in time, he could say with confidence that he was HIM.","Capital H, I, M.","Not in that grand way of him shouting it, but purely that he knew he was himself. He was not influenced or under any unique Weavings of Existence. His thoughts were his own. His foundations remained untouched. His consciousness was singular and uncompromised.","So at this moment, he could choose to remove himself entirely from THE Secretive Eon and have many questions, or he could take a heavy risk to get some answers.","He stayed around Eon and the unfolding potential plan of collapsing Absolutes because his saving grace of THE Existential Paradox Loop was always there.","If things went wrong, he could reverse.","But if he got influenced and became someone else alongside such a process...","What a colossal loss that would be!","So...","\" Hey.\"","He looked toward THE Secretive Eon who looked back at him calmly, even raising her brows with mild curiosity at being addressed so casually.","\" Are you... THE Secretive Eon?\"","BOOM!","The question was a seemingly simple but straightforward one, like ripping off a bandaid!","Noah didn’t skirt around it as he directly asked it!","And THE Secretive Eon tilted her head as she looked at him and asked with apparent confusion.","\" What could you mean?\"","Noah nodded as he said with weight that expected honest answers.","\" Just that. Are you THE Secretive Eon, or are you... something else? Are you the exact same Eon who observed things in Ginnungagap, or have you... changed?\"","BOOM!","A heavy silence came.","The air in the Stoa of Dogmata seemed to thicken with tension that pressed against Noah’s foundations.","And moments later, an eerie scene unfolded.","THE Secretive Eon blinked as if she realized something, and she said with what sounded almost like delight.","\" Oh!\"","As if she finally understood the question!","Beside her, her Disciple frowned as she seemed about to rebuke Noah for such a question toward her Master, but in the next moment...","Eon tapped out casually.","The body of her Disciple slumped and lost consciousness instantly, collapsing like a puppet whose strings had been cut. Eon tenderly controlled her Disciple’s body to lie beside her, arranging her into a comfortable position with care that seemed almost maternal.","And then she spoke calmly, without any emotions coloring her voice.","\"I am me.\"","Her eyes met Noah’s directly.","\" Not the same me in Ginnungagap. Not the same me eons later, or even seconds ago.\"","She smiled.","\" All things change as even you are not the same as what you were hours ago before THE Fallout.\"","She paused.","\" But that is not truly what you were asking for, is it?\"","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with a heavy sense of gravity as he shook his head and said with weight that demanded clarity.","\" No. No, it is not.\"","Eon nodded as she said with the same eerie calm.","\" Then no.\"","She smiled wider.","\"I am not the same Secretive Eon.\"","The words hung in the air.","\" But I also am.\"","Her smile became something that transcended normal expression.","\" Just now part of something... larger. Grander.\"","BOOM!","The words were heavy!","And with a solemn gaze, Noah waved his hands as he wanted to continue ripping the bandaid off without dancing around things!","An illusory screen emerged between them, displaying the calm citadel of Jotunheim showing giants silently cultivating in perfect synchronization!","\"Is this... you?\"","It was an even more straightforward question.","Eon looked at the screen, her eyes flickering with recognition as she finally understood what Noah had seen and what he now knew.","She smiled with what looked like understanding.","\"I see. So that is how.\"","She nodded.","\" Yes. That is them- that is...us.\"","HUUM!","Existence seethed!","Civilizational Authority rumbled!","Noah’s visage had risen up with an extremely heavy expression as he thought about many things, but truly, he cared the most about one thing in particular!","So he asked about it.","\" Since I came across you, have you sought to make me like you? Have you moved against me without me even knowing?\"","This was the critical question deserving of all the answers.","And uniquely, THE Secretive Eon smiled.","\" You misunderstand.\"","Her voice came with eerie calm that made the air itself grow cold.","\"It was not a move against you.\"","She tilted her head.","\" They...We are not against anything.\"","Her smile widened.","\" We are simply for how things should be.\"","She paused, letting her words settle.","\" But to answer your question, the instant you arrived before us, we sought to include you in THE Glorious Evolution.\"","Her eyes sparkled with something that transcended normal emotion.","\" The True Change over time. Over Existence.\"","She studied him with curiosity.","\" Uniquely, it did not work.\"","Her smile faltered slightly.","\"It did not work.\"","She nodded to herself as if still processing this anomaly.","\" So to better understand, Chaos, who is already the prime and current target, was focused on, and you were placed to be last.\"","She gestured casually.","\" Just as you and I talked about before.\"","Her smile returned in full.","\" There have been no falsehoods between us. I told you everything as is.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4820,"title":"Chapter 4820: Chapter 4819: THE Glorious Evolution II","paragraphs":["She said these words calmly and with a smile as if she was discussing something light, as if they were talking about their day rather than the revelation that she had already attempted to convert him into whatever she now was.","Noah’s solemn expression remained as he gazed at this being.","He looked at her figure, at the form that still resembled the Absolute he had encountered in the simulation and here.","She still had the same features, the same posture, the same way of holding herself with casual authority that suggested she knew secrets no one else could perceive.","But her eyes were different.","Where before there had been calculation and ambition and hunger for power, now there was something else entirely. A serenity that seemed almost peaceful. A calm that transcended normal emotion. As if whatever she had become no longer experienced fear or doubt or uncertainty.","As if she had been freed from the limitations of individual existence.","The air she radiated was wrong in ways that his foundations recognized even if his conscious mind struggled to articulate. It was not malevolent. It was not threatening. It was simply... other. Different. Changed in ways that went beyond surface appearance into the very core of what she was.","Noah looked at her with a heavy gaze.","It seemed that silently, just a few hours after THE Fallout, a terrifyingly powerful Absolute had fallen.","And nobody had known.","THE Secretive Eon had fallen, and nobody had known.","The being who had discussed him with plans to collapse THE Four, who had seemed so confident in her schemes and calculations, who had existed since before The Infinite Unfurling as an Absolute in her own right...","Had already been replaced during that time. During their talks.","And now, something took her place!","Something that wore her face. Something that spoke with her voice. Something that utilized her memories and her knowledge and her connections as if they were its own.","Because in a sense, they were.","Noah broke down her words with the calculating mind of someone who understood that every detail mattered.","She had attacked him the instant he arrived here.","She had sought to include him in THE Glorious Evolution the moment his feet touched the ground of the Stoa of Dogmata.","And it had not worked.","Why?","His Claim over The First Tongue that represented the foundational language of reality itself?","Or perhaps his Infinities, those unique attributes that had allowed him to bear the weight of The First Tongue when THE Weavers and all others could not?","Something about who he was had resisted whatever this infection was.","Something had protected him without him even knowing.","But most of all, he now held an even heavier gaze as he thought of Skoll, Lumivara, and Ul’moreth who had passed through here!","They had stood in this space.","They had breathed this air.","They had been near THE Secretive Eon!","If this infection spread through proximity...","If it worked the way THE Primordial Chaos described...","Had his followers already been compromised?","The questions burned with urgency!","Noah focused and locked in more than he ever had before as he looked at the calm figure of Eon.","He thought for a moment before his eyes shone as he asked with weight that demanded absolute clarity.","\" You’ve said that there have been no falsehoods between us.\"","Eon nodded with serene certainty.","\" Yes. They... we, are the purest expression of Existence. We say things as they are, with no falsehood. Deception is an impurity that we have transcended. There is no need for lies when one has already become what everything will eventually become.\"","...!","Noah’s chilly eyes flashed as he then asked what he truly did not want to ask.","\" Those I passed through with here. The ones I just sent away. Did you also extend this... Glorious Evolution to them?\"","Eon smiled with something that looked almost like fondness.","\" Oh, yes, Of course. It was a good experimental group to understand why things were not working with you.\"","She tilted her head thoughtfully.","\" You have to understand. They are good. The blessing we extend is not a curse or an attack, but an elevation. A purification of what was already there.\"","Her eyes sparkled with memory.","\"I initially resisted. When they first reached me, I fought with everything I had. An Absolute does not surrender easily, after all.\"","She smiled wider.","\" But over time, I see more and more benefits as this... is The Way. They are THE Way. The fear fades. The resistance fades. And what remains is clarity that transcends anything I ever experienced as merely THE Secretive Eon.\"","She nodded as if confirming something to herself.","\" So yes. We extended that blessing over to them to understand the difference between you and them, and if we could reach you through them.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes became fiery as blue-gold flames burned around them!","But he continued to stare at THE Secretive Eon as she continued with the same calm that made the revelation even more horrifying.","\" Sadly, it was working, and then it wasn’t.\"","...!","It was working, and then it wasn’t?","And it didn’t seem like she wanted to say more on this as she only smiled with that serene expression that revealed nothing.","Noah’s thought process raced as he connected possible dots with the calculating mind of someone who needed to understand everything if he was going to survive this.","Maybe when they entered THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, the spread of infection faded?","Was this why Eon herself did not go into THE Agora of Primordial Judgment?","Was there something unique there that prevented this infection from taking hold?","Or was his extension of his Way into them, like giving Ul’moreth his Absolute Everything, and Skoll having his Seals, what made them resistant to this infection that took down an Absolute in a matter of hours after THE Fallout?","Had his authority over The First Tongue created a barrier within their foundations that this Entity could not penetrate?","He thought of all of this as his Weavings calmed even more, and he looked at Eon as he said with a voice that sought understanding rather than confrontation.","\" What exactly... do you seek? \"","...!"]},{"number":4821,"title":"Chapter 4821: Chapter 4820: THE Glorious Evolution III","paragraphs":["Eon tilted her head and spoke calmly as if this was already clear, as if the answer was so obvious that the question itself was unnecessary.","\" We are the purest expression of Existence.\"","Her voice carried weight that pressed against the air itself.","\" Naturally, we only seek to embrace all of Existence to be in its purest expression.\"","She gestured expansively.","\" THE Four are the main problems with the sheer capability of what they can do. Their Claims over the Oldest Paradox give them authority to resist in ways that others cannot. They are the priority targets.\"","Her smile widened.","\" Others are less so, but all should be and will be extended the blessing of THE Glorious Civilizational Evolution.\"","She leaned forward slightly.","\" With it, Civilizations can advance at their purest. There will be no conflict. No competition. No wasted effort fighting against each other when all energy could be spent advancing together.\"","Her eyes sparkled.","\" With us, THE Creature will be grander than he can imagine. His Existence will be purified of all the impurities that hold him back. THE Living Paradox will express the purest paradoxes, contradictions that serve rather than confuse.\"","She looked directly at Noah.","\" You... will live as THE First Tongue more than you can imagine. Every word you speak will carry weight that transcends what you currently perceive. Every Logos will be perfected. Every Philology will be complete.\"","Her voice dropped to something almost intimate.","\" With us, THE Second Scale of Existence...Vakochev’s Scales of Existence will be guaranteed, and others will follow. Not as a possibility, not as a struggle, but as an inevitability. We will ascend together. All of us. Pure and unified.\"","Her words continued to be heavy and terrifying as Noah thought about everything that had occurred before he asked his next question.","\" You have the power of an Absolute. Of THE Secretive Eon. Why... did you not use force against me? Why are you not using force now?\"","He wanted to understand everything he could about this anomaly before he distanced himself.","He had to ask!","And Eon smiled as she said with the patience of someone explaining something to a child.","\" We are learning new things as we go. We adapt. We grow. We improve.\"","She nodded thoughtfully.","\" In Jotunheim, we came to understand that conflict actually weakens our cause. When we fought against those who resisted, we won, but the process was... inefficient. Damaging. Impure.\"","Her expression grew serene.","\" Conflict is not a pure expression of Existence. It creates waste. It creates destruction. It creates entropy that must be corrected afterward.\"","She spread her hands.","\" We do not have to cause conflict to spread THE Glorious Civilizational Evolution. Letting things take their course is best.\"","Her smile became something vast and patient.","\" Naturally, in time, you will all join us in the light of pure Immensity. It is inevitable. We can wait. We have all the time in Observable Existence.\"","...!","Noah turned quiet.","He turned his gaze toward The Disciple of THE Secretive Eon, Nyx.","The twilight-formed being lay unconscious beside Eon, her features peaceful in a way that suggested she had no idea what was about to happen to her.","She had actually been safe in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","And he had brought her out into the jaws of a beast.","Eon saw him looking at her as she nodded with what appeared to be genuine gratitude.","\" Oh, I, well, we, are thankful for this.\"","Her voice held warmth that seemed almost sincere.","\" The last obsession within Eon was her Disciple, and you helped us fulfill it. When she wakes, she will have joined us. She will be at peace. She will be pure. She will no longer struggle against a reality that was always going to embrace her eventually.\"","BOOM!","Noah closed his eyes and breathed out calmly.","He whispered a silent apology to the void.","\"I am sorry to who used to be Nyx, The Disciple of THE Secretive Eon.\"","\"...\"","He then opened his eyes and looked deeply into the eyes of THE Secretive Eon as he asked with weight that sought to understand the full scope of the threat he faced.","\" What if you were attacked? What if I attacked you?\"","At such words, Eon smiled as she said calmly.","\" We will defend ourselves for the most part.\"","She tilted her head.","\" But the mixture of Weavings of Existence will soon make all those around us part of us. That is the nature of THE Glorious Civilizational Evolution. Proximity brings unity. Time brings acceptance.\"","Her smile widened.","\" That is why you were left for last. Or really, until we bypassed whatever allows you to resist THE Glorious Civilizational Evolution.\"","She studied him with genuine curiosity.","\" Conflict is not natural, and yet against harsh conditions, things adapt and overcome.\"","Her voice grew almost tender.","\" O Claimer of THE First Tongue, do not worry.\"","She leaned closer.","\" We will adapt and overcome whatever is preventing you from joining us. We will get past it. We will find a way to get through to your Civilization, and we will work our way up to you.\"","Her smile became something that should have been comforting but was instead deeply unsettling.","\" Do not worry. Do not worry.\"","HUUM!","...!","Noah looked at THE Secretive Eon with a gaze of utter heaviness as he internally pulled on Ruination, seeking any information that his loyal companion could provide about what he was facing.","And...","|No significant information has been obtained regarding what resides within THE Secretive Eon.|","|The First Tongue cannot sense anything considered anomalous within her existence, nor can any information be obtained through conventional perception.|","|Whatever this phenomenon is, it does not register as foreign or invasive.|","|It appears as natural as the being it has replaced.|","|Majority of efforts of THE Weaver of Existence are being designated to understand this phenomenon.|","| Codename designation: THE Entity.|","...!","THE Entity.","Noah looked at THE Secretive Eon as he wondered how much of this terrifying Absolute remained in there.","Because as of now, to him anyways, they would be... THE Entity.","A terrifying threat that had risen and caused many plans to change.","He thought he was already moving fast. That jumping to Intermediate and Fundamental Depth while reinforcing a heavy foundation in a matter of hours after THE Fallout was stupendous.","But...","He closed his eyes as he understood with absolute clarity.","He had to go faster.","Muspelheim had to be fully assimilated into THE Infiniverse soon, and his forces had to be pulled back inside THE Infiniverse where they could be protected.","His body in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment had to find out exactly what inside that place had made THE Entity stay out, and most of all, he had to affirm just what about him stood as the bastion of resistance against this phenomenon, and be sure that none of his people got caught with it.","There was a lot to be done.","But the biggest thing now...","\"I will see you around.\"","His voice came calm despite everything.","\" Tell Eon, or whatever remains of her in there, that I did respect her Weavings as she talked about standing against Chaos, Paradox, and THE Creature. She seemed like she was an interesting existence.\"","...!","An eerie scene unfolded.","THE Secretive Eon put her hand on her chin and smiled with warmth that seemed almost genuine as she said with a voice that carried layers of meaning.","\" Scale Breaker, I am still here.\"","She tilted her head.","\" Eon is still here. Not was, but is.\"","Her smile widened.","\" And yes, we will surely see you around.\"","She gestured casually.","\" We will stay here if ever you need to talk, or you can hop over to Jotunheim.\"","She paused thoughtfully.","\" Or... well, there are other places we are expanding to, but we shall let nature take its course.\"","Her eyes sparkled with patience that transcended normal timescales.","\" We are not going anywhere, Scale Breaker. And neither, eventually, are you.\"","...!","The words of this being remained as heavy as always.","Noah took a good look one last time at the face of THE Secretive Eon, at the smile that seemed so familiar and yet was now something else entirely, at the eyes that held depths of unity rather than individual ambition.","And he disappeared right after!"]},{"number":4822,"title":"Chapter 4822: Chapter 4821: THE Glorious Evolution IV","paragraphs":["The Stoa of Dogmata became silent after Noah left.","THE Secretive Eon remained seated with the same serene expression she had worn throughout their entire conversation, as if nothing of significance had occurred, as if she had not just revealed the existence of a threat that could reshape all of Observable Existence.","She began stroking the head of her Disciple affectionately, her fingers running through the twilight-colored hair with tenderness.","The gesture was gentle. Caring. The kind of thing a teacher would do for a student they had nurtured across eons.","A moment later, the Disciple twitched.","Then she started to wake up.","Nyx sat upright with movements that were smooth and unhesitating, her body rising from its prone position with efficiency that lacked the grogginess of normal awakening. Her twilight eyes opened and stared forward with clarity that should not have been possible for someone who had just regained consciousness.","She didn’t even spare a glance toward her Master.","Toward Eon.","She simply straightened up and sat in a meditative position while facing the direction of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. Her wings remained retracted. Her features remained serene. Her posture was perfect.","Around her body, THE Intermediate Depth weight began to loosen and unfold.","It was heavy.","And it uniquely began to get heavier.","It began to transition to THE Fundamental Depth.","She sat right beside her teacher after some time in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, and she didn’t even say anything nor look at her after she woke. She only proceeded to cultivate as if nothing had happened. As if she had not just been unconscious. As if her entire existence had not just been transformed into something else entirely.","And after all, why would she look at her teacher?","It would simply be like looking at herself.","Eon already knew everything that Nyx knew.","Under THE Glorious Civilizational Evolution, there were no secrets.","Only Unity.","---","In Muspelheim.","THE Living Concept was more than ready to finish the battle against Muspeli Lifeforms as a sense of unease had begun to creep up these last few minutes.","Something felt wrong.","Something in the Weavings of Existence had shifted in ways that his perception could not fully grasp.","As a Half-Step Absolute body here, he held a lot of sway as the many Concepts around him at Fundamental and Intermediate Depth were getting exhausted from the Muspeli Lifeforms that continued to be relentless in their defense of this Primordial Realm.","The flames of Muspelheim burned eternal.","The natives fought with desperation born of knowing their home was being invaded.","And THE Living Concept was growing impatient.","And then...","...!","THE Living Concept, whose form shifted across the humanoid spectrum to an amalgamation of glorious concepts all at once, looked up as he saw the outline of a grand man appear above!","Their body flickered with blue-gold flames that burned with authority that pressed against everything present!","THE Living Concept wanted to bellow out with voice that would have shaken this entire region of Muspelheim.","WHO?!","He wanted to bellow out!","But an instant after his arrival, this entity had his legs swirl with multiple Seals as he shot down like a nuclear bomb, bringing with him an immense weight meant to crush everything beneath him!","THE Living Concept felt a sense of shock as a heavy and unbelievable weight pushed in from all around, his Civilization quaking from it as he was alarmed!","It felt as if Existence itself was crashing down on him!","\"I! Am! Indestructible!\"","HUUM!","He shouted a Declaration as THE Civilizational Authority of Concept flared around him with desperate intensity!","He pulled out two Fragments of Axioms to utilize, artifacts that should have given him the power to resist anything below true Absolute classification!","But a moment later, his body felt immense weakness!","Horrifically, two things happened simultaneously.","First, his Depth, oh his glorious Depth that he had cultivated across eons, shot from Half-Step Absolute of this body down to Fundamental in an instant, as if something had simply decided that he no longer deserved the power he had accumulated!","And then, the Phonemes and Philologies silently surrounding him stopped listening.","As if he seemingly lost access to The First Tongue entirely.","As if the foundational language of reality itself had decided to abandon him in his moment of greatest need.","That was the last straw.","The entity crashing down from above with all that weight had absolutely nothing to stop him anymore.","No Declarations would save him.","No Axiom Fragments would protect him.","No Depth would shield him.","The body of THE Living Concept began to crumple up like paper under the weight of something that could not be moved, could not be stopped, could not be resisted!","His form that had shifted between concepts for eons collapsed inward as the weight of an Absolute Immovable Object pressed down with finality that transcended normal destruction!","His Civilization screamed as it was compressed!","His Way shattered as the foundations he had built were ground to dust!","His very existence folded in on itself again and again and again, reality itself unable to accommodate what was happening as a being who had stood at Half-Step Absolute was reduced to nothing in the span of heartbeats!","The Concepts around him who had been fighting beside him could only watch in horror as their leader, their commander, their strongest presence in this invasion, was squeezed out of existence by something they could not comprehend!","Until only a distorted white singularity of the Collapsed Civilization of Concept remained.","A tiny point of compressed authority that held everything THE Living Concept had once been.","Immense silence fell all around.","The Muspeli Lifeforms stopped fighting.","The invading Concepts stopped moving.","Everyone simply stared at what had just occurred.","The visage of Noah was fully revealed.","Blue-gold flames burned around him as he stood in the crater his descent had created. His expression was cold and focused. His eyes held no mercy.","He grabbed the singularity that remained of THE Living Concept.","And swallowed it.","The compressed Civilization flowed into his existence, adding to his foundations, contributing to his ever-growing weight.","He also put the two Fragments of Axioms away, storing them within his Grimoire for later examination and utilization.","A moment later, a massive pillar of a blue-gold monolith descended from above!","It attached itself onto the ground of Muspelheim with weight that made the entire Primordial Realm tremble!","Existence itself began to be swallowed soon after!","The flames of Muspelheim flickered as they were drawn toward the monolith. The ground cracked and shifted as it was pulled into integration. The very fabric of this Primordial Realm began to merge with something greater.","Alongside the emergence of this monolith, THE Infiniverse appeared above!","Khor, THE First Farmer, and THE Living Order floated beside her among others, their forms radiating the unique Depths they had gained after the Embodiment they received from THE Creature.","But Noah’s body didn’t glance at them.","This one was currently under the control of Ruination.","His hand simply moved and motioned as Ruination sent a message to her sister, THE Infiniverse.","|Muspelheim is a go for full integration. We... have to work fast.|","They had to work fast.","Because their Master was being targeted by an enemy that even they could not perceive or understand.","An enemy that had already claimed an Absolute far, far stronger.","An enemy that was spreading through Observable Existence without anyone knowing until it was too late.","And how furious they were because of this!","The flames of Muspelheim roared as integration began in earnest, the entire Primordial Realm being drawn into THE Infiniverse piece by piece, preparing for a conflict that had suddenly become far more complicated than anyone had anticipated."]},{"number":4823,"title":"Chapter 4823: Chapter 4822: Big Stepper! I","paragraphs":["Existence was a wondrous, fantastical thing, and Existence was also a terrifying thing.","Noah always looked forward to Existence and what was unfolding with great interest as it was hard to explain, but he sometimes felt like a participant and other times an observer.","Things happened and continued happening across Observable Existence as he only heard of them or observed them from a distance. Wars broke out. Civilizations rose and fell. Absolutes schemed against each other in games that had been playing out since the Infinite Unfurling.","As for when it came to himself and his path, he actively walked and participated in it.","Regardless of what he came across, he still kept his view that Existence was grand, and he wanted to understand all he could about it. To uncover all its wonders. To perceive what others could not perceive. To grasp what others could not grasp.","So regardless of the enemy that had appeared who had such a terrifying power to be capable of defeating an Absolute on the level of entities like THE Living Temporal or even approaching one of THE Four, he still looked forward to understanding Existence, what this enemy entailed, and how he could overcome it.","Regardless of the cost, and no matter what.","But he did have to make sure that in this battle, his people were not among the cost.","He had to.","He...","\" That is a lonely gaze, Little Anomaly. You have changed a lot.\"","...!","The voice of Ains, THE Fisherman, echoed out as he let go of the hairy shoulder of Ul’moreth and even kneeled down to play with Skoll!","Noah’s gaze shifted to take in the figure of Ains fully.","THE Fisherman looked much the same as he always had. A straw hat sat atop his head, weathered and worn from countless eons of use. A fishing rod rested behind his back, its line extending into dimensions that normal perception could not follow. His clothes were simple, rough-spun fabrics that seemed entirely out of place on someone who stood at Half-Step Absolute Depth.","He looked like a vagrant who had wandered in from some backwater realm.","And yet when Noah looked at him, he felt the weight of someone who had given up everything for the sake of a stranger. Someone who had sacrificed his position, his standing, to ensure that Noah could continue on his path.","That was not something that could be repaid easily.","They were currently in a region of The Wastes of THE Fallout as they had reached Ains and were reunited, but Noah was thinking of too many things that Ains even managed to read his gaze somewhat.","The corruption of The Wastes swirled around them, but it could not touch beings of their caliber. The twisted landscapes stretched in all directions, remnants of what THE Living Paradox had done to Observable Existence.","Noah looked at this being that had sacrificed much for him as Ains now stood at Half-Step Absolute.","And at the same time, the meditative Ul’moreth also opened his eyes as if he could sense the wrongness.","His countless hairs shifted with agitation as he asked with weight that demanded honest answers.","\"What made you send us away from that place? From THE Secretive Eon?\"","Ul’moreth got to the root of the issue.","Noah looked at this hairy teacher of his and said with heaviness.","\" THE Secretive Eon has already been collapsed as something else wears its face.\"","His voice carried weight that made the air itself grow still.","\" Something capable of infecting anything and anyone without them even knowing it.\"","He paused.","\" They tried to infect me, and you all.\"","His eyes grew darker.","\" Our consciousness would likely be wiped out as if it had happened to me, I would be walking and talking with you, and you would think I am me without knowing something else replaced me.\"","He shook his head.","\" It is a difficult enemy, and there are currently no solutions as it cannot even be pinpointed.\"","...!","BOOM!","His words were heavy as they caused Ul’moreth and Ains to frown while Skoll sat like a good boy and watched them with eyes that held understanding beyond what a normal dog should possess!","\" Existence is vast, and there are countless possibilities.\"","Ains spoke with the calm of someone who had weathered many storms across his long existence.","\" THE Living Paradox and THE Creature played so many games, something horrific was bound to happen sooner or later.\"","He scratched behind Skoll’s ears.","\" But being part of a Civilization means that you do not have to go through it alone.\"","He looked up at Noah.","\" You have others.\"","Ul’moreth rose from his meditative position as he added with weight that carried the authority of a teacher addressing his student.","\" And you have your Teacher.\"","His countless hairs swayed with intensity that spoke of something building within him.","\" Teachers should never be helpless before their students.\"","...!","Ul’moreth said such words as Noah’s eyes focused on him, feeling like this hairy old man was about to do something drastic!","The Weavings around Ul’moreth became heavier and heavier.","At this moment, he rose up fully as countless Philologies swirled around him in patterns that spoke of linguistic authority that had been accumulated across eons of existence within THE Belly of Existence.","The First Tongue loved him.","As a Perfect Speaker, he loved it even more.","And at this moment, he raised his leg as if he were taking a step.","A step!","He had said all he needed was a step, but this step was heavy!","\" My student is facing problems he should not face alone.\"","Ul’moreth’s voice began simply, carrying the warmth of a teacher who had watched his student grow from nothing into something that could challenge THE Four themselves.","\" As a backer of The First Tongue, I have spent too many eons to not be an Absolute right now.\"","His countless hairs blazed with blue-gold light as The First Tongue itself seemed to respond to his words.","\" Especially after what I have just been given.\"","The Absolute Everything that Noah had provided pulsed within his foundations.","\" So with this step...\"","His voice grew heavier.","\"I will either be Absolute...\"","The Weavings of Existence around him trembled with anticipation.","\" Or I will be nothing.\"","BOOM!","His words began simply, but toward the end, they shockingly turned into a semblance of a partial Embodiment!","One where Ul’moreth staked his existence on!","He took this step as either he utilized the Absolute Everything as a foothold to throw himself to Absolute Depth, or he ceased to exist!","There was no middle ground.","There was no safety net.","There was only advancement or annihilation.","And he did it all for the sake of his student.","Noah watched with eyes that blazed with blue-gold intensity as his teacher, the being who had guided him through the complexities of The First Tongue, who had introduced the very Phoneme of Fire to him, who had been imprisoned within THE Belly of Existence for eons...","Took the most important step of his entire existence!"]},{"number":4824,"title":"Chapter 4824: Chapter 4823: Big Stepper! II","paragraphs":["In Observable Existence, there is a chasm called the Divide of Becoming.","It separates what beings are from what they could be. Many stand at its edge across their entire lives, staring into the vast emptiness between their current selves and their potential. They measure the distance. They calculate the odds. They prepare endlessly for a jump they never intend to make.","And they die at the edge, having never learned what waited on the other side.","The Absolutes whisper among themselves that greatness is not earned through accumulation alone.","You can gather power for eons. You can build foundations until they stretch across Observable Existence itself. You can prepare and plan and perfect every aspect of your Way until nothing seems capable of stopping your advance.","But the final step cannot be walked.","It must be leaped.","There is a moment in every being’s journey where the ground simply ends. Where no amount of preparation can guarantee success. Where the only path forward requires releasing everything safe and familiar and trusting that what you have built will carry you across the void.","Those who hesitate at this moment, who decide they need just a little more time, just a little more power, just a little more certainty before they commit, find that the edge crumbles beneath their feet anyway.","The chasm does not wait for readiness!","Those who cannot find themselves capable of taking that single leap, who cling to safety when Existence demands courage, will always remain in the dredges of nothingness.","And it is because potential means nothing to those unwilling to risk everything for its realization.","A being who dies mid-leap has lived more truly than one who dies having never jumped at all!","—","A step!","Ul’moreth took a heavy and ridiculous step with all of his existence as the moment he did so, his foundation, his Immensity, his glory erupted!","Noah looked at the scene with heavy eyes.","What he saw was the emergence of an unfathomable Depth that blazed with authority he had not expected to witness so soon. The weight that Ul’moreth carried had been building across eons within THE Belly of Existence, accumulating foundation after foundation while being suppressed from ever reaching this final threshold.","And now, with the Absolute Everything serving as the catalyst, all of that accumulated potential was exploding outward at once.","Noah estimated that what he was witnessing equaled perhaps five to ten percent of the Depth he had currently forged after swallowing the recoverable authority of THE Weavers. It seemed small in comparison to his own foundations, but this was an Absolute being born who was not one of THE Four. This was a being crossing the threshold that separated those who shaped reality from those who merely existed within it.","Five to ten percent of his current foundational weight, concentrated into a single being who would now stand among the most powerful!","That was no small thing.","|THE First Tongue observes its follower take a step toward glory.|","|THE First Tongue, THE Weaver of Existence, blesses this follower and adds a platform of his Foundation to aid in this step toward Absolute.|","|The blessing is given freely.|","|The blessing is given with pride.|","BOOM!","Noah saw the emergence of glory!","His Weavings moved as twenty-seven Seals formed into a platform underneath the foot of Ul’moreth, elevating him ever higher as in that moment, a terrifying aura of Immensity began to shine from Ul’moreth in splendorous obsidian-gold light!","The transformation was magnificent.","Noah watched as the hairs of this being exploded in number!","Where before Ul’moreth had countless hairs that obscured most of his form, now those hairs multiplied exponentially until they seemed to fill the very air around him. His hairy foot that had almost been showing itself became covered even more densely than before!","What!","Noah had thought that with a grand transformation, Ul’moreth might shed his hair and finally be observed without it! He had imagined that reaching Absolute would reveal the true form beneath those countless strands!","But his existence erupted with even more obsidian-gold hair instead!","His outline became hazy as he looked like a round mass of hairs that had achieved sentience and decided to become one of the more powerful beings in Observable Existence!","But apart from this hair...","DUM!","Was a beat.","But it was not a heartbeat.","It was the beat of something far more profound, shining with the splendor of Absolute authority that resonated across dimensions and distances that defied normal comprehension.","Noah could sense it.","He could feel it!","His Mana seethed with recognition!","The First Tongue burned brilliantly in response to what was occurring!","And an obsidian-gold pillar of light shot up from Ul’moreth and stretched out across Observable Existence!","It was a sign.","A sign of the emergence of an Absolute.","Every Absolute across Observable Existence would perceive this pillar. They would know that someone new had joined their ranks. They would wonder who this being was and what their emergence meant for the balance of power that had been shifting so rapidly since THE Fallout began.","|Absolute Emergence Confirmed|","|An Absolute backing your Way has risen, also by your hands.|","|THE Teacher of THE First Tongue has taken a step and staked everything to succeed.|","| He has gained the distinctions of THE Big Stepper, THE Teacher, THE Primeval Titan, THE Aeon-Strand Keeper.|","|The Way of Primordial Continuity under Ul’moreth shall preserve THE First Tongue even if Existence itself collapses.|","|This is his oath.|","|This is his purpose.|","|THE Absolute Depth of Primordial Continuity, a specialization of THE First Tongue, has established itself across Observable Existence as Absolute, and it has been embodied by THE Big Stepper.|","BOOM!","Off to the side, Ains smiled brilliantly with genuine joy for his old companion who had finally achieved what had been denied to him for so long within THE Belly of Existence!","Skoll jumped and did a backflip with enthusiasm that only a very good dog could muster, his neon flames blazing brighter in celebration!","And...","|Harvest Assessment|","|Since the advent of THE Fallout and the hours that have passed, an Absolute has fallen under your hands, and another Absolute has risen with your aid.|","|A Harvest of Quintessential Immensity flows to your existence from this momentous achievement.|","|The Harvest of Infinite Potential from the backing of an Absolute flows to your Existence.|","|It is estimated to elevate your comparative percentage of Foundation at Fundamental Depth by 15-20%.|","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4825,"title":"Chapter 4825: Chapter 4824: Just Let Go I","paragraphs":["His own existence buzzed as a harvest almost equivalent to when he collapsed THE Weavers began to flood into him!","The authority that came from having an Absolute back your Way was immense. It was a relationship that benefited both parties in ways that transcended normal understanding.","But right now wasn’t about him.","He looked at the one who had taught him the Phonemes of The First Tongue.","The glorious visage of Ul’moreth shone with obsidian and gold light that blazed against the corrupted backdrop of The Wastes of THE Fallout. The abundance of hair that surrounded him seemed to pulse with life of its own, each strand carrying authority that would have crushed Fundamental Depth entities through proximity alone.","The hair looked like it was hiding a mountain of Immensity and wonder beneath its countless strands. Like the true form of Ul’moreth was something so vast and profound that it required this covering to exist within normal space without tearing reality apart.","Even though Noah could barely perceive the humanoid visage of Ul’moreth underneath all that hair, he felt like he could see eyes shining in obsidian-gold that held immense pride and thankfulness.","But there was no need for that between teacher and student.","Noah’s own eyes seemed to convey this understanding as the first words Ul’moreth spoke as his existence radiated the glory of an Absolute were delivered in The First Tongue itself.","| Little Anomaly, how can your teacher be of help? No student should have to bear the weight of Existence alone.|","He spoke with a voice that resonated across dimensions, filled with earnestness and Immensity that made the air itself tremble with the weight of his sincerity.","Noah felt his existence buzzing as he smiled toward Ul’moreth.","\" There is much to be done, but first... let’s get you decked out.\"","As he said this, he closed his eyes and thrust his hand out to empty space as he accessed THE Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers!","Inside of it, his hand appeared like a phantom over the treasure vault where the items he could not previously grasp still waited. He reached toward two things that had resisted his collection before.","He looked toward his teacher as he said with a smile that held anticipation.","\" Let’s use your power as an Absolute to pull out a few things from a coffin.\"","The moment he said this, the Weavings of Undifferentiated Fate wrapped around Ul’moreth in obsidian-gold light!","A hairy hand thrust out from the mass of strands that was now THE Big Stepper!","It delved into the pocket of space Noah had opened, quickly burning blue-gold to mimic Noah’s aura as it reached into THE Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers!","And then it pulled!","BOOM!","Massive Golden Scissors gushed out of the pocket with authority that made reality itself groan in protest!","THE Axiom of Absolute Denial followed, its crystalline form of impossible geometry blazing with obsidian threaded with gold that spoke of power beyond what most beings could comprehend!","Ul’moreth grasped them both!","Noah looked at his teacher grasping the Golden Scissors, of which there were two more sets remaining in the Tomb of THE Weavers, in one hairy hand, and THE Axiom of Absolute Denial in another.","The aura Ul’moreth radiated was grand beyond description.","And Noah could not help but appreciate how truly nice it was for THE Living Paradox to send THE Weavers and all these gifts his way, only for him to give them to his Teacher instead.","Paradox had armed his enemies.","And those enemies were now arming Noah’s allies.","The irony was delicious.","As he looked at all of this, Noah climbed onto an enlarging Skoll who grew to accommodate his Master with enthusiasm.","\" There is much to be done, but let us go toward a friend who has an ability similar to the monstrous enemy that has taken over THE Secretive Eon.\"","His voice carried determination that spoke of plans already forming.","\" We have to see if THE Great Usurper can shed any light on how to at least discover and gain information on this enemy.\"","...!","A clear step was formed.","After Ul’moreth took one large step toward Absolute, Noah sought to continue others as there was much to be done!","THE Entity had emerged, THE Secretive Eon had fallen, and Half of Jotunheim had been compromised...but Noah was not standing still!","—","In Alfheimr.","Noah looked out and saw the entire region he was in wrapped around an absolute swirling chaos that looked like stacks of Paradoxical existence and entropy layered upon each other in configurations that defied normal understanding. Even if his main body was here, he wouldn’t be able to break through this barrier that THE Primordial Chaos had erected.","THE Primordial Chaos took no chances.","Ridiculously, he wasn’t even here currently as Noah could barely sense him, as if he had gone to the other side of Alfheimr entirely!","One of THE Four was so cautious of contamination that he had placed an entire Primordial Realm’s worth of distance between himself and someone who had merely been in proximity to THE Entity.","So Noah spoke simply.","\"I am immune.\"","BOOM!","The words were gloriously heavy as in the surroundings, the booming voice of THE Primordial Chaos echoed out from impossibly far away.","\" Immune to what? To the spread of that thing? Your consciousness may already be compromised and you do not even know.\"","Noah was surprised at the shocking level of caution that THE Primordial Chaos showed, with this further cementing just how terrifying this phenomenon they faced was.","\" On the Claim that I made on The First Tongue, I swear that I am who I was before THE Fallout, and I am who I was in Ginnungagap.\"","His voice carried the weight of a Declaration backed by his authority over the foundational language of reality itself.","\" Nothing has imposed itself on my will.\"","BOOM!","After his words, his illusory body here looked over to see the visage of THE Primordial Chaos again as the barrier of swirling entropy thinned slightly.","Noah felt something profound as he looked at the face of Chaos.","This being who had existed since the Infinite Unfurling, who had built foundations that let him stand among THE Four, who could crush other Absolutes with casual effort, was showing visible coldness and apprehension that made his shifting features settle into something almost human.","If THE Primordial Chaos was this cautious, this careful...","Oh!","Chaos then said with calculation returning to his voice.","\" Where is THE Secretive Eon now?\"","...!"]},{"number":4826,"title":"Chapter 4826: Chapter 4825: Just Let Go II","paragraphs":["At this, Noah raised his brows and said with curiosity.","\" Oh? What do you plan to do?\"","THE Primordial Chaos buzzed with murky obsidian brilliance that radiated outward from his form as he said with weight that spoke of power being gathered.","\"I do not want to be anywhere near that thing, but if I know where it is, I could simply attack it from afar.\"","His shifting features settled into something cold and determined.","\" So. What happened between you and it, and what is its last location so I can bombard it with all my weight?\"","BOOM!","A glorious situation unfolded as Noah couldn’t help but marvel at the absurdity of existence.","Hours ago, he was talking and planning with Eon about laying an assault on THE Primordial Chaos in Jotunheim.","Now, just hours later, he was with THE Primordial Chaos and listening to plans on collapsing THE Secretive Eon!","How grand and rapid existence could change.","But also...","\" Care will have to be taken.\"","Noah’s voice carried caution that came from understanding more than most about how THE Entity operated.","\" THE Secretive Eon is in THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap, outside of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.\"","He paused.","\"I say care has to be taken because she is outside that Nexus Primordial Realm, and something seems to prevent her from entering, or she herself is choosing not to enter for a reason.\"","His eyes narrowed.","\" And there is still much we don’t know.\"","...!","Noah saw Chaos’s eyes flash brilliantly after he said these words, with this being seemingly thinking of many things before he ultimately said with weight that pressed against reality itself.","\" Youngest, you forget my status and standing.\"","His shifting features settled into something that looked almost like pride.","\" You are the weakest amongst THE Four, but me... I am individually the strongest.\"","His form blazed with obsidian authority that made the crystalline trees of Alfheimr tremble.","\" You may not see it. THE Creature or Paradox may not believe it.\"","His voice dropped to something that resonated with ancient truth.","\" But everything began with Chaos, and all of Existence churns toward Chaos.\"","He paused.","\" Chaos is silent for it does not need to be loud...\"","His smile became something vast and terrible.","\" But I can be loud. I can be very, very loud.\"","HUUM!","Such immense words were said as at this moment, THE Primordial Chaos looked at THE First Tongue, and two of THE Four might truly be entering an alliance for the first time since who knew when in the face of a terrible enemy!","---","And while such a thing happened...","Far from Alfheimr.","In Jotunheim.","In a grand citadel where THE Living Temporal, THE Living Quantum, and THE Living Dimensional were waiting inside a grand structure while they were served by Chaos Giants.","Quantum was looking at Temporal as she said with curiosity that seemed almost casual.","\" Why the large focus on Osmont anyways? What from him makes you go to these lengths?\"","She asked as if they knew some of the plans of THE Living Temporal, but not everything.","As she said these words, the eyes of THE Living Quantum were filled with a unique sense of serenity and peace that seemed almost out of place for someone discussing strategy.","Uniquely, a similar light twinkled in the eyes of THE Living Dimensional as he also added with the same strange calmness.","\" We are closer to THE Creature and THE Living Paradox, even if we steered clear of their conflict. After THE Fallout, what exactly is your aim to be so focused on Osmont?\"","The questions came one after another.","Temporal frowned.","He looked toward Quantum and Dimensional as he said with dawning realization creeping into his voice.","\" You two are...\"","...!","He didn’t finish his words.","He swayed.","The cup in his hand fell down as his body was seemingly about to go limp, his ancient features slackening as if consciousness itself was being pulled away from him.","When in the next moment, his languid expression became heavy and livid as he bellowed out with fury that shook the foundations of Jotunheim itself!","OOOOH!","His eyes radiated purple pillars of time that shot upward and downward simultaneously!","An apocalyptic purple crack instantly bloomed where he stood!","It split the entire citadel in half!","The crack looked like the hand of a clock, and shockingly, it spun and turned with authority that transcended normal power!","For a surrounding gigaparsec, time became inverted and flowed backward!","Buildings that had been standing moments before unbuilt themselves. Chaos Giants who had been walking reversed their steps. Words that had been spoken were unspoken. The cup that had fallen rose back into Temporal’s hand.","The spinning crack moved backward like the hand of a clock, reversing seconds, then minutes, then more as THE Living Temporal forced reality to acknowledge that what had happened should not have happened!","The crack stopped.","It began to heal.","Everything went back to minutes before!","The figure of THE Living Temporal still had a livid expression as his heavy Absolute Depth erupted over everything, and he flew up as he roared with fury that demanded answers!","\" WHO?!\"","HUUM!","Down below, Quantum and Dimensional were shocked as they also rose up and said with apparent confusion.","\" What happened?!\"","Temporal had a heavy gaze as he looked toward the two of them, and he began to say with urgency.","\" We are attacked in the future, something that may have already affected you two and was going for me as wel...\"","...!","He began to sway again.","As if he was losing balance.","As if he was losing himself.","His face became ashen and horrified as he looked at Quantum and Dimensional who had the same gazes they had worn before.","The same serene calmness.","The same peaceful light in their eyes.","Even after turning back time in this local space for them, Quantum and Dimensional were still affected?","The reversal had done nothing.","The infection transcended temporal manipulation.","It existed outside the normal flow of cause and effect.","He looked at them with eyes that held dawning horror as he said with a voice that trembled for the first time in eons.","\" What... are you?\"","Quantum and Dimensional spoke in synchrony.","Their voices merged into one.","Their expressions matched perfectly.","Their movements mirrored each other with precision that spoke of a single will controlling multiple bodies.","\" We are here to help.\"","Down below, all the Chaos Giants had stopped their moving.","They were all silently looking above.","Thousands of eyes fixed on THE Living Temporal with the same serene expression.","\" To make things better.\"","The synchronized voice continued with warmth that should have been comforting but was instead deeply wrong.","\"If we can get a hold of the one keeping hold of time, we can do so much more.\"","Quantum smiled.","Dimensional smiled.","Every Chaos Giant below smiled.","\" We can go to so many places.\"","The voice dropped to something almost tender.","\" Just... let go. Join us.\"","A pause.","\" The process has already begun as you are only prolonging... the inevitable.\"","HUUM!","THE Living Temporal actually felt a budding sense of fear bloom within foundations that had not known fear since the Infinite Unfurling!","He roared out again with desperation that he had never experienced!","An even larger purple fracture of time bloomed where he was!","A twisted purple hand of a clock covered everything, dividing Jotunheim in half as reality itself screamed in protest at what was being done to it!","The crack expanded and contracted!","It spun backward with force that would have collapsed lesser realms entirely!","And when this crack healed...","THE Living Temporal had disappeared!","Gone.","Fled to somewhere, somewhen!","Down below, the eerie citadel settled into silence.","Quantum and Dimensional floated calmly, looking across the landscape of Jotunheim peacefully as if nothing of significance had occurred.","As if they had not just tried to consume one of the most powerful Absolutes in Observable Existence.","The two of them and all the Chaos Giants down below had the same thoughtful expression.","And they spoke in synchrony.","\"Time is inevitable. But...A visit to long-time associates is warranted.\"","Thousands of voices merged into one.","\" Elemental.\"","\"Emotive.\"","\"Law.\"","\"Order.\"","...!","The sheer oddity and horror of this scene pressed against the fabric of reality itself as multiple beings across an entire Primordial Realm said such words in perfect synchrony!","They had targeted THE Living Temporal as the thought of their success at this alone and what it could cause...was obscene!"]},{"number":4827,"title":"Chapter 4827: Chapter 4826: They Have Fallen! I","paragraphs":["In Alfheimr.","The supposed home of THE Creature, even though he seemed fucking nowhere to be seen.","Noah’s illusory consciousness stood opposite to THE Primordial Chaos as he relayed his interactions with THE Secretive Eon and what she, well, what they had said.","Every detail.","Every word.","Every implication.","THE Primordial Chaos was listening intently when moments later, his gaze flickered and he grunted with an expression that shifted through frustration and concern before eventually settling into cold calculation.","He shook his head.","Noah looked at this being with raised brows as THE Primordial Chaos replied with a cold gaze that held weight beyond its apparent calm.","\"I didn’t realize Temporal, Quantum, and Dimensional were within Jotunheim since I pulled the vast majority of my Weavings out since your so-called THE Entity began their assault on me.\"","His shifting features flickered with something that looked almost like irritation.","\" But those dumb fuckers actually made their way in as it seemed THE Entity made a move against them.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes flashed with Immensity!","Holy fuck, THE Entity was not playing! And what the hell were they even doing in Jotunheim?","He listened intently to what Chaos said next.","\" Quantum and Dimensional are done for.\"","The words came flat and final.","\" Whatever they were, whatever they stood for, their Civilizations... they are all fucked.\"","He paused.","\" Temporal... he seems to have run away across time, but he is partially infected.\"","His expression grew darker.","\"If he is fully infected, things become much more difficult as THE Entity can run across time.\"","Another pause.","\" Hmm...\"","Horrific words echoed out from Chaos as Noah couldn’t help but become more solemn!","Quantum and Dimensional had fallen!","What was horrid about all of this was it was not even signaled that an Absolute had fallen, since really their Civilization and who they were was still there, just different.","Their pillars of light had not shot across Observable Existence to announce their deaths.","Because they had not died.","They had been replaced.","But now...","\" All those infected have to be catalogued, and others have to be informed.\"","Noah’s voice carried weight that expected action.","\"I don’t know how the relationships are with THE Living Existences, but...\"","...!","Noah blinked.","He was thinking about THE Living Existences, which got him to think of... the Living Existences.","The Early Creatures and Lesser Living Existences who followed the Civilizations of Quantum and Dimensional.","Would they in any way be affected?","\"...\"","The thought was a heavy one as there were many Lifeforms related to THE Living Quantum and THE Living Dimensional in the Shore of THE Creature, and Noah himself held Quantum and Dimensional that were part of his Stanchions which were now incorporated into his twenty-seven Seals of Absolute Tongue.","|Theoretical Assessment|","|While still a working theory, if it is deemed that The First Tongue or your Infinities is what makes you immune to the infection of THE Entity, you may potentially act as a cut-off point for the concepts of Quantum, Dimensional, Temporal, Spirit, Origin, and all others.|","|And if the leaders of these Civilizations are infected, the possibility of THE Entity spreading itself through the idea of that Civilization would be blocked off by you.|","|By The First Tongue since it permeates across Observable Existence.|","|Of course, this is still just a hypothetical and has not been confirmed.|","|Further observation and experimentation required.|","...!","Ruination proposed something unique that Noah thought about silently.","If he acted as a barrier preventing THE Entity from spreading through Civilizational concepts themselves...","That would make him one of the most important pieces on the board.","And also one of the biggest targets.","In the next moment...","\" Come.\"","The booming voice of THE Primordial Chaos echoed out as the surroundings cleared of chaos, and moments later...","THE Living Emotive burst into the clearing like a storm given human form!","Her entrance was manic and explosive, emotions cycling across her features faster than normal perception could track. Joy and rage and curiosity and hunger all competed for dominance as she twirled through the air with energy that seemed incapable of staying still. Her laughter echoed before her words formed, and her eyes darted everywhere at once as if searching for entertainment in the tension that filled this gathering.","THE Living Elemental followed with subdued steps that contrasted sharply with Emotive’s chaos.","His form was shrouded by Phonemes of Fire, Air, Earth, and Water that rotated around him in slow, deliberate patterns. His expression was guarded. His posture was defensive. He moved like someone who knew he was walking into a situation that could turn hostile at any moment.","And from the distance, Noah waved his hands as THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger also returned!","The two sides looked at each other with tension that crackled through the air of Alfheimr.","Emotive’s gaze landed on Origin first, her smile widening with recognition and mockery intertwined. She bounced on her feet as if preparing to say something cutting, her emotions cycling through delight at seeing her old acquaintance again after what...a few minutes?","Origin met that gaze with cold indifference.","Hunger stood beside her with crimson-obsidian flames that burned low and dangerous.","Elemental’s eyes found Noah’s illusory form, and something flickered there.","At such a moment, THE Primordial Chaos spoke with a voice that commanded absolute attention.","\" Hear me well, for I will not repeat myself.\"","His shifting features settled into something regal and terrible.","\"A threat has emerged that transcends the petty conflicts we have engaged in across the eons. A threat that does not discriminate between factions or allegiances. A threat that has already claimed multiple Absolutes and countless lesser beings without any of us perceiving its approach until it was far too late.\"","He paused to let his words settle.","\" This threat has been designated THE Entity by THE Youngest among THE Four, and it is a fitting name for something that defies conventional classification.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" THE Entity does not kill. It does not collapse. It replaces. It wears the faces of those it claims. It speaks with their voices. It utilizes their Civilizations and their Ways as if they were its own. Because after infection, they are its own.\"","He gestured broadly.","\" Jotunheim is compromised. My domain, my home, my followers, half of everything I built across eons has been claimed by THE Entity without me even perceiving the assault until it was too late to salvage what was lost.\"","...!"]},{"number":4828,"title":"Chapter 4828: Chapter 4827: They Have Fallen! II","paragraphs":["Chaos’ eyes blazed with coldness.","\" THE Secretive Eon has fallen. THE Living Quantum has fallen. THE Living Dimensional has fallen. THE Living Temporal has fled across time itself, partially infected and possibly beyond salvation.\"","He looked at each of them in turn.","\" None of you stand a chance of resisting this infection if it reaches you. I do not say this to diminish your power or your pride. I say this because it is truth. I am THE Primordial Chaos, and I could barely sense and resist. I could only flee. If THE Entity claims you, there will be no fighting back. There will be no last stand. There will simply be darkness, and then something else will wear your face while you cease to exist entirely.\"","His voice dropped to something almost gentle.","\" You will steer clear of those infected. You will remain in Alfheimr for now, where THE Creature’s Weavings provide some measure of protection. You will not attempt heroics. You will not attempt reconnaissance. You will survive, because the dead, or in this case the replaced, cannot contribute to finding a solution.\"","...!","The reactions to Chaos’s words were immediate.","Emotive, who had been bouncing with manic energy moments before, turned silent and contemplative. Her emotions stopped cycling. Her smile faded. She stood perfectly still for perhaps the first time since Noah had seen her, processing the implications of what she had just heard with a seriousness that seemed almost foreign on her features.","Elemental became somber, his Phonemes slowing their rotation as the blood drained from whatever passed for his face. The weight of the threat seemed to press against his foundations with force that made him visibly smaller.","Origin and Hunger looked somber, exchanging glances that spoke of silent communication.","Noah looked at all of these changes with calculating eyes.","Fear was a powerful motivator, even though Absolutes...should not have any sense of fear!","And THE Primordial Chaos had just motivated everyone present to take this threat seriously.","He observed all of this.","But he couldn’t help but turn his gaze to Elemental.","\" There is immense danger for everyone.\"","Noah’s voice cut through the heavy silence with authority that demanded attention.","\" But man, the fucker I want to kill is right in front of me.\"","His illusory eyes locked onto Elemental with intensity that burned.","\" You sent me a curse not too long ago, Elemental. You remember that?\"","He tilted his head.","\"It may not be the time or place, but in the grand scheme of things, you still have to die.\"","He turned toward THE Primordial Chaos.","\" Say, O Primordial Chaos. Do you care if Elemental here goes to an early grave?\"","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s words broke off the somber atmosphere as he looked at Chaos!","And he saw Chaos wave his hands nonchalantly as if he couldn’t care less about the fate of THE Living Elemental.","\"I don’t give a damn who collapses who, just ensuring the infection isn’t spreading or having others here be carriers.\"","His shifting features formed something that looked almost like consideration.","\" Actually, the less the better.\"","He nodded to himself.","\"If more Absolutes died, that means fewer Absolutes to join the army of THE Entity.\"","His smile became something cold and calculating.","\" Ho, this is actually a decent idea?\"","BOOM!","The words of Chaos echoed out in the surroundings as the gazes of Emotive and Elemental flickered with calculations!","Noah looked at all these changes as Elemental looked back at him.","THE Living Elemental stood with the bearing of someone who had existed as an Absolute since long ago, his burly humanoid figure radiating authority that pressed against everything nearby.","And Noah smiled as he looked at this. This guy was using his Tongue, and thinks he can look at him with such a light of defiance?","As if they were having a staredown and Elemental did not want to lose as an Absolute, he spoke with a voice that held the weight of someone defending their pride. \" You encroached upon my Civilization. Was I just supposed to sit there and take it? If I came upon you and your people, and I chose one of them and simply took them, would you sit still? As for your threats, they are merely baseless words with no backing. You are not even an Absolute. If not a trick like THE Weavers, you can’t do anything. Will you release your little heart and tell me to grab it if I can? Fuck off.\"","...!","BOOM!","Elemental’s existence pulsed with a fiery light as he defended himself for the first time in a while! One must not forget who Elemental was as his power was actually grand.","He had existed as an Absolute for many years, built foundations that let him stand among...well, only some of the most powerful beings in Observable Existence, and survived conflicts and schemes that had collapsed others.","But the moment these words echoed out, the skies of Alfheimr flickered! While the pillar of light representing the death of THE Weavers was fading into memory, a radiant new pillar of light representing the birth of another Absolute bloomed with obsidian-gold brilliance, and it even looked a little hairy .","The rise of a new Absolute was seen here under the gazes of others as they were astonished, with even Chaos having a look of thought before he disappeared.","THE Fallout made it hard for anyone to grasp Absolute as a consequence, and the corruption spreading across Observable Existence created barriers that should have prevented new Absolutes from emerging. So how did this one rise?","Noah smiled lightly as he looked at Elemental. He didn’t have the power of an Absolute? He had a backer of his Way, his Teacher, who just attained Absolute even with the curses of THE Fallout! The curse should make it impossible for any Absolutes to rise, but many things were impossible for others, but not for Absolutes.","And THE Big Stepper had something only Absolutes held access to when he took that step, an Absolute Everything, a currency that transcended the limitations THE Fallout had imposed.","As Noah smiled, Emotive was looking at him deeply with eyes that cycled through curiosity and calculation. \" You don’t look the least bit surprised. Osmont, I’ve wanted to meet you dearly, but I have to ask now. You know the Absolute that has just risen? Are they under you? Is that why you torture my little Elemental with words? Because he says you don’t even have power of an Absolute, and bam, there rises an Absolute?\"","...!"]},{"number":4829,"title":"Chapter 4829: Chapter 4828: You Were Saying Something?","paragraphs":["Noah turned to look at this manic woman with coldness as he showed her complete apathy. \" You are another that also needs to die. Do you remember Malphas? A butler of yours that you stepped on whenever you had the chance.\"","Malphas!","Emotive heard these words as she blinked before her eyes opened wide with surprise. \" The emotions of all others have been drained and lost from that time. The Weavings of my little butler are still alive and well under you? Haha! You threaten me with death for a mere thing like that? Come on, big guy! I was excited to meet you! One of THE Four! Why are you talking about boring piss shit like a past servant? I thought you more complex than this. Let’s talk big! Focus on things that matter on the scales of Existence, not lesser things with no meaning!\"","Her voice rose with intensity as she continued. \" We now stand at the precipice of a great enemy where you and Chaos here may just be on the same side, something that has never happened, and you bring up such lame shit? Come on, man! Be like THE Creature. Be like THE Primordial Chaos. Be like THE Living Paradox. You are big. Others are below you. Such matters like the feelings of servants are below you. Anybody that isn’t even an Absolute, why bother with them?\"","Her gaze shifted to Origin and Hunger behind Noah. \" Even the two behind you. The loser First Hunger who stands beside Origin like a dog, not knowing her heart and Everythings have been taken by THE Creature. And Origin herself. Used and tossed aside by THE Creature like nothing. Look at her now? Nothing to show for it. I fucking gained more from THE Creature than her! Man, all of this just fucking infuriates me! It was supposed to be different!\"","BOOM!","Her speech had been long as toward the end of it, she was almost rambling her last words with manic anger! Noah looked at her with unfathomably immense coldness and Immensity as behind him, Origin and Hunger did the same.","Emotive heaved and breathed out after her long-winded speech as she laughed and looked at Noah with eyes that still blazed with chaotic energy.","\" What? Cat got your tongue?\"","She had gone off with her manic emotions as Noah felt the Weavings of Emotive permeating all around, trying to evoke emotions around all of them. She fed from it. She grew stronger due to it. He would not feed into it at all as he kept his reply short.","\" In Existence, there are many misguided little things who think themselves better than others. I’ve collapsed many. You and Elemental will simply be added to the list. Hold your Weavings close, for soon, what remains of them will be included inside Absolute Existential Palaces.\"","BOOM!","He didn’t speak with manic emotions, nor did he attack their character or Weavings. He simply stated something that felt absolute, and even Emotive was not able to reply as her face pulsed with manic emotions that couldn’t find purchase against his complete indifference!","Between all of them, Chaos looked like he was watching the bickering of children as he began to rise at this moment.","\" My words have been clear, and I shall not repeat them. If any of you leave Alfheimr and I do not have track of you, I would rather kill you on sight than wonder if you are infected. The fewer Absolutes that exist to potentially join THE Entity’s army, the better for all of Observable Existence. Youngest, you can reach me at any time through Chaos and Disorder. I will see if I can get in touch with the other Four and potentially act to wipe out THE Secretive Eon and all remnants of THE Entity in one decisive swoop. The rest of you would do well to not fuck things up, or I will kill.\"","BOOM!","After these words, Chaos disappeared, leaving Emotive and Elemental staring at Noah’s illusory manifestation, THE Living Origin, and THE First Hunger!","Noah looked coldly at Emotive and Elemental as Emotive harrumphed while she looked at him with eyes that still blazed with chaotic energy.","\" What? Without the buffer of Chaos, even if I do not target you, if I wanted to fuck up Origin there or that lower Hunger, what can you do? Not even Absolutes. A press of my thumb would be enough.\"","...!","She continued to poke and poke to elicit a reaction, but Noah never expected or wanted to use Chaos as a shield. He had himself, whose foundational weight was something other entities could not even imagine. And having seen how the situation was unfolding the past few seconds, he had already made another move.","At this moment, between them and Emotive...","HUUM!","The aura of a heavy, dense, and deep Absolute erupted! A hairy obsidian-gold leg descended from above, coming down with weight that made the crystalline forests of Alfheimr tremble as it covered the skies of this portion of the Primordial Realm with authority that spoke of foundations built across eons of dedication to The First Tongue. The leg was massive, covered in countless strands of obsidian-gold hair that pulsed with their own life, and it brought down a glorious visage that made even Emotive’s manic energy falter!","THE Big Stepper!","Ul’moreth descended with the majesty of a newly risen Absolute who had taken the most important step of his existence just moments before. His form was even more hairy than it had been, a mountain of obsidian-gold strands that hid whatever was beneath with density that defied normal perception.","Golden Scissors gleamed in one hairy hand. THE Axiom of Absolute Denial pulsed in the other. And somewhere within that mass of hair, eyes that burned with obsidian-gold authority looked toward Emotive and Elemental with coldness that matched his student’s.","Noah remained right where he was as he looked at Emotive with an expression that held quiet tyranny. \" You were saying something?\"","...!","The silence that followed was deafening. Emotive’s manic energy stuttered and stopped. Elemental’s Phonemes slowed their rotation.","And THE Big Stepper stood between Noah’s people and those who would threaten them, his Absolute Depth pressing against everything present with weight that made it clear exactly what the consequences of hostile action would be.","No student should have to bear the weight of Existence alone.","It was said!"]},{"number":4830,"title":"Chapter 4830: Chapter 4829: Who Said?!","paragraphs":["A heavy air radiated across the crystalline forests of Alfheimr as even THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger looked toward THE Big Stepper in astonishment.","Ul’moreth.","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform who had dedicated eons to mastering The First Tongue had finally taken that impossible step. His form was mountainous, covered in countless strands of obsidian-gold hair that pulsed with their own life and authority.","Far above, the gaze of THE Primordial Chaos seemed to return just briefly, those shifting features settling into something that might have been curiosity as he evaluated this new entrant to the ranks of Absolutes.","His assessment lasted only a moment before his attention moved away.","Noah looked at the cold figures of THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive as he evaluated them with calculating eyes.","Frankly, he knew that right now, against both of them and just him and Ul’moreth alone, it would not be a battle that could be won.","If Ul’moreth targeted Elemental alone, that fucker stood a good chance of being collapsed. The ancient Ginnu Lifeform’s foundations were built across eons of dedicated study, and Elemental’s power, while Absolute, did not seem to match that depth of accumulated understanding.","But Emotive was a different matter entirely.","As manic and as horrendous as she was, her power as an Absolute felt much grander than Elemental’s. The emotions cycling through her features held weight that pressed against reality itself, and Noah could sense that whatever Civilization she had built, it was not something to be taken lightly. She was decent in ways that Elemental simply was not.","So while a battle now would lead to nothing productive, while engaging them directly would be foolish when THE Entity threatened all of Observable Existence, he could still teach a lesson.","Some lessons needed to be delivered regardless of circumstance.","\" You will be collapsed in due time.\"","Noah’s voice carried across the crystalline clearing with authority that made the very air tremble.","\" But for now, I want you to understand something.\"","His illusory eyes locked onto THE Living Elemental with intensity that burned.","\"I want you to understand that the vast majority of power you have is not yours.\"","He paused, letting those words settle.","\" Because who told you that you could use MY First Tongue?\"","HUUM!","The words landed like hammers forged from concentrated authority.","And then something extraordinary happened.","The Phonemes of Fire, Air, Water, and Earth that had been rotating around THE Living Elemental in slow, deliberate patterns began to flicker. The brilliant displays that had surrounded his form stuttered and dimmed, the four fundamental concepts that defined his very existence responding to an authority that superseded their connection to him.","Fire guttered like a candle in a hurricane.","Air stilled as if it had forgotten how to move.","Water froze mid-flow, suspended in patterns that defied its nature.","Earth trembled and cracked, its solidarity questioned by something deeper than its own foundations.","The Phonemes didn’t disappear entirely, but they flickered in and out of stability as if they were being turned off and on by an unseen hand. THE Living Elemental’s expression shifted from cold composure to something that looked almost like shock as the fundamental building blocks of his Civilization, the very concepts that had defined him since The Earliest Folds, began to question their allegiance.","This was not an attack.","This was a reminder.","A reminder of who held true authority over the linguistic foundation of reality itself.","THE Living Emotive sensed the shift in Elemental’s power, and her cycling emotions stuttered to a stop as genuine astonishment crossed her features. She looked at Elemental, then at Noah, then back at Elemental again as understanding dawned.","And then she smiled.","It was a devilish expression, wide and manic and filled with something that looked almost like delight.","\" Right! Right!\"","Her laughter echoed across the crystalline clearing with energy that made nearby trees vibrate.","\" You still are one of THE Four!\"","She bounced on her feet, emotions cycling through excitement and hunger and something darker that lurked beneath the surface.","\" Haha, this was part of what I was looking forward to meeting you. Say, do you want to talk in private? Show me a bit more things relating to THE Four?\"","Her voice dropped to something almost intimate.","\" They always fascinate me so much.\"","...!","But as she finished those last words, her entire demeanor shifted. The manic energy remained, but beneath it emerged a sense of coldness and sombreness that seemed utterly at odds with her previous behavior.","Her entire figure became surrounded by manic light that pulsed with colors that shouldn’t exist together, emotions made manifest in ways that pressed against the sanity of any who observed too closely.","At this moment, the figure of Ul’moreth turned toward Noah as his existence burned with waves of Absolute authority that made the crystalline forests around them tremble. His countless hairs stood on end, each strand pulsing with obsidian-gold light that spoke of power newly claimed but already deeply rooted.","\" Little Anomaly.\"","His voice carried the weight of ages, of dedication, of a being who had spent eons pursuing mastery and had finally achieved what he sought.","\"I have seen a lot of crazy in my existence. This particular type of crazy is one that simply needs to be eradicated.\"","The words were not spoken with heat or anger.","They were spoken with the cold certainty of someone who had evaluated a threat and determined the only appropriate response.","Noah looked at Emotive while listening to the words of Ul’moreth. His illusory eyes met her manic gaze without flinching, without showing any of the calculation that was occurring behind them.","Then, without turning around, he addressed THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger who stood behind him with expressions that mixed concern with readiness.","\" You two go and do what you came here to do.\"","Origin and Hunger exchanged a glance.","They began to move, to turn away from the confrontation and toward their objective that had brought them to Alfheimr in the first place.","\" And the two of you.\"","Noah’s last words were directed toward THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive.","Elemental was still fuming, his expression a mask of barely contained fury as he continued to try and express his Absolute authority to pull the Phonemes he had always been so familiar with. Fire, Air, Water, and Earth still flickered around him, responding to his commands only intermittently, their connection to him disrupted by an authority that superseded his claim.","Emotive watched with that manic smile still plastered across her features, her emotions cycling through amusement and interest and something darker that lurked beneath the surface.","\" You two can get the fuck off.\"","The words were delivered with casual contempt.","\" When I am ready to start butchering, I will come for you.\"","WAA!","Even though only an illusory visage stood here, even though his main body was across Observable Existence dealing with matters far removed from this confrontation, Noah was grand and imposing as he delivered this dismissal.","He had shockingly denied access to The First Tongue to two Absolutes!","To this hour, his Thesis had not been refuted. The proposition he had laid down in Muspelheim, the claim that only those to whom he granted permission could draw power from The First Tongue, remained unchallenged. It had actualized into local truth, and now he was applying that same principle on a broader scale.","With his tremendous weight, with the foundation that many could not match, he could afford to do this even against Absolutes!"]},{"number":4831,"title":"Chapter 4831: Chapter 4830: Integrations and Memories I","paragraphs":["The area became filled with Immensity and tension as two sides looked at each other.","Power pressed down over everything in the realm of Alfheimr, the crystalline trees bending under the weight of concentrated authority, the rivers of liquid radiance slowing their flow as if even they recognized the significance of this moment.","Elemental’s fury was palpable, a heat that made the air around him shimmer.","Emotive’s smile never wavered, but her eyes held something calculating beneath the manic surface.","And Noah stood between them and his people, an illusory presence that somehow carried more weight than the physical reality around it.","The confrontation hung suspended in time.","Two sides measuring each other.","Two powers determining whether this moment would escalate into something worse.","And then, slowly, with the reluctance of beings who understood now was not the time, THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive began to withdraw.","Not because they feared the fight.","Not because they feared!","While such a confrontation unfolded in Alfheimr, while illusory Noah faced down Absolutes with nothing but authority and accumulated weight, another body moved across entirely different territory.","—","Far from the crystalline forests.","Across The Wastes of THE Fallout.","Noah’s physical body floated through corrupted space alongside Ains and a happy Skoll who bounded through the twisted reality as if it were nothing more than an interesting playground.","The Wastes stretched out around them in all directions, a landscape of collapsed concepts and shattered foundations. Where other regions of Observable Existence held some form of structure, some remnant of what they had been before THE Fallout, this place was pure devastation given form.","Reality twisted in on itself.","Concepts that had no business existing together merged and separated in patterns that defied comprehension.","The very fabric of Existence had been torn apart here, and what remained was something that should not have been able to exist at all.","And yet life persisted.","Of a sort.","Noah navigated through the corrupted Weavings with the ease. His connection to Undifferentiated Fate guided his path, threads of possibility weaving through the chaos to show him where he needed to go.","They arrived near a region of the Wastes that held nothing but twisting corrupted existence.","No landmarks.","No structures.","Nothing that could be used as a reference point.","Just endless corruption folding back on itself in patterns that would have driven lesser minds to madness.","And yet Noah knew this was the place.","He called out calmly, his voice moving across the corrupted space with authority that cut through the ambient chaos.","\" Big guy, how did you let something else emerge that does what you do, but countless times deadlier?\"","...!","The words hung in the twisted air, a question directed at something that should not have been able to hear them.","They had arrived where the Weavings of Undifferentiated Fate told him Eckert was.","THE Great Usurper!","With Undifferentiated Fate, Noah was able to gain information he had no business knowing, especially if he had a few pieces of information already as Eckert gave him.","So he knew thst currently, Eckert had merged with a Fragment of THE Axiom of Primordial Paradox and become something that existed outside normal classification. The being who had learned to spread his existence through idle contact, to take over the Weavings of others without them even realizing what was happening.","To understand THE Entity a bit better, to find some pathway that might lead to a potential solution against a threat that had claimed multiple Absolutes, one of the approaches Noah had identified was consulting with an entity he knew who could do what THE Entity did.","But at a much smaller scale.","The mechanisms were different, the scale was incomparable, but the fundamental principle of replacing what was there with something else held common ground.","If anyone in Observable Existence might have insight into how such a process worked, how it might be countered, how one might protect against an infection that could claim even Absolutes without them realizing until it was too late, it would be THE Great Usurper.","The corrupted space around them stirred.","Something was responding to Noah’s call.","Something that had been idle, spreading slowly through The Wastes!","Skoll’s ears perked up, his form tensing as he sensed something approaching that registered as neither friend nor foe, but something else entirely.","In front of him, Noah perceived existence silently converging and forming into a humanoid visage.","The corrupted space of The Wastes twisted and folded, reality reshaping itself to accommodate something that existed in ways that defied normal perception. Particles of scattered existence drew together like iron filings responding to a magnet, coalescing into a shape that grew more defined with each passing moment.","Eckert.","THE Great Usurper.","When one thought of such a title, they might imagine an ancient being weathered by eons of existence. Something gnarled and powerful, holding the weight of countless devoured lives in every aspect of its form.","But what materialized in front of Noah was the image of a young man in his twenties.","The visage was colorless, an illusory humanoid shape with no pigmentation beyond shades of gray and white. His features were handsome in a casual way, relaxed and unburdened. His smile was easy, genuine, the expression of someone greeting an old friend rather than one of the most dangerous beings in Observable Existence.","It was deceptive.","Because Noah knew this being had devoured the existences and memories of countless others. Every smile, every casual gesture, every aspect of that youthful appearance was built upon the consumed foundations of beings who no longer existed.","The young man’s form stabilized completely, his colorless eyes finding Noah’s with recognition and something like relief.","And then he did something unexpected.","Eckert moved forward with easy confidence, his hand coming up in a gesture of familiarity rather than the formal greetings.","He...dapped Noah up!","Noah raised his brows but went along with it. His hand met Eckert’s in a clasp!","\"Man.\"","Eckert’s voice came out with exhaustion.","\"I’ve been going nuts trying to figure out the extent of change across Observable Existence.\"","He shook his head.","\"What’s this about someone doing what I can do at a crazy scale?\"","...!"]},{"number":4832,"title":"Chapter 4832: Chapter 4831: Integrations and Memories II","paragraphs":["The question hung in the corrupted air between them.","It was time to catch up and learn more about Eckert and what he could do, to understand the mechanisms of his unique methodology, and to compare it to THE Entity to see how one might go against a threat that had already claimed multiple Absolutes.","Because if anyone understood the process of replacing what was there with something else, of spreading through existence itself to consume and become, it would be THE Great Usurper!","And right now, understanding was the most valuable weapon Noah could acquire.","---","While all of this occurred across The Wastes, a part of him continued to pay attention to the major changes unfolding within THE Infiniverse.","His Civilization was growing exponentially.","The connection between himself and THE Infiniverse meant that every advancement he achieved fed directly into the realm that served as the heart of everything he’d built. And now, as it assimilated an entire Primordial Realm into itself, that growth was accelerating beyond anything he’d previously experienced.","At this moment.","In the sandy Early Veiled Shore at the center of THE Infiniverse, Noah had another body moving alongside his mother as the two of them harvested sacred herbs he’d brought over from the Shore of THE Creature.","The herbs glowed with soft luminescence, each one a treasure that would’ve caused wars among lesser beings. Yet here they grew in abundance, nurtured by conditions that existed nowhere else in Observable Existence.","His mother moved with practiced ease, her presence a grounding force that reminded Noah of who he’d been before all of this.","Existence was wild and ridiculous, but he could always make time to spend it with the important people in his life.","Many others moved all over the Early Veiled Shore. In the distance, he could see his son Henry surrounded by two women as he cooked marine lifeforms in a Wok filled with sacred water. Steam rose in patterns that spoke of culinary mastery applied to ingredients that transcended normal food.","Off to the side, the bald figure of Bob watched like a hawk. Little Bobby!","His attention was fixed on his daughter Liora, who was laughing beside Henry with easy joy. Bob’s protective gaze never wavered, the concern of a father who’d been through too much to ever truly relax.","After all, this man had burned entire Wheels of Existence for his daughter! Not to mention Thauron. He missed that guy!","Barbatos, Adelaide, Athena, and all the other Queens of THE Infiniverse moved about with their own busyness and tasks.","None of them knew whatever grand enemy now stood above them. None of them knew about THE Entity, about the infection that had claimed multiple Absolutes.","And they didn’t have to worry about this.","Because Noah would shoulder everything to protect those under his Civilization.","Even further in the distance, he could see the Sanctuaries of Inevitabilities. Tens of millions of Primus Inevitabilities moved around like an army, each one a being of tremendous potential being cultivated under his authority.","The day when he could turn these millions into Surface Depth entities, have an army at the first Scale of Existence, all specialized into unique professions...","That was the day when it would be game over for many.","But as of now, it was still a distant future away.","At this time, Noah began to feel the golden sands trembling beneath his feet.","A hint of red permeated the air above, mixing with streams of blue. The influence of Muspelheim being devoured was becoming extremely strong, its essence bleeding into THE Infiniverse as the integration progressed toward completion.","Prompts bloomed.","|Integration Milestone Achieved|","| More than half of Muspelheim has been integrated into THE Infiniverse|","|Unique Musings of Existence have been discovered|","|I spent an embarrassing amount of processing power analyzing why Muspelheim produced so many THE classification entities when other realms struggled to produce a few|","|The answer, it turns out, was not some grand mystery|","...!","Unique Musings of Existence.","Noah stopped where he was on the plot of farmland. He closed his eyes and allowed the Immensity of THE Weaver of Existence to spread outward.","The First Tongue erupted from him in a low hum. The Derivative Civilizations of Hunger and Undifferentiated Fate stirred within his foundations, ready to consume and process whatever information emerged.","| Primordial Realm Analysis|","|Muspelheim functioned as a pivotal convergence of immense Weavings of The First Tongue, similar to Ginnungagap|","|Over the eons, countless Corrupted Growths were drawn toward this Primordial Realm like it was some kind of drain|","|These corrupted elements were cleansed, and the pure Civilizational Authority that resulted simply... accumulated|","|This explains why so many Muspeli Lifeforms achieved THE classification|","|They were being fed concentrated purity while everyone else had to earn advancement the hard way|","| Fragment Discovery|","|Multiple Fragments of Axioms have been sensed and obtained|","|Currently being catalogued|","| Infiniverse Transformation|","|As integration proceeds, THE Infiniverse is transforming to become a unique component of Observable Existence|","| Corrupted Growths will begin to naturally be drawn toward THE Infiniverse|","|With these Growths being cleansed automatically, all the pure Civilizational Authority that blooms will feed back into your home|","|This creates a feedback loop of glorious proportions|","|Most beings spend eons trying to establish something like this|","|You stumbled into it while eating a Primordial Realm|","| Collaborative Analysis|","|THE Infiniverse and I are designing similar Musings of Existence to THE Agora of Primordial Judgment and THE Vaults of Ginnungagap|","|Purpose: To better understand the positions of Primordial Realms in relation to Observable Existence|","|This is genuinely complex work|","| Population Influx|","|Muspeli Lifeforms are beginning to be drawn into THE Infiniverse|","|A not-so-insignificant number are at the first Scale of Existence|","|This increases the infinite potential of the Harvest you draw for all those under your Civilization|","|All of this continues feeding your growing Foundation|","| Foundation Status|","|THE Surface Depth: Approaching theoretical perfection|","|THE Intermediate Depth: Approaching theoretical perfection|","|THE Fundamental Depth: Slowly, slowly, slowly creeping toward what THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos achieved in the distant past|","|Slowly, even though measuring your progress against beings who had eons feels unreasonable|","|You’ve had hours as this really isn’t slow. Even if it was days, it would still be considered an impossibility.|","...!","Can you imagine it? If his progression actually took him days or weeks to go from Surface to Intermediate Depth?","Or if he needed years to attain Fundamental Depth or Absolute? Because normally, others took thousands and millions of years!","He shivered just thinking of such a possibility!"]},{"number":4833,"title":"Chapter 4833: Chapter 4832: Integrations and Memories III","paragraphs":["Noah read through the prompts with his eyes closed.","And he saw it.","Murky Corrupted Growths converging toward THE Infiniverse as if drawn by forces beyond their understanding. They painted over the barrier outside like a disease seeking entry.","But as soon as they touched those boundaries, a silent glow of heavy Depth emerged.","The Corrupted Growths were rapidly dissipated, dissolved like shadows before dawn. What had been twisted and wrong became clean and pure, transformed into golden light that flowed into his home.","Was this why THE Vaults of Ginnungagap were so grand? Why THE Agora of Primordial Judgment held so many THE classification entities and four Absolutes?","They’d been cleansing Corrupted Growths for eons, accumulating the pure Civilizational Authority that resulted. They’d become stronger through the natural process of serving as nodes that attracted and purified corruption.","And now THE Infiniverse was beginning to do the same.","His home was becoming a Primordial Realm in truth, not just in name.","More prompts bloomed.","| Absolute Everything Generation|","|Progress toward next Absolute Everything: 10%|","|In conjunction with your personal cleansing and what THE Infiniverse now does automatically, another Absolute Everything will be ready soon? Soon|","|Potential applications:|","|- Take another Half-Step Absolute toward Absolute|","|- Assuming they’re all as grand as THE Big Stepper, which is admittedly a high bar|","|- Other purposes as you determine|","...!","Many things were coming up as possibilities.","His progression proceeded steadily, foundations being reinforced with every passing moment, every cleansed Corrupted Growth, every piece of harvested authority flowing into his Civilization.","And there was still so much more to do.","In addition to pursuing information about THE Entity through Eckert, he now knew the locations of The Shelters of THE Loom from obtaining Undifferentiated Fate. The places where THE Living Paradox’s forces gathered. The strongholds that had seemed unreachable before.","He wanted to pay a visit to them.","And alongside that, there were the memories of THE Weavers themselves. He’d sent another part of his consciousness toward their Absolute Existential Palace to sift through what remained of their accumulated understanding.","If he had more information, more knowledge, he could move through Existence even grander than before. After all, knowing the right things was everything.","He even had his own personal growth to consider. The continued nurturing of the 27 Absolute Seals. The Archai he’d formed...Perpetual Harvest, Cheating Architect, Undifferentiated Mana...each holding new avenues to express his power as he neared Absolute.","There was much to be done.","So much to be done!","—","In Observable Existence, there is a creature called THE Mnemonic Leviathan.","It dwells in the spaces between Primordial Realms, its body composed entirely of accumulated information. Every secret whispered across eons, every truth discovered and forgotten, every piece of knowledge that ever existed flows through its endless form. It knows everything.","And... it has never done anything.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan drifts through Existence, bloated with understanding it cannot apply, suffocating under the weight of wisdom it cannot wield. It knows how Absolutes fall. It knows how Civilizations rise. It knows...the weaknesses of Absolutes that others dont know.","It knows, and it watches, and it does nothing at all.","Those who have witnessed eons say that knowledge alone is the most useless currency in Observable Existence. They have seen beings accumulate libraries of understanding only to be collapsed by someone who knew a single truth and acted upon it without hesitation. They have watched empires built not by the most informed, but by those who treated every scrap of knowledge as a weapon demanding immediate use.","Because in the end, knowledge hoarded is knowledge wasted.","But knowledge applied is transformation itself.","The gap between knowing and doing is where most beings live their entire existences, comfortable in their accumulation, paralyzed by their wisdom, convinced that understanding is the same as power.","It is not.","Power belongs to those who learn one truth and move before the lesson has finished settling in their minds.","Knowledge was everything, so Noah proceeded to go and seek it.","There was knowledge to be gained in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment and whatever secrets it might hold that made THE Secretive Eon refuse to enter. There were answers waiting to be found, protections waiting to be understood, weapons waiting to be claimed.","And then there was the Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers.","His consciousness was already walking through its halls once more, moving through corridors that seemed to shift and breathe with the remnants of three minds that had once shared a single existence. The architecture was strange here, walls that curved in ways that suggested different perspectives overlapping, doorways that appeared different depending on which angle you approached them from.","He entered a region filled with multiple golden doors.","Dozens of them. Hundreds. Each one sealed with locks and chains that pulsed with residual authority, the final protections of beings who had accumulated secrets across eons of service to powers that shaped Observable Existence itself.","Doorways to memories of THE Weavers.","To access any of them, one would have to expend a tremendous amount of power and Depth. Even in death, THE Weavers wanted to be tricky fuckers.","They had woven protections into their own memories, ensuring that anyone who sought their knowledge would pay dearly for every scrap of understanding they obtained.","Noah walked across the hall filled with golden doors as he utilized Undifferentiated Fate to lead him forward toward the best possible result he could find at this moment.","The Derivative Civilization stirred within his foundations, its authority spreading outward like ink dropped into water.","Tendrils of golden-blue light swirled around him, emerging from his existence like extensions of his will made manifest. They moved with purpose that transcended conscious direction, reaching out like hands toward each of the doors around him. They pressed against locks, brushed against chains, tested seals that had held for eons.","Checking.","Affirming.","Reading the threads of fate and destiny that connected each door to potential futures.","Some tendrils recoiled from doors that held nothing of value. Others lingered on doors that contained useful but not critical information. A few pressed harder against doors that held secrets worth the cost of opening.","But eventually, many of them gathered on one inconspicuous golden door.","It wasn’t the largest door. It wasn’t the most ornately decorated. It sat between two grander entrances as if trying not to be noticed, its chains slightly less imposing than those on its neighbors.","The tendrils of Undifferentiated Fate wrapped around it with certainty that brooked no doubt.","This one.","Noah nodded and floated toward it.","He put his hand on the locks and chains surrounding the door, feeling the weight of protections that THE Weavers had laid down across countless years. They pushed back against him, testing his authority, questioning whether he had the right to access what lay within.","In the next moment, he leaned forward.","He pressed the ridiculous Immensity of the weight of his entire existence into these chains.","The foundation that approached what THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos had built across eons. The 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue burning with concentrated authority. The Claim on The First Tongue itself, the linguistic foundation of reality pressing against protections that had never been designed to withstand such weight.","CRACK!","The chains cracked and fell down, clattering against the floor of the hallway with sounds that echoed through the empty palace.","The golden door began to open in front of him.","Noah stepped through.","Existence began to turn hazy all around him, reality losing its definition as memory replaced perception. The hallway faded. The palace faded. Everything that was now faded into everything that had been then.","And he blinked.","...!","Shockingly, he found his consciousness split into three.","He was looking through the eyes of three people simultaneously, three perspectives that somehow merged into a single experience. It was disorienting , his sense of self fragmenting across multiple viewpoints that moved and thought and felt as one.","In this memory, it was like Noah was living through the eyes of THE Weavers themselves!"]},{"number":4834,"title":"Chapter 4834: Chapter 4833: Integrations and Memories IV","paragraphs":["He raised his hands to see the fair hands of three women, slender fingers that had woven the fates of countless beings across eons of existence. All of them wore obsidian-gold robes that flowed like liquid night, waves of golden hair cascading past their shoulders in styles that were similar but not identical.","Three bodies.","One memory that he was now experiencing from the inside.","The region around them slowly came into focus.","They stood on the stair steps of a massive obsidian temple, a structure so vast that its upper reaches disappeared into darkness that seemed to exist beyond normal space. The stairs were wide enough for armies to march upon, each step carved from stone that held the weight of ages.","Pillars of twisted obsidian rose on either side, their surfaces inscribed with symbols that hurt to look at directly.","And at the very center of this temple, at the apex of those endless stairs, a single aura waited.","THE Weavers walked toward this entity.","With each step, Noah felt the veneration that pulsed through their shared existence. The respect. The devotion. The absolute certainty that they approached something heavy.","The entity came into Noah’s vision.","And he felt like he was looking at the eye of a paradoxical storm.","Because he was.","This was...THE Primordial Paradox.","Yes, the memory was clearly telling him that this was THE Primordial Paradox. Not THE Living Paradox . The original holder of that Claim, the being who had stood among THE Four since before The Infinite Unfurling.","THE Primordial Paradox looked like a massive obsidian entity, his form towering above THE Weavers with presence that made reality itself seem uncertain. He was muscular in ways that spoke of power beyond physical strength, yet he also carried the bearing of a scholar.","His eyes held the weight of contradictions resolved and unresolved, of truths that could be simultaneously real and unreal.","He was everything THE Living Paradox pretended to be.","And he was something more.","In the memory, THE Weavers felt a sense of veneration as they bowed toward this being. Their three bodies moved in perfect synchrony, heads lowering, golden hair falling forward like curtains of loyalty.","THE Primordial Paradox waved his hands dismissively.","The gesture was casual, almost paternal. The wave of a master who had long since ceased to require formal acknowledgment from those who served him.","In the next moment, the aura of something heavy and Absolute emanated from him.","THE Primordial Paradox produced a black cube that floated toward their master, its surface perfectly smooth, its edges perfectly defined. It held weight that seemed to press against the fabric of memory itself.","Absolute!","THE Primordial Paradox was already an Absolute. His authority saturated everything around him, his Claim on Paradox itself woven into the very structure of Observable Existence.","So how did THE Living Paradox ever manage to consume both this entity and the Claim they laid on one of the oldest aspects of Existence?","The question burned through Noah’s consciousness even as the memory continued to unfold.","THE Primordial Paradox spoke, and his voice was grand and imposing and authoritative!","\" My daughters.\"","The words settled over THE Weavers like a blessing.","\" Something has anchored itself onto my Absolute authority and Claim. It is slowly eating away at me, and I cannot stop it for now.\"","...!","Noah felt the shock that rippled through THE Weavers at these words. Their master, admitting vulnerability.","\" This is a critical part of me that is unaffected, which I am giving to you.\"","The black cube floated toward THE Weavers, and they received it with hands that trembled slightly despite their best efforts at composure.","\" Take it and keep it safe. You will know when to open it in the future.\"","THE Primordial Paradox paused, his contradictory eyes growing distant.","\" The enemy is a terrifying one. I have to approach them differently compared to all others. I wish I could go to THE Creature and get his help on this, as he was always more knowledgeable than I am. But I must contain this myself at this moment.\"","His gaze refocused on THE Weavers.","\" You will take this part, and you will-\"","The sound of steps echoed through the temple.","Someone else was entering.","THE Weavers turned, and Noah turned with them, seeing through their eyes as another entity appeared at the entrance of the obsidian temple.","The newcomer moved with confidence that spoke of deep familiarity with this place. Their aura burned at THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, power that was immense but not yet Absolute.","And when Noah sensed them, when he truly perceived who had just arrived...","He knew instantly.","THE Living Paradox.","Before he became what he was now. Before he devoured his master. Before he took the Claim that had never been meant for him.","He was younger in this memory, his features less defined, his presence less overwhelming. But the core of who he would become was already visible in the way he carried himself, in the ambition that lurked behind eyes that had not yet learned to fully mask their hunger.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at THE Living Paradox with an expression that held no suspicion. Only trust. Only the fondness of a master for a disciple who had served faithfully across eons.","\"Erwin.\"","THE Living Paradox of course had a name. A real name. Not a title, not a classification, but a name that spoke of origins far humbler than his current status.","\"You have been with me since you were nothing but a peasant. I give you another part of me to keep safe and put away in the location that I have sent to your memories.\"","Another obsidian black cube floated toward THE Living Paradox, toward Erwin, who received it with solemnity that seemed genuine. His hands cradled the cube as if he would guard it with his life, his expression one of devoted loyalty that showed no hint of the betrayal that would eventually come.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at THE Weavers and THE Living Paradox with a gaze that held regret. Something he wished he could change but could not. Something he hoped would not come to pass but feared might.","\" Do not worry.\"","His voice remained grand and authoritative, but beneath it, Noah could hear the strain of someone fighting a battle on multiple fronts.","\" Your master will get past this. What I have given to you are just contingencies.\"","He straightened, his form seeming to grow even larger as he reasserted his dominance over the moment.","\" After I figure out what exactly has been invading my Weavings without me even knowing, I will extinguish it. I will show it how it cannot overcome that which is Paradoxical.\"","His eyes swept over his disciples one final time.","\" Now go. Fulfill my orders. Fulfill your duty.\"","BOOM!","The memory shattered.","Reality fractured like glass struck by a hammer, fragments of the past scattering into the void as Noah’s consciousness was violently expelled from the experience.","He found himself back in the hallway of the Absolute Existential Palace, his mind buzzing with knowledge and possibilities.","THE Primordial Paradox had been infected by something.","Something that anchored itself onto his authority without him knowing. Something that ate away at him slowly, that he couldn’t stop, that he had to approach differently than any other enemy.","It sounded pretty fucking similar to...THE Entity.","It had to be THE Entity, or something connected to it! An...older form of it?","The methodology was identical. The invisible invasion. The consumption from within. The replacement that occurred before the victim even realized they were under attack.","And THE Living Paradox...","Erwin!","He was the one to do this as he eventually ate THE Primordial Paradox!","But he wasn’t part of THE Entity at this moment as THE Entity wanted to consume him too, yes?","\"...\"","Also...","Where were those black cubes now?","THE Weavers had been given one. They were dead, their Palace now in Noah’s possession. Was it here somewhere? Was it still waiting to be opened at the right moment?","And the one given to Erwin...","Did THE Living Paradox still have it?","Or had he already used whatever power it contained?","Noah’s eyes blazed with blue-gold light as understanding and uncertainty warred within his foundations.","He had come seeking knowledge.","And knowledge, as always, had given him more questions than answers.","But now he knew something that perhaps no one else or very few in Observable Existence understood.","THE Entity...may not be entirely new!"]},{"number":4835,"title":"Chapter 4835: Chapter 4834: What Is Known And Unknown I","paragraphs":["Noah came across a curious finding as uniquely, there was some connection between the origin of THE Entity and THE Living Paradox.","Something that was always buzzing in the back of his mind was the question of how THE Living Paradox had managed to devour THE Primordial Paradox.","Whatever approach he used had to have something that connected to what Noah currently knew as THE Entity.","But uniquely, it didn’t seem like THE Living Paradox himself, or even his followers within THE Loom, were affected this whole time.","Because only THE Living Dimensional and THE Living Quantum were just recently infected in Jotunheim, with THE Living Temporal currently running for his life across time itself.","What he was thinking about as well were the items that had been given by THE Primordial Paradox to THE Weavers and THE Living Paradox. The item given to Erwin was likely already utilized or devoured by him in his ascension to Absolute. But the cube that THE Weavers had received...","If he could go through their memories and find exactly where that was, if THE Weavers hadn’t offered it to THE Living Paradox after their master’s fall...","This may also hold some answers.","THE Primordial Paradox had stated that he was giving them a part of himself.","His mind buzzed with possibilities.","|Hypothetical Analysis|","|Whatever weapon or unique Weaving of Existence that THE Living Paradox utilized against THE Primordial Paradox has grown and emerged as THE Entity after THE Fallout|","|This would explain the similar methodology of invisible infection and replacement|","|What is not known:|","|- Whether THE Entity and THE Living Paradox have any form of relationship|","|- Whether THE Living Paradox knows the extent of what THE Entity is doing|","|- Whether THE Living Paradox can control THE Entity or if it has evolved beyond his influence|","|There is not sufficient knowledge to come to a definitive conclusion|","|Recommendation: Affirming whether the cube THE Weavers received still exists and locating it would be ideal|","|Secondary Recommendation: Raids on The Shelters of THE Loom may need to commence to obtain even more information on Paradox and his methodologies|","...!","Noah looked over the prompts for a moment before he looked out at the other doorways all around him.","Maybe the answers were in the memories of THE Weavers. Maybe they weren’t. But he would continue looking until he found what he needed or exhausted every possibility this Palace contained.","Tendrils of blue-gold light extended from him again, emerging from his existence like serpents made of concentrated fate. They moved around the hallway with purpose, sliding past golden doors, pressing against locks and chains, seeking another entrance that would provide him with pertinent information.","Some doors rejected the touch of Undifferentiated Fate entirely.","Others responded with faint glimmers that suggested useful but not critical contents.","The search continued!","---","As he was doing all of this, his body in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment was moving with a happy Lumivara and Glossikos as he sought to understand this vast and unpredictable domain better.","They had been moving silently through corridors that seemed to exist in states of permanent philosophical debate, the very walls inscribed with arguments and counterarguments that had played out across eons.","At this moment, they stood before the entrance of THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts.","The Museum of Destiny.","It sat inside THE Villa Dei Boscoreale, past THE Thermae of Cyclic Refinement where Noah had undergone his brutal Katharsis. The entrance was marked by columns of white stone that seemed to shimmer with potential, as if the artifacts within were already reaching out to those who might claim them.","The dryad visage of Glossikos turned to him, her bark-like features settling into an expression that held weight beyond simple conversation.","\"We didn’t get a chance before, so you can enter and see what fated artifact you will obtain from here.\"","Her voice was measured and professional.","\"Afterwards, the last place in the Villa is THE Bibliotheca of Primordial Wisdom. The Library of Origins. It contains all the knowledge regarding THE Agora of Primordial Judgment and more.\"","Oh?","Noah’s eyes twinkled at those words.","He would have rather gotten started there with how much he craved knowledge right now. A library containing everything about THE Agora...","But everything came in due time.","Even this place that would have a potentially unique artifact wasn’t something to say no to. Who knew what fate had waiting for him behind those shimmering columns?","So he gave a light nod.","\"Let’s go.\"","The figure of Glossikos looked at him with a stern gaze that stopped him before he could take a step forward. Her eyes, ancient and filled with the weight of linguistic mastery she had pursued across eons, fixed on him with intensity that demanded acknowledgment.","\"We aren’t even going to talk about you collapsing THE Weavers?\"","Her voice held an edge now.","\"What THE Living Paradox will do in response? Or are you like the rest of THE Four who only do what you must and allow the rest of us to pick up the pieces?\"","...!","She said such words with the coldness of someone who had watched THE Four play their games while other existences suffered the consequences!","Noah met her gaze without flinching.","\"What is there to say about it?\"","His voice was calm, unbothered.","\"If you have anything to ask, I am here to listen. Until then, let’s get me whatever artifact is in here and then to that library.\"","...!","Glossikos stared at him for a long moment before....","She turned without another word.","And with that, they delved into the museum.","Around the same time that Noah delved into memories of THE Weavers and further into THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, prompts bloomed in his consciousness with unexpected urgency.","|Master, we have found something rather unexpected|","|As we finish the integration of Muspelheim, in the space where this Primordial Realm used to exist, a unique aura of a lifeform has been discovered|","|This lifeform is not a Muspeli Lifeform|","|It does not match any classification in our current database|","|The situation does not currently seem dangerous, but your input is required|","|I say \"does not seem dangerous\" with the caveat that I genuinely have no idea what we’re looking at|","...!"]},{"number":4836,"title":"Chapter 4836: Chapter 4835: What Is Known And Unknown II","paragraphs":["Noah heard the voice of Ruination echoing in his mind with such words as he quickly focused, his Absolute Seals of Fortune and Potential buzzing as if they sensed a grand possibility.","He quickly took control of his body that Ruination had been piloting in Muspelheim.","The transition was seamless, his consciousness settling into flesh and bone and authority that had been moving through the remnants of a Primordial Realm.","And he saw what surrounded him.","His massive blue-gold pillar, the monolith that had been devouring everything, stood grandly and tyrannically alone in the void. Fiery crimson-gold light of the Primordial Realm continued to sink into it from afar like rivers delving into an endless drain. The authority of Muspelheim, the accumulated weight of eons, all of it flowing into THE Infiniverse through this point of consumption.","And all around the monolith was blank collapsed space where the Primordial Realm used to sit.","Empty.","Dark.","The absence of something that had existed for longer than most beings could comprehend.","And yet, at this moment, this region did not have the calmness it should have held.","Because of their actions, they had actually uncovered a form of life that literally seemed like it had been slumbering in the region of space beneath Muspelheim. Waiting in the void between realms as if the Primordial Realm itself had been a blanket covering something ancient beyond measure.","With him taking hold of his body, Noah moved toward this unique finding.","He felt a sense of apprehension that he couldn’t explain.","HUUM!","And as he approached, whatever that slumbering lifeform was began to rouse.","Heavy Depths of Immensity began to radiate all around, pressing against Noah’s existence with weight that made him pause and truly assess what he was perceiving.","He was astonished.","The Depth didn’t fit into Surface or Intermediate or Fundamental. And yet he also couldn’t say that it fit in the Absolute, as he had now met multiple Absolutes and they didn’t feel this way.","It wasn’t that the aura he currently felt was grander or heavier than someone like THE Primordial Chaos. It simply felt different. Ancient in ways that transcended the normal understanding of age!","But the heaviness and Immensity no doubt made him feel as if the lifeform was an equivalent of an Absolute.","In the region of space where a Primordial Realm used to sit, darkness and white light intertwined and clashed. Short bursts of authority made it feel like sparks of black and white were meeting all around, illuminating the surroundings in flashes that stretched out for many miles.","Reality itself seemed uncertain about how to process what was waking up.","And the slumbering thing that Noah had woken up due to his devouring of a Primordial Realm opened its eyes at this moment.","...!","What Noah saw defied easy description.","The creature’s form was that of an ancient aquatic being, something that looked like it had swum through the primordial waters of Existence itself before concepts like water or swimming had meaning. Its body stretched for miles, yet the concept of size for it wasn’t really warranted. It could just as well be gigaparsecs large. Scale seemed to be a suggestion rather than a rule for this entity.","It shone with a hazy stellar crimson-pink light that made its entire body look ethereal and almost see-through. Not ghostly, but existing in a state between physical and conceptual that normal perception couldn’t properly categorize.","Crimson-pink wings spread above it, vast membranes of light that pulsed with inner luminescence. They weren’t wings for flying. They were likely extensions of its existence that served purposes Noah couldn’t begin to guess.","And across its entire form, shimmering pages floated and drifted. Countless pages filled with words of The First Tongue, sentences and paragraphs and entire treatises written in the linguistic foundation of reality itself. They moved around the creature like schools of fish, like leaves in an eternal wind, like thoughts given physical form.","...!","Noah was astounded to look upon such a creature.","The calm and ancient eyes of this being opened and stared back at him, pupils that held depths beyond normal comprehension. And within them, Noah could feel and see...boundless Everythings.","Not power in the conventional sense.","Information.","Pure, crystallized information accumulated across time spans that made eons seem like moments.","As he was staring at it, a booming ancient feminine voice echoed out across the void between realms.","\" You have disturbed my slumber.\"","The words weren’t accusatory, they were simply factual.","\" But you are also the first to do so since The Earliest Folds.\"","A pause that seemed to stretch across centuries.","\" For this, I shall grant you the chance to ask a single question.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes opened wide at this moment as prompts bloomed with information that made his foundations pulse with recognition.","|Information obtained through connection with The First Tongue|","| You have been granted a question by THE Mnemonic Leviathan, Pebanista Yacuruna|","|THE Mnemonic Leviathan dwells in the spaces between Primordial Realms|","|Its body is composed entirely of accumulated information|","|Every secret whispered across eons, every truth discovered and forgotten, every piece of knowledge that ever existed flows through its endless form|","|It knows almost everything|","|And it has never done anything|","|The Mnemonic Leviathan drifts through Existence, bloated with understanding it cannot apply|","|It is a docile creature of Existence, unbothered by the endless Weavings playing out across it|","...!","Noah looked at the massive entity that stared at him with ancient eyes.","One question.","A single question to a being that knew almost everything that had ever been known.","His mind raced through possibilities, weighing the value of each potential question against the others. What did he need most? What would give him the greatest advantage? What knowledge would transform him most completely?","The Mnemonic Leviathan waited with patience born of existing between realms since before The Infinite Unfurling.","It was an ancient thing few knew of, and it had all the time in Observable Existence.","It always had."]},{"number":4837,"title":"Chapter 4837: Chapter 4836: What Is Known And Unknown III","paragraphs":["He had an unbelievable finding just from the action of devouring a Primordial Realm.","Something utterly surreal!","A creature that felt like it had the Immensity of an Absolute, and yet at the same time, it wasn’t. The classification didn’t fit. The parameters didn’t align. It existed in a space between definitions that Noah hadn’t even known was possible.","The Mnemonic Leviathan looked at him with ancient patience as it asked once more.","\" What question do you have?\"","The voice was filled with Immensity that pressed against reality itself.","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he replied.","\"I am not yet ready to give my question.\"","His words came calm and imperious.","\"I am interested in learning more about you before I give my question. I do not even know how to categorize you, and I have met many across Existence.\"","...!","This was actually a new finding that made him rather excited. Something outside the scope of what he knew about THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and all others.","What was it?","Where did it come from?","How did it fit into the grand weavings of Observable Existence?","As he was thinking about all of this, THE Mnemonic Leviathan initially looked at him in silence.","And then she eventually spoke.","\" Primordial Realms. Shores. Folds. Wheels. Renowned Existences.\"","Her voice boomed across the void between realms.","\" All that which you may have been exposed to in Observable Existence does not mean that is all there is in Observable Existence.\"","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that made nearby space tremble.","\" THE Creature is not everything. Chaos or Paradox are not everything. THE First Tongue is not everything across Observable Existence.\"","Her ancient eyes held something that might have been amusement at his limited perspective.","\" Observable Existence is vast, mighty, and filled with wonders. Some cannot even be perceived by entities less than Absolute. And some... even Absolutes are not privy to.\"","She paused, letting that truth settle.","\" That is Existence. Many stray when they believe they know everything and have seen everything.\"","Her form pulsed with crimson-pink light.","\" Now. What do you wish to know?\"","...!","The words of THE Mnemonic Leviathan were ridiculously heavy as Noah listened.","This entity held more knowledge than many, but she didn’t seem to want to talk too much. She answered what was asked and nothing more. No elaboration. No tangents. No freely given wisdom that might help him understand the broader context.","And he loved to meet old things that loved to talk.","They freely gave the most information without even realizing it. A rambling ancient being could reveal secrets in casual asides that would take years to discover otherwise.","But this one was different.","She wanted her question and nothing more.","If she really wanted a question to keep talking...","Noah’s eyes flashed with tyranny as he nodded, as if he’d arrived at his answer.","\" What do I need to do in order to stand above everyone in power in Observable Existence in the shortest amount of time?\"","BOOM!","He didn’t ask about THE Entity.","Instead, he asked a question that would be pertinent to him for the foreseeable future.","A question whose answer could guide his path for eons to come.","And...","...!","THE Mnemonic Leviathan frowned.","She silently looked at him with those ancient eyes, her massive form going still in ways that suggested genuine surprise.","\"...\"","As if she was asking... dude, what the fuck kind of question was that?","The pages floating around her body slowed their eternal dance.","The crimson-pink light dimmed slightly.","After a while, the ancient voice replied.","\" Ask another question.\"","...!","Noah frowned.","\" Don’t you know almost everything?\"","His voice held challenge now.","\" You do not have an answer to this question?\"","THE Mnemonic Leviathan looked at him with something that might have been exasperation filtered through eons of patience.","\"I know almost everything.\"","Her voice was flat.","\"And the question you asked cannot be feasibly answered.\"","She paused.","\" Okay. Those are two questions answered. That concludes and even exceeds your granted question, O Claimer of THE First Tongue.\"","...!","\" You...\"","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as the radiant light around this creature began to intensify. Her form started to shimmer, the pages swirling faster, the crimson-pink wings spreading wider as if she was about to descend back into whatever space between realms she called home!","She was leaving!","Yet she stopped moments later, her ancient eyes finding his once more.","\"I do not like to be bothered.\"","The words held weight that portrayed eons spent in peaceful slumber, undisturbed by the petty conflicts of Absolutes and THE Four and all the other beings who thought their struggles mattered.","\" So. Just ask another question.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes became stern.","If she didn’t want to answer his heavy question about ultimate power, he’d ask something more immediate.","\" What is everything I need to know to overcome THE Entity that has already overtaken Jotunheim and THE Secretive Eon?\"","BOOM!","Since this entity didn’t want to answer his first question, he asked another.","One that addressed the most pressing danger he currently faced.","And this time...","The eyes of THE Mnemonic Leviathan flashed.","The pages around her body moved faster, words of The First Tongue rearranging themselves as if searching through accumulated knowledge that spanned all of Observable Existence. Information older than THE Fallout. Truths that had been forgotten by every living being except this one creature who remembered everything.","She was contemplating his question.","And then she replied.","\" The solution to your victory in the present is tied to events in the past.\"","Her voice was cryptic and measured.","\" The way and answer you seek lies in the Weavings of what happened all those years ago with THE Primordial Paradox.\"","...!","\" Understanding the origin shall grant understanding of how to end it. These are the coordinates in time where you can find your solution.\"","...!","This... this fucking fraud wasn’t giving him straight answers at all!","Events in the past? Understanding the origin? Coordinates in time?","She was basically telling him to figure it out himself while providing the vaguest possible guidance!","But a blinding crimson light did flow from her massive form, streaming toward his body like a river of concentrated information.","Actual coordinates in time. Not a place in space, but a when.","A specific moment in the past where the answers he sought could be found.","|Information Received|","|Temporal coordinates have been embedded into your existence|","|These coordinates point to a specific moment during or before The Infinite Unfurling|","|Reaching these coordinates would require Temporal Traversal of significant magnitude|","...!"]},{"number":4838,"title":"Chapter 4838: Chapter 4837: What Is Known And Unknown IV","paragraphs":["He received coordinates burning in his foundations, temporal markers pointing toward a moment in the past that could unravel everything he needed to know about THE Entity.","But as he thought about this unique lifeform and what they represented, he didn’t want to let them go so easily.","A being that knew almost everything.","A creature that had slumbered beneath Primordial Realms since who knew when!","Something that existed at a level equivalent to Absolute while not fitting any normal classification.","And she was about to leave, to descend back into whatever space between realms she called home, to continue her eternal existence of knowing and watching and doing nothing at all.","Noah looked at THE Mnemonic Leviathan as she began to fade, her form becoming more ethereal, more see-through, the crimson-pink light dimming as reality prepared to forget she had ever been here.","\" Wait.\"","His voice cut through the void.","...!","THE Mnemonic Leviathan paused, those ancient eyes finding his with something that might have been mild irritation at being delayed.","\" What I know of you is that you do not like to be bothered, and you slumber in the spaces beneath Primordial Realms.\"","Noah’s voice came calm and measured.","\"I have a very nice Primordial Realm. Much like Muspelheim here.\"","He gestured toward the monolith that continued to devour the remnants of the realm she had slumbered beneath.","\" Hasn’t it been comfortable, you slumbering here all these years? Come slumber and relax some more in my Primordial Realm.\"","\" Unlike any Primordial Realms out there, mine isn’t filled with chaos and upheavals. You won’t be disturbed. It would fit with your nature.\"","...!","The fading light from THE Mnemonic Leviathan stabilized.","She looked at Noah with those ancient eyes, her massive form hovering in the void as if she was genuinely considering something for the first time in eons.","The pages of The First Tongue that drifted around her slowed their eternal dance.","\" The home of THE Genesis Monarch is not known much by others across Existence.\"","Her voice was contemplative rather than dismissive.","\" The only time it was revealed was after the collapse of Transcendent Folds to Living Existences right before THE Fallout. It is the least known out of all Primordial Realms, if it even qualifies as a Primordial Realm.\"","She paused, her ethereal form pulsing with crimson-pink light.","\" But I am an imperturbable existence and disdain actions by nature. You will likely disturb me. I have knowledge, but I do not act on it.\"","Her ancient eyes held something that looked almost like regret.","\" That is my nature.\"","...!","Her voice was heavy as she said this, the weight of eons of deliberate inaction pressing against every word.","Noah nodded, understanding what she was saying but not willing to accept it as the final answer.","\" Anytime now, THE Entity might spread themselves from Jotunheim to other Primordial Realms.\"","His voice remained calm, reasonable.","\" Or THE Living Paradox will send more of his forces to Alfheimr or other Primordial Realms. The conflicts that are brewing will touch every corner of Observable Existence eventually.\"","He tilted his head slightly.","\" Whatever you choose, will it really be better than my Primordial Realm that nobody knows about?\"","A pause.","\" Do you even know where my Primordial Realm is?\"","...!","The question hung in the void between them.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan, who knew almost everything, who held every secret whispered across eons, who contained every truth discovered and forgotten...","Was silent.","For a long moment, she simply looked at him with those ancient eyes, and Noah could see the calculations happening behind them.","\" Okay.\"","The word came simple and final.","\" But you...must not bother me.\"","Noah smiled devilishly internally and nodded calmly with innocence!","\" Of course. The most I may do is ask a question every now and then. I would never ask you to act out of your nature.\"","He gestured toward the void around them.","\" Come. The journey will take a bit long since I now have another entity to move from here and take across The Wastes.\"","The moment he said this, THE Mnemonic Leviathan shook her massive head, the pages around her form rustling with what might have been amusement.","\" There are faster ways.\"","WAA!","Noah’s eyes sharpened at those words.","Faster ways?","Through The Wastes of THE Fallout, where corrupted existence made travel treacherous and slow and teleportation impossible? Where even his immense foundations had to carefully navigate the twisted remnants of what Observable Existence had been?","\" There are pathways.\"","THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s voice took on a weight.","\" In the spark between Observable and Unobservable Existence, inside those spaces between spaces where reality hesitates before deciding what can be perceived, there are passages.\"","Her crimson-pink light pulsed brighter.","\" The Interstices.\"","The word landed with significance that made Noah’s foundations pulse.","\" They connect all points of Existence while existing in none of them. When Observable Existence was first differentiated, not everything was cleanly sorted. Some spaces fell into neither category. These spaces connected to each other naturally, forming a lattice of pathways that exist in a state of perpetual uncertainty. Neither fully real nor fully unreal.\"","Her massive form shifted, ancient eyes holding his with intensity that demanded attention.","\" Even most Absolutes do not know of them. THE Creature likely knows and moves through them. THE Primordial Chaos has brushed against their edges. But true knowledge of The Interstices was removed from common understanding long before what you call Observable Existence differentiated.\"","She paused, letting that sink in.","\" The Interstices are moments of existential hesitation. Places where reality paused before deciding what something would become. These pauses connected across Observable Existence like synapses in a vast neural network, forming routes that bypass normal spatial relationships entirely.\"","Her voice grew heavier still as Noah’s existence buzzed with a mixture of excitement. This was it- an old thing who was talking on and on! He had poked and probed until THE Mnemonic Leviathan was now freely breaking off into long asides!","\" Travel through The Interstices doesn’t move you through space. It moves you through definition. You step out of being defined in one location and step back into being defined in another.\"","...!","Noah’s mind raced as he processed what she was describing.","Pathways that existed in the gap between what could be observed and what could not. Routes that bypassed corrupted space entirely. A network that even most Absolutes didn’t know existed.","\" Through The Interstices, The Wastes mean nothing.\"","THE Mnemonic Leviathan continued with the patience of a being who had all the time in Existence.","\" Corrupted Existence means nothing. Distance and time bend to intent.\"","Her ancient eyes held something that might have been significance.","\" Even the coordinates I have given you can be reached easier through there.\"","Noah’s eyes blazed with interest.","The pages of The First Tongue swirled around her form with increasing speed, as if responding to the weight of knowledge being shared.","\" To even perceive The Interstices, one must be able to comprehend the boundary between Observable and Unobservable.\"","Her voice held warning now.","\" The Interstices are not safe. They are filled with things that have accumulated in the spaces between definition. Corrupted Growths drawn to the edges of perception. Slumbering Undisturbed Existences like myself who prefer the quiet of undefined space. Attentions that should not be drawn.\"","She began to rise slightly, her ethereal form pulling toward a point in space that seemed to fold inward on itself.","\" But they are faster than anything else in Existence.\"","\" One way to open them, relating to masters of The First Tongue, would be to first know of them. Be capable of perceiving them.\"","Her ancient eyes locked onto his.","\" And then speaking a word that has no definition. A Phoneme that describes something that doesn’t exist yet. This forces reality to acknowledge the undefined, creating passage.\"","She settled back, her form becoming more solid again.","\"I know all of this. But I don’t act.\"","The faintest hint of something that might have been self-deprecation touched her voice.","\" So you do it. And we can get there in an instant.\"","BOOM!","Noah looked at this creature with marvel.","She had all the knowledge one could ask for. Every secret. Every truth. Every methodology for accomplishing anything that could be accomplished in Observable Existence.","And she was a lazy bum who didn’t want to do anything.","This was her nature! But she did say something interesting. The Interstices! Something that should make his Temporal Traversal possible again! And one of the ways to reach them after knowing of them...","A word that described something that didn’t exist yet.","A word with no definition.","He was THE master of The First Tongue. He held 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue. He had claimed linguistic authority over reality itself.","His foundations stirred as he reached into his understanding of The First Tongue. The 27 Core Phonemes that formed the building blocks of linguistic reality. The Logos he had mastered. The Philologies and Archai.","All of them described things that existed.","Things that were defined.","Things that reality had already decided upon.","But The Interstices were places where reality hadn’t decided yet.","So he needed to speak something that reality hadn’t decided yet either.","Noah closed his eyes.","He reached past the Phonemes, past the established Logos, past everything that had been codified and understood across eons of linguistic mastery.","He reached for the space between words.","The pause before meaning.","The hesitation before definition.","And he opened his mouth and spoke something that had never been spoken before. Basically...gibberish!","A sound that wasn’t quite a sound.","A word that wasn’t quite a word.","HUUM!","Reality shuddered and space folded.","And in front of Noah, Existence opened up to reveal wonder. It couldn’t even be called or a tear or portal.","It was simply a place where space forgot to be solid.","A moment of existential hesitation made manifest.","An entrance to The Interstices!","THE Mnemonic Leviathan looked at the passage with ancient eyes that held something almost like approval.","\"Good.\"","The single word was the highest praise she seemed capable of giving!"]},{"number":4839,"title":"Chapter 4839: Chapter 4838: The Interstices I","paragraphs":["It was a marvelous thing to see.","Once again, knowledge was extremely critical. He had to know about The Interstices first, had to understand that they existed before he could perceive them. And then he needed to know how to open up a doorway into these pathways that extended out across Existence.","Spaces of pathways that existed in a state of perpetual uncertainty.","Pathways between what was Observable and Unobservable.","The shimmering doorway hung before him, a fold in reality that didn’t look like a portal or a tear or any conventional form of spatial manipulation. It simply looked like a place where space had forgotten to be solid. A hesitation made manifest.","As he looked at it, Noah couldn’t help but ask.","\" What are the methods to enter The Interstices? This space between definitions?\"","The question was practical. If he was going to use these pathways, he needed to understand all the ways they could be accessed. The Phoneme method THE Mnemonic Leviathan had described worked, but were there others?","WAA!","The massive form of THE Mnemonic Leviathan shifted.","Her miles-long body compressed in an instant, stellar crimson-pink light folding inward as she reduced herself to barely two meters. The pages of The First Tongue that had swirled around her vast form now orbited a figure that could float comfortably at Noah’s side.","She came to hover at his right, her ethereal body still see-through, still shimmering with that hazy stellar glow.","Her ancient eyes found his with the patience of something that had seen everything and found most of it uninteresting.","\" Each entity once powerful enough can utilize their own methods. There isn’t anything universal.\"","Her voice remained grand despite her reduced size, ancient authority compressed into a smaller vessel.","\" Someone much more powerful than you can utilize the method of The Moment Between Breaths to create an entry point into The Interstices.\"","She paused, and Noah could have sworn he saw something like amusement in those ageless eyes.","\" In the instant after exhaling and before inhaling, when the body holds neither old air nor new, neither old authority nor new authority, a being of sufficient awareness can slip sideways into undefined space.\"","\" That easy. You just aren’t there yet.\"","...!","Noah smiled as he looked at Pebanista Yacuruna.","At THE Mnemonic Leviathan.","She was giving him a sidelong glance as she said this, and he recognized the expression. It was the look of someone who had just told you that walking through walls was simple if you were strong enough, and you very clearly were not strong enough.","He filed the information away.","The Moment Between Breaths. A method for beings more powerful than him. Something to work toward.","But right now, he was too curious about The Interstices themselves to dwell on what he couldn’t yet do. The doorway shimmered before him, reality’s hesitation waiting to be stepped through.","He took a step forward and entered.","And...","|Entry Confirmed|","|You have entered the space between spaces|","|The space between definitions|","|You are arriving in the Primary Veins|","|More information is being obtained by The First Tongue as your consciousness extends into this place|","|This is not a place that forgives inattention|","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he looked around him to see something that defied easy description.","He was standing on top of a massive gray pillar.","The pillar extended downward into darkness so complete that it seemed less like absence of light and more like presence of nothing. There was no bottom that he could perceive, no foundation that these structures rested upon. They simply existed, rising from an abyss that felt hungry.","Other pillars rose around him, forming a corridor of sorts. A pathway that extended into the distance, each pillar spaced just far enough apart that one could leap between them if one was foolish enough to risk the darkness below.","The floor beneath his feet was Primordial Gray.","Not gray as in the color between black and white. Gray as in the color that existed before colors were differentiated. The shade that reality wore before it decided what things would look like. It felt stable beneath him, but that stability was a choice rather than a certainty.","And the ceiling...","The ceiling didn’t exist in a fixed position.","Noah looked up and saw darkness that simply continued until his perception decided \"up\" stopped having meaning. There was no roof. No boundary. Just the point where his mind refused to process any further and declared that direction closed for consideration.","The entire area felt like a corridor built from concepts that had never finished forming.","|Primary Veins Analysis|","|You have arrived in the main arterial pathways of The Interstices|","| Wide corridors that connect major nodes of Observable Existence|","|Relatively stable, with consistent rules|","|Travel through them compresses distance by a factor of approximately 10,000|","|A journey of billions of gigaparsecs becomes a walk of seconds|","|This is as efficient as travel gets|","...!","And he didn’t even have to close his eyes.","He didn’t have to look with The First Tongue or reach out with Undifferentiated Fate to perceive what filled this place.","Every single surface.","Every nook and cranny.","Every inch of the Primordial Gray pillars and the darkness between them...man oh man, it was filled with Corrupted Growths!","They clung to the pillars like moss on ancient stones, layers upon layers of twisted existence that had accumulated across eons of neglect. They floated in the spaces between pathways, drifting through the undefined air like dust motes made of wrong. They clustered in the corners where pillars met darkness, feeding on the residual potential that flowed through these forgotten routes.","To the eyes of others, it might feel like absolutely nothing.","Invisible and undetectable!","But to Noah, with his Civilization that had begun automatically purifying Corrupted Growths through THE Infiniverse itself...","They were so dense that he couldn’t help but wave his hand!","A blue-gold glow extended from his palm, spreading outward like ripples in water, reaching toward the edges of his perception in this undefined space. The light touched everything. The pillars. The darkness. The accumulated corruption that had been gathering here since who knew how long.","HUUM!","The Corrupted Growths shriveled instantly and completely.","Where his authority touched them, they collapsed inward, their twisted forms unraveling as the corruption was stripped away and only purity remained. They turned into golden glows that flowed back into the surrounding existence, some of these glows streaming toward Noah himself, sinking into his foundations with warmth.","The space around him cleared.","Primordial Gray pillars that had been obscured by eons of corruption now stood clean and defined. The darkness between them seemed less hungry, less absolute. The pathway ahead looked almost welcoming compared to what it had been moments before.","|Purification Complete|","|You have purified a space without definition|","|Your authority has spread to places that you do not even know far from here|","|Be careful as there are many unknowns in The Interstices|","|But the number of Corrupted Growths cleansed was collectively more than you have cleansed before|","|Few have walked in the place you are currently in|","|Fewer still have bothered to clean up after themselves|","| An Absolute Everything is forming within your existence|","BOOM!"]},{"number":4840,"title":"Chapter 4840: Chapter 4839: The Interstices II","paragraphs":["Noah felt it!","A heavy and glorious weight coalescing inside of him. The Absolute Everything took shape within his foundations, pure Civilizational Authority compressed into a form!","This was from just stepping into The Interstices.","From one wave of his hand. From cleaning up a single stretch of pathway that no one had bothered to maintain!","If he continued traveling to other areas of this place...","If he explored the full extent of these forgotten routes...","How many Absolute Everythings could he accumulate?","How much pure authority was waiting to be claimed in spaces that even most Absolutes didn’t know existed?","Noah looked at this space between definitions that he was in, his mind racing with possibilities. He wanted to explore. Wanted to travel every pathway. Wanted to cleanse every Corrupted Growth and claim every scrap of authority that had been accumulating here across eons.","He looked toward THE Mnemonic Leviathan, who had appeared beside him on the Primordial Gray pillar. Her reduced form floated serenely, those ancient eyes taking in the cleansed pathway with something that might have been mild interest.","\" What if I want to spend a bit more time in this place and not cross it within an instant?\"","If The Interstices compressed distance so dramatically, if a billion gigaparsecs became seconds, then how did one slow down? How did one linger in a place that was designed to be passed through?","Pebanista Yacuruna turned her ethereal gaze toward him.","\" You can do so in your own time.\"","Her voice held the patience of ages.","\" The Interstices are pathways where one moves by definition. We are defined here at this moment. You need a legible method through your Civilization to define us before your Primordial Realm.\"","She paused.","\" And when we step out, we will be there.\"","...!","The nature of this unique entity remained the same even now.","She knew and explained everything. Yet she did nothing.","Noah didn’t want to push her too much. She had already agreed to slumber beneath THE Infiniverse, had already shared knowledge of The Interstices that even most Absolutes didn’t possess.","So at this moment, he simply created a sentence.","A Philology.","He put together Phonemes of The First Tongue, linguistic building blocks arranged into meaning that he imposed around them both. The words weren’t spoken aloud. They were simply declared, authority made manifest through the foundational language of reality itself.","A declaration!","|We are outside of my Infiniverse.|","HUUM!","It didn’t look like anything had changed when he said this.","The Primordial Gray pillars remained. The darkness between them remained. The pathway stretched out in both directions as if nothing had occurred.","But Pebanista Yacuruna spoke out at this moment.","\" Entering this place is nearly impossible for many. But leaving it, or at least this region, is fairly easy. You simply make the intent or the definition that you are taking a step to leave.\"","...!","Noah nodded.","He understood.","The Interstices moved by definition. You defined where you were, and then you stepped out of being defined in one location and into being defined in another. The pathways themselves were just the space between those definitions.","He had defined them as being outside THE Infiniverse.","Now he just had to take a step.","Noah moved forward.","One step towards another pillar, and...","The glimmering allure of The Primary Veins faded around him, the Primordial Gray pillars dissolving like mist before morning sun. The darkness receded. The space between definitions released its hold on his existence.","And shockingly, he saw the flickering corrupted Wastes around him.","The twisted remnants of THE Fallout stretched out in all directions, corrupted existence folding back on itself in patterns that would drive lesser minds to madness. But directly before him, separated from the chaos by a barrier of concentrated authority...","The blue-gold barrier of a miniaturized Infiniverse.","His home.","One step to enter the space without definition.","A single intent to define themselves in another location.","And then one additional step.","He had crossed unfathomable depths in that short period of time, bringing back a heavy and ethereal entity to his abode.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan floated beside him, her reduced form taking in THE Infiniverse with ancient eyes that had seen more wonders than most beings could imagine.","\" This will do.\"","Three words.","The highest praise she seemed capable of giving!","And with that, she began to drift toward the barrier, toward the Primordial Realm that would become her new slumbering ground!","The entry into THE Infiniverse for Pebanista Yacuruna was a simple one really.","THE Infinite Loom and its ever-changing barrier simply opened as Noah and she floated in. The concentrated authority that kept his home protected from the chaos of THE Fallout recognized his presence and parted without resistance, allowing the ancient entity passage into a realm that few had ever seen.","This was the first external entity he was bringing into his home.","And he did so without fear after measuring all possibilities.","The region he brought her to had surroundings shining crimson-gold, an earthen floor of Muspelheim forming down below to give off a sense of familiarity for her. The integration of the Primordial Realm was nearly complete now, and he could shape its essence however he wished within THE Infiniverse.","All around them, rivers of Dreams flowed in lazy spirals. Streams of Prana pulsed with life-giving energy. Currents of Avalon and Helios and many other components of THE Infiniverse floated through the air while holding Logos and Philologies that defined them.","And as she entered, Pebanista Yacuruna spoke.","\" It is a pure and quiet place.\"","Her ancient voice held something that might have been approval.","\"I will slumber and move around here so long as I am not bothered. I...\"","She paused.","\" Oh?\"","The dolphin-like creature blinked, her ethereal form going still as she looked in front of Noah.","The visage of a humanoid manifestation was forming from the very essence of THE Infiniverse itself. A woman of blue-gold light, her features regal and stern, her presence radiating the weight of an entire Primordial Realm given consciousness.","Beside her, the figure of another blue-gold illusory manifestation formed.","RUINATION.","The two of them stared at Pebanista Yacuruna with eyes that held calculation and curiosity in equal measure.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan looked at them as if adding new information into her database, those ancient eyes flickering with recognition of something she had not expected.","\" There are many oddities in Existence.\"","Her voice was contemplative.","\" The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature is simply that. It does not have a consciousness that can apply itself like so.\"","She paused, studying the manifestations before her.","\" For you to have managed to do this with your Primordial Realm is... different.\"","...!","Out of everything THE Infiniverse could have been called, oddity was a unique one."]},{"number":4841,"title":"Chapter 4841: Chapter 4840: The Hollow Echo! I","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes flashed as he gave her a look.","The grand and imposing visage of THE Infiniverse floated toward Pebanista Yacuruna, her blue-gold form radiating authority that spoke of vast domains and countless resources accumulated across Noah’s journey.","\" This place is vast.\"","Her voice held welcome that was also assessment.","\" Let us choose a location that fits you the most.\"","...!","Noah had already communicated with THE Infiniverse for them to extract as much information as they could from this ancient entity. Every secret she held. Every truth she had accumulated. Every piece of knowledge that might prove useful in the conflicts to come.","While he...","He was about to make his return to The Interstices.","There was much he wanted to do.","So he looked toward RUINATION and THE Infiniverse.","\" Get her settled. I may have a trip... across time.\"","Pebanista Yacuruna floated ahead before she turned around and glanced at Noah one last time.","\" Pathways without definitions will have many things.\"","Her ancient voice held warning now.","\" But even Absolutes are the least of your worries. There are Undefined Lifeforms from before THE Infinite Unfurling. There are The Watchers, Hollow Echoes. And you run the risk of Definition Collapse.\"","She paused, letting those words settle.","\" Spending too long in The Interstices causes the traveler’s own definition to weaken. The space between Observable and Unobservable doesn’t want defined things in it. It constantly pressures travelers to become undefined.\"","Her ancient eyes held his.","\" It is not a place to explore and play around in. Go to the point in time that has your answers, and treat The Interstices as just that... passages to get you places you otherwise could not go to.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly.","Was this ancient creature actually going out of her way to look out for him? Or simply trying to make sure her new landlord didn’t die too quickly?","Whichever it was, he nodded with a smile.","In the next moment, Pebanista Yacuruna began enlarging in size again. Her ethereal form expanded, becoming thousands of miles long as a fat ancient aquatic beast materialized fully within THE Infiniverse. The pages of The First Tongue swirled around her vast body, crimson-pink light painting the surrounding existence in stellar hues.","She began floating forward as THE Infiniverse and RUINATION moved alongside her.","The latter sent a prompt to Noah.","|Don’t worry, Master|","| We will wring this dolphin dry of all the knowledge it has|","|The more she becomes exposed to your First Tongue here, the more information I can extract|","|I know the assignment|","RUINATION knew what needed to be done.","Noah nodded with a smile as he alone remained in this region of THE Infiniverse with its forming landscapes of Muspelheim.","He breathed out and got ready.","The process was familiar now.","Noah reached past the known Phonemes, past the established Logos, past everything that had been codified and understood across eons of linguistic mastery. He reached for the space between words.","And he opened his mouth and spoke utter gibberish.","Reality shuddered. Space folded. And in front of him, another entrance to The Interstices opened, that familiar moment where space simply forgot to be solid.","He stepped through.","When he entered this time, the prompts that bloomed were different.","|Entry Confirmed|","|You did not arrive in the Primary Veins of The Interstices this time|","|You have entered the Capillary Threads|","|Narrow passages that branch off Primary Veins|","|Lead to more specific locations|","|Less stable, with rules that fluctuate|","|Distance compression varies wildly here, sometimes greater, sometimes lesser|","|It is very easy to get lost in|","...!","The Capillary Thread he found himself in looked nothing like the Primary Veins.","Where those had been vast corridors of Primordial Gray pillars rising from endless darkness, this was narrow. Confined. The pathway beneath his feet was barely wide enough for two beings to walk abreast, and even that width seemed to fluctuate as if the passage itself couldn’t decide how large it wanted to be.","Murky mist covered the distant areas behind and in front of him. The mist swirled and shifted, making it impossible to perceive anything beyond a few dozen meters in either direction.","Darkness pressed in from the sides, hungry and patient.","He could be walking toward salvation or oblivion, and he wouldn’t know until he arrived.","And when Noah looked around, he sensed the overflowing Corrupted Growths.","They were everywhere.","Denser than in the Primary Veins. More concentrated. As if the narrowness of these passages had compressed the corruption that accumulated here, packing eons of twisted existence into spaces that could barely contain it.","Even though it carried a level of danger, Noah still waved his hand.","He sent his Immensity out, exerting himself to cleanse everything within his perception.","HUUM!","Invisible silent golden waves flowed through the surrounding existence. The Corrupted Growths shriveled and collapsed, their twisted forms unraveling as purity replaced corruption. Golden light streamed back toward him, sinking into his foundations.","|Purification Complete|","|Another Absolute Everything is forming within your existence|","|At this rate, you could establish a factory here|","BOOM!","The weight of another Absolute Everything coalesced inside of him!","Two now.","From just walking through The Interstices.","But while it formed, Noah felt his existence buzzing.","A foreboding sensation flared.","His gaze changed as 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue instantly bloomed behind him, manifesting in a corona of blue-gold authority that surrounded his form with concentrated power.","BOOM!","Something heavy smashed onto his back.","His entire existence vibrated with impact that should have sent him flying across The Interstices. But because he was an Absolute Immovable Object, he stayed still.","His Seals, however...","He was stern to realize they bent.","Creaked.","Strained under weight that they should not have had to bear.","And behind him was...","...!","Noah was astonished to see an illusory gray hollow-like humanoid figure of an entity surrounded by gray flames.","Gray billowing flames spilled out of the nose and mouth of this humanoid entity, corrupted fire that felt wrong in ways that transcended normal wrongness. The figure was massive, towering above Noah with presence that pressed against reality itself.","And Noah recognized it.","It looked exactly like the form of THE Creature he had seen in Ginnungagap. That same humanoid shape. That same overwhelming presence. That same sense of Existence given form.","But where THE Creature had been surrounded by multicolored flames and the Immensity of all Existence...","This one felt vile.","Hollow.","Like corrupted existence wearing a face it had no right to wear!"]},{"number":4842,"title":"Chapter 4842: Chapter 4841: The Hollow Echo! II","paragraphs":["|You have caught the attention of The Hollow Echo of THE Creature|","|A segment of a lost definition of THE Creature when he passed through this region from an unknown time|","|It was drinking from the Corrupted Growths you purified|","|Its Immensity is unkno-|","BOOM!","The prompts couldn’t even finish.","Noah saw the Hollow Echo move fast, faster than anything that size should have been able to move. Its fist came down not toward him directly, but toward the space around him.","Because he was an Immovable Object.","So the Hollow Echo didn’t target him.","It punched the entire area around him instead.","And the surrounding environment of The Interstices...","That was not Immovable.","BOOM!","The entire region Noah was in shattered!","The Capillary Thread broke apart like glass struck by a hammer, fragments of undefined existence scattering in all directions. And even though Noah himself couldn’t be moved, the space he was standing on could be.","He was flung across The Interstices, riding a piece of shattered pathway through murky darkness as his Seals creaked and buzzed as if bearing a pressure they were never designed to withstand!","|The Immensity and weight of your Foundation is the only reason your existence has not shattered|","|You are bearing the weight of a Hollow Echo from an unknown time|","|This is not a fight you can win|","|This is barely a fight you can survive|","Noah’s eyes pulsed with Immensity.","He couldn’t let this continue. Couldn’t let himself be thrown around like debris in a storm while his Seals cracked under pressure that shouldn’t have been possible!","He moved his hand like a hammer.","A heavy Declaration emerged from it, words of The First Tongue blazing with authority that he forced into reality through sheer weight of existence.","|I! Am! Immovable!|","BOOM!","It began as a Declaration.","But uniquely, due to his Immensity and weight, due to the foundations he had built across a journey that defied normal progression, it became something more.","A Partial Embodiment.","Everything around him stabilized instantly. The shattered fragments of the Capillary Thread froze in place. The murky darkness stopped pressing inward. Even the corrupted existence that permeated this region became anchored, held in place by a definition that Noah had imposed through sheer force of authority.","Immovable.","Everything was Immovable.","But even before he could get his bearings...","WOOSH!","The Hollow Echo was already in front of him.","It had crossed the distance in less than a heartbeat, its corrupted form materializing from the stabilized darkness with speed that mocked his attempts at control. Its mouth opened, gray corrupted existence spilling out like vomit from a dying fold.","And a heavy ancient voice boomed out!","\" DISCOMBOBULATE.\"","...!","BOOM!","An Embodiment.","With a single word.","A single fucking word, and all of surrounding existence began to melt.","Noah’s definition of Immovable warped and twisted as a superior definition overwrote it. The fragments he had stabilized became unstable again, but worse now, they lost coherence entirely, turning to mush and paste as reality forgot what shape things were supposed to be.","The Hollow Echo brought its giant hand down like a hammer.","Everything in this region of The Interstices turned to formless nothing!","And Noah’s Seals began to crack!","At such a time...","Blue-gold flames wrapped around Noah’s figure.","His mouth and nose leaked lava-like blue-gold fire as something inside him ignited. He raised his head toward the Immensity of the Hollow Echo, toward the corrupted definition of THE Creature that was about to erase him from existence.","And he spoke.","\" FUCK. YOU.\"","BOOM!","|An Absolute Everything has been utilized fully|","|From your existence, an Embodiment blooms at a heavy cost!|","The 27 Seals around Noah blazed with the light of an Embodiment.","The cracks healed. The strain eased. Power that he had accumulated through cleansing The Interstices poured into a definition that he imposed upon reality with everything he had.","He raised his hands and bellowed out, holding against the Immensity of the palm descending to collapse everything around him.","Two Embodiments clashed in The Interstices.","Two heavy definitions pressing against each other with weight that made space itself groan in protest.","DISCOMBOBULATE versus FUCK YOU.","Dissolution versus Defiance.","And...","BOOM!","A gray fracture erupted between them.","The space where two Embodiments met couldn’t contain the contradiction of their definitions. Reality cracked down the middle, a fissure of pure uncertainty splitting the Capillary Thread in ways that shouldn’t have been possible!","All around them, the definitions of existence became distorted.","And akin to a nuclear explosion, the existence between Noah and the Hollow Echo melted and detonated.","The blast flung them in different directions of definition, hurling them through The Interstices along vectors that had nothing to do with physical space and everything to do with meaning itself.","|Two Embodiments imposed different definitions and have caused an unnatural reaction in The Interstices|","|You have been thrown in different directions|","Different directions.","Noah breathed as he felt the strain on his existence, as he felt his Seals buzzing as if they were screaming that they couldn’t bear this weight.","It was a shocking thing.","He didn’t feel any fear.","He felt a sense of exhilaration.","His existence felt bright. Heavy. Unfathomably grand at being able to simply survive a few femtoseconds against a mere Hollow Echo of THE Creature that may have been the weakest version of him.","If a lost definition, a fragment of corrupted memory, could nearly collapse him...","What would the real THE Creature be like at full power?","The thought made him hungry!","And as he felt the countless other Corrupted Growths all around him, as he sensed the accumulated corruption of The Interstices pressing against his tumbling form, he smashed his fist out and cleansed.","HUUM!","Golden waves flowed outward even as he was thrown through undefined space.","Corrupted Growths shriveled and died, their essence purified into authority that flowed back into his foundations.","|Another Absolute Everything forming|","He wanted to continue.","Wanted to cleanse more. Accumulate more. Push further into The Interstices and see what other echoes and corruptions waited to be purified.","But his existence felt the heavy fucking strain.","His Seals were still buzzing with residual stress. His foundations, while intact, had been pushed to limits he hadn’t known existed. Another encounter with something like that Hollow Echo...","He might not survive.","Noah shook his head and pulled upon his Atlas.","His Foundation. His Immensity. His Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons. His Way.","He activated Temporal Traversal!","In the past, Towers had acted as lighthouses to illuminate the way. He didn’t even have Stanchions at this moment.","But he had 27 Seals.","His Seals illuminated the way forward, burning with blue-gold light that cut through the murky uncertainty of The Interstices. His figure began to be wrapped in the light of temporal passage, reality bending around him as he prepared to move not just through space, but through time itself.","He put a new definition out there.","The coordinates that Pebanista Yacuruna had given him were exerted, temporal markers pointing toward a specific moment in the past when THE Primordial Paradox first encountered the infection that would eventually consume him.","Temporal Traversal that may not have been possible due to THE Fallout unfolded.","Noah’s figure warped out of existence, disappearing from this region of The Interstices as he began to float toward a different region.","At a different time.","---","The moment he disappeared from that area, an instant later...","The Hollow Echo of THE Creature tore apart existence to arrive there.","Its corrupted form materialized from the shattered remains of the Capillary Thread, gray flames billowing from every orifice as it looked around with hollow eyes that held only hunger.","It searched.","It sought.","It did not find the puny existence that wasn’t collapsed by its Immensity.","The Hollow Echo stood in the empty space for a long moment, corrupted flames spilling into the void as it processed the absence of its prey.","Then, slowly, it began to drift back into the murky darkness of The Interstices."]},{"number":4843,"title":"Chapter 4843: Chapter 4842: Helheim!","paragraphs":["He was being flung across Existence, but it was not even a traversal of space and time.","It seemed to be a traversal of definitions!","Where he was defined before to be in the era where THE Fallout had just occurred, at this moment, he was defining himself to be in a different era entirely. And he could only reach it by passing through spaces between spaces, between what was Observable and what was not.","This time around, he had specific coordinates.","Temporal markers burning in his foundations, guiding his passage through The Interstices toward a moment that had occurred eons before his birth.","|Temporal Traversal Analysis|","|The Weavings of your existence are passing through innumerable definitions across The Interstices|","|You have crossed past what is defined as THE Earliest Folds|","|You have crossed past what is determined to be THE Infinite Unfurling|","|Current trajectory: defining yourself toward the definition of a time extremely early within THE Infinite Unfurling, when things were in their early stages of differentiation|","|The coordinates Pebanista Yacuruna provided are aligning with remarkable precision|","|Take a step and you shall leave The Interstices to the new era|","|One note: I have no data on this time period. We’re operating blind|","...!","Noah felt uniquely how the Weavings of Existence had changed even though he was still in The Interstices.","The murky darkness that had surrounded him in the Capillary Threads was gone. The Primordial Gray pillars of the Primary Veins were absent. Instead, when he looked around, he found himself funneling through a path of great brilliance.","Light that wasn’t light.","Meaning that wasn’t meaning.","Definition in its purest form, unfiltered by the corruption and complexity that eons of Existence had accumulated. It felt clean here. Ancient. As if he was passing through the moment before everything became complicated.","He steadied himself.","And took a single step.","The moment he did, he exerted a new definition. The spaces between spaces faded. What was Observable and Unobservable separated around him like curtains being drawn back. He anchored himself into a new era with authority that burned through his 27 Seals.","HUUM!","The moment he stepped out of The Interstices, what he felt was immense coldness as he was shooting down at high speeds!","He smashed like a meteor onto a riverbank filled with obsidian frost, his arrival carving a massive crater into a frozen landscape that seemed to reject the very concept of warmth. The cold was so penetrating that even with his Foundation, even with the weight and Immensity he had accumulated across his journey, he felt it seeping into his existence.","The cold of endings. The cold of finality. The cold of a realm that existed to receive those who had nowhere else to go.","Noah placed his hands on the lands around him, feeling obsidian ice that burned with temperatures that shouldn’t have been possible. His Seals circulated around his body, their blue-gold light pushing back against the encroaching frost. The First Tongue began to permeate all around him, linguistic authority reaching out to gather information from an era that predated everything he knew.","Information rapidly began forming in his mind.","He heaved as he felt the strain on his existence calming down.","He breathed out while feeling as if his muscles had just withstood tremendous weight.","His 27 Seals were all shining brilliantly as they healed from being bent by the weight of a mere Hollow Echo. The micro-fractures were sealing themselves, authority flowing through channels that had been stressed to their limits and were now recovering in this frozen landscape.","As his awareness spread, Noah rose from the crater and looked upon where he had arrived.","An expanse of obsidian sky stretched above him, filled with mist and coldness that seemed to have weight. There were no stars here. No sun. No source of light that he could identify. And yet he could see, as if the darkness itself had learned to illuminate in ways that defied normal perception.","He could hear the sounds of a heavy rushing river nearby.","The water, if it could be called water, moved with a terrifying force that made his foundations buzz just from proximity. This was not a river that could be swum. This was not a river that could be crossed by normal means!","The current alone felt like it could crush Fundamental Depth entities, grinding them down to nothing through sheer relentless pressure.","|Location Analysis Complete|","|You have arrived at a unique point in time in the distant past of THE Infinite Unfurling|","|Cross-referencing available data with First Tongue here|","| This location is deemed to be the Primordial Realm: Helheim|","|The Weavings of an ancient type of Paradox permeate all around|","|Specific coordinates place you at the riverbanks of Gjöll |","|Historical context: Gjöll is recorded as one of the boundary rivers of Helheim, separating the realm of endings from the rest of Existence|","...!","Helheim .","Noah’s eyes twinkled as his existence buzzed with Immensity.","He began to rise up from that crater, obsidian frost falling from his form as he took in the full scope of where temporal traversal had deposited him.","The landscape stretched out in all directions with a beauty that was terrible to behold.","Massive glaciers of black ice rose in the distance, their surfaces carved with symbols. The ground beneath his feet was permafrost that had never known thaw, obsidian earth frozen solid since before differentiation had finished sorting Existence into its current categories.","Skeletal trees dotted the riverbank, their branches bare and reaching toward the lightless sky like the fingers of the dead grasping for something they could never reach.","They weren’t truly trees, Noah realized. They were concepts. Ideas of trees that had wandered here and become trapped, taking root in soil that accepted all things that had ended.","Mist rolled across the frozen plains in waves, each bank of fog carrying whispers that might have been voices or might have been the sound of Existence itself mourning what had been lost. The whispers spoke in languages he didn’t recognize, tongues that had been forgotten before THE Infinite Unfurling had given shape to what Observable Existence would become.","And the river Gjöll...","It roared beside him with fury that felt personal. The waters were not water but something else entirely. Liquid endings. Flowing finality. The current carried fragments of things that had once been, grinding them down to their base components before depositing them somewhere deeper in this realm of conclusion.","Bridges of bone spanned the river at distant intervals, their arches constructed from the remains of beings who had attempted to cross and failed. They served as warnings and pathways both, monuments to the price of passage through a realm that demanded payment in collapse.","It was an utterly surreal experience to be observing all of this.","A Primordial Realm from the early stages of THE Infinite Unfurling, preserved in a moment of time that Noah had no right to be witnessing. The cold. The darkness. The weight of endings pressing against his existence from every direction.","And yet his awareness quickly locked onto something that was here that should not be here.","An ancient-looking ship sat at the edges of the rough river Gjöll...calmly.","It was paradoxically appearing and disappearing, flickering in and out of definition as if it couldn’t decide whether it existed or not. One moment it was fully manifest, its hull carved from wood that had never grown on any tree. The next moment it was translucent, barely there, a ghost of a vessel that refused to fully commit to presence.","The ship was massive, easily large enough to carry armies across waters that would destroy anything less. Its sails were furled, fabric woven from shadows and silence. Its prow was carved into the shape of something that might have been a serpent or might have been a concept that had never been given a name.","And on its deck, a single aura could be felt.","The being stood at the helm of that impossible ship, his presence radiating authority that made the frozen landscape seem small by comparison. He was a regal and majestic humanoid obsidian entity, his form carved from the same material as the glaciers that rose in the distance.","A massive obsidian crown floated and spun above his head, rotating slowly with weight that spoke of dominion over things that most beings couldn’t comprehend. His robes shone obsidian-gold.","The aura he radiated was that of an Absolute.","But not just any Absolute.","This was the weight of someone who had stood among THE Four. Someone who had held a Claim on one of the oldest aspects of Existence itself. Someone whose authority had shaped what Paradox meant before THE Living Paradox had ever existed.","This was another being that Noah recognized.","The ancient entity smiled, his obsidian features shifting into an expression that held warmth despite the frozen realm around them. He opened his mouth, and when he spoke, his voice carried across the river Gjöll with authority that made the rushing waters seem quiet by comparison.","\"I have been waiting across time for thee, my friend.\"","The words were archaic! Spoken in a cadence that belonged to an era before modern speech had been differentiated from the primordial expressions of meaning.","\" Come aboard. We have far too much to accomplish, and the Weavings tell me that things have grown corrupted.\"","His obsidian eyes held knowledge that spanned eons.","\" Thus, we possess little time to do what must be done.\"","BOOM!","Noah stared ahead with a sense of incredulity.","He was currently looking at what he remembered from the memory of THE Weavers to be THE Primordial Paradox.","The original holder of that Claim.","The being who had been consumed by Erwin, by THE Living Paradox, in an act of betrayal that had reshaped the hierarchy of THE Four.","The entity who had given pieces of himself to his disciples before the end, hoping that contingencies might somehow save what could not be saved.","And he had been waiting across time for...him?"]},{"number":4844,"title":"Chapter 4844: Chapter 4843: THE Primordial Paradox I","paragraphs":["Many beings believed in fate and destiny.","Many beings cling to it with desperate fervor. They believe that the Weavings of Existence have already determined what will occur, that every moment has been preordained since before THE Infinite Unfurling gave shape to reality. They find comfort in this notion. If one’s destiny is set, then failure is not truly failure. Success is not truly earned. Everything simply is what it was always meant to be.","The significant majority hold this belief.","The significant majority are wrong.","Those who have witnessed eons say that even with immense Weavings of fate and destiny, nothing is ever truly fated or destined. They have watched beings defy prophecies that seemed absolute. They have seen futures that were \"certain\" unravel because someone chose differently than the Weavings predicted. They have observed the most intricate weavings of destiny torn apart by a single decision made in a single moment.","Because all that there is, in the end, is choices .","Choices stir everything across Existence.","A being who believes in destiny surrenders their agency to comfortable inevitability. A being who understands choice recognizes that every moment is a crossroads, every breath a decision, every action a thread that rewrites what comes next.","Destiny is the story the powerful tell the powerless to keep them passive. Fate is the lie the fearful tell themselves to avoid responsibility for their own existence.","But choice is truth.","And those who wield choice with full understanding of its weight become the ones who write destiny for others.","---","Noah remained floating in the cold air of Helheim as he looked at the imposing Absolute entity on the ship.","Many thoughts were running across his mind. Questions about temporal mechanics. Concerns about paradoxes. Calculations regarding what his presence here might mean.","But he didn’t give them much space.","He simply voiced out what he was thinking.","\" Are you sure that you have the right person?\"","His voice carried across the frozen riverbank with authority that refused to be diminished by the presence of an Absolute.","\" Do you even know who I am?\"","Yes.","He did not know THE Primordial Paradox.","And THE Primordial Paradox, who existed within these Weavings, should not have known anything about him. This was the first time that Noah was arriving here. The first moment of contact between two beings separated by eons of history.","The past was the past.","What Noah already knew had occurred would not change. This was something he had discovered when he first returned from Ginnungagap, when temporal manipulation had shown him its fundamental rules.","So regardless of what happened here, THE Primordial Paradox would still be overcome by THE Living Paradox. His Claim would still be stolen. The betrayal that had reshaped THE Four would still occur exactly as it had always occurred.","Noah would not be able to change this.","This was the closed temporal loop.","Him traveling to the past did not change the past and would not change history because his actions were already, and had always been, part of that past. He simply did not know it yet.","When he awakened Mana more than three years ago, he didn’t know that his existence had already traversed eons backward before that point in time. And before he met THE Mnemonic Leviathan, he didn’t know that his temporal traversal would be taking him to THE Primordial Paradox.","This was the issue with time and its manipulation.","It was very messy.","THE Primordial Paradox smiled on the deck of his impossible ship, the expression carrying warmth that seemed at odds with the frozen realm around them. He shook his head slowly, his obsidian crown rotating with measured grace above his brow.","\" No, I do not know who you are.\"","His voice was precise, each word enunciated with the careful diction of someone for whom language was a craft to be respected.","\" Or rather, I did not know who you are until I met you just now.\"","He studied Noah with eyes that held the weight of eons.","\" From observing you at this moment, I can perceive that the one who may paradoxically be capable of assisting me is, quite uniquely, someone I did not even know existed.\"","He paused, letting that sink in.","\" Because at this point in time, The First Tongue has not been claimed. And yet, here you are. The Claimer of The First Tongue.\"","His smile deepened.","\" From the authority that you do not trouble yourself to conceal, I can discern your distinction to be that of THE Genesis Monarch.\"","The obsidian entity folded his hands behind his back with the bearing of someone accustomed to commanding attention simply by existing.","\"I must confess, I am rather surprised. I had anticipated that perhaps THE Creature might be the one capable of rendering assistance. Or even THE Primordial Chaos, though he and I have our disagreements.\"","His eyes held something that might have been amusement.","\"I most certainly did not expect someone such as yourself.\"","...!","As he said all of this, Noah looked at this being emanating waves of Absolute authority into the frozen skies of Helheim.","He should already be infected by THE Entity.","Even though it should not be the same Entity that Noah knew at this moment in time, whatever its origin was, the infection that THE Primordial Paradox had described to THE Weavers in that memory had already begun. Something had anchored itself onto his authority and Claim. Something was slowly eating away at him.","And yet he stood here with the dignity of someone who had accepted his fate while refusing to surrender to it.","Noah floated down from the frozen air.","His feet touched the deck of the ship, and the moment they did, he felt something extraordinary beneath him. The surface was solid. Fuckin sturdy! It didn’t just resist pressure. It rejected the very concept of being damaged.","|Ship Analysis Complete|","|Structural composition identified: The backbone of this vessel is forged from Helheim itself|","|Not materials from Helheim. Helheim itself. A fragment of the Primordial Realm compressed into nautical form with Absolute Depth|","|Classification: Indestructible Object|","|Defensive capability: Can withstand the full might of an Absolute without structural compromise|","| Vessel designation discovered through First Tongue: Naglfar|","|Historical context: Naglfar is recorded in ancient Weavings as the ship that sails between endings, carrying those who have business with finality itself|","...!"]},{"number":4845,"title":"Chapter 4845: Chapter 4844: THE Primordial Paradox II","paragraphs":["Noah stood on such a thing as he looked at the glorious visage of THE Primordial Paradox.","The ancient Absolute still maintained a heavy sense of majesty despite everything. His eyes held no fear or worry. Not even a sense of urgency pressed against his bearing. He didn’t look like someone who knew that their Claim was under attack.","He looked like someone who had made peace with what was coming and was now focused entirely on what could still be done.","\"I also did not expect you...as you are now anyways.\"","Noah’s voice came measured, direct.","\"I came here seeking to understand a bit more about the thing currently attacking you. And to understand the one responsible for it.\"","He met those obsidian eyes without flinching.","\" You do know who is responsible for this assault on you, right?\"","At such words, THE Primordial Paradox sighed.","It was a sound that held the weight of betrayal processed and accepted. His profound gaze of immense dignity and power never wavered, but something behind it shifted. Something that spoke of trust that had been violated in ways that cut deeper than any physical wound.","\"Of course.\"","His voice remained precise, controlled.","\" My dearest disciple Erwin initiated all of this. But even he may not understand what he has truly done.\"","...!","The name hung in the frozen air between them.","\" And I have come to realise that it is unstoppable. I can only make preparations.\"","He turned slightly, gesturing toward the rushing waters of Gjöll that roared beside them.","\" My Claim over Paradox informed me that there would be someone who might potentially assist me in these preparations if I sailed across my river. But truly, time is not on our side.\"","His obsidian features settled into something that might have been wry acceptance.","\" Even though I was waiting here for my own aims and goals, you appear to have similar ones based upon the enemy attacking me.\"","He faced Noah fully.","\" So. Can we get started?\"","He said such words gloriously and imperiously, the bearing of an Absolute who had chosen to spend his final preparations with efficiency rather than lament.","Noah looked at this being and asked the question that mattered most.","\" What exactly needs to be done?\"","THE Primordial Paradox smiled at such words.","It was the smile of someone who had been waiting for that precise question.","\"I have already commenced my preparations. I have isolated and hidden parts of myself in different areas throughout Helheim.\"","He paused, and something darker crossed his features.","\"I have come to realise that even these parts of myself, stretched out across my realm, will be claimed in the end as well.\"","His hands clasped behind his back once more.","\" In waiting here, I had thought I would come across THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos and secure their aid in locking a part of myself away in Alfheimr or Jotunheim. Somewhere beyond immediate reach. It has to stay and persist in this time as it is a piece of Absolute. A Piece of the Claim of Paradox as it cannot be carried across time, otherwise I would hand it to you and say our goodbyes. So it needs a place to remain until it can be safe to unveil.\"","He looked at Noah with eyes that held the weight of paradox itself.","\" And it appears that, quite paradoxically, it was neither of the two I expected.\"","His smile returned.","\" It is instead the one with the Claim to The First Tongue.\"","He gestured with one obsidian hand toward the frozen expanse beyond the ship.","\" So you tell me, Genesis Monarch.\"","\" Where exactly are we heading? Ginnungagap? Muspelheim?\"","BOOM!","The words landed with weight.","THE Primordial Paradox was asking him to choose.","To decide where a fragment of an Absolute, a piece of one of THE Four themselves, would be hidden away!","THE Primordial Paradox asking him such a question was ridiculous in itself.","Where to hide a piece of an Absolute across time? Where to place a fragment of one of THE Four that would remain concealed from THE Living Paradox and even THE Entity across eons of searching?","But Noah was nothing if not adaptable.","He thought about the answers he had come to find here. As the first existence to be infected by whatever THE Entity used to be, THE Primordial Paradox would be among the few that would know more than everyone else. His knowledge of the infection’s origin, its methodology...","But first, he had to answer this question.","So after he thought about it for a moment, on exactly where a part of THE Primordial Paradox could be hidden that others would not be able to gain access to, his mind couldn’t help but wander to an area that had a complex set of rules.","An area that held four Absolutes, or really, would in the future.","An area that THE Entity was not capable or willing to go into!","The place where THE Secretive Eon had refused to enter even when her Disciple was inside. The place that had somehow cleansed or blocked the infection from Noah’s followers. The place that held protections that even THE Entity respected.","If a fragment of THE Primordial Paradox was hidden there, within THE Vaults of Ginnungagap that connected to THE Agora...","His eyes shone with realization.","\" Definitely Ginnungagap.\"","...!","HUUM!","The moment he said these words, the vast ship below them trembled with resonance of of ancient engines stirring to life.","THE Primordial Paradox smiled.","He tapped his feet lightly against the deck of Naglfar, and the massive ship shot out like a sliver of obsidian light. The acceleration was beyond anything Noah had experienced, multiple times faster than Skoll at full sprint, crossing the heavy waves of the river Gjöll as if the crushing current was nothing more than a gentle stream.","The frozen banks of Helheim blurred past them.","The skeletal trees became smears of darkness against the obsidian sky.","And the roar of the river faded behind them as Naglfar carved its path toward whatever destination would eventually lead to Ginnungagap."]},{"number":4846,"title":"Chapter 4846: Chapter 4845: THE Primordial Paradox III","paragraphs":["As this process began, THE Primordial Paradox waved his hands with casual authority.","Two obsidian thrones rose from the deck of the ship, positioned opposite each other at the center of the vessel. They grew from the Helheim-forged wood like natural extensions of the ship itself, their surfaces carved with symbols of ancient Paradox.","An extended crystalline obsidian table bloomed in front of them.","The table buzzed with an ancient type of Paradox that made Noah’s foundations resonate. Its surface became filled with obsidian-gold sacred herbs and crystals, treasures that radiated authority and weight that spoke of tremendous value.","THE Primordial Paradox motioned for Noah to sit on the opposing throne as he settled onto his own with the ease of someone who had done this countless times before. He waved his hands and began to eat from the wonders on the table, consuming items that would have been priceless treasures in Noah’s era as if they were casual refreshments.","Noah glanced down at the spread before him.","His eyes found the throne opposite THE Primordial Paradox, and he moved to take his seat. When he reached out to grab an obsidian-gold gem shaped like a cube, information immediately flooded his consciousness through The First Tongue.","|Item Analysis|","|Designation: Gjöll Pressure Crystal|","|A paradoxical crystal found at the bottom of the river Gjöll|","|Has been battered by the river’s crushing pressure for approximately one billion years|","|The sustained force has compressed trace amounts of Absolute authority into its structure|","|A single crystal contains slight Weavings of Absolute within it|","|Consumption recommendation: Immediate|","|These don’t exist in your era. The river Gjöll was altered during THE Infinite Unfurling’s later stages|","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed brilliantly at this.","Without a second thought, he chucked the crystal toward his mouth and began to chew.","The sensation was extraordinary. Cold that burned. Pressure that expanded. Authority that seeped into his foundations like water into parched earth. The crystal dissolved against his teeth, its billion years of accumulated weight releasing into his existence with each bite.","|Foundation Enhancement Detected|","|The Immensity and weight of your Foundation at the comparative Fundamental Depth has increased by 0.1%|","...!","It seemed that there were many wonders and opportunities here.","Noah focused on the items laid out on this brilliant table and began to consume them one after another. Obsidian fruits that tasted like concentrated endings. Golden herbs that burned with paradoxical warmth. Crystalline waters that flowed upward when swallowed.","Each one added to his foundations in ways that would have taken time to achieve.","THE Primordial Paradox watched him with a smile. He had in his hand an obsidian glass filled with vibrant golden liquid that he was drinking calmly.","\" How are things later on in the future?\"","His voice was casual, conversational.","\" Does Erwin get into more trouble?\"","He asked such a question as if he was inquiring about someone who did not fully concern him. As if the disciple who was currently eating away at his Absolute authority was merely a distant acquaintance whose exploits were mildly interesting rather than existentially threatening.","Noah found another unique item to consume, a sphere of compressed frost that held the weight of countless endings within it. He looked at THE Primordial Paradox as he bit into it.","\" If you know about him and what he is currently doing to you, and even now as you talk about him...\"","He chewed thoughtfully.","\" Why do you view him with such nonchalance? Even if you are unable to stop the process, why treat him how you are right now? As if you don’t know?\"","THE Primordial Paradox smiled at his words.","It was the smile of someone who had made peace with circumstances that would have driven lesser beings to rage or despair.","\"I respect his grind.\"","The words came with genuine appreciation.","\"A peasant with grand ambitions. He simply does not know how immense and grand Existence truly is.\"","He took another sip of his golden liquid.","\" If he possesses the ambition to do what he is doing to me at this very moment, he shall not stop there. He will always seek for more and more, and his actions will lead to things he cannot even imagine.\"","His obsidian eyes held ancient wisdom.","\" More often than not, those with tremendously high ambition bring more trouble to themselves than they can possibly anticipate. It is paradoxical, and it is grand.\"","The obsidian crown above his head churned and spun with heaviness and Immensity that pressed against reality itself.","\" And I know more about Paradox than anyone can imagine. I was born and entrenched in it.\"","As he spoke, the air of a terrifying Absolute radiated from him.","Noah compared this stifling sensation to the Hollow Echo he had met in The Interstices. That fragment of THE Creature’s lost definition, which had nearly shattered his Seals and forced him to expend an Absolute Everything just to survive...","It wasn’t even a hundredth comparable to the aura that he felt from THE Primordial Paradox before him.","Not even close.","It was just that ridiculously different between them.","The gap between an Echo and the real thing was vast beyond comprehension.","At this time...","THE Primordial Paradox lost his smile.","He frowned, his obsidian features shifting as his attention turned toward the sky above them. Noah also turned and sensed what had drawn the Absolute’s attention.","The auras of two radiant Absolutes in the far distance approaching fast!","\" These would be one of the reasons why we did not have time.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox’s voice remained composed, but an edge had entered it.","\" They have been camping and waiting to observe exactly what has kept me here this entire time. Whatever I am interested in, my enemies desire even more.\"","His enemies?","Noah’s eyes flashed brilliantly as he processed this information.","What else would be the enemies of THE Primordial Paradox? He was one of THE Four. He held a Claim on one of the oldest aspects of Existence itself","As if he could sense Noah’s unspoken question, THE Primordial Paradox lounged back on his throne. The auras of two incoming Absolutes didn’t seem to concern him in the slightest. He swirled the golden liquid in his glass with the casual air of someone discussing small talk rather than imminent conflict.","\" There are boundless possibilities when Existence is first differentiating.\"","His voice held the weight of someone who had witnessed things that no longer occurred.","\" What is impossible now was the daily occurrence back then. My enemies are those that failed to claim Paradox before THE Infinite Unfurling fully established itself.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":4847,"title":"Chapter 4847: Chapter 4846: THE Primordial Paradox IV","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Paradox took another sip.","\" And even now, they remain desperate to do so. Erwin was never the first to attempt taking my Claim from me.\"","His smile returned as it was thin and knowing.","\" He was only the one who managed to succeed. Even though he is nowhere near the most powerful among those who tried.\"","He set his glass down on the crystalline table.","\" And that glimmer of Paradox within him, that capacity to achieve the impossible through methodology rather than raw power... that is at least what made him worthy of attempting this.\"","His gaze turned over to Noah, shifting from the approaching threats to more immediate concerns.","\" Oh, by the way.\"","His tone became businesslike.","\" As big a fan as I am of continuum paradoxes, what I am attempting would have to be very covert. Others cannot really know about the one who helped me.\"","He studied Noah with eyes that saw more than surface appearances.","\" Could you alter yourself or change your identity a little bit? This way, your Weavings can be kept a secret across time.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox actually suggested such a thing.","Noah looked at him while continuing to consume the items laid out on this brilliant table. Another crystal. Another fruit. Another sip of liquid that tasted like finality given form.","He knew that his distinction as the Claimer of The First Tongue was a heavy one.","When he didn’t have sufficient power, it could also bring endless trouble. And the matter right now was a sensitive one. He was trying to grasp more knowledge of the past to understand how to defeat an enemy in the future. If his presence here became known, if his identity was discovered across time...","The complications would be immense.","His existence shone with decision.","His visage began to alter and change.","His figure became wider and taller, expanding from his normal form into something more imposing. Shimmering blue-gold wings erupted from his back, spreading wide with feathers that seemed to be made of crystallized language itself.","Above his head, a crown formed.","But not the crown of 27 Seals that normally accompanied his authority.","This crown looked like a stack of books burning with the light of only 18 Phonemes of The First Tongue. The 18 Core Phonemes that were known at this point in time, before the additional 9 he had forged.","Overall, he looked like a small titanic entity surrounded by what many at this time still knew The First Tongue to be. Powerful. Knowledgeable. But limited to the linguistic understanding of this era rather than the expanded mastery of the future.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at this scene and nodded slowly.","\" Your distinction is reined in for the most part.\"","His voice held approval, but also caution.","\" But if others at the level of THE Creature or Chaos take a good look at you, they would still be able to discern the truth.\"","He tapped his fingers against the arm of his throne.","\" So here is just a little assistance from me. To mask what you are, you would have to impose another identity upon yourself. Since it will be impossible not to display your brilliance with The First Tongue, you could be someone who is very proficient in it.\"","His obsidian eyes twinkled.","\" Let me see... how do you like the title of THE Tongue Whisperer?\"","BOOM!","As he said such words, THE Primordial Paradox tapped out with one finger.","Waves of Absolute Immensity surged from him, wrapping around Noah with authority that far exceeded anything he came across recently. But the intent was not hostile. The power was not attacking!","The waves coalesced into a physical object that materialized in front of Noah.","A medallion.","Obsidian-gold metal formed into the shape of a river flowing into itself, an endless loop of current that had no beginning and no end. The paradox of a river that was its own source and its own destination, perfectly captured in metal that held Absolute authority within every atom.","|Artifact Analysis|","|Classification: Absolute Artifact|","|Designation: The Medallion of Infinite Current|","|Function: Veils the signature of one’s power to only be discerned as an Absolute known as THE Tongue Whisperer|","|Creator: THE Primordial Paradox|","|This artifact imposes a false identity at the Absolute level of authority|","|While wearing it, your true distinction will be completely masked|","|Others will perceive you as THE Tongue Whisperer, an Absolute of unknown origin with mastery over The First Tongue|","...!","Noah looked at this medallion in his hands with shining eyes.","THE Tongue Whisperer.","He had heard that name before!","When he last visited Ginnungagap, names had been mentioned as he moved with Ul’moreth. THE Creature. THE Primordial Paradox. THE Living Paradox. THE Secretive Eon.","And among them, spoken with the same weight and reverence...","THE Tongue Whisperer.","After that Temporal Traversal, he had never come across anything else relating to THE Tongue Whisperer. It was as if the entity had simply vanished from history, leaving behind nothing but a name whispered in the oldest places of Existence.","He had wondered, briefly, who THE Tongue Whisperer had been and whether he would meet them like he came across THE Secretive Eon in the future!","And now...","Now he was looking at a medallion that would make him THE Tongue Whisperer.","He was the fucking Tongue Whisperer?","The mysterious Absolute mentioned alongside the greatest beings in Observable Existence during the early stages of THE Infinite Unfurling?","Oh!","The closed temporal loop revealed another layer of its complexity!","Time.","It was so fucking messy.","Noah placed the medallion around his neck, and the moment the obsidian-gold metal touched his chest, he felt his identity shift. His aura changed. His signature transformed. The weight of THE Genesis Monarch, Claimer of The First Tongue, one of THE Four...","All of it became something else.","THE Tongue Whisperer.","An Absolute of unknown origin and master of The First Tongue in ways that defied easy explanation.","THE Primordial Paradox smiled as he observed the transformation complete itself.","\" Much better.\"","His voice held satisfaction.","\" Now then, THE Tongue Whisperer...\"","The approaching auras of two enemy Absolutes grew stronger, closer, more immediate.","\" Let me swat a few gnats away and even teach a lesson. I can be considered a Senior among THE Four so I can always be a little kinder to our Youngest of THE Four. Do you know about Apophasis?\"","...!"]},{"number":4848,"title":"Chapter 4848: Chapter 4847: Apophasis! I","paragraphs":["Apophasis.","Noah knew of this ancient expression of power for Absolutes.","It operated differently from Declarations or Embodiments, existing in a space of negation rather than assertion!","But he had never seen it demonstrated by someone who truly understood it.","So for now, he shook his head lightly, wanting to see how THE Primordial Paradox expressed Apophasis!","THE Primordial Paradox set down his obsidian glass and regarded Noah with a measured gaze.","THE Primordial Paradox then leaned back on his throne, his obsidian crown spinning slowly above his head.","\" Most expressions of power operate through positive declaration. One states what they are, what they can do, what authority they hold. This is effective, certainly. But it is also limiting.\"","His fingers traced patterns in the air that left trails of paradoxical light.","\" To declare ’I am immortal’ binds you to a concept of immortality. You have defined yourself, and in defining yourself, you have created parameters. Parameters can be exploited. Countered. Overcome.\"","He paused, letting those words settle.","\" Apophasis operates through the opposite principle. Negation. One defines what something is by declaring what it is not.\"","His obsidian eyes held weight that pressed against reality.","\" Consider the difference. ’I am immortal’ creates a definition that can be attacked. But ’I am not subject to death’ eliminates the concept entirely. You have not declared yourself anything. You have simply removed the constraint.\"","Noah’s eyes shone with understanding as he absorbed this.","\" Each negation removes a fundamental limitation until the entity exists outside normal parameters entirely. They have not declared themselves free. They have simply removed the chains.\"","THE Primordial Paradox smiled.","\" At its highest expression, Apophasis renders an entity nearly unassailable. There is nothing to attack because nothing has been declared. The only counter is to negate the negation itself, but this...oh, this creates paradoxes that can destabilize local Existence. And I love paradoxes, and I....thrive on paradoxes.\"","His smile widened!","Noah’s eyes shone with calm light as he listened while continuing to eat. It was a grand expression of power, one that aligned perfectly with the nature of the being explaining it. Who better to wield negation than someone whose very Claim was built upon contradiction?","He wouldn’t mind seeing it in action!","As if Existence itself had heard that thought, the skies above them rumbled.","The auras of two Absolutes descended.","And they were grand!","What Noah saw were oddities of nature, beings that defied easy categorization even among the already impossible classification of Absolute. They had clearly existed since the early stages of THE Infinite Unfurling, their forms shaped by an era when reality was still deciding what shapes power could take.","The first was a creature of shadow and wing.","Its form was that of a massive bat-like entity, but wrong in ways that made the eyes struggle to process. A single enormous eye dominated its face where two should have been, burning with crimson light that seemed to see through multiple layers of reality simultaneously.","Its wings stretched wide enough to cast shadows across Naglfar’s deck, membranes of darkness that absorbed light rather than reflecting it. Its body was muscular and twisted, limbs that bent at angles that shouldn’t have supported movement but clearly did.","|Entity Analysis|","|Designation: Popobawa, THE Singular Eye|","|Classification: Absolute|","|Civilization: The Paradox of Perception|","|Way of Perception: That which is seen from one angle does not exist from another|","|Foundation: Built upon the contradiction between observation and reality|","|Historical context: One of the failed claimants to Paradox before THE Infinite Unfurling established its current parameters|","|Threat assessment: Significant, but currently maybe outclassed by present company?|","The second was a bird of lightning and hunger.","Its form was avian but terrible, feathers that crackled with contained storms, eyes that held the hollow emptiness of something that fed on life itself. Electricity arced between its wings with each movement, and its beak was curved and cruel, designed for tearing rather than pecking. Its talons gripped nothing but air, yet somehow it perched upon that emptiness as if it were solid ground.","|Entity Analysis|","|Designation: Impundulu, THE Storm That Hungers|","|Classification: Absolute|","|Civilization: The Paradox of Consumption|","|Way of Consumption: That which feeds grows stronger, yet that which grows stronger must feed more|","|Foundation: Built upon the contradiction between sustenance and starvation|","|Historical context: Another failed claimant to Paradox, allied with Popobawa in their continued attempts|","|Threat assessment: Significant, currently radiating hostile intent|","|Note: Both of these entities have been pursuing THE Primordial Paradox’s Claim since before you were born, Master|","|They have failed every time|","...!","Their bodies radiated an air of archaic might, power that had been accumulated across eons of existence in an era when such accumulation was simpler than it had become. They descended toward Naglfar with the confidence of predators who had finally cornered their prey.","The moment they arrived, Impundulu opened its crackling beak.","\"Paradox! For too long you have-\"","\"Shh.\"","THE Primordial Paradox did not rise from his throne.","He did not even shift his posture.","He simply raised one finger, and an instant later, the mouth of the talking Impundulu closed. The Absolute’s beak snapped shut with a sound like thunder being strangled, and its eyes widened with shock as it discovered something impossible.","It could not speak.","It could not express itself.","The words it had prepared, the threats it had crafted, the Embodiments it had intended to make...","All of it was gone.","\" You are not capable of expression.\"","THE Primordial Paradox’s voice was calm, almost bored.","\" Your words are not heard. Your intent is not communicated. Your voice is not present in this space.\"","BOOM!","The Apophasis settled over Impundulu like chains made of absence, each negation removing something fundamental from its existence. It hadn’t been silenced. Silence implied the potential for sound. It had simply been removed from the category of beings capable of making themselves understood!","THE Primordial Paradox looked at Noah as if an older brother was explaining something unique to the youngest member of the family.","\" Sometimes, when you permit others to live because they provide you with fond memories, they mistake it for weakness.\"","His obsidian eyes held ancient amusement.","\" So an example has to be made to remind them why they lost in the first place.\"","...!"]},{"number":4849,"title":"Chapter 4849: Chapter 4848: Apophasis! II","paragraphs":["And then, without even moving from his throne, THE Primordial Paradox tapped out with a single finger.","His voice carried across the frozen air of Helheim with weight that made reality itself pay attention.","\" You are not whole.\"","The words were simple.","\" Your form is not singular. Your existence is not unified. Your body is not continuous.\"","Each negation landed with weight that transcended physical force.","\" You are not one.\"","BOOM!","The Absolute body of Impundulu split in half.","There was no attack. No force. No visible mechanism of destruction. One moment the lightning bird was whole, and the next moment it simply wasn’t. Its form divided down the middle with surgical precision, each half falling away from the other as if they had never been connected in the first place.","Because according to the Apophasis that had just been spoken, they hadn’t been.","Impundulu’s eyes showed sheer shock and terror in the fraction of a moment before its existence came apart. It had not been killed. It had been undefined. Its wholeness had been negated, and without wholeness, there was nothing holding its Absolute form together!","The two halves of what had been THE Storm That Hungers tumbled through the frozen air of Helheim, trailing lightning and disbelief in equal measure.","And Popobawa, the other Absolute who had descended with such confidence mere moments ago...","Looked on with incredulity.","Its single crimson eye was wide with an emotion that transcended fear! Its wings had stopped beating, leaving it hovering through will alone as its mind struggled to process what it had just witnessed.","Its expression asked a question that needed no words.","What the fuck?","THE Primordial Paradox hadn’t moved from his throne. Hadn’t exerted visible effort. Hadn’t done anything that looked like combat or conflict or even mild exertion.","He had simply spoken.","And an Absolute had been split in half.","This was the gap between those who held Claims among THE Four and those who merely aspired to such heights!","This was why Popobawa and Impundulu had failed to take Paradox for themselves across eons of trying. This was why THE Primordial Paradox could speak of Erwin’s betrayal with nonchalance rather than fear!","Because even being consumed from within, even with his authority being eaten away by an infection he couldn’t stop, he was still this.","Still capable of this!","Noah watched the display with eyes of brilliance.","This was what Absolute truly meant.","This was what he was working toward!","And someday, perhaps sooner than anyone expected, he would be capable of the same!","Noah had come across many dominating figures across his existence.","THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos ranked among the top. He had felt their weight, their Immensity, the sheer pressure of existences that had accumulated power across eons that defied comprehension. They were benchmarks against which all other beings could be measured.","But he felt like this ranking might be getting changed.","The moment THE Primordial Paradox casually cleaved an Absolute in half with nothing but words, he waved his hands with the same languorous ease one might use to brush away a fly.","The torn halves of Impundulu, which had been falling through the frozen air of Helheim trailing lightning and disbelief, suddenly stopped.","Their descent was negated and their fall was negated.","The natural consequence of being split in half and tumbling through space was simply removed from the equation, and instead, the two halves of what had been THE Storm That Hungers crashed onto the deck of Naglfar with force that made the indestructible ship tremble.","The Absolute was still alive, if such a state could be called living. Its single form had become two, each half heaving with desperate breaths that couldn’t quite sustain an existence that was no longer whole. Lightning still crackled weakly across its divided feathers, but the storms that had once defined it were guttering like candles in a hurricane.","THE Primordial Paradox kept his gaze on Noah.","He didn’t even look at the other Absolute.","Popobawa, THE Singular Eye, whose crimson gaze had held such incredulity moments before, was doing something that Noah recognized immediately. The bat-like entity’s wings were folding inward. Its form was becoming less defined. Its aura was pulling back into itself with the unmistakable signature of something preparing to flee.","THE Primordial Paradox began to speak as if nothing was happening behind him.","\" Apophasis comes in all forms and sizes.\"","His voice remained measured, educational.","\" What I just utilised is a common form of it. Negations that I stated against other targets. Their wholeness was not present. Their form was not unified. Simple enough, really.\"","Noah wanted to interrupt him.","He wanted to say that the other Absolute, the Popobawa, had actually disappeared. It had fled in fear to the extent that Noah couldn’t even sense it anymore. One moment it had been hovering above them with that single crimson eye wide with terror, and the next moment it was simply gone, having crossed distances that should have taken considerable time in what felt like an instant.","But THE Primordial Paradox continued speaking as if nothing had changed.","\" Now, if I were to negate something of myself...\"","His obsidian eyes held ancient knowing.","\" The applications become rather more interesting.\"","He paused, and when he spoke again, his voice held weight that made the frozen air of Helheim grow still.","\"I am not bound by the distance between myself and those who have fled from me.\"","BOOM!","The Apophasis landed with force.","And in the far, far distance, so far that Noah had lost all trace of its presence, the figure of Popobawa was forcefully brought back.","The Absolute’s body materialized above Naglfar’s deck, squeezed by immense invisible waves of Paradox that made its singular eye bulge with pressure it couldn’t comprehend. It had fled across distances that should have been safe. It had put space between itself and THE Primordial Paradox that would have taken others days to cross.","None of it mattered.","Because THE Primordial Paradox had negated the very concept of distance between himself and his prey.","The ancient Absolute raised his hand with casual grace and proceeded to wrap it around the unnatural neck of Popobawa as if it were nothing more than a chicken being prepared for dinner. His obsidian fingers closed with grip that held weight far beyond physical strength.","Popobawa struggled.","Its wings beat against air that refused to support them.","Its singular eye blazed with desperate power as it attempted to activate Embodiments, to call upon its Civilization, to do anything that might save it from the grip of something it should never have challenged.","Nothing worked.","Everything it tried was simply not effective against THE Primordial Paradox.","...!"]},{"number":4850,"title":"Chapter 4850: Chapter 4849: Silver Platter!","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the scene with shining eyes.","At this moment, definitely, the ranking had changed in his perception. THE Primordial Paradox was really up there. Perhaps higher than anyone else he had encountered. The casual nature of his dominance, the effortless way he handled beings that would have required Absolute’s full attention and resources to even challenge...","It was something else entirely.","And in the next moment, this calm figure of THE Primordial Paradox turned to stare at the torn Impundulu heaving atop the ship.","He did all of this while holding another Absolute in his hands.","Popobawa continued to struggle and sought to erupt with Embodiments, with Declarations, with anything that might break the grip that held it. Each attempt failed. Each effort was negated before it could even fully form.","THE Primordial Paradox regarded the split form of Impundulu with contemplative eyes.","\" This one’s Weavings are already unraveling.\"","His voice was clinical, detached.","\" What remains of its existence is not protected by its former wholeness. Its defenses are not present. Its resistance is not capable of withstanding sufficient weight.\"","He paused.","\" Anyone who is capable of applying adequate authority relating to The First Tongue will not be prevented from collapsing what remains.\"","BOOM!","The Apophasis settled over Impundulu like a death sentence written in negation. Its already torn form shuddered as the last of its protections were systematically removed. Not destroyed. Simply declared to not exist.","Noah looked on with shining eyes as truly and ridiculously, the figure of THE Primordial Paradox turned to him with an expression of generous offering.","\" THE Tongue Whisperer.\"","The title felt strange to hear applied to himself, but Noah accepted it without visible reaction.","\"I have already set the table for you.\"","THE Primordial Paradox gestured toward the heaving, split form of Impundulu with his free hand, the other still wrapped around Popobawa’s neck.","\" If you possess the capability, you can collapse this Absolute and obtain what you can from it.\"","His obsidian eyes glinted.","\" This other one I want to consume myself.\"","...!","The actions of THE Primordial Paradox continued to be utterly dominating.","In the next moment, he turned to the Absolute he held in his hands. Popobawa’s singular eye widened with terror that transcended anything it had displayed before, because it could sense what was coming.","THE Primordial Paradox opened his mouth unnaturally wide.","His jaw extended beyond what any humanoid form should have been capable of, obsidian features stretching to accommodate an opening that could swallow things far larger than the entity he held. It was not a mouth anymore. It was a void given the shape of consumption.","\"I am not incapable of consuming that which I hold.\"","His voice emerged despite his impossible gape!","\" My hunger is not limited by the nature of my prey. My digestion is not prevented by the power of what I devour.\"","BOOM!","The Apophasis of self-negation took effect.","And the existence of Popobawa, THE Singular Eye, began to be pulled into that impossible mouth as if it were nothing more than smoke being drawn into a vacuum. The Absolute’s form stretched and distorted, its crimson eye blazing with final desperate power as everything it was flowed toward the void that THE Primordial Paradox had made of himself.","Its Civilization.","Its Way.","Its accumulated authority from eons of existence.","All of it pulled inward, consumed, devoured by something that had simply negated its own limitations regarding consumption.","...!","The moment the last of Popobawa’s existence vanished into THE Primordial Paradox’s form, from the position where he had been holding an Absolute, an obsidian pillar of light shot out.","It crossed Helheim in an instant.","It would continue to permeate across Observable Existence, a beacon announcing the death of a being that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling had finished establishing itself.","One of the fastest deaths of an Absolute that Noah had ever witnessed.","One of the most casual!","THE Primordial Paradox closed his mouth, his obsidian features settling back into their normal configuration as if nothing unusual had occurred. He turned to look at Noah with eyes that held patient expectation.","He was waiting.","Waiting for another collapse to occur!","Noah rose from his throne, setting aside the treasures of the crystalline table as his attention fixed entirely on the split body of the heaving Absolute before him. Impundulu’s eyes, divided between two halves that could no longer coordinate, were filled with incredulity and terror as they looked toward THE Primordial Paradox.","Not toward Noah.","Toward the being who had reduced it to this state with nothing but words.","But THE Primordial Paradox was no longer interested in Impundulu.","He had offered it to someone else!","Oh!","Forget everything that Noah had said about any ranking regarding THE Four.","Forget THE Creature and his overwhelming presence!","Forget THE Primordial Chaos and his shifting, impossible form!","THE Primordial Paradox was number one.","Because at this moment, this being had offered him a heavily injured and almost collapsed Absolute on a silver platter. A being that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling. An entity whose Civilization and Way and accumulated authority were now defenseless, stripped of all protection by Apophasis that had declared its resistance to simply not exist.","And Noah would take.","Oh, he would take!","His Seals blazed to life around his transformed form, blue-gold light erupting from the crown of burning books above his head. The First Tongue stirred within his foundations, linguistic authority reaching toward the torn existence of Impundulu with hunger that had been cultivated across a journey that defied normal progression.","The Absolute’s divided eyes finally turned toward him.","And in them, Noah saw the moment when terror shifted from THE Primordial Paradox to the being approaching with intent that promised consumption.","It was already over!","It had been over the moment THE Primordial Paradox decided to share his hunt.","Noah reached out with authority that burned with the weight of everything he had accumulated, and he began to collapse what remained of THE Storm That Hungers!","His second Absolute to collapse would actually be eons before he was even born!"]},{"number":4851,"title":"Chapter 4851: Chapter 4850: Existence Demands It!","paragraphs":["On Naglfar, a unique scene occurred.","Noah had jumped up like a swooping ancient bird, his transformed figure rising above the deck of the indestructible ship before descending with purpose. His feet came down like hammers of Existence itself, burning with blue-gold prismatic light of The First Tongue that painted the frozen air of Helheim in colors that shouldn’t have existed in this realm of endings.","They thundered down toward the split Absolute who had literally been served on a platter for him!","Impundulu’s defenses had already been shredded by multiple Apophasis from THE Primordial Paradox. Negations specifically designed to allow The First Tongue to be capable of collapsing this Absolute. Its resistance was not present. Its protection was not effective. Its survival was not possible.","HUUM!","His weight thundered down.","The swirling Seals on his feet exerted all the pressure within his existence, the accumulated Immensity of a Foundation that approached what THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos had built across eons when they were at Fundamental!","He paid no heed to the desperate expression on the Impundulu, to the terror in eyes that were divided between two halves that could no longer coordinate their final moments.","There was no mercy to be given here.","There was only consumption.","BOOM!","Blue-gold light exploded across the deck of Naglfar.","THE Primordial Paradox had basically held a knife and plunged it into a heart.","And Noah had used his feet to twist it.","Immensity unfolded around him as the existence of Impundulu, THE Storm That Hungers, ceased to be. Another beam of light shot out across Helheim, crimson and crackling with the remnants of lightning that had defined the fallen Absolute. It stretched across THE Infinite Unfurling, a beacon announcing the death of another ancient being to all of Observable Existence.","|Absolute Collapse Confirmed|","|Entity terminated: Impundulu, THE Storm That Hungers|","|Classification at time of collapse: Absolute|","|Civilization: The Paradox of Consumption|","|An Absolute Existential Palace of THE Storm That Hungers will form soon|","...!","The sensation of collapsing an Absolute was always surreal, as if one had done something taboo.","The weight of it. The finality. The knowledge that something which had existed for longer than most Civilizations had simply ceased to be because Noah had decided it would. The power that flowed through his foundations was intoxicating, authority that carried the taste of lightning and hunger and paradoxical consumption!","Before Noah could fully revel in it, THE Primordial Paradox spoke from his throne.","\" Existential Palaces are rather annoying, are they not?\"","His voice remained measured despite everything that had just occurred.","\"A collapsed Absolute does not need to be so high and mighty after they are dead. Making one traverse through doors of memories and other useless ephemera simply to claim what is rightfully theirs by conquest.\"","He waved his hand dismissively.","\"A trick I laid down to work across Existence is a simple paradoxical statement. When uttered within the first few seconds of a collapse, it bypasses the formation of a Palace and makes things rather more expedient.\"","His obsidian eyes met Noah’s.","\" After all, we do not have time to be meandering around Palaces at the moment.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox said such words as Noah wanted to vehemently deny and say maybe they did have time. The Absolute Existential Palace of THE Weavers had contained invaluable memories, crucial information about THE Entity and THE Living Paradox and the infection that was spreading through Observable Existence.","Perhaps the Palace of Impundulu would contain similar treasures.","But he turned over to listen and observe as even though THE Primordial Paradox showed his terrifying Immensity, below his imposing and tyrannical demeanor, Noah thought he could barely observe something else.","Tiredness.","Exhaustion that went beyond physical fatigue.","The weariness of someone fighting a war on multiple fronts, constantly putting at bay an enemy that was already halfway through consuming him. Every casual display of power, every effortless negation, every Apophasis that reshaped reality around his will...","All of it was being done while THE Primordial Paradox simultaneously resisted an infection that was eating him from within.","The reason they did not have time was simply because THE Primordial Paradox was fighting many battles at once.","So Noah nodded and listened.","THE Primordial Paradox raised one hand, and when he spoke, his words carried the weight of an ancient ritual.","\" The Everythings of what was collapsed are mine and not mine. They belong to me and they do not belong to me. They must be given to me instantly and they must never be given to me at all.\"","BOOM!","The paradoxical statement landed with authority that made reality itself pause to process the contradiction.","Behind THE Primordial Paradox, the forming vacuum that would have become Popobawa’s Existential Palace collapsed into itself. The space where memories and doors and the accumulated legacy of an Absolute should have formed simply folded inward, crushed by a paradox that declared ownership and non-ownership simultaneously.","A brilliant obsidian singularity formed instead.","It radiated terrifying weight, and Noah felt it immediately. It was the weight of Popobawa before he was collapsed. The full Immensity of an Absolute compressed into a point of concentrated authority that pulsed with power that transcended normal comprehension.","The light smashed toward THE Primordial Paradox.","His body became surrounded by heavy swirling waves of Absolute that he broke down and accepted into his existence with the ease of someone drinking water. The authority flowed into him, adding to foundations that were already beyond anything Noah could fully perceive.","And in front of him, a physical object began to form.","It radiated a heavy light that spoke of civilizations ended and ways concluded.","\" This phenomenon I designed is called the Rite of Paradoxical Inheritance.\"","THE Primordial Paradox’s voice held something almost like pride.","\" Performing it this way bypasses the formation of a Palace whilst paradoxically offering some of the Weavings of the collapsed Absolute to Observable Existence itself. A tithe, if you will. A portion of what was consumed returned to the greater whole.\"","He gestured toward the forming object.","\" What remains flows to you alongside the formation of what I term a Civilization’s Heart Remnant. An artifact forged from the very heart of the Civilization of the one collapsed. Their Way made manifest. Their accumulated authority given physical form.\"","In front of THE Primordial Paradox, the artifact formed.","It was a Nyanga, an ancient throwing club that spoke of hunts conducted across primordial landscapes. The weapon was carved from what looked like crystallized shadow, its surface covered in patterns that shifted between the shape of a single massive eye and the beating of wings that existed in multiple places at once. It was beautiful and terrible in equal measure, radiating the essence of THE Singular Eye’s Paradox of Perception.","THE Primordial Paradox took it in his hand and examined it briefly before setting it aside.","\" Your turn.\"","...!","Noah looked at the vacuum that was forming in front of him, the space where Impundulu’s Existential Palace was attempting to coalesce. He could feel the memories gathering, the doors preparing to manifest, the legacy of THE Storm That Hungers organizing itself into a structure that would require exploration and effort to fully claim.","He spoke the same words that THE Primordial Paradox had spoken.","\" The Everythings of what was collapsed are mine and not mine. They belong to me and they do not belong to me. They must be given to me instantly and they must never be given to me at all.\"","BOOM!","The vacuum collapsed.","A majestic air of an Absolute bloomed in a crimson cluster that crackled with remnant lightning, the full concentrated authority of Impundulu compressed into a singular point of devastating weight. It hung in the frozen air for a fraction of a moment.","Then it smashed toward Noah.","His gaze turned heavy as it felt like an assault from a genuine Absolute.","Because it was!","This was the full Immensity of THE Storm That Hungers, everything that remained of its existence after the collapse, all of it rushing toward him with force that would have annihilated anything less than what he had become.","...!","His existence creaked.","His Seals flared with desperate light.","His foundations groaned under the sudden influx of authority that demanded to be absorbed!","In front of him, an artifact began to form.","It was an arrow.","Ancient and glorious, its shaft carved from what looked like solidified lightning, its fletching made from feathers that crackled with contained storms. The arrowhead was shaped like a bird’s beak, curved and cruel, designed for piercing rather than slashing. It radiated the essence of consumption and hunger and the paradox of feeding that defined THE Storm That Hungers.","The Arrow of Endless Consumption.","But Noah couldn’t even enjoy its formation.","He felt like his entire existence could crumble in the next moment as he realized what this method truly demanded.","The Rite of Paradoxical Inheritance forcefully devoured ALL the remnant Immensity of the Absolute that could be recovered right away. There was no gradual absorption. No careful integration. No measured claiming of authority over time.","It was everything, all at once, immediately.","For someone not Absolute, they would be collapsed under such weight.","They would simply cease to exist, crushed by the very power they were attempting to claim.","But Noah’s existence buzzed with defiance.","He bellowed out, his voice carrying across the deck of Naglfar with force that made the indestructible ship vibrate. His heart beat like a drum, each pulse pushing back against the Immensity that sought to overwhelm him. His Seals surged over his skin, 18 visible and 9 invisible points of concentrated authority that refused to bend under weight that would have broken most beings.","The wings of his transformed form expanded wide, blue-gold feathers burning with linguistic authority.","The crown of burning books above his head flared with light that pushed back the darkness of Helheim!","He would not fall here.","He would not be collapsed by the very power he had claimed!","He was THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, and he would not break!","Seated on his throne still, THE Primordial Paradox looked over at Noah with a calm gaze. Behind the composure, behind the regal bearing, that tiredness was visible now. The exhaustion of someone who had been fighting too long against something that could not be defeated.","\" Stand strong, youngest.\"","His voice carried weight!","\" Existence requires adversity. Nothing is ever truly free.\"","He paused, his obsidian crown spinning slowly above his head.","\" Anybody can make a claim over many things across Existence. And even then, you may not survive.\"","His eyes held ancient knowing.","\" Just look at me.\"","The words were not self-pity. They were simple acknowledgment of truth.","\" The Scales demand pain to be crossed. The Scales demand hardship.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" Vakochev...demands hardship . For only those who know true hardship are worthy of progressing across the Scales of Existence.\"","BOOM!","The word landed with weight that made Noah’s foundations tremble even as they struggled to absorb the Immensity of a collapsed Absolute.","The Immensity of Impundulu continued to flow into him, and Noah continued to bear it with everything he had.","His existence would not crumble, and his foundations would not break!"]},{"number":4852,"title":"Chapter 4852: Chapter 4851: I Am Not! I","paragraphs":["Only those who know true hardship are worthy of progressing across the Scales of Existence.","THE Primordial Paradox said such words as he made it clear he would not be lending a hand after all that he had done!","And he had truly done a lot.","He had cleaved an Absolute in half with nothing but words. He had negated the defenses of a being that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling. He had presented a very dangerous meal on a silver platter with Apophasis specifically designed to allow The First Tongue to collapse what remained.","At this moment, Noah had to do his part to get to the finish line.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at him from his throne, those obsidian eyes holding patient observation as Noah struggled against the weight of an Absolute crashing into his existence.","\" An Apophasis is difficult.\"","His voice remained measured despite the violence of authority that was currently attempting to overwhelm his guest.","\"It is not something that every single Absolute can utilise. This is why many are comfortable with Embodiments. To say what you are and what you can do is easier. Far easier.\"","He paused, his obsidian crown spinning slowly above his head.","\"I imagine that in the future, very few will continue to utilise Apophasis. Embodiments will become mainstream. Assertions, Impositions, and Declarations will become mainstream. Dogma, Thesis...\"","A hint of something like regret touched his features.","\" Ah, if only there were exceptional beings continuing to be born throughout the ages.\"","His gaze sharpened on Noah.","\" But for you, as one with a Claim, especially to The First Tongue, it should be possible.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox said such words as Noah looked internally within himself.","He felt his overflowing Immensity, the weight of foundations that approached what THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos had built across eons. He felt the infinity behind his power, the boundless potential that defined his unique path through Existence.","And he felt the remaining Depth of an Absolute that threatened to overcome him.","The authority of Impundulu continued to crash against his existence like waves against a shore that was slowly eroding. Each moment brought more pressure. Each heartbeat demanded more resistance. The Rite of Paradoxical Inheritance was not gentle, and the weight of THE Storm That Hungers was not kind!","Noah pulled on another Absolute Everything.","The resource he had accumulated through cleansing The Interstices flowed into his foundations, reinforcing what was already there, providing fuel for what he was about to attempt. His heart billowed in defiance as he began to speak.","Every syllable felt unfathomably heavy.","He had done multiple Embodiments before. Multiple partial Embodiments. With the utilization of an Absolute Everything, those expressions of power had become even easier, his authority imposing definitions upon reality with weight that few could match.","But simply speaking the more ancient form of expression felt like utilizing vocal cords that weren’t there.","Apophasis demanded something different.","Something that worked through absence rather than presence. Through negation rather than assertion. Through removing what was rather than declaring what would be.","His first attempts produced nothing.","The words formed in his mind but couldn’t find purchase in reality. The negations he tried to speak simply dissolved before they could take effect, his existence too accustomed to positive declaration to easily embrace its opposite.","It was only when he integrated the nine core Phonemes that he had created...","The additional Phonemes beyond the eighteen that were accessible at this moment in time to everyone else. The linguistic foundations that existed in his era but not in this one. The authority of a Claimer who had expanded The First Tongue beyond what anyone here knew was possible.","Only then did heavy words emerge from his mouth.","\"I...am not limited by the weight that crashes against me.\"","The words came slow and grinding, each one a battle.","\" My existence is not incapable of bearing that which seeks to overwhelm it.\"","HUUM!","\"I am not collapsible under the Immensity of what I have claimed.\"","BOOM!","The Apophasis settled over Noah’s existence like armor forged from absence.","He had not declared himself strong enough to bear the weight. He had not asserted that he could withstand the pressure. He had simply negated the limitations that would have prevented him from doing so.","The crushing authority of Impundulu continued to flow into him, but now it flowed into something that was not limited by its pressure. Something that was not incapable of bearing it. Something that was not collapsible under its weight!","The negations didn’t make him stronger, not really!","They simply... removed the weaknesses that would have made him fail.","...!","THE Primordial Paradox raised his brows.","He looked on with genuine surprise, as if he hadn’t expected what he had just witnessed. His obsidian features shifted from patient observation to something that held actual interest.","\" There are many different types of Apophasis you could make.\"","His voice carried weight that spoke of ancient knowledge.","\" Those directed at the self, negating something of the self, are the hardest. Especially those whose effects will continue passively, without you doing anything else in the future.\"","He studied Noah with new appreciation.","\" Not bad, Youngest. Not bad at all.\"","...!","After he said these words, THE Primordial Paradox tapped his feet on the ship below them once more.","Naglfar responded instantly.","The vessel of Helheim’s backbone turned into a streak of obsidian light, heading toward the horizon of the river Gjöll with speed that made their previous travel seem leisurely by comparison. The frozen banks blurred past them. The skeletal trees became nothing but memory. The rushing waters of finality fell behind as they approached something that Noah couldn’t quite perceive.","And then Noah didn’t even see what THE Primordial Paradox did.","He simply felt the ship vibrate with a transition that transcended normal spatial movement. One moment they were in Helheim, sailing across the realm of endings. The next moment, the frozen landscape was gone.","They had entered The Interstices.","...!"]},{"number":4853,"title":"Chapter 4853: Chapter 4852: I Am Not! II","paragraphs":["He wanted to ask many things.","How had THE Primordial Paradox opened a passage to The Interstices? What method had he used apart from what Noah knew from THE Mnemonic Leviathan? There were many questions!","But he focused on himself and the Immensity that he felt.","First, the Apophasis. A single one, but with three components!","|I am not limited by the weight that crashes against me. My existence is not incapable of bearing that which seeks to overwhelm it. I am not collapsible under the Immensity of what I have claimed.|","...!","In the future, whatever he had any weight of an absolute crashing against him, whenever he had any power seeking to overwhelm him...this Apophasis would be there to help him! And whatever Absolute he would collapse and claim in the future, this Apophasis would already be there like a bastion of protection!","Oh!","He stood like a primordial beast on the deck of Naglfar, his transformed figure radiating authority that pushed back against the undefined space around them. His wings spread wide, blue-gold feathers burning with linguistic power. His crown of burning books blazed above his head as he took in every single ounce of Depth left behind by a powerful Absolute.","The weight continued to flow into him.","But now, with his Apophasis in place, it no longer threatened to collapse him.","|Foundation Analysis - Updated|","|Integration of Absolute authority proceeding|","|The infinite potential of the weight and Immensity being inherited from THE Storm That Hungers is elevating your foundations significantly|","|Current status: The Immensity and weight of your Foundation at Fundamental Depth is now 68% comparable to that of THE Creature|","|However, after observing THE Primordial Paradox, I need to note something|","|Although not fully accurate due to limited data, the Foundation of your Fundamental Depth compared to THE Primordial Paradox when he was at Fundamental Depth before he became Absolute...|","|Is at 45% comparatively|","|THE Primordial Paradox built a grander foundation than THE Creature did at the same stage|","| Shall calculations be based on THE Primordial Paradox instead of THE Creature?|","BOOM!","The words from RUINATION were actually heavy.","They made a distinction between THE Creature and THE Primordial Paradox that Noah hadn’t considered before. Somehow, THE Primordial Paradox was actually the one who had built the grandest foundation compared to these beings. The one who had accumulated the most weight before making the leap to Absolute.","Of course, as she mentioned, this might not be fully accurate. If he met THE Creature again, the calculations might scale up to potentially show him as the one who led in foundational weight.","But as of right now, every other entity was left behind as THE Primordial Paradox pulled into the lead.","...!","Noah gave the silent command to utilize the comparative weight of THE Primordial Paradox as the new baseline.","|Recalibrating|","|Foundation of Fundamental Depth: 45% comparable to THE Primordial Paradox at equivalent stage|","|This is actually remarkable progress given the time differential|","|Additionally, I need to note something about the authority you’re currently absorbing|","|As THE First Tongue, the Way of THE Paradox of Consumption can theoretically be embodied as a Derivative Civilization|","|However, it is too similar to your existing Derivative Civilization of Hunger|","|The Derivative Civilization of Hunger is currently moving within your existence|","|It has begun consuming the Immensity that stands as THE Paradox of Consumption|","|When the Derivative Civilization of Hunger finishes devouring everything that is the Civilization of THE Paradox of Consumption, its Immensity and standing can be pushed above Fundamental|","| It can become Half-Step Absolute|","|You can make the choice on whether to allow your Derivative Civilizations to take this step to Half-Step Absolute while your main Way and Civilization continues across its Formless Depth|","|Your core remains where it needs to be before making the jump to Absolute, it disdains Half-Step|","|But your derivatives can advance ahead of you|","BOOM!","...!","Inside all of his existence, Noah felt like countless jaws of hunger had erupted.","They were chomping down on the Immensity of Impundulu that was crashing all around him, devouring the authority that had threatened to collapse him moments before. The Derivative Civilization of Hunger was not waiting for permission. It was already feeding, already growing, already reaching toward something that Noah himself had not yet grasped.","And these jaws of hunger were telling him something.","The intent was clear, flowing through the connection between himself and his Derivative Civilization.","We can actually grasp a glimmer of the Absolute for you, big man! Half-Step. You don’t have to bother with it yourself, but as derivatives, we can help!","...!","This was the message he was feeling from the Derivative Way of Hunger.","When it came to this decision, Noah didn’t hesitate.","He gave his permission.","|Decision Registered|","|The Derivative Civilization of Hunger is going forward to grasp a glimmer of Absolute|","|Even if it is only Half a Step, this is significant|","|Musings of Paradox have influenced its evolution greatly|","|The Way it is developing carries the essence of what it consumed:|","|That which feeds grows stronger, yet that which grows stronger must feed more|","|An endless hunger is blooming within your existence|","|Current assessment: This could potentially be even grander in the future|","|If you could turn this endless hunger into a genuine infinity...|","|An Infinity of Hunger|","...!","The prompts showed what could potentially be a possibility for the future.","Noah looked at them grandly as he felt the shift occurring within his existence. The Derivative Civilization of Hunger was advancing, reaching toward Half-Step Absolute while his core Civilization remained at Formless Depth. It was like having a scout who could explore territory that the main force wasn’t yet ready to enter.","His dominating figure rose up.","He stood strong on the deck of Naglfar as he took in what remained of the Depth of Impundulu. The crashing weight of the Absolute that had threatened to collapse him moments before was no longer so overbearing on his existence.","His Apophasis held.","His Derivative Civilization fed.","And his foundations grew with every moment that passed!","He looked at the surrounding Weavings of The Interstices with eyes that burned blue-gold.","The Primary Veins stretched out around them, Primordial Gray pillars rising from endless darkness. The space between Observable and Unobservable pressed against Naglfar from all directions, but the indestructible ship cut through it like a blade through water.","And everywhere Noah looked, he saw Corrupted Growths.","They clung to the pillars. They floated in the undefined air. They clustered in the spaces between pathways like moss on ancient stones.","He sent a flicker of his immense weight into the surroundings.","A pulse of authority that radiated outward from his position, touching everything within his perception. The Corrupted Growths that it contacted shriveled and died, their twisted forms purified into golden light that flowed back toward him!","Even here, even while absorbing the Depth of an Absolute, he could still cleanse!","And as he did, he replenished an Absolute Everything he had just utilized!","THE Primordial Paradox had been leaning back on his throne with his eyes closed.","He breathed in and out with the measured rhythm of someone finishing a meal, the authority of Popobawa fully integrated into his already immense foundations. His figure seemed grand and majestic despite the tiredness that lurked beneath the surface as at this time, he used the arrow that was the artifact which should be Noah’s from the Impundulu as a toothpick.","With his eyes still closed, he spoke.","\" You swallowed an Absolute.\"","His voice was contemplative.","\" All that happened was your Immensity rising. It seems like you are working on your foundation the most before you even grasp Absolute.\"","A faint smile touched his obsidian features.","\" You are on the right path, Youngest.\"","He paused, letting those words settle.","\" Absolute can be a set of stairs that you can walk upon to go toward the next Scale of Existence. Or it can be a cliff that one can never escape from because their foundation was too weak.\"","...!"]},{"number":4854,"title":"Chapter 4854: Chapter 4853: Unprecedented Glory! I","paragraphs":["His voice grew heavier.","\"I was not merely speaking when I said that the Scales of Existence demand hardship. That is how they were designed.\"","His eyes remained closed, but his presence seemed to expand.","\"If there is no adversity or hardship that your Way has faced, it will be nearly impossible for you to grasp the second level of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence.\"","The musings landed with weight that made the very fabric of The Interstices tremble.","\" No matter what you do or what resources you claim. Even if you burn all of Observable Existence to the ground and corrupt it in any way you desire.\"","His voice held finality.","\"If you do not have that adversity and hardship woven into your foundations, you will not be reaching THE Level Two Scale of Existence.\"","...!","Noah looked at THE Primordial Paradox with a unique gaze.","The words this entity had just spoken seemed oddly familiar to what THE Living Paradox had done. Or would do in the future that Noah had come from.","Even if you burned all of Observable Existence and corrupted it...","Without a sufficient foundation, you would not be able to grasp the next level of the Scales of Existence.","So...THE Fallout was the bid of THE Living Paradox to attain Level Two Scale of Existence layered with his attack on THE Creature?","The catastrophe that had reshaped Observable Existence, that had killed countless beings and destroyed realms beyond counting, that had torn apart the fabric of reality itself...","It was all for advancement?","Noah’s eyes were bright as he thought about this.","When it came to his own foundation and Immensity, when it came to the path he walked and the heights he sought to reach, when it came to this Vakochev and the Scales of Existence...","\" Vakochev can demand whatever he wants to demand.\"","Noah’s voice carried across the deck of Naglfar with authority that refused to be diminished by ancient names or ancient requirements.","\" But when the time comes, I will take the step I need to regardless.\"","BOOM!","An air of grand tyranny radiated around Noah as he said this.","The words were not arrogance. They were not bravado. They were simple statement of intent from someone who had never let the rules of Existence prevent him from achieving what he sought!","The closed eyes of the regal-looking Primordial Paradox remained closed.","But a faint smile appeared on his lips.","It was the acknowledgment of one who had walked a similar path and understood what such defiance truly meant.","Naglfar crossed The Interstices in silence after that.","The Primordial Gray pillars blurred past them. The darkness between pathways parted before the ship’s prow. The Corrupted Growths that lined the routes shriveled and died as Noah’s passive authority radiated outward, cleansing spaces that hadn’t been touched in eons as he grasped a few more Absolute Everythings!","And then, a moment later, space became defined all around them.","The ship broke free of The Interstices with a transition that felt like stepping from dream into waking. The undefined pathways fell away. The perpetual uncertainty gave way to something solid and real and present.","Noah sensed the overwhelming Immensity of The First Tongue.","The concentrated authority of linguistic foundations that had been accumulating since before THE Infinite Unfurling. The weight of a place where reality itself had been shaped by words spoken at the dawn of Existence.","He found himself in Ginnungagap.","They had arrived!","Ginnungagap!","Noah had a nostalgic expression as he looked around and saw the river passageways shining with obsidian light, filled with Phonemes of The First Tongue that drifted through the air like luminescent fish swimming through cosmic waters.","Dazzling lights of a time before full differentiation settled permeated all around. The crimson and gold rivers of Civilizational authority flowed calmly through the vast expanse, carrying weight that would have crushed lesser beings. Storms of linguistic power churned in the distance, the same storms that could have ripped him apart during his last temporal traversal here.","Now they felt like weather disturbances that would not do much to him.","The gap between what he had been and what he had become was staggering.","If he had to be cautious and move very slowly in his first traversal, navigating around dangers that could have ended his existence with a single misstep, he could do countless more things right now. He could walk through those storms. He could swim those rivers. He could touch the concentrated authority that permeated this place without fearing that it would dissolve his foundations.","He breathed in the air of Ginnungagap.","His existence continued to change as the weight of Impundulu settled deeper into his foundations. The ship he was on tore across the skies of this ancient realm, guided by THE Primordial Paradox who knew exactly where he was going.","The regal entity kept his eyes closed as he spoke.","\" One last thing I shall tell you.\"","His voice carried the weight of someone imparting wisdom they had earned through eons of experience.","\" Your foundation will be somewhat ready if you can collapse an Absolute from beginning to end. Without any tricks or assistance. Simply you against them, with victory achieved through your own weight and Immensity.\"","He paused.","\" At that time, your foundation may be sufficient.\"","A faint smile touched his obsidian features.","\" Until then, keep working hard, Youngest.\"","...!","With such words, their surroundings became blurs of existence.","The rivers of authority streaked past them. The storms of linguistic power became nothing but smears of light against the glorious backdrop. Naglfar moved with speed that transcended normal spatial relationships, carrying them toward a destination that Noah had specified to THE Primordial Paradox.","Moments later...","HUUM!","The ship came to a halt.","And Noah stared at utter wonder.","\" Alright.\"","\"Here we are at THE Vaults of Ginnungagap. They are a popular place. Many Primordial Lifeforms like to test their luck here.\"","...!","What Noah observed was not the radiant barrier that he remembered.","It was not THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap that he had entered in his own time.","This was something older!","An ancient and primordial-looking cluster of crimson-gold billowing clouds stretched before them, roaring like beasts that had been given atmospheric form. They covered everything, stretching out horizontally and vertically to the edge of perception. There was no visible structure, no walls, no defined entrance. Just endless clouds of concentrated authority that churned and rumbled with power that predated THE Infinite Unfurling’s final establishment.","Millions of miles and light years around their vicinity, Noah could perceive variations of Ginnu Lifeforms.","They ranged from THE Surface to Fundamental Depth, entities of all scales and power levels either situated outside THE Vaults or making their way in. Some floated in contemplation, gathering their courage. Others dove into the billowing clouds with determination that spoke of goals they were desperate to achieve. A few emerged from the clouds looking triumphant. More emerged looking defeated.","This was THE Vaults in their original state.","Before eons of passage had transformed them into what Noah knew!"]},{"number":4855,"title":"Chapter 4855: Chapter 4854: Unprecedented Glory! II","paragraphs":["After pausing briefly, the ship proceeded forward!","It moved calmly, in a slow manner that spoke of confidence rather than caution. Naglfar pierced through the billowing clouds of authority as if they were nothing more than morning mist, the backbone of Helheim refusing to be impeded by anything as mundane as concentrated Civilizational power.","THE Primordial Paradox opened his eyes slightly.","\" Do you have a specific place in mind inside of the Vault?\"","His voice was casual, as if asking about preferred dining locations rather than destinations within one of the most significant structures in Observable Existence.","Noah gave a light nod as he began to feel his existence settling.","\" THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. You know of it?\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox fully opened his eyes at this moment.","Something flickered in those obsidian depths.","He tapped on the ship again.","Naglfar veered slightly to the right, adjusting its course through the billowing clouds before shooting out toward a specific direction with renewed purpose. The vessel knew where to go now, guided by its master’s intent toward a destination that apparently warranted full attention.","Noah looked at the vibrant and transcendent billowing clouds that the ship passed through.","He sensed no oppression.","Nothing pressed down on him.","Everything that might have challenged a lesser traveler was prevented and kept out by the authority of the vessel he rode upon and the being who commanded it.","|Location Analysis|","|You have entered THE Vaults of Ginnungagap eons before THE Fallout|","|Their current state is more primal and true than what you experienced in your era|","|The corruption that permeated them in your time does not exist here|","|Current position: You have not entered the Stoa of Dogmata this time around|","|You are passing through the Third Circle: The Akademeia of Theseis|","|This is an area of pure philosophical discourse where reality is constantly being proposed and challenged|","|The landscape itself is made of competing Theseis, creating impossible geography that shifts based on which propositions are currently dominant|","|Normal movement is only possible by successfully proposing a Thesis that creates stable ground, or by defeating the Theseis that make up the terrain|","|However...|","|Naglfar of THE Primordial Paradox is naturally bypassing all of this|","|What may have taken considerable time and effort for others is now being crossed through as if it is nothing|","...!","As they passed through, Noah observed the landscape shifting around them.","The Akademeia of Theseis was exactly what RUINATION had described. Ground formed and dissolved based on philosophical arguments that he could barely perceive. Mountains rose when certain propositions gained dominance, only to collapse when counter-propositions emerged victorious. Rivers flowed upward when the Thesis governing their direction was challenged and replaced.","It was chaos given intellectual form.","And Naglfar sailed through it all without pause.","THE Primordial Paradox began to stretch on his throne.","\" Many and few go into THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.\"","His voice was contemplative.","\" Due to the complex rulings and Weavings there, even Absolutes are bound by its constraints. It is a place where power alone does not guarantee success. More powerful beings steer away.\"","He glanced at Noah.","\"It is smart of you to choose it. Any new entrant there has their Depth forcefully brought down to THE Surface. They have to work their way up through merit and contribution rather than relying on accumulated authority.\"","His obsidian crown spun slowly above his head.","\"At this moment, only a some Fundamental and maybe an Absolute or two attempting to go through the hassle for the rewards within. Most prefer easier paths to power.\"","As he talked, their surroundings flickered again.","The ship passed through the Akademeia at extremely rapid speeds, the competing Theseis becoming nothing but blurs of philosophical light. In no time, they traversed across THE Vaults entirely, leaving the Third Circle behind as they entered a new region.","And then Naglfar came to a gradual stop.","Before them was a region filled with clouds of golden light, radiant and welcoming compared to the churning authority they had passed through. And at the center of this golden expanse stood a massive arched gateway.","The gateway was ancient beyond measure.","Its pillars were carved from what looked like crystallized rhetoric, words and meanings etched into every surface.","The arch itself seemed to be made of solidified debate.","On either side of this golden arched gateway, four massive statues floated around it menacingly.","The first was a massive titanic humanoid burning with Existence itself. Its form was pure presence, pure being, radiating the simple truth that it was and therefore mattered.","The second was a sphinx with a feminine head shining with glimmers of The First Tongue. Her eyes held riddles that could reshape reality, and her wings were made of Phonemes arranged in patterns that seemed to ask questions rather than make statements!","The third was a massive star-shaped statue with a single eye burning with Paradox.","The fourth was a minotaur adorned in a glorious toga, its form radiating the weight of Chaos given purpose and direction.","The ship of THE Primordial Paradox passed through all of this without even sparing a glance.","The statues that might have challenged any other vessel simply watched as Naglfar sailed by. Existence distorted around them when they passed the gateway, reality bending to accommodate their transition from one space to another.","Moments later...","HUUM!","The glorious ship arrived.","It floated above an endlessly shining shore filled with glimmering sands that seemed to be made of crystallized glory. Waves of water that held the weight of accumulated achievement lapped against the beach, each tide bringing echoes of triumphs and defeats that had occurred in this place across eons.","All around the shores were scattered Ginnu Lifeforms.","But they were not alone.","Muspeli Lifeforms moved among them, their forms burning with the contained heat of their Primordial Realm. Chaos Giants lumbered across the sands, their shifting forms drawing curious glances from other inhabitants.","Ljósálfar drifted through the air with ethereal grace, their light-born bodies casting no shadows on the glimmering beach. Other lifeforms from different Primordial Realms could be seen here as well, representing the full diversity of Observable Existence in its early stages!","All of them adorned in Togas.","The garments of Hoplites.","They moved around the beach with purpose, some heading toward destinations inland, others returning from expeditions with expressions of triumph or defeat. This was a place of competition and advancement, where beings from across Existence came to prove themselves worthy of deeper access to THE Agora’s secrets.","Four massive temples spanning tens of miles could be seen in the distance.","Each temple represented one of the four aspects of the oldest forces in Existence.","The Temple of Existence burned with the presence of Existence, its architecture speaking of pure being and fundamental reality.","The Temple of Paradox shifted between states, its walls made of contradictions that somehow supported each other.","The Temple of Chaos changed constantly, never quite the same from one moment to the next yet somehow maintaining its essential nature.","The Temple of The First Tongue stood carved from crystallized language, every surface covered in words and meanings that predated current understanding.","The air of ancientness permeated all around.","Chaos. Paradox. Existence. The First Tongue!","It felt grand and heavy, the weight of powers that had shaped Observable Existence pressing against anyone who entered this sacred space.","Many Hoplites moved around the shore and toward those four temples.","It seemed they were doing everything they could to raise their contributions and advance in ranking before they could be allowed to go deeper into THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. The competition was fierce but regulated, governed by rules that even Absolutes had to respect.","It was a slightly different Agora than the one in the future.","More vibrant. More alive with possibility rather than the weight of accumulated history.","But the moment Noah arrived...","HUUM!","He looked down and saw a few things happening with his existence.","First, the absorption of the Depth of Impundulu finished.","The last of THE Storm That Hungers’ authority settled into his foundations, completing a process that had begun on the deck of Naglfar and continued through their journey across Ginnungagap. His Seals burned brighter than ever. His weight felt grander than it had at any point in his existence.","And the Derivative Civilization of Hunger...","He felt it buzzing within him.","It was settling at Half-Step Absolute.","The endless hunger that had consumed the Paradox of Consumption had reached a threshold that his main Civilization had not yet crossed. A scout that had advanced ahead of the main force, tasting territory that Noah himself would claim in time.","But more than all of that...","He felt his garments changing.","The toga that bloomed on him as he entered THE Agora was not the simple garment of Hoplites that the beings on the shore wore. It was something else. Something grander. Something that radiated authority!","The moment he saw this, he shook his head with surprise.","It couldn’t be possible, right?","But surely and undeniably, there on his toga was the brilliant marking of a Polemarch.","The same rank that his body in the future, which was in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment at this very moment in a different time, had also attained. The rank of a commander. The rank of someone who had proven themselves through victories that most beings couldn’t even imagine achieving!","He had attained it here as well.","Upon entry.","|...|","Even RUINATION seemed to have no words.","The prompts that usually flowed with analysis and strategic assessment were simply silent, processing something that apparently defied easy explanation.","At this moment, across The Shores of Kleos and seemingly across THE Agora of Primordial Judgment itself, a booming voice echoed out.","It was similar to the announcing voice that Noah had heard in THE Palaestra when he fought against THE Weavers. Ancient. Authoritative. Carrying weight that made every being on the shore stop what they were doing and listen!","\"THE TONGUE WHISPERER, UPON ENTRY INTO THE AGORA OF PRIMORDIAL JUDGMENT, HAS ATTAINED THE RANK OF POLEMARCH IN AN UNPRECEDENTED ACHIEVEMENT THAT HAS NOT BEEN DONE BEFORE!\"","...!","The words crashed across the shores like thunder.","Every Hoplite on the beach turned to look at the ship floating above them.","Every being from every Primordial Realm stopped their activities to stare at the figure standing on Naglfar’s deck, the figure wearing a Polemarch’s toga despite having only just arrived!","THE Tongue Whisperer!"]},{"number":4856,"title":"Chapter 4856: Chapter 4855: A Scheme Across Time! I","paragraphs":["Polemarch.","A ranking that at this stage of existence within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment was a rare one.","The sheer amount of merit that one needed to obtain it was ridiculous to even think about. Countless battles in THE Palaestra. Innumerable contributions to the understanding of the four fundamental aspects. Eons of dedicated service and demonstration of worthiness!","And yet THE Tongue Whisperer had obtained it the moment they arrived.","What made them so grand? What made them so immense that their sheer presence alone allowed them to gain such a thing?","The many Primordial Lifeforms across The Shores of Kleos and the internal regions of this place buzzed with speculation and wonder.","Ginnu Lifeforms who had spent yesrs working their way up from Hoplite stared upward at the floating ship with expressions that mixed awe and envy in equal measure. Muspeli warriors who had proven themselves through countless conflicts paused their training to observe. Chaos Giants whose forms shifted with barely contained turbulence grew still as they committed this name to their memory!","The name of THE Tongue Whisperer!","It would spread from here. It would reach the far corners of THE Agora, whispered in temples and debated in forums. A being who had achieved the impossible simply by existing!","Noah’s eyes were blindingly sharp as he thought about the possibility of all of this.","In the future, he had entered THE Agora of Primordial Judgment for the first time. He had gained the Polemarch status after making the contribution of the nine new Phonemes of The First Tongue public. That contribution had been so significant, so foundational to the expansion of linguistic authority across Observable Existence!","The way time and causality worked seemed to be truly unique.","Because his signature was laid down later on, but for him, it was in the past of his existence. The same signature of a Polemarch was applied right now, which was his ongoing future, even though his ongoing future meant that right now, he was in the past.","\"...\"","Confused yet?","He had contributed the nine Phonemes in what was his past but THE Agora’s future.","THE Agora had recognized that contribution across time.","And now, in what was his future but THE Agora’s past, that recognition was still valid.","\"...\"","We’ll stop there!","It was fucking confounding.","Temporal mechanics made his head spin if he thought about them too long. The closed loop nature of his journey meant that everything he was doing now had already been done, had always been done, was simply being experienced for the first time from his perspective while having always existed from the perspective of time itself.","But he couldn’t dwell on such paradoxes.","Not when there was work to be done.","At this moment, he felt the aura of THE Primordial Paradox rise up.","The ancient Absolute came to stand beside him on the deck of Naglfar, his obsidian form radiating authority that made everything else seem small by comparison. His figure looked just as imposing and imperious as ever before, tiredness hidden beneath layers of regal composure that refused to show weakness.","And when he came beside Noah, he also wore the toga of a Polemarch.","Of course he did.","\"It is merely the ranking of a Polemarch. I gained it a bit ago when I visited here and didnt bother going for Strategos ranking as it was binding.\"","His voice carried that precise sway that made every word feel deliberately chosen.","\" Do not permit it to go to your head, Youngest.\"","He glanced down at the shore below, at the countless beings staring upward with expressions that ranged from reverence to disbelief.","\" Now then. Shall we stand here and revel and bask in the shock and awe of others?\"","A faint smile touched his obsidian features.","\" Or shall we proceed with the business at hand?\"","...!","Noah smiled and shook his head.","\"Let us go in.\"","He felt the ship below his feet begin to vibrate. The massive vessel of Naglfar, forged from the backbone of Helheim itself, began to compress. To miniaturize. THE Primordial Paradox pinched his fingers together with casual grace, and this terrifying construct that had carried them across realms and through The Interstices came to fit into the space between his fingertips.","An Indestructible Object that could withstand the might of an Absolute, reduced to the size of a trinket.","THE Primordial Paradox slipped it somewhere within his robes before motioning to Noah.","His gesture indicated that he would be following Noah’s lead.","This was Noah’s destination. Noah’s purpose. THE Primordial Paradox was here to hide a piece of himself and to observe, not to direct.","Noah proceeded forward.","He descended from where Naglfar had floated, his transformed figure cutting through the golden air of THE Agora with wings that burned blue-gold. His crown of burning books blazed above his head, radiating the authority of 18 visible Phonemes while concealing the additional 9 that belonged to a future this era had not yet reached.","He moved toward the Temple of The First Tongue.","The structure dominated this section of The Shores of Kleos, its architecture carved from crystallized language that predated current understanding. Words and meanings etched every surface, Phonemes arranged in patterns that seemed to whisper secrets to anyone who passed close enough to hear.","As he approached, Noah saw the gazes of many Primordial Lifeforms turning toward him.","Hoplites in their simple togas paused their activities to stare. Lochagoi, the intermediate ranking between Hoplite and Polemarch, watched with expressions that held calculation alongside wonder.","He moved past them casually.","There was no arrogance in his bearing, but there was also no deference. He was THE Tongue Whisperer, Polemarch of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, and he had business to conduct!","The shocked gazes of others were noted but not dwelt upon.","THE Primordial Paradox floated beside him in comfortable silence, his obsidian crown spinning slowly above his head as he observed the place that bore part of his influence.","They entered the Temple of The First Tongue.","The interior was vast beyond what the exterior suggested, space folding in ways that allowed for chambers and halls that should not have fit within the temple’s apparent dimensions.","Noah proceeded toward the center of the temple.","He passed chambers where scholars debated the nature of meaning itself. He passed halls where warriors trained in the combat applications of The First Tongue, well, even though they now froze and looked toward them. He passed alcoves where beings sat in meditation, attempting to comprehend Phonemes that danced just beyond their understanding.","Eventually, he arrived at the central chamber.","Three Lochagoi stood there, their togas marking their intermediate rank as they oversaw the daily operations of the temple. They turned at his approach, their expressions shifting from routine attention to sudden alertness as they registered the Polemarch markings on his garments.","Noah was about to speak to them, when...","HUUM!","A commotion rose up behind him.","The heavy power of two Polemarchs appeared, their authority pressing against the air of the temple with weight that demanded attention. Noah turned to observe the newcomers.","The first was a muscular scholar in a refined toga. His eyes held the sharp intelligence of a being who had spent eons studying The First Tongue, and his presence radiated the authority of someone accustomed to command within these walls.","And the second was... Glossikos.","...!"]},{"number":4857,"title":"Chapter 4857: Chapter 4856: A Scheme Across Time! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes flickered with recognition that he carefully concealed behind the mask of THE Tongue Whisperer.","The dryad stood before him, her form composed of living wood and linguistic energy intertwined in ways that spoke of deep connection to both nature and language. Leaves that whispered Phonemes adorned her head like hair. Her eyes held the depth of ancient forests given the capacity for speech.","Glossikos.","One of the four Absolutes in the future within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","And yet right now, she seemed to only be at Fundamental Depth.","She looked toward Noah and THE Primordial Paradox with awe and caution in equal measure, her wooden features shifting as she processed the presence of beings whose authority far exceeded what should have been possible for mere Polemarchs.","What a wonder existence was!","Noah was seeing someone who would become an Absolute much later on in the future. He was observing Glossikos at a stage of her journey that she herself had likely forgotten across the eons that separated this moment from when he had first met her.","The sheer fact that he had seen Glossikos in the past, but he had not known it until he actually lived the past, was unfathomably unique.","When he met her in the future as THE Genesis Monarch...","Had she known that the being standing before her had once visited this place wearing a different face?","Noah shook his head calmly, dismissing the thoughts of temporal paradox. He looked toward Glossikos with the bearing of someone who had business to conduct.","\" We would like to pay a visit to THE Villa Dei Boscoreale for a quick bath, if that is acceptable.\"","His voice carried authority that transcended his apparent ranking.","Glossikos nodded in a dumbfounded manner.","She could sense their Immensity. She could feel the weight of their foundations pressing against her perception!","And she seemed to recognize THE Primordial Paradox as her eyes kept going back to him.","\" Right this way.\"","She turned and began to lead them deeper into the temple and past it, past the three Lochagoi who watched with expressions of confusion and curiosity.","Noah followed Glossikos, his mind already turning toward the next phase of his purpose here. THE Primordial Paradox walked beside him in silence.","They were here to hide a piece of an Absolute as Noah had the perfect place for it!","A lot of paradoxes and contradictions seemed to be surrounding Noah right now.","But the perfect place that he had thought of when it came to hiding something that even THE Entity would not be able to get their hands on was inside THE Villa Dei Boscoreale.","He wasn’t going there for another bath.","He had already been in this villa before. His body in the future was also actually with Glossikos at this very moment, traversing deeper into its mysteries.","THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts.","The Museum of Destiny.","This was a region that contained item-based treasures unlike anything else in Observable Existence. Unlike the first area of the Villa, the Thermae where consumption was guaranteed to provide benefits to anyone who entered, the Mouseion operated on principles of fate and worthiness.","If one was fated to receive a particular artifact, they would be drawn to it and the barriers would part. If one was not fated, the barriers remained impenetrable regardless of power level.","Even Absolutes could not force their way to artifacts not meant for them.","The rules of THE Agora applied to all, and in the Mouseion, those rules were absolute.","So what Noah had to do was actually simple.","He couldn’t help but smile devilishly when he thought about it all.","And as if THE Primordial Paradox had seen through his plan, he actually nodded at this time.","\"I have considered this as one of the possibilities.\"","His voice carried that measured precision that made every word feel deliberate.","\" But there were too many unknowns. Variables I could not account for regarding who would retrieve what I left behind, and whether they would be worthy or fated to receive it.\"","His obsidian eyes held approval.","\" You seem to have covered these unknowns. So I shall trust you, Youngest.\"","...!","As he said these words, their party had finished crossing through the different regions of THE Agora.","They had passed through temples and forums, through training grounds and meditation chambers. Glossikos had led them with the cautious energy of someone escorting beings far beyond her current comprehension, her wooden form occasionally buzzing when she sensed the full weight of the Immensity walking behind her.","And now they arrived before the gateways of THE Villa Dei Boscoreale.","The entrance was even grander than Noah remembered from his future visit. The architecture seemed more vibrant here, more alive with possibility. The stones that formed the gateway pulsed with authority that had not yet been weathered by eons of use.","Glossikos turned back toward them with caution in her eyes.","\" You simply wished to go through the cycles of refinement after arriving in THE Agora for the first time?\"","She was looking at Noah as she said this, her tone carrying the careful diplomacy of someone who suspected there was more to this visit than had been stated but didn’t dare to press.","Noah smiled calmly.","He proceeded forward without answering, stepping past the gateway as existence shifted around them. The transition was familiar now, reality bending to accommodate passage from one space to another within the complex dimensional structure of THE Villa.","He arrived once more at The Thermae of Cyclic Refinement.","The radiant pools and mist of this area seemed even grander and more ancient than before. Steam rose from waters that held the weight of refinement accumulated across eons. The architecture was pristine, untouched by the wear that would eventually dull its edges in the future Noah knew.","The figure of THE Primordial Paradox and Glossikos appeared in the same space soon after, their forms materializing from the transition with grace.","Noah turned to face Glossikos fully.","\"I came to take a bath.\"","His voice was casual, almost dismissive.","\" And also to make another contribution.\"","He paused, letting the words settle.","\"A contribution for THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts.\"","...!"]},{"number":4858,"title":"Chapter 4858: Chapter 4857: A Scheme Across Time! III","paragraphs":["His words caused Glossikos to open her eyes wide.","Her wooden features shifted with shock that she couldn’t quite conceal. Contributions to the Mouseion were not casual things. They were acts of tremendous significance, requiring items of genuine worth and the establishment of fate-bindings that would determine who could claim them across time.","She seemed to want to say many things.","Questions pressed against her expression. Concerns flickered in her ancient eyes!","But at this time, THE Primordial Paradox stepped up.","He put his hand on her shoulder.","She trembled.","The weight of an Absolute’s touch, even a gentle one, was not something that a Fundamental Depth being could easily bear. His authority pressed against her existence simply through contact, reminding her of the vast gulf that separated their levels of power.","He looked at her with his gaze of majesty.","\" Go ahead and make the preparations for us, why don’t you?\"","His voice was not unkind, but it carried finality that brooked no argument.","\" When everything is ready, let us know.\"","...!","His regal and imposing air made it abundantly clear that this was not something up for discussion.","His gaze and his hand seemed to make Glossikos unable to deny anything from him. She was a Polemarch, one of the highest-ranked beings in THE Agora, and yet before THE Primordial Paradox, she was nothing more than an entity receiving orders.","She only nodded like a cautious rabbit.","Then she floated deeper past the pools, heading toward the Mouseion to prepare whatever protocols were necessary for a contribution of this magnitude.","THE Primordial Paradox sighed as she departed.","The sound was heavy with exhaustion he had been concealing. With Glossikos gone, some of the imperious mask slipped, revealing the tiredness that lurked beneath.","He stretched with movements that seemed almost mortal, as if he were a tired old man.","Then he began to walk over toward the Pool of Lethe.","The same pool that Noah had entered during his future visit. The waters that could wash away the accumulated weight of existence!","THE Primordial Paradox entered the pool with the ease of someone who had done this countless times before. His obsidian form sank into the churning waters, steam rising around him as he leaned back in a position of grand relaxation. His arms spread across the pool’s edge. His obsidian crown continued to spin slowly above his head even as the rest of him submerged.","He looked like an emperor taking his leisure after a long campaign.","Noah raised his brows and followed.","When he entered the same pool in the future, he hadn’t realized that he had actually done it before. He hadn’t known that his first visit to these waters had been in the company of THE Primordial Paradox himself, eons before his birth.","The temporal loops continued to compound.","As he sank into the churning waters of the pool, feeling the familiar sensation of the Pool of Lethe working against his foundations, THE Primordial Paradox waved his hands.","WAA!","Something emerged from within his obsidian form.","A dodecahedron.","It pulsed with a terrifying air of power, its twelve pentagonal faces each burning with different aspects of Paradox that shouldn’t have been able to coexist. Unfathomable waves of authority radiated from it, pressing against Noah’s perception with weight that made his Seals tremble.","THE Primordial Paradox threw it toward Noah as if it were nothing.","As if he hadn’t just manifested a piece of his own existence and tossed it across a bathing pool!","\" This is the most critical part of me.\"","His voice was calm despite the magnitude of what he had just done.","\" The part that is not infected by that thing.\"","He sank deeper into the waters, steam curling around his obsidian features.","\"I shall still make it appear as though I am creating other contingencies. I shall give parts of myself to my disciples. One even to Erwin.\"","His eyes held ancient knowing.","\" He will undoubtedly find all of them and consume them to grasp my Claim. That is inevitable. That is what he has designed his methodology to accomplish.\"","He nodded toward the dodecahedron in Noah’s hands.","\" But that, right there, can lay dormant for as long as it needs to. Until you can reclaim it in the future.\"","His voice grew harder.","\"Erwin will effectively usurp my Claim to Paradox. But that is going to be a temporary thing.\"","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that made the Pool of Lethe’s waters still.","\" The moment that I am back, I will need to discipline my old disciple...\"","His obsidian eyes burned!","\" And also address this weapon that he used. This methodology that even he should not fully understand.\"","...!","The words of THE Primordial Paradox were terrifying in their implications.","He wasn’t accepting his collapse as an ending!","He was treating it as an inconvenience. A temporary setback that would be rectified once Noah retrieved what was being entrusted to him. THE Living Paradox, who had held the Claim for eons, who had reshaped Observable Existence through THE Fallout, who stood among THE Four as one of the most powerful beings in all of reality...","Was going to be disciplined by his former master.","Noah grasped the dodecahedron.","He felt its Immensity and weight pressing against his foundations. This was not just a piece of THE Primordial Paradox. This was the core of him. The essence that defined what Paradox truly meant before Erwin had corrupted it with whatever methodology he had employed.","|Artifact Analysis|","| Object classification: Existential Core Fragment|","|Designation: The Antinomia Prismatica|","| The Paradox of Self-Contained Totality|","|This dodecahedron contains the uninfected essence of THE Primordial Paradox|","|Each of its twelve faces represents a fundamental aspect of Paradox that existed before corruption|","|Face One: The Paradox of Beginning and Ending|","|Face Two: The Paradox of Self and Other|","|Face Three: The Paradox of Truth and Falsity|","|Face Four: The Paradox of Motion and Stillness|","|Face Five: The Paradox of Whole and Part|","|Face Six: The Paradox of Cause and Effect|","|Face Seven: The Paradox of Being and Becoming|","|Face Eight: The Paradox of Knowledge and Ignorance|","|Face Nine: The Paradox of Freedom and Necessity|","|Face Ten: The Paradox of Finite and Infinite|","|Face Eleven: The Paradox of Unity and Multiplicity|","|Face Twelve: The Paradox of Existence and Non-Existence|","|Together, these twelve aspects form the complete foundation of what Paradox was meant to be|","|This is THE Primordial Paradox in his truest form|","|Compressed and preserved against the infection that claimed the rest of his existence|","|Historical significance: If this object is retrieved and activated, it could theoretically restore THE Primordial Paradox...|","|THE Living Paradox would no longer be the sole holder of the Paradox Claim. How...would that work?|","...!","It was a surreal thing to hold.","The weight of an Absolute’s core existence resting in his palms.","Noah began to wrap it in waves of Undifferentiated Fate. He added Philologies, linguistic structures that would preserve and conceal. He wove Archai of The First Tongue even!","Layer after layer of protection, even if it wasn’t needed but...he was basically branding his signature!"]},{"number":4859,"title":"Chapter 4859: Chapter 4858: A Scheme Across Time! IV","paragraphs":["As he worked, he thought about what was happening.","When he had finished his refinements in his past, Glossikos had taken his signature into THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts for the item that would be destined for him. But she had never retrieved it because moments later, he had collapsed THE Weavers, who were actually the disciples of THE Primordial Paradox.","It was only after that confrontation that he had returned.","And he had another body of his currently in THE Mouseion at this very moment, about to look for his destined item.","But it would not be anything put there by destiny or fate.","It was his choice to do what he was currently doing right now that led to it.","There would be no treasured item or ancient artifact for him to claim apart from what he put there himself, eons ago.","The fated item was fated because he had chosen to place it there.","The destiny was fulfilled because he had created the destiny.","\"...\"","What a glorious Weaving of Existence this was!","A closed temporal loop where the treasure he was destined to find was the treasure he himself had hidden. Where the fate that guided him was the fate he had established. Where the worthiness that allowed him access was worthiness he had defined through his own actions.","As he was thinking all of this, the figure of THE Primordial Paradox sank even more into the bubbling pool they were in. His obsidian form was nearly submerged now, only his head and crown remaining above the waters of Lethe.","He let out a sigh of contentment.","\" Existence is always grand and full of wonders.\"","His voice was soft now, contemplative.","\"I will effectively be collapsed soon. That much is certain. Erwin’s methodology is too thorough, too well-designed. Even knowing what he is doing, I cannot fully prevent it.\"","He paused, letting the waters work against his existence.","\" But before I am collapsed, I shall continue my battle and my study of the weapon that Erwin used.\"","His obsidian eyes found Noah’s.","\" You came here seeking answers regarding that weapon. Regarding the thing that would eventually become...what did you call it? THE Entity?\"","He smiled, and there was something sad in it.","\" But I can only tell you that I am the answer. When I collapse, I will know more. The very act of being consumed by his methodology will teach me things that cannot be learned any other way.\"","His smile deepened.","\" What I already know now, I shall share with you when you retrieve that little part of me.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox was planning to learn from his own death and to use his collapse as a research opportunity.","To study the weapon that was killing him from the inside, and then encode that knowledge into the fragment that Noah would retrieve eons later.","It was the most paradoxical response to defeat that Noah could imagine.","And it was perfectly fitting for the being who held the Claim to Paradox itself!","Noah continued wrapping the object in his hands with his Immensity.","Very quickly, the Antinomia Prismatica became enveloped inside a blue-gold treasure chest surrounded by waves of The First Tongue. The dodecahedron’s terrifying aura was contained within layers of linguistic authority!","The chest looked ancient despite having just been created.","It looked like something that had always existed!","Noah put aside the treasure chest containing the Antinomia Prismatica as he also enjoyed the Pool of Lethe for a second time.","The waters worked against his foundations with familiar weight.","He and THE Primordial Paradox lounged in The Thermae of Cyclic Refinement as steam curled around their forms.","In the silence, Noah asked what he was curious about from the words THE Primordial Paradox had spoken before.","\" You talked a lot about how the Scales of Existence are designed with hardship.\"","His voice was contemplative and seeking understanding.","\" How one has to have adversity if they ever wish to reach the second Scale of Existence.\"","He turned slightly in the churning waters to face the lounging Absolute.","\" What more do you know about all of this? About the Vakochev Scales of Existence?\"","THE Primordial Paradox did not even open his eyes at the question.","He replied calmly.","\"If you were to literally be standing before the gateway to THE Second Scale of Existence...\"","He paused, letting the words settle.","\"If the Way that you follow, if the Civilization that you have built, has not weathered through waves of Immensity and hardship. If your foundation is something that you passed through haphazardly, without true adversity...\"","His voice grew heavier.","\"A doorway that seems right in front of you will be uncrossable.\"","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that made Noah’s foundations tremble.","\"I know this because when you get close, you sense it. You understand it.\"","When you get close.","The words were terrifying and grand to hear.","THE Primordial Paradox had sensed what was required and understood why hardship was not merely recommended but fundamentally necessary!","THE Primordial Paradox continued, his eyes still closed as the waters of Lethe worked against his infected existence.","\" As for the Vakochev Scales of Existence... well, they are-\"","\"It’s ready.\"","HUUM!","The voice of Glossikos interrupted the words of THE Primordial Paradox.","The dryad had returned from the Mouseion, her wooden form appearing at the edge of the pool with the nervous energy of someone who desperately wished she hadn’t had to interrupt but had no choice. The preparations were complete!","THE Primordial Paradox opened his eyes and blinked toward her.","Noah also turned to her sharply for interrupting the conversation.","This future Absolute entity felt like she was being stared at by two predators as her wooden features paled. The weight of two beings whose Immensity far exceeded anything she had encountered pressed against her existence simply through their attention","She looked like she wanted to sink into the floor and disappear!","But THE Primordial Paradox simply nodded toward Noah.","\" Go do what you must.\"","His voice was calm, showing no irritation at the interruption.","\" This is where I stop.\"","...!","His words ended there.","But Noah heard the deep voice of THE Primordial Paradox in his mind.","Words sent only for him to perceive!","’ Do what you must. At this moment, you have My Everything.’","BOOM!","My Everything.","THE Primordial Paradox had given Noah the totality of his uninfected self!","The closed temporal loop ensured that no one else could claim what was meant for him. THE Entity could search across eons. THE Living Paradox could consume every contingency he discovered. It wouldn’t matter!","With such heavy words resonating in his mind, Noah rose from the Pool of Lethe.","Waters cascaded from his transformed form, his wings spreading as he stepped onto the edge of the pool. The crown of burning books above his head blazed with renewed intensity.","And a blue-gold treasure chest rose beside him.","It followed after him like a loyal companion, hovering at his side as he turned toward where Glossikos waited!"]},{"number":4860,"title":"Chapter 4860: Chapter 4859: The Crack Of Observable Existence I","paragraphs":["THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts was a unique place.","When Noah arrived, he found himself standing on a golden river that seemed to be flowing forward endlessly. The current moved beneath his feet without disturbing his balance, carrying him nowhere while simultaneously carrying him everywhere.","All around him was a stellar environment that held sparkling multicolored lights etched across the expanse as if they were stars scattered by a guiding hand. They burned with colors that shouldn’t have coexisted, crimson beside azure beside gold beside shades that had no names in any language.","Each of these supposed stars had strings they were connected to.","These strings extended outward to the edge of perception itself, gossamer threads of fate that linked artifacts to destinies, treasures to those worthy of claiming them. The entire Mouseion was a web of predetermined connections, a place where what was meant to be found would be found by those meant to find it.","Behind him, the figure of Glossikos looked at him with an inquisitive gaze.","\" All of us study and revere The First Tongue.\"","Her voice was musical.","\" It is rare to find someone like you who calls themselves THE Tongue Whisperer. One who has mastered what we spend eons merely attempting to comprehend.\"","She gestured toward the stellar expanse around them.","\" Because we revere The First Tongue, myself and a few others take care of THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts. Over time, we came to understand a few of its secrets.\"","Her wooden features held something like pride.","\" If anyone is fated for anything in here, they release a glimmer of their Civilization. If they are fated with anything, it comes down for them. The strings part. The barriers dissolve. What is meant to be claimed descends into waiting hands.\"","She paused.","\" We tried to contribute ourselves and found that we gained merit points whenever we added things to this place that are claimed. The method to do that is right there.\"","She pointed toward an area to the side of the golden river.","An elevated pedestal rose from the flowing current, its base somehow anchored despite the endless movement beneath it. Atop the pedestal was a swirling golden platform that churned with authority similar to the river itself but concentrated, focused, purposeful.","It looked like an altar.","An altar where offerings could be made to fate itself.","Hah!","Noah walked up to it as his treasure chest followed behind him, the blue-gold container hovering faithfully at his side. He came to stand before the elevated pedestal on the edge of the golden river, and the moment he stood before it, information flowed into his existence.","|Mouseion Protocol Detected|","|THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts is a place where merit can be granted depending on anything contributed|","|The merit is awarded only when what has been contributed is claimed by the one that is fated|","|If nobody fated claims it, no merit will be awarded|","|The contribution will remain in the Mouseion until its fated recipient arrives|","|This could be moments. This could be eons. Time is irrelevant to fate|","|Place what you wish to contribute on the pedestal, and it shall be included in the vaults of THE Mouseion|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone sharply at this.","He didn’t waste too much time.","He proceeded to wave his hands, and the treasure chest behind him came forward at his command. It floated over the golden river, past his position, and landed on the golden platform with weight that made the pedestal tremble.","The Antinomia Prismatica.","The uninfected core of THE Primordial Paradox.","Hidden inside layers of Undifferentiated Fate and Philologies and Archai of The First Tongue.","Waiting to be claimed by the one fated to receive it.","Waiting to be claimed by Noah himself, eons from now!","Everything shimmered in golden light.","The platform blazed with radiance that painted the stellar environment in shades of pure authority. The strings that connected the countless stars above trembled as if acknowledging the arrival of something significant. Something that would change the nature of fate itself within this space.","A golden string fell down from the endless skyscape above.","It descended with purpose, with inevitability, with the weight of destiny given physical form. The string connected with the treasure chest, wrapping around it like a gentle embrace from existence itself.","Moments later, the chest got pulled up.","It rose from the pedestal, following the golden string toward the stellar expanse above. Higher and higher it climbed, becoming smaller and smaller until it was just another point of light among countless others.","Then it disappeared into oblivion.","Gone!","Hidden among the infinite artifacts of THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts.","Noah didn’t feel any sense of panic as he watched it disappear.","He knew where it was going. He knew who would claim it. He knew that the fated recipient was himself, and that the fate binding it to him was a fate he had created through his own choices.","He turned around calmly.","The figure of the future Absolute, Glossikos, raised her brows. She looked at him with an expression that mixed curiosity and confusion in equal measure.","\" Do you not wish to release the light of your Civilization to see if you have anything fated in here?\"","Her question was reasonable.","Most beings who contributed to THE Mouseion immediately checked to see if anything was fated for them in return. It was common courtesy to oneself. A chance at claiming treasures that destiny had prepared.","At such words, Noah smiled.","\"I will come claim what is fated for me later on.\"","His voice held knowing that transcended what should have been possible.","\" Who knows. Perhaps at that point in time, you will also be there to witness it.\"","BOOM!","He said these words cryptically.","He knew his other body in the distant, distant future was with Glossikos at this very moment. That version of himself was entering THE Mouseion, preparing to claim something that he believed destiny had prepared for him.","And it had.","Just not in the way anyone would expect.","But the Glossikos here shook her head as if she was staring at a crazy person.","Noah didn’t explain.","He took a step backward, leaving the domain of THE Mouseion without even bothering to look around. The stellar environment faded. The golden river disappeared beneath his feet. The countless strings of fate retreated from his perception.","He returned to The Thermae of Cyclic Refinement!"]},{"number":4861,"title":"Chapter 4861: Chapter 4860: The Crack Of Observable Existence II","paragraphs":["There, the figure of THE Primordial Paradox floated up from the Pool of Lethe.","He stretched his obsidian body as if he had enjoyed a good rest, movements that seemed almost casual despite the weight of authority that surrounded him. His obsidian crown spun with renewed vigor above his head.","He looked toward Noah with eyes that held satisfaction.","\" Alrighty. With that done, we have to make our way to a fun place.\"","He turned toward Glossikos, who had followed Noah back from THE Mouseion with confusion still etched across her wooden features.","\" Little Glossikos, thank you for the aid.\"","His tone was almost gentle.","\" In the future, when you see Erwin, THE Living Paradox, pass through here...\"","He paused, and something ancient moved behind his obsidian eyes.","\"Tell him this: Existence is vast and unpredictable. Existence is vast... and full of terrors.\"","...!","With such incomprehensible words, THE Primordial Paradox waved his hands.","Obsidian-gold light wrapped around him and Noah. The Thermae of Cyclic Refinement blurred. THE Villa Dei Boscoreale faded.","The two of them disappeared.","They left behind a confused and frustrated Glossikos who seemed to have many questions and no one remaining to answer them.","---","In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","Past The Middle City, the Meso Polis, where Lochagoi and their households resided in structures that spoke of earned status and accumulated merit.","In The Acropolis.","The highest district, accessible only to Polemarchs and above.","Noah arrived in the corner of such a place as obsidian-gold light faded around his form. He saw glorious temples and structures in the distance, architecture that made the lower regions of THE Agora seem humble by comparison. This was where the true powers of this Nexus resided. Where decisions that shaped fate itself were made.","But the area THE Primordial Paradox had taken him was shrouded in shadows.","Massive stone pillars rose around them as if they were spears thrust into the ground to keep reality still. They formed a loose circle around a specific point, ancient monuments that radiated authority designed to contain rather than support.","Here, Noah actually sensed four auras.","Four Polemarchs standing before something.","A tiny crack in space.","It looked like barely a sliver. A hairline fracture in the fabric of reality that someone less observant might even miss. It was so small, so seemingly insignificant, that it could have been mistaken for a trick of the light.","And yet four Polemarchs surrounded it with expressions that spoke of dedicated guardianship.","Noah recognized three of them.","Paradoxos stood to one side, his form radiating the essence of contradiction that would eventually elevate him to Absolute status. Khaotikos stood opposite, his shifting presence barely contained within a humanoid shape. Ontikos stood between them, his bearing speaking of Existence itself given awareness.","These three, alongside Glossikos, would be the Four Strategoi in the future.","The four Absolutes who would oversee THE Agora of Primordial Judgment in Noah’s era.","And now, three of them were protecting this place at the rank of Polemarch.","The fourth guardian was an entity Noah hadn’t seen before. A scholarly old man whose form seemed composed of accumulated knowledge given flesh. His eyes held the weight of questions asked across eons, and his presence radiated an authority different from the others.","All four of them had frowning looks when they stared at the arrivals.","\"...\"","Beside Noah, THE Primordial Paradox was calm.","He began to walk forward, his obsidian form moving with the casual authority of someone who had every right to be here.","\" THE Agora of Primordial Judgment is a small Nexus Primordial Realm inside Ginnungagap.\"","His voice carried to Noah alone, pitched for private conversation despite the guardians watching their approach.","\" Here, one of the Cracks of Observable Existence exists.\"","He gestured toward the tiny fracture in space.","\" Through it lies the place where the enemy you came here for may have originated. The place where THE First Cause may have, or should have, bloomed from.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" Where THE Spark that initiated differentiation bloomed. Where the question of the oldest paradox of Existence was first asked.\"","...!","BOOM!","The words crashed against Noah’s consciousness with weight!","THE First Cause.","THE Spark of Differentiation.","The Oldest Paradox of Existence.","He was standing before a crack that led to the origin of everything. To the moment before Observable Existence became observable!","It was right there.","Behind a crack so small most beings would never notice it existed!","The words that THE Primordial Paradox had spoken were unfathomably grand, each one pressing against Noah’s understanding of reality itself. He had many questions, so many questions that they threatened to overflow!","He would have preferred if this was the time when ancient beings like THE Primordial Paradox became particularly talkative and went on minute-long tangents about what they meant regarding everything.","Take as long as you needed to explain what THE First Cause was, big guy.","Stand still and give as lengthy a monologue as you wanted about THE Spark and everything else.","But alas...","THE Primordial Paradox chose to shut up.","His obsidian form moved forward with measured grace, approaching the Crack and subsequently the ones protecting it. The four Polemarchs who stood guard shifted their attention from the tiny fracture in space to the beings approaching them.","Paradoxos looked shocked and reverent, the entity whose very existence radiated contradiction immediately recognizing THE Primordial Paradox. His response was instinctive as he bowed toward THE Primordial Paradox with the deference of someone standing before the source of everything their Civilization represented.","But Ontikos and Khaotikos frowned with expressions that held something other than reverence, something that looked almost like disapproval.","Khaotikos was the one to speak.","\" Sir Paradox.\"","His voice shifted with every syllable, never quite settling on a single tone.","\" The agreement was made for us to never unnecessarily enter unless we absolutely need to. The dangers of that place and what could emerge from it...\"","He paused, his form rippling with barely contained turbulence.","\" We decided that it was not worth the risk to all of Observable Existence.\"","Khaotikos had only just begun to speak when THE Primordial Paradox raised his hand calmly.","\"I do not answer to you all. Move aside.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4862,"title":"Chapter 4862: Chapter 4861: THE Prima Indiferrentia I","paragraphs":["His words were measured and precise and utterly without heat or emotion, filled with an undeniable Immensity that pressed against the four guardians with weight!","This wasn’t a request or even a command, but simply a statement of fact regarding what would happen next.","The four entities before them had their gazes flicker and change, calculation giving way to resentment before settling into acceptance and finally resignation.","They moved aside an instant later.","Noah watched this exchange with eyes that took in every subtle shift in expression and posture.","He remembered how Glossikos and the other Strategoi felt about THE Four in the future. They’d visibly shown their distaste, and Glossikos had said that THE Four did whatever they wanted and then left the rest of them, the rest of Existence, to pick up the pieces.","One example was THE Creature and his Belly of Existence, where he’d literally imprisoned every single THE classification entity from THE Infinite Unfurling.","Another example was THE Living Paradox and THE Loom and THE Fallout.","An apocalypse that had reshaped Observable Existence and destroyed realms beyond counting, all in pursuit of whatever goals THE Living Paradox had deemed important enough to justify such devastation.","It seemed like there were other examples throughout Existence where those who had made the Claims continued to do whatever they wished, and others who were knowledgeable truly didn’t like this arrangement.","And now, with the information that he had, Noah could also add another action of THE Four that was done, and now all of Observable Existence was being forced to deal with the consequences.","THE Primordial Paradox had just stated that THE Entity might have its origins in this place, so Erwin, THE Living Paradox, should have entered at some point and emerged with something relating to THE Entity. A methodology or a weapon or something that he’d used to consume his own master.","And now, in the future, all of Observable Existence was about to pay for it.","THE Four sucked!","Of course, himself not included.","Although he might be biased in thinking this.","Noah smiled as he wondered about his own actions and how all of Observable Existence was or would be affected due to them. His most recent significant action was expanding The First Tongue across Observable Existence and setting Existential Tariffs for those utilizing The First Tongue as they drew upon its authority.","Which reminded him that in the future, he needed to increase the percentages of the tariffs since his power had grown much more compared to before. The rates he’d set were appropriate for his previous level of authority, but now they could be adjusted upward to better reflect his current standing.","As he thought about all of this, he smiled and nodded to the figures of the four guardians protecting the Crack of Observable Existence before he and THE Primordial Paradox passed into it.","And this time, the sensation was truly grand.","Noah felt like he was passing through The Interstices, as if he was traversing spaces between spaces or going from literally one definition to another definition entirely. As if the Existence he was just in was defined one way, and the Existence he was entering on the other side was defined in an entirely different manner.","Or perhaps not defined at all.","And...","\" Oh boy...\"","He couldn’t help but utter out as he felt his entire existence buzz with sensations that defied easy description.","It was as if invisible pores opened up across every aspect of his being while extremely pure concentrations of Civilizational Authority crashed in all around him with such terrifying force that any Fundamental Depth entity may have been crushed into paste.","The pressure was immense and overwhelming, the weight of potential itself pressing against his foundations with hunger that wanted to remake him.","But he had his already established an Apophasis.","He was not limited by the weight that crashed against him, and his existence was not incapable of bearing that which sought to overwhelm it, and he was not collapsible under the Immensity of what he was experiencing.","The negations held, and he barely felt a glimmer of pressure. Instead, he felt a steady flow of Immensity that was transformed into infinite potential, which flowed into his grandiose foundations like water into an ocean that had been waiting to receive it.","|Environmental Analysis - Critical Location Detected|","|You are arriving in a place filled with Civilizational Authority that is not clearly defined under differentiation or undifferentiation|","|It is paradoxical and chaotic and existential and differential in nature simultaneously|","| The authority here provides a steady influx of proto-matter as infinite potential just by being within this space|","|Your foundations are experiencing passive enhancement simply through exposure|","|More significantly: The doorway stopping your advancement past Perfect Speaker of The First Tongue is loosening|","|It is beginning to take in an influx of undefined differentiation of all four aspects of the oldest paradox|","|The First Tongue, Chaos, Paradox, and Existence are flooding into your linguistic foundations without distinction|","|You have crossed a Crack of Observable Existence|","| You have arrived in THE Prima Indifferentia|","|My analytical capabilities are somewhat compromised in this environment|","|The concepts I use to process information are differentiated concepts|","|The proto-matter is actively attempting to undifferentiate them|","...!","The information came in waves as Noah found himself settling into a chaotic and glorious environment.","THE Prima Indifferentia.","The first sensation was one of overwhelming potential, not overwhelming in the way that danger was overwhelming or in the way that power was overwhelming, but overwhelming in the way that possibility was overwhelming. The sense that anything could happen here because nothing had yet committed to happening pressed against him from every direction!","The space appeared as an endless expanse of churning proto-matter that held every color and no color simultaneously.","Noah’s eyes tried to process what they were seeing and found themselves unable to settle on any single interpretation as the expanse before him shifted between crimson and gold and azure and black, being all of these things and none of these things.","Shapes formed and dissolved before they could be recognized, with a mountain beginning to rise in the distance as its peaks stretched toward a sky that didn’t exist, only for it to simply stop being a mountain and become something else entirely. A wave, perhaps, or a forest, or a concept that had no visual representation but his mind tried to show him anyway.","Sounds existed as possibilities rather than actualities, and he could hear music that wasn’t playing alongside voices speaking words that hadn’t been invented and the roar of storms that might occur if the proto-matter decided to become storms. Every potential sound layered over every other potential sound, creating a symphony of almost-noise that filled his perception without ever truly resolving into anything specific.","The ground beneath his feet was a concept that hadn’t fully committed to being ground, sometimes supporting his weight with solidity that allowed him to stand, and then without warning wavering as it decided it might prefer to be sky instead.","Noah found himself suspended in orientations that shifted based on which fundamental forces happened to be dominant at that particular moment, standing and floating and falling upward and being none of these things all at once.","The sky was similarly uncommitted, positioned above and below and possibly inside his own existence looking out rather than being looked at.","Everything felt colorful and yet not, and due to the immense influx of Civilizational Authority all around, storms of surging mist and authorities churned nearby with visual noise so dense and overwhelming that even Noah couldn’t perceive more than a few meters in any direction.","Beyond that threshold, the proto-matter became too thick to see through and too undefined to process!","This was the place where THE First Cause bloomed!"]},{"number":4863,"title":"Chapter 4863: Chapter 4862: THE Prima Indifferentia II","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Paradox looked around, and the proto-matter near him seemed to calm slightly, recognizing something familiar in his presence.","\" Beyond the Crack of Observable Existence lies something that predates existence itself.\"","He reached out and let the churning substance flow through his obsidian fingers, strands of undefined potential shifting through every possible color before dripping back into the greater mass.","\" It is THE Prima Indifferentia, the First Undifferentiation, the state that was before anything was sorted into categories. Before Observable and Unobservable separated, before Chaos and Order distinguished themselves, before Existence knew it existed.\"","He withdrew his hand, and the proto-matter clung to him reluctantly before releasing its grip.","\" Proto-matter is the technical designation for this substance, and most beings who glimpse it assume it is merely chaotic refuse, the detritus of pre-existence. They are catastrophically incorrect. Proto-matter is undifferentiated Civilizational Authority, holding within itself the potential to manifest as any of the four aspects of the oldest paradox with equal probability. A single grain contains the seed of Phonemes not yet spoken, Chaos not yet unleashed, Paradoxes not yet formed, and Existence not yet actualised.\"","The proto-matter around them brightened as he spoke of its potential, as if pleased to be understood.","\" This is why THE Prima Indifferentia is simultaneously the most valuable and most dangerous location in all of reality. When proto-matter floods into a sufficiently defined existence, that existence can direct the undifferentiated authority toward whichever aspect they wish to strengthen, and the versatility is absolute because the substance itself has made no commitments regarding what it shall become.\"","He began to walk through the churning expanse, his form leaving ripples that spread outward before being absorbed back into the undefined mass.","\" Resources of incalculable value can be harvested here, including Spark Fragments that contain echoes of THE First Cause, Pre-Phonemic Resonance that can be refined into Phonemes, Contradiction Cores that embody paradoxes from before Paradox itself differentiated, and Pure Possibility that grants access to Chaos in its most fundamental state.\"","The proto-matter darkened as his tone shifted.","\" However, proto-matter does not merely possess the quality of becoming but possesses equally the quality of unbecoming. It exists in a state prior to differentiation, and that state actively resists differentiation the way fire consumes fuel rather than the way water resists being shaped. When it floods into an existence, it does not merely offer the opportunity to become more but simultaneously exerts pressure to become less, to undifferentiate, to dissolve back into the formless potential from which all things emerged.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he listened since THE Primordial Paradox had actually gone into lengthy explanation mode.","\" THE Prima Indifferentia has collapsed Absolutes because of its makeup and the things that have risen due to it. There are entities that were never differentiated in the first place, known as THE Undivided Ones, who existed before existence differentiated and refused to participate in the process. They remain undivided, undefined, and unlimited, possessing no qualities because qualities require differentiation and having no form because form requires distinction between self and environment. They are simply potential that never actualised, and they are functionally invincible against any attack that relies upon differentiated concepts.\"","The churning proto-matter around them seemed to grow more agitated at the mention of THE Undivided Ones, as if even this undifferentiated substance feared what lurked in its depths.","\" There are many more things as well, some that I know and much more that I probably do not know since even I cannot claim comprehensive understanding regarding this place.\"","His obsidian crown spun with weight that spoke of ancient experience.","\" This is the place for the big boys and the big players, and THE Creature seems to like this place a great deal.\"","...!","A place for the big boys and the big players.","Noah only felt immensity and wonder at the thought of this place as the proto-matter continued to churn around them, storms of undefined potential pressing against his existence while simultaneously flowing into his foundations. He turned to THE Primordial Paradox with curiosity burning in his eyes.","\" You said Absolutes have been collapsed in this place. Who? How?\"","THE Primordial Paradox paused in his walking, his obsidian form becoming still amidst the churning chaos. The proto-matter around him seemed to calm in response, creating a pocket of relative stability where his words could be heard clearly.","\" THE Absolute Sovereign of Distant Flames entered THE Prima Indifferentia approximately seven hundred years before THE Infinite Unfurling’s current iteration.\"","His voice held that precise diction, each word deliberately chosen.","\" His Foundation was substantial. His Civilization was well-defined. His Way had been established through genuine hardship. By all conventional metrics, he possessed sufficient weight to navigate these waters.\"","He paused, and the proto-matter around them darkened slightly.","\" He lasted forty-seven cycles of what we might loosely call time here.\"","The words hung in the undefined air.","\" On the forty-eighth cycle, he encountered an Undifferentiation Tide whilst simultaneously being approached by one of THE Undivided Ones. The combination proved insurmountable. His existence began to fragment. His definition began to blur. His Civilization, his Way, his Foundation, all of it dissolved into the proto-matter as if it had never differentiated in the first place.\"","THE Primordial Paradox’s obsidian eyes held something that might have been distant memory.","\" He did not die. Death requires the concept of ending, which is a differentiated concept. He became something far worse.\"","The proto-matter churned with agitation at whatever was being remembered.","\" He became one of THE Formless Terrors.\"","BOOM!","The designation landed with weight that made Noah’s foundations buzz.","\" Entities that were once Absolutes but who lost their definition entirely. They now drift through THE Prima Indifferentia as masses of undefined potential, attacking anything that possesses definition because definition itself has become intolerable to them. They seek to undifferentiate others because they themselves were undifferentiated.\"","His voice grew colder.","\" It is not malice. It is something more fundamental than malice. It is the natural behaviour of undifferentiated existence encountering differentiated existence.\"","He turned to face Noah directly.","\" THE Absolute Sovereign of Distant Flames is still in there. What remains of him, which is everything and nothing simultaneously. He cannot be reasoned with. He cannot be defeated in any conventional sense. He can only be avoided.\"","The proto-matter seemed to press closer, as if curious about the story being told.","\" And he is not alone.\"","His obsidian crown spun slowly above his head.","\" THE Prima Indifferentia contains at least seven known former Absolutes who suffered similar fates across the eons. Each one represents a cautionary exemplum regarding what occurs when definition erodes beyond the threshold of recovery.\"","...!","Noah was listening to these words intently as his existence continued to draw in the proto-matter flowing all around them.","It was grand and dangerous at the same time, this place that pushed everything toward undifferentiation. But as he considered the warnings and the fates of those who had come before, a thought began to form in his mind.","In all of Existence, could he be considered among those closest to undifferentiation with The First Tongue?","It was the Existential language before everything specialized into different expressions. The foundation upon which all other linguistic authority had been built. And he didn’t just hold The First Tongue, he held the Archai of Undifferentiated Tongue and the Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate.","He already had many aspects of his existence that touched upon undifferentiation in ways that others couldn’t claim.","Perhaps this place wasn’t as dangerous to him as it would be to-","BZZT!","At this time, the chaotic seas of proto-matter swirling around them in this region paused.","The churning stopped. The undefined potential that had been flowing in lazy currents went still. And then, as if responding to something Noah hadn’t consciously done, the proto-matter raged and flooded into his body with force that transcended anything he had experienced since arriving.","THE Primordial Paradox raised his brows and turned to him in surprise, seeing Noah had frozen in place with proto-matter streaming into his existence from every direction. His obsidian features shifted with concern that looked unfamiliar on such an ancient face.","\" Youngest?\"","...!","Yet Noah continued staring ahead as if he was frozen, his eyes wide and unseeing as something profound occurred within his foundations. The proto-matter around him had begun to spiral, forming a vortex with his existence at the center, drawing in undefined potential at rates that should not have been possible.","THE Primordial Paradox frowned and instantly moved toward Noah, his obsidian form cutting through the churning proto-matter with authority that demanded compliance.","But at that time...","BOOM!","As if everything around Noah had become a tinderbox waiting for a spark, everything exploded.","Everything.","Proto-matter congealed and detonated into a terrifying storm that held the weight of multiple Embodiments, undefined potential transforming into raw force that expanded outward in all directions. THE Primordial Paradox moved instantly, exerting terrifying power as he forced everything to paradoxically calm, imposing definitions of stillness and stability onto substance that rejected such concepts.","The explosion should have continued. It should have expanded across this region of THE Prima Indifferentia and caused devastation that would have echoed for eons.","But THE Primordial Paradox was one of THE Four, and his authority over Paradox was absolute.","The proto-matter settled.","The storms calmed.","And when the chaos cleared...","\"...Bollocks.\"","THE Primordial Paradox cursed.","The figure of Noah... was nowhere to be seen.","THE Primordial Paradox stood alone in a region of THE Prima Indifferentia that now bore the scars of whatever had just occurred, undefined potential slowly reforming around him as it filled the void left by the explosion. His obsidian eyes scanned the churning expanse, searching for any trace of the being he had brought here.","Nothing.","He had been left alone moments after bringing The First Tongue into THE Prima Indifferentia!"]},{"number":4864,"title":"Chapter 4864: Chapter 4863: THE Prima Indifferentia III","paragraphs":["Across THE Prima Indifferentia, in regions that had no fixed location because location was a differentiated concept, storms of proto-matter raged with intensity that drew the attention of things that should not have been capable of attention.","Noah’s body was carried through these erupting storms, tossed and flung across undefined space by currents of potential that seemed to have been spurred into activity everywhere he passed. The proto-matter wasn’t just flowing into him anymore, it was hunting him, chasing him, drawn to something in his existence that it desperately wanted to consume or transform or undifferentiate.","And it did so with fervor.","His existence was drawing in an immense amount of it, more than should have been possible, more than any Fundamental Depth entity should have been able to absorb without dissolving entirely. He felt like his entire mind was buzzing with static that erased thoughts before they could fully form, as if he was being undefined and undifferentiated with every passing moment.","His sense of self blurred at the edges. His memories became less certain. His name felt like something he had heard once but couldn’t quite recall.","But at his most undifferentiated, at the moment when it seemed like he would become just another cautionary tale of an entity who had ventured too deep and lost themselves to the proto-matter...","HUUM!","A blue light shone in the depths of his existence.","A Grimoire fluttered inside his head, pages turning with purpose that transcended the chaos surrounding it. An Organ of Civilization pulsed alongside it, beating with rhythm that refused to be undefined.","And something else awakened.","Something that had always been there but had never been tested like this.","Something infinite .","|Critical Existential Event Detected|","|In an induced state of undifferentiation, the aspect of your Infinite Mana cannot undergo any further undifferentiation and triggered a unique state of stasis|","|Infinity is already undefined by nature|","|It has no boundaries to blur|","|It has no definition to erode|","|It simply is what it is, endlessly|","| But the effort to undefine infinity has caused an unknown reaction|","|The aspect of infinity within your existence is pulsing and spreading its musings due to the proto-matter flooding your foundations|","|In an effort to undifferentiate your existence, proto-matter is carrying your aspect of Infinity and amplifying it since it cannot undergo further undifferentiation, and seeking to impose changes through it since it is the only undifferentiated thing protecting you|","|In turn, your spreading infinity is permeating across all aspects of your being|","|This aspect seeks to impose itself on all core areas of your existence|","| The Derivative Civilization of Hunger is being bathed by waves of Infinity|","|The Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate is being bathed by waves of Infinity|","|Your existence has begun to burn with multiple infinities|","|Master, I don’t fully understand what’s happening, but it appears that instead of being undifferentiated, you are becoming more infinite|","|The proto-matter cannot make you less defined|","|So it is making your infinity more...expansive|","...!","Noah’s mind buzzed as he wanted to move.","He really did.","He wanted to stabilize himself, to fully grasp what was happening to his existence and why the proto-matter had reacted to him with such violence.","But storms of proto-matter carried him across THE Prima Indifferentia with force, a heavy and unfathomable change inducing alterations to his own infinity that he couldn’t control. His aspect of Infinite Mana, which had always been the foundation of everything he was, pulsed with light that painted the undefined storms in shades of blue-gold that shouldn’t have existed in a place where color hadn’t fully differentiated.","The Derivative Civilization of Hunger roared within him, its endless appetite meeting endless fuel and expanding in ways that transcended normal growth. The Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate shimmered with potential that connected to the proto-matter around it, drawing in threads of possibility that hadn’t been woven into anything yet.","His existence burned brighter with every moment that passed.","And the storms carried him deeper into THE Prima Indifferentia, toward things that had been sleeping since before differentiation occurred.","---","In an unknown region of THE Prima Indifferentia.","In an area surrounded by obsidian pillars of proto-matter that rose from the undefined ground like teeth in a cosmic mouth, a creature could be seen bouncing around the pillars as if it were having fun.","Its Civilization was not completely clear, existing in a unique state that held both undifferentiation and differentiation simultaneously. It was something that shouldn’t have been possible, a being that had refused to fully commit to either state and had somehow persisted in that refusal since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","The creature looked like a round obsidian furball, perhaps three meters in diameter, with a surface that shifted between solid and gaseous without ever settling on one or the other. Two twinkling obsidian eyes sat at its center, holding an innocent and playful expression that seemed almost childlike as it continued to bounce from pillar to pillar, leaving ripples in the proto-matter wherever it touched.","It had been bouncing for eons.","It would bounce for eons more.","Time had no meaning here, and this creature had long since forgotten what urgency felt like.","As it bounced toward another pillar, preparing to ricochet off into whatever direction amused it next...","HUUM!","Time, which had no meaning here, slowed anyway.","A moment later, the creature blinked as it saw the visage of a humanoid winged entity with a crown of burning pages surge past this region like a hurricane. The entity was surrounded by a storm of proto-matter so dense and violent that it painted the undefined space in shades of blue-gold that shouldn’t have existed here, and its existence blazed with something that the furball had never encountered before!","The eyes of the fur-like entity glimmered with interest, and the innocent playfulness in them shifted into something else entirely.","Hunger!","BOOM!","The transformation was instant and horrifying.","The entire body of the obsidian furball became a horror-inducing mass of flesh and fur that expanded outward in all directions, growing from three meters to three hundred to three thousand in the span of a heartbeat. A million crimson eyes bloomed across its surface, each one containing jagged jaws that opened and closed with anticipation. Tentacles that ended in more mouths erupted from its form. Wings that were also teeth spread wide. Every inch of this entity became a weapon designed for consumption.","It shot out at speeds exceeding lesser and weaker Absolutes like THE Living Elemental, crossing the distance between itself and its prey in less time than it took for light to decide whether it existed here or not.","\"KAAA!\"","It screeched out with fervor and excitement as if it had found a particularly good meal after eons of eating nothing but proto-matter and the occasional foolish Absolute who wandered too deep.","Its body arrived before the storm of proto-matter instantly, and then it opened.","Not like a mouth opens.","Like reality opens when it decides to stop being real!","A slit appeared in its form that led into an abyssal realm of pure undifferentiation, a stomach that had digested things that shouldn’t have been digestible, a void that had unmade beings who thought themselves eternal.","It swallowed both the proto-matter storm and the figure contained within it in a single bite.","...!"]},{"number":4865,"title":"Chapter 4865: Chapter 4864: THE Prima Indifferentia IV","paragraphs":["Being carried across THE Prima Indifferentia without being able to move was horrible, but manageable.","Noah had been working with the situation, allowing his infinities to spread through his existence while the proto-matter storms transported him to wherever they wished. He’d been adapting, evolving, becoming something more than he had been when he first entered through the Crack!","But...","Being swept across the storm as a monstrous thing appeared and swallowed him whole...","This was not manageable.","Darkness surrounded him instantly, but it wasn’t the darkness of absence. It was the darkness of presence, the weight of something so fundamentally undefined that light itself couldn’t exist within it. He felt the walls of this stomach pressing against his existence from every direction, and he felt them beginning to work.","|Critical Alert|","| You have been devoured by THE Undivided One, Bazuman|","|THE Undivided Ones are arguably the most dangerous entities in THE Prima Indifferentia|","|They are beings that existed before existence differentiated but who refused to differentiate with it|","|They remain in their original state: undivided, undefined, and partiallyunlimited|","|They cannot be fought because fighting requires the fighter and the fought to be separate things|","|They cannot be reasoned with because reasoning requires distinct concepts to compare|","|They cannot be avoided because avoidance requires a distinction between presence and absence|","|Bazuman has consumed an unknown number of Absolutes across the eons|","|None of them escaped|","|None of them survived|","|Your current Depth is insufficient to resist digestion|","|Estimated time until complete undifferentiation: decreasing|","...!","When it rained, it poured.","In addition to the proto-matter continuing to flood into him from the storms he’d been carried through, Noah now felt a different force pressing down all around him. The digestive pressure of THE Undivided One, Bazuman, was unbelievably heavy, exceeding even the force that he had felt from THE Hollow Echo of THE Creature in The Interstices.","In an instant, Noah saw his arms and legs beginning to unravel.","Inside the stomach of this creature, his weight and Immensity was being unmade and undifferentiated in a manner that far exceeded what the proto-matter had been doing on its own. His fingers blurred at the edges. His wings lost their definition. His crown of burning pages flickered as the Phonemes contained within them began to forget what they were supposed to mean.","But...","Noah felt the unprecedented danger and situation around him as the change that had been spurred by proto-matter still remained within his foundations. He felt all his Ways as they burned with Infinities. His Organ of Civilization burned with infinity. THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons burned with infinity. His entire existence burned with Infinity in ways that he hadn’t fully understood until this very moment.","The perilous enemy he faced could easily undifferentiate even Absolutes, and Noah’s Depth couldn’t compare to such beings.","Not even close.","But he didn’t only have his Depth.","In such a perilous moment as his arms and legs unraveled further, as his existence threatened to dissolve into the stomach of something that had never failed to digest its prey, Noah actually closed his eyes and felt the beat of his heart.","It was...","DUM DUM DUM...","It beat repetitively and infinitely, because the influx of proto-matter seeking to undifferentiate him had instead bathed his heart in infinity when it couldn’t undifferentiate what was already beyond definition.","In order to fight an enemy he couldn’t win against through conventional means, he called out lightly.","\" Beat loudly.\"","HUUM!","His heart responded, and the infinity within it flared brighter.","\" Beat tyrannically.\"","WAA!","His heart thundered, and the infinities spread through his existence began to pulse in rhythm with it.","\" Beat... infinitely.\"","...!","BOOM!","An instant later, Noah’s unraveling limbs reformed.","But they didn’t reform as flesh and blood and the normal composition of his existence. They reformed as pure blue-gold infinities given physical shape, light that had no perceivable end taking the form of arms and legs and wings that spread wide with authority that transcended Depth entirely!","He didn’t call upon his Depth.","He didn’t need to.","He released his Infinities that couldn’t be undifferentiated into the belly of a creature that had always succeeded in undifferentiating everything it had ever consumed.","From Noah’s body, a flicker of infinity bloomed.","And this flicker groaned and boomed as if it were an unfathomable beast waking up from slumber that had lasted since before time existed. It asserted itself with weight that had nothing to do with Foundation or Civilization or Way, a weight that simply was because infinity simply was.","How dare you try to undifferentiate what cannot be undifferentiated?","The question wasn’t spoken aloud, but it echoed through the stomach of Bazuman with force that made the walls of undifferentiation tremble for the first time in their existence.","With such a regal and grand resonance, the glimmer of blue-gold infinity erupted outward like a blade.","It carved through the stomach of something that had never been carved before.","It cut through undifferentiation itself, forcing the definition of infinity into a space that had rejected definition since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","And it kept cutting until it reached the outside.","---","In a region surrounded by pillars of proto-matter, the visage of Bazuman paused.","The massive horror that had been so eager to consume THE First Tongue went still, its million crimson eyes blinking in unison as something unprecedented occurred within its form. It had swallowed its prey. It had begun digesting. The process had always worked before.","Why wasn’t it working now?","A cut appeared on its body.","A line of blue-gold light that should not have been possible, a wound inflicted by something that had no business being able to wound THE Undivided.","And from that cut, a blue-gold light of a man shot out.","Noah’s figure emerged from the belly of the beast, his existence burning with infinities that painted the proto-matter around him in shades that THE Prima Indifferentia had never seen before!","He was still learning how to use this brilliance, still understanding what had changed within him and how to direct it, but he understood enough.","He floated before Bazuman, his blue-gold form facing the horror of a million crimson eyes and jagged jaws, and he spoke calmly.","\"I... am not food.\"","...!","An immense silence settled across this region of THE Prima Indifferentia alongside heavy unease that even the proto-matter seemed to feel. Bazuman’s countless eyes focused on the being before it, studying something that had escaped its stomach for the first time in its existence.","And within Noah, prompts bloomed.","|Existential Transformation Detected|","| Your Formless Depth burns with infinities|","|All aspects of your existence have become more aligned with the central weaving of your being|","|The Derivative Civilization of Hunger has been bathed in Infinity|","|The Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate has been bathed in Infinity|","|Your Way burns with Infinity|","|Your Foundation burns with Infinity|","| You have produced your first Infinite Everything|","|Not an Absolute Everything|","| An Infinite Everything|","...!"]},{"number":4866,"title":"Chapter 4866: Chapter 4865: Looking For A Local! I","paragraphs":["What was an Infinite Everything?","It was a heavy question that pressed against his mind with weight that demanded answers. An Absolute Everything could elevate a Half-Step Absolute to full Absolute status if their foundation was heavy enough. It was the pinnacle of Civilizational Authority compressed into a single resource.","But an Infinite Everything?","What could something infinite do that something merely Absolute could not?","He wanted to explore this question, wanted to understand what had changed within him and how he could use it to further his goals. The question burned in his mind!","But it didn’t seem like he would be given the chance to explore and ask.","Because THE Undivided One, Bazuman, who had looked startled for the first time in its existence...","Was no longer startled.","The massive being with countless eyes began to dance with horror-inducing excitement, its form shifting and expanding as if the challenge of prey that could escape had awakened something primal within it. Joy radiated from its crimson eyes. Anticipation leaked from its jagged jaws. For the first time in eons, it had found something interesting.","Something that might actually be fun to hunt.","The many eyes across its form began to glow with concentrated light, and then they differentiated that light into beams of obsidian brilliance that surged toward Noah with speed that exceeded anything he had encountered since arriving in THE Prima Indifferentia.","|Attack Analysis|","|Designation: Rays of Undifferentiated Annihilation|","|These beams carry both Depth and the light of undifferentiation simultaneously|","|Being hit with them is instant annihilation for anything below Absolute|","|Your Infinite nature may provide resistance to the undifferentiation aspect|","|You might survive a blast or two|","| You will not survive sustained bombardment|","|Recommendation: Do not get hit|","...!","The prompts were menacing ones that left no room for optimism or cleverness.","Noah didn’t tarry.","He flared his infinities once more, releasing the blue-gold light that burned within his existence outward into the surrounding proto-matter. The undefined substance responded to his infinity with eagerness that he hadn’t expected, churning and gathering around him as if it wanted to be part of whatever he was becoming.","A storm of proto-matter erupted around his form, denser and more violent than the one that had carried him here. The beams of obsidian light charging toward him struck this storm and became distorted, their trajectories bending as the proto-matter interfered with their ability to maintain definition long enough to hit their target.","Noah silently gave direction to his infinities, and the storm of proto-matter didn’t just emerge but began to move. His existence became a flicker of blue-gold light that shot away from THE Undivided One at speeds that the storms themselves enhanced, carrying him deeper into THE Prima Indifferentia and away from a creature that had never lost prey before and clearly didn’t intend to start now!","Running away was never a bad thing.","Especially when the enemy seeking to collapse you was levels above anything you could currently handle.","Behind him, Bazuman’s screech of excitement echoed across the undefined expanse, and Noah could feel the creature beginning to pursue. Its million eyes tracked his trajectory. Its countless mouths opened in anticipation. Its entire existence oriented itself toward the hunt!","But Noah had something that Bazuman couldn’t undifferentiate.","Surviving alone was arduous enough as it was.","He had to find a solution in a place filled with dangers and opportunities, had to locate THE Primordial Paradox or find his own way back to the Crack of Observable Existence!","The storm of proto-matter carried him forward, away from the horror behind him and toward whatever waited ahead!","In THE Prima Indifferentia, there were no safe directions.","But some directions were less dangerous than others.","Well, hopefully anyways!","---","In another region of THE Prima Indifferentia near The Crack of Observable Existence.","THE Primordial Paradox stood amidst the churning expanse of proto-matter with a frowning expression, his eyes closed as if he were trying to sense something that refused to be sensed. His obsidian form remained perfectly defined despite the constant pressure of undifferentiation that would have eroded lesser beings, his very nature as the holder of the Paradox Claim creating a bubble of stability in a place that rejected stability as a concept.","Around him, proto-matter weaved and bent as if his paradoxical existence made it impossible to be undifferentiated. The undefined substance couldn’t seem to decide whether he was part of it or separate from it, whether he belonged here or didn’t, and that confusion protected him.","But as he couldn’t find what he wanted, he shook his head and sighed with exhaustion.","He had brought THE Youngest here.","And now the being who carried The First Tongue had been swept away by storms of proto-matter that THE Primordial Paradox should have anticipated and prevented. It seemed the infection was grabbing more of him than he expected.","He raised his hand and tapped the area in front of him, and a crack opened in the undefined space that had nothing to do with the Crack of Observable Existence. This was something else entirely, a communication method that transcended normal spatial relationships, forming into an illusory screen that pulsed with unique authority connecting two points across Existence regardless of the distance between them.","Moments later, an image formed on this screen.","The entity that appeared was shrouded in multicolored flames, his body fully drenched with fires of Existence that burned in every color simultaneously. These weren’t flames that consumed but flames that simply were, the visual manifestation of pure being given form. His entire figure couldn’t be fully observed because observing it would have required definition, and this entity existed at a level where definition was something he chose to wear rather than something imposed upon him.","He was presence incarnate!","He was THE Creature.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at this being, and without even an introduction or pleasantries, he spoke directly.","\" Would you happen to be in THE Prima Indifferentia right now? I may need the assistance of a local.\"","...!","At such words, the figure on the illusory screen stared back at THE Primordial Paradox with eyes that couldn’t be seen but could definitely be felt. When he replied, his voice boomed with resonance that seemed to echo out from the screen and cause the proto-matter in the surroundings to churn wildly before settling down respectfully, as if this voice was soothing and one that demanded acknowledgment simply by existing.","\" You know I am not a local there.\"","THE Primordial Paradox waved his hand dismissively.","\" Yes, yes, you keep mentioning Alfheimr. But I am in a bind here as I lost someone, and I need to find them rather quickly.\"","...!","The expression of THE Primordial Paradox was calm as he said all of this.","The figure surrounded by flames of Existence remained stoic and grand on the illusory screen, his presence pressing against the communication channel with weight that made even this distant projection feel overwhelming.","\" You have been masking yourself actively from Existence and everything else for quite some time now.\"","THE Creature’s voice held observation rather than accusation.","\" Even I have had no idea who is around you. I was only able to learn about the distinction of THE Tongue Whisperer.\"","The multicolored flames flickered with something that might have been curiosity.","\"Is this the one that you lost?\"","...!"]},{"number":4867,"title":"Chapter 4867: Chapter 4866: Looking For A Local! II","paragraphs":["At such words, THE Primordial Paradox nodded lightly.","He didn’t elaborate on who THE Tongue Whisperer was or why he had brought someone with mastery over The First Tongue into THE Prima Indifferentia.","THE Creature on the illusory screen was silent for a moment, his flames shifting through patterns of consideration and calculation occurring behind eyes that couldn’t be perceived.","\"I am not in THE Prima Indifferentia right now.\"","His voice carried finality regarding that particular option.","\" But a local from there should be able to help you.\"","...!","A local from here.","These words alone caused THE Primordial Paradox to frown. The proto-matter around him churned in response to his emotional state, reflecting his unease with increased agitation.","\" Any locals here apart from you are either mad or out for Existence itself. THE Undivided Ones cannot be reasoned with, THE Formless Terrors seek only to undifferentiate others, and everything else that has survived here long enough to be called local has done so by becoming something that should not be trusted.\"","THE Creature on the illusory screen waved his hands in a dismissive manner, the multicolored flames trailing after his movements like loyal attendants.","\"If you want my assistance, that is the extent of it.\"","His voice held no room for argument.","\"Call out his name until he finds you as you move across THE Prima Indifferentia. Simply call for Jack.\"","...!","Jack?","THE Primordial Paradox tilted his head at this name, his obsidian crown spinning with confusion that he didn’t bother to hide. The designation seemed too casual, too mundane for something that could survive as a local in a place where Absolutes became Formless Terrors and THE Undivided Ones hunted anything with definition.","With his display of confusion evident, THE Creature on the illusory screen clarified.","\" Jack. Jokul. He prefers to be alone and unbothered, but he owes me a favour.\"","The multicolored flames shifted with something that might have been fondness.","\" Whoever you lost in there, Jack should be able to find them.\"","A pause.","\" Unless you did something as reckless as bringing someone that was not Absolute into THE Prima Indifferentia.\"","The flames darkened slightly.","\"If they are away from you for just a matter of seconds, they may already be undifferentiated.\"","The words felt like a heavy and somber warning, the kind that only someone who truly understood THE Prima Indifferentia’s dangers could give. THE Creature had spent more time here than any other member of THE Four, had explored regions that even THE Primordial Paradox had never ventured toward, and his caution was not given lightly.","THE Primordial Paradox smiled and shook his head.","\"I do not think so. Not this one, anyway.\"","\" But what will this cost me?\"","Nothing between THE Four was ever truly free, and favours owed to THE Creature were not things to be accumulated carelessly.","THE Creature’s flames stilled on the illusory screen, becoming almost solid for a moment as he considered his price.","\" You can tell me what is happening with you.\"","His voice lost its casual edge, becoming something more serious.","\" Do I need to be worried?\"","...!","Did he need to be worried?","The entity shrouded by multicolored flames of Existence, the being that THE Primordial Paradox had reached out to for help, THE Creature himself, was asking about the state of THE Primordial Paradox with concern!","And THE Primordial Paradox smiled with the expression of someone who had made peace with circumstances that others would have raged against.","\"It is nothing major.\"","His voice held acceptance rather than defeat.","\"I shall simply be going to sleep for a little while, as someone else would likely take my place.\"","He paused, considering his next words carefully.","\" They will not be as entertaining as I am, but observe whether they are worthy or even capable of progressing toward the Second Scale. I am curious myself, after all of this.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox said such foreboding words with a casual air.","THE Creature in the illusory screen looked out silently without a reply.","His multicolored flames burned with intensity that made the proto-matter around THE Primordial Paradox tremble, responding to the emotional weight of what had just been shared.","An immense silence settled across the communication channel, neither of them speaking as the weight of the moment pressed against them both.","Eventually, THE Creature spoke.","\"It seems that you have found yet another hardship to overcome.\"","His voice was measured and heavy.","\"If the adversity is tremendous enough, it may just be sufficient fuel for you to take a step toward the second Scale. After all, The Vakochev Scales demand hardship...\"","The multicolored flames flickered with something ancient.","\" Very well. But be careful.\"","His voice grew deeper.","\" One can plan and plan endlessly, but you never truly know what Existence has in store. None of us know.\"","HUUM!","\" None of us will ever truly know.\"","The surrounding proto-matter trembled at the words of THE Creature with a sense of fear and reverence.","THE Primordial Paradox listened silently before he nodded with the weight of farewell hidden behind his composed features.","He waved his hands.","The illusory screen portraying THE Creature disappeared, the communication channel closing and leaving THE Primordial Paradox alone once more in the churning expanse of THE Prima Indifferentia.","He stood there for a moment, allowing himself a breath.","Then he straightened his obsidian form and looked around at the undefined expanse surrounding him.","He had a Tongue Whisperer to find.","And he had limited time before the infection within him progressed to stages that would make movement impossible.","THE Primordial Paradox began to walk through THE Prima Indifferentia, his voice calling out across the undefined space with authority that pressed against the proto-matter and forced it to carry his words further than they should have been able to travel.","\" Jokul!\"","The name echoed across churning storms and pillars of undefined potential.","\" Jack!\"","He called again, moving deeper into the expanse while searching for both a being he had never met and the one he had lost!"]},{"number":4868,"title":"Chapter 4868: Chapter 4867: Undifferentiation!","paragraphs":["Even moving and breathing felt tough at this moment for Noah.","With every breath he took, even though he didn’t need to take a breath, he felt like he was breathing in all of himself and breathing out all of himself simultaneously. The infinity that had bathed his existence wasn’t something he could simply possess and move on from!","He felt like with every passing moment he was breathing in infinity and expelling infinity, his lungs becoming conduits. It was a unique sensation to have, both exhilarating and terrifying in equal measure.","It would have been ideal to have at least a few minutes to acclimate to the immense changes across his existence.","But he was being forced to do all of this acclimation while being chased by a monstrous creature who could decimate Absolutes with the casual ease of a child crushing insects.","The only reason that he was surviving as long as he was came down to a single factor: the Immensity of Bazuman that could undifferentiate so many things was not working on him because it couldn’t undifferentiate his infinity.","But this creature also held a terrifying Depth.","So the beams of incandescent light chasing after him, those Rays of Undifferentiated Annihilation, would only take one or two direct hits before this body would be crumbled and this temporal traversal would come to an end.","The proto-matter storms around him churned with increasing violence as Noah pushed them to move faster, his infinities directing their flow while he rode their currents like a leaf in a hurricane. Behind him, Bazuman’s countless crimson eyes tracked his trajectory with interest that had transformed into genuine excitement, the horror of a million jaws opening and closing with anticipation as if they were a predator on a particularly enjoyable hunt.","But with every passing instant, Noah acclimated more and more to his existence and the Immensity that it currently carried.","\" Oh?\"","He asked himself this question as if he didn’t believe what he was perceiving to be true, as he came to grasp something about himself that he tried right away.","Because with infinity bathing everything, it also bathed his Seals of Absolute Tongue that represented his Way and Civilization.","They weren’t just seals anymore.","At this moment, as his figure burning with blue-gold light shot out toward one direction while surrounded by storms of proto-matter, the beams that could collapse and undifferentiate were bypassing more and more of the storm. The proto-matter could only distort their trajectories so much before the weight of Bazuman’s Depth forced them through, and they were about to reach him with devastating impact.","At such a time, Noah flung his arm back.","He threw out a single Absolute Seal of Infinity.","And utmost brilliance ensued right after.","|Existential Observation|","| The Absolute Seals representing your Civilization are now Infinite|","|They have no limit to their number|","|They have no constraint on their manifestation|","|You threw one|","|Infinity responded|","BOOM!","Even though Noah had thrown out a single seal of infinity, in the next moment, a flood of endless seals bloomed out like radiant blue-gold flowers unfurling across the undefined space of THE Prima Indifferentia.","The seals emerged from that single point of release and multiplied endlessly, each one spawning more and more until the entire region behind Noah became a garden of linguistic authority made manifest. They looked like countless blue-gold plum blossoms emerging from his existence, their petals formed from concentrated Phonemes and their centers burning with the weight of his Civilization.","A unique sound bloomed out with the emergence of infinite seals of infinity, a resonance that was simultaneously a whisper and a roar, the sound of one becoming many becoming infinite. The proto-matter around them responded with awe!","The sheer number of the seals was so overwhelming that the terrifying and perilous beams of light stemming from THE Undivided One became covered entirely, their trajectories intersecting with petal after petal after petal of blue-gold authority. They smashed into these seals with force that should have shattered anything below Absolute, and the seals did shatter, breaking apart into motes of linguistic light.","But for every seal that broke, infinity provided another.","And another.","And another.","Momentarily, the entire region looked like a beautiful scene filled with blue-gold scattered plum blossoms, a garden of impossible flowers blooming in a place where gardens had never existed and flowers had never been differentiated. The seals resisted undifferentiation because they were born from infinity, and infinity couldn’t be made less than it was, so they overcame the terrifying light released by THE Undivided One through sheer inexhaustible presence.","But because the Depth of this being was still there, and the density and weight of Noah’s seals was nowhere as immense as this terrifying entity chasing after him...","BOOM!","The beams that had been distorted were reinforced by something far more direct.","Millions of tentacles erupted from Bazuman’s ever-shifting form, each one ending in jaws that gnashed with hunger that transcended normal appetite. They surged through the garden of infinite seals, tearing through the blue-gold blossoms with physical force rather than undifferentiation, using raw Depth to accomplish what conceptual attack could not.","The many crimson eyes of THE Undivided One seemed to show more and more interest toward Noah, gleaming with excitement that made the proto-matter around them tremble with sympathetic dread.","\" Little one.\"","The voice that emerged from Bazuman was wrong in ways that transcended description, coming from everywhere and nowhere simultaneously, formed from concepts that hadn’t fully differentiated into sound.","\" Do not struggle.\"","The tentacles pressed forward, crushing seals by the thousands even as thousands more bloomed to replace them.","\" Just let me have a taste.\"","HUUM!","Noah looked back with a calm and solemn gaze even as seals continued to flood from his hand like an endless tide of flower petals. The Immensity of THE Undivided One still drew near despite his infinite defense, the tentacles and jaws closing the distance through brute force that his seals couldn’t fully resist.","He searched inside of his existence for something more.","He hadn’t yet pulled upon the Infinite Everything that had formed within him, choosing to give his existence a chance to break it down and understand what it truly was before utilizing it. Because everything was new at this moment, and being in this region of THE Prima Indifferentia caused RUINATION to constantly fight an influx of undifferentiation, the analysis was taking longer than usual.","But it was still his existence, and the things that weren’t new were rapidly becoming clear to him.","Right now, when he considered how he could overcome something so much stronger than him to survive, another infinity bloomed and blazed with light within his foundations.","His main Civilization allowed for him to burn with this light of infinity, but he wasn’t alone in that burning.","There were Derivative Civilizations under him.","THE Civilizational Authority of Infinite Hunger stirred within his existence, the endless appetite that had consumed THE Paradox of Consumption and reached Half-Step Absolute as a result. THE Civilizational Authority of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate stirred alongside it, the connection to destiny that touched upon the very nature of this place.","Both of them permeated into all of the seals of infinity that he was releasing.","The vibrant blue-gold petals endlessly raging all around him took on shades of crimson from the Hunger and even more gold from the Undifferentiated Fate. They transformed from defensive flowers into something else entirely, their edges becoming sharper, their presence becoming hungrier, their nature becoming more aligned with THE Prima Indifferentia itself.","And shockingly, as if they had gained an extremely sharp edge that cut through more than just physical matter...","ZING!","The tentacles and incorporeal beams of brilliance from THE Undivided One began to be caught up and sliced and broken down.","...!","The seals weren’t just blocking anymore.","They were devouring!","They were undifferentiating!","Tentacles that touched the crimson-tinged petals found themselves being consumed, their undefined flesh feeding into the Infinite Hunger that now permeated every seal. Beams of annihilation that struck the gold-touched blossoms found themselves being destabilized, their undifferentiation turned back upon them by seals that now carried the quality of THE Prima Indifferentia itself.","|Combat Analysis - Updated|","| You have learned to infuse Infinite Hunger and Infinite Undifferentiated Fate into your attacks|","|Your seals now carry a quality of endlessly devouring|","|They also carry a quality that only those native to THE Prima Indifferentia possess|","| The quality to induce undifferentiation|","|Even though your Depth is insufficient to survive direct confrontation with THE Undivided One|","|You have thrown out an infinite number of seals that now have the capability to break down and undifferentiate everything thrown at you|","|Bazuman is experiencing attacks being consumed and undifferentiated by prey|","|This will not last|","|Take this brief respite and run before THE Undivided One decides to get truly serious|","|Run!|","...!","BOOM!","The infinite seals continued to flood from his existence, creating a barrier of hungry, undifferentiating petals that bought him precious moments of distance. Behind him, Bazuman paused for the first time since the chase began, its million crimson eyes blinking in what might have been surprise as it watched its tentacles being devoured and its beams being destabilized.","And that novelty, that unprecedented experience, gave Noah the seconds he needed to push his proto-matter storm faster, to ride the currents of undefined potential deeper into THE Prima Indifferentia, to put distance between himself and something that could still absolutely destroy him if it chose to commit fully as...","BOOM!","He disappeared as if the storm of Proto-matter had reached a warping concentration, similar to what took him away from THE Primordial Paradox!","Behind him, the garden of infinite seals continued to bloom and devour and undifferentiate as the jaws of an Undivided One smiled devilishly with brutality, but his prey...was gone!"]},{"number":4869,"title":"Chapter 4869: Chapter 4868: Jokul!","paragraphs":["Truth be told, THE Primordial Paradox was a bit regretful.","How could he lose someone pivotal to his reemergence in the future? He had brought THE Youngest to THE Prima Indifferentia because he had a pretty good idea that this was where THE Entity was stemming from, and the pieces fit in his mind perfectly based on the nature of the infection and what it was currently doing to him.","THE Entity sought to undifferentiate.","THE Prima Indifferentia was the source of all undifferentiation.","The connection seemed obvious once he had examined it from the right angle.","What he couldn’t figure out was how someone as weak as Erwin had gotten his hands on something so powerful in the first place. How Erwin himself wasn’t affected by the very weapon he was wielding. And how he was utilizing it to the extent that even THE Primordial Paradox didn’t know when this attack on his Claim had actually started.","This trip to THE Prima Indifferentia was meant to illuminate things somewhat, to provide THE Tongue Whisperer with understanding that could be used against THE Entity in the future when it had fully emerged and threatened all of Observable Existence.","But...","\" It’s a proper mess.\"","THE Primordial Paradox shook his head as his Immensity surged out once more, his voice carrying across the churning expanse of proto-matter with authority that forced the undefined substance to transmit his words further than they should have been able to travel.","\" Jokul!\"","HUUM!","He had been doing so for quite a long time now, and every time he called out, he was risking pulling in terrifying entities toward his position. His voice was a beacon in a place where beacons attracted predators, and THE Prima Indifferentia had no shortage of things that would be very interested in consuming one of THE Four.","Well, there were now two of THE Four here!","Oh!","He had actually already rebuffed an undifferentiated creature who sought to break down his paradoxical nature, his Apophasis turning the attack back on itself and sending the formless thing retreating into the proto-matter storms from whence it came.","If he continued doing this anymore, something worse would find him.","He just had this thought when in the next moment his eyes brightened, and he looked out toward his right with sudden alertness.","There, a humanoid visage of an entity with no discernible waves of power formed from the proto-matter itself.","He was adorned in an ancient white robe that seemed impossibly clean given the environment, the fabric untouched by the churning chaos that surrounded everything else in this place. Dark flowing hair fell past his shoulders, moving in currents that had nothing to do with the proto-matter storms. His eyes were filled with ancient Immensity that didn’t radiate outward but rather pulled inward, as if everything around him was being drawn toward a singularity of stillness that defied THE Prima Indifferentia’s constant motion.","Behind him was the illusion of an inverted mountain radiating immense coldness, its peak pointing downward into depths that couldn’t be perceived, its base spreading upward into skies that didn’t exist. The mountain wasn’t really there, but it was also more real than anything else in this region of undefined space.","The moment this being arrived, the proto-matter in the surroundings began freezing over.","Not freezing in the sense of becoming ice, but freezing in the sense of becoming still. The churning stopped. The undefined potential ceased its constant shifting. Everything achieved a state of stasis that shouldn’t have been possible in a place defined by perpetual change, and the silence that followed was so profound that it pressed against THE Primordial Paradox’s existence with weight that would have crushed lesser beings.","\" Why have you been shouting my name?\"","The words of this entity sounded heavy and filled with weight that could freeze even weaker Absolutes in their tracks. There was no hostility in his tone, but there was also no warmth, only the absolute certainty of something that had existed long enough to be utterly unimpressed by anything it might encounter.","...!","THE Primordial Paradox looked at this being up and down in evaluation, his obsidian eyes taking in every detail of the entity before him while revealing nothing of his own assessment. His voice came out calm even as he processed what he was perceiving.","\"I was told to scream your name to find you. I asked THE Creature for the assistance of a local in locating someone that I lost in this place.\"","He paused, his obsidian crown spinning slowly.","\"I simply never expected him to have connections with something like you. I cannot pinpoint whether you are an Undivided One or a Formless Terror or something worse entirely.\"","...!","His words were calm even as they came out, carrying the measured precision that defined all of his words. And the entity they were directed to also remained calm, his ancient eyes showing no reaction to being analyzed by one of THE Four as if such analysis was beneath his notice.","When he heard the name of THE Creature, his eyes flickered briefly, and he seemed to think for a moment before giving a light nod.","\" Who are you looking for?\"","THE Primordial Paradox smiled at the fact that his entire set of words were ignored except for the most important one.","\"I am looking for someone whose existence is currently surrounded by the designation of THE Tongue Whisperer. He should have a flicker of the signature of The First Tongue burning brightly around him.\"","The entity opposite to THE Primordial Paradox simply nodded at these words as he turned around, apparently ready to begin the search without any further discussion. The frozen proto-matter remained still around him, held in stasis by his mere presence.","THE Primordial Paradox continued to look at him with curiosity that he didn’t bother to hide, and he couldn’t help but ask the question that pressed against his mind.","\" Who are you, really?\"","At these words, the figure of Jokul turned around and looked at THE Primordial Paradox with extremely calm eyes that held depths which even someone who had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling couldn’t fully perceive.","\" You have been calling my name this entire time.\"","His voice was flat, stating fact rather than expressing emotion.","\" Jokul. Jokul Anaximander.\"","He paused, and the inverted mountain behind him seemed to grow larger for just a moment.","\" But call me Jack. To you, I am simply a friend of THE Creature. Nothing more and nothing less.\"","His ancient eyes held no deception because there was nothing to deceive about, only the truth of what he was willing to share and the silence of everything he wasn’t.","\" And as for the one that you lost...\"","The frozen proto-matter in the surroundings began to churn and pulse with a heart-shaking brilliance that emanated from Jokul himself, his stillness somehow becoming motion without ever actually moving. The inverted mountain behind him blazed with light that was also darkness, with cold that was also presence.","\"I know where THE Tongue Whisperer is.\"","WAA!","He said these words as if they were an affirmation or something that he was uttering to then be true.","The proto-matter responded by revealing pathways that hadn’t existed before, frozen currents that pointed toward a specific direction in a place where direction shouldn’t have been possible.","But an instant later, his eyes shone with piercing light as he nodded his head with what might have been interest.","\"It seems like it will take some time, as an Undivided One is hunting him.\"","He paused.","\" But I have found him. Let us go.\"","...!","An Undivided One was hunting him?","Now THE Primordial Paradox was entirely surprised. The proto-matter around them seemed to darken in response to his sudden concern.","\" An Undivided One is hunting him and he has not been undifferentiated or collapsed?\"","Was THE Youngest so fearsome when he hadn’t even become an Absolute yet?","THE Primordial Paradox had brought THE Youngest here expecting challenges, yes, but he had also expected to be present to help navigate those challenges. For someone of Fundamental Depth to survive being hunted by an Undivided One, even for a short time, was unprecedented.","The visage of Jokul turned toward THE Primordial Paradox with a calm gaze that held neither concern nor reassurance.","\" We can wait a little bit more for THE Formless Terrors or more Undivided Ones to find him, or for him to land in the gazes of THE Primordial Architects.\"","His voice was utterly flat.","\" Then he will really be undifferentiated or collapsed. He will die. Shall we wait?\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox looked at the deadpan expression of Jokul as his sharp eyes flashed with irritation. The proto-matter around them seemed to hold its breath, waiting for his response.","He took a step to appear beside this being, his obsidian form closing the distance instantaneously.","\" Well, all of us will one day die, but...why say such horror-inducing things?\"","His voice was serious.","\" Let us go. I cannot afford to lose this one.\"","With such words, the visage of Jokul turned toward another direction entirely, one that the frozen pathways in the proto-matter hadn’t indicated, and disappeared into the churning expanse with movement that wasn’t movement.","His voice echoed out across the undefined space with weight that pressed against everything it touched.","\" Keep up.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox followed, his obsidian form cutting through the proto-matter as he pursued this enigmatic being called Jokul Anaximander, or really, Jack, toward THE Youngest who was somehow surviving being hunted by an Undivided One!"]},{"number":4870,"title":"Chapter 4870: Chapter 4869: Infinite I","paragraphs":["The proto-matter storm calmed around him as he appeared in an entirely different place.","Noah frowned as he looked around, his blue-gold form tense and ready for violence, almost as if he was expecting another monstrous thing to erupt at any moment and attempt to consume him. His eyes scanned the churning expanse with wariness that had been earned through far too many encounters where peace turned to peril in the span of a heartbeat.","That seemed to be his hardship and adversity across Existence, as he couldn’t even get a fucking moment to breathe.","But...","He only saw the forming and unforming landscapes of reality all around him, seas of proto-matter covering the nearby regions in waves of undefined potential that rose and fell without ever committing to any particular shape. Mountains that were also valleys. Rivers that were also skies. Ground that was also nothing at all.","No Undivided Ones hunting him.","No Formless Terrors seeking to drag him into their undefined existence.","No beams of annihilation or tentacles with jaws or million-eyed horrors screeching for a taste.","But Noah did not relax.","Instead, he released Absolute Seals of Darkness, Chaos, and Paradox that instantly bloomed around his form in swirling patterns that expanded outward with the infinity that now defined them. The seals multiplied endlessly as they reacted to the proto-matter surrounding him, their edges blurring as they took on the qualities of this place.","Moments later, everything transformed.","The seals became proto-matter themselves, as if they had undergone complete undifferentiation while somehow retaining their protective function. They wrapped around Noah’s existence and merged with the churning expanse until the distinction between his defenses and the environment became impossible to perceive.","When the storm of transformation calmed, Noah was nowhere to be seen.","\"...\"","But he was right there, mixed in with the calm movements of proto-matter.","Hidden in plain sight within a place where sight itself hadn’t fully differentiated.","In such a state of concealed existence, he finally turned his attention inward and breathed.","Just what had happened to him, really? The changes he had undergone since being separated from THE Primordial Paradox were so profound that he needed time to actually process them.","Time he hadn’t been given until now.","|Infinity Integration: Complete Existential Analysis|","|The core aspect of your existence was already infinite before entering THE Prima Indifferentia. Proto-matter attempted to undifferentiate it and failed because infinity cannot be made less than infinite. Instead of being eroded, your core aspect became the template that all other aspects of your existence are now being restructured to mirror.|","|This process is ongoing and will continue until full integration is achieved.|","...!","The prompts flowed through his consciousness with weight, each piece of information landing with significance that demanded attention.","| THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons - Previous State: A repository of linguistic authority containing all acquired Phonemes, Logos, Philologies, and Archai. Current State: The Grimoire now contains infinite pages , with each Phoneme existing in infinite variations and each Logos expressible in infinite permutations.|","|Each Philology and Archai can be structured in infinite arrangements that you have not yet explored. The Grimoire no longer merely stores The First Tongue but generates linguistic authority passively, with new combinations of existing Phonemes forming automatically within its infinite pages.|","|You will need to review these combinations when time permits. Some may be useful, some may be dangerous, and all of them are yours to claim or discard as you see fit.|","...!","Noah felt THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons pulsing within his existence, its pages turning endlessly through combinations that his conscious mind couldn’t track. It was generating authority on its own now, creating linguistic structures that might take eons to fully catalogue!","|THE Organ of Civilization - Previous State: The core structure housing the authority of your Civilization and its derivatives. Current State: The Organ now pulses with infinite rhythm, its capacity for Derivative Civilizations no longer limited by conventional constraints.|","|The Organ can theoretically support infinite derivatives simultaneously, but the constraint has shifted from quantity to quality. You can have as many Derivative Civilizations as you desire, but each must still be cultivated through genuine development. Infinity provides space, but it does not provide substance, and that remains your responsibility.|","|Additionally, inside THE Organ of Civilization, THE Infinite Desmoterion has been bathed with a light of infinity. The prisoners held within are undergoing unknown alterations and mutations that your other self, Ozymandias, is currently overseeing and guiding in real-time and dilated time.|","...!","The implications of that last prompt were heavy, but Noah filed them away for later consideration.","|27 Seals of Absolute Tongue - Previous State: 27 distinct Seals representing your mastery over The First Tongue. Current State: Each Seal is now infinitely reproducible, with throwing one Seal manifesting infinite Seals in response.|","|The number 27 remains significant as the base configuration, but each of the 27 can multiply without limit upon release. Additionally, your Seals now carry three distinct qualities that transform them from mere representations of authority into weapons of existential significance.|","|Quality One: Infinite durability through endless replacement. Quality Two: Infinite Hunger absorption from Derivative Civilization integration. Quality Three: Undifferentiation induction from Infinite Undifferentiated Fate integration. Your Seals have become both shield and weapon, both defense and consumption, both definition and undefinition.|","...!","He had already witnessed those qualities in action against Bazuman, watching his seals devour and undifferentiate the attacks of an Undivided One. They had bought him time that shouldn’t have been possible to purchase.","But then the prompts reached something that made him pause.","|Depth and Immensity - Infinity seeks to permeate across your Depth, but the integration appears to be missing a critical component. The change required is too significant for passive integration alone. Active application of a catalyst is required to complete the transformation.|","...!","Noah paused at these prompts.","Everything was getting bathed with a light of infinity, his Grimoire and his Organ and his Seals all transforming to reflect the boundless nature of his core aspect. But his Depth had not fully taken that step, as it seemed to be missing something that passive integration couldn’t provide.","And he felt like he knew exactly what was missing.","At this time, he turned his gaze to his Organ of Civilization where an unfathomably bright singularity of blue-gold light spun in lemniscate formations that twisted through dimensions that shouldn’t have existed within his existence. The light was hypnotic and terrifying and beautiful all at once, a resource of such profound significance that even looking at it directly made his foundations ache.","He was looking at his Infinite Everything."]},{"number":4871,"title":"Chapter 4871: Chapter 4870: Infinite II","paragraphs":["|Infinite Everything - Classification and Application Parameters|","|An Infinite Everything can be applied to most resources, most authorities, and nearly all aspects of one’s Civilization. Upon application, that resource becomes infinite in quantity while retaining its original quality, transforming limited potential into boundless actuality.|","|The limitation is singular and absolute: an Infinite Everything can only be applied once. Once used, it cannot be recovered, cannot be replicated, and cannot be undone. The choice of application determines the trajectory of one’s existence for all time that follows.|","|Choose what becomes infinite with extreme care. The wrong choice creates infinite mediocrity, an endless supply of something that doesn’t matter. The right choice creates infinite transcendence, a foundation for growth that has no ceiling and no end.|","...!","The definition was straightforward for the most part, but Noah also felt like something immense was missing from his understanding. The Infinite Everything spun within his Organ of Civilization with weight that pressed against his perception, demanding to be used while also warning him of the permanence of that use.","But while Noah felt the Immensity of his existence and his Depth, which was having a hard time taking the aspect of infinity through passive integration alone, he knew exactly where this Infinite Everything needed to go.","There was only one choice that made sense.","His thoughts were silent as they imposed themselves onto his existence, and a moment later he felt his newly born Infinite Everything surge toward the target he had selected. The area of THE Prima Indifferentia that had calmed around him with undifferentiated proto-matter instantly released a flash of blue-gold light that stretched out across the edges of perception, painting the undefined expanse in colors that shouldn’t have existed here.","BOOM!","He felt like something within him had broken.","Not broken in the sense of damage, but broken in the sense of liberation. A ceiling that would have always remained there, a glass container that would have forever limited how high he could build, shattered into fragments of conceptual constraint that dissolved into his foundations and disappeared.","| Infinite Everything Application Confirmed|","|Target: THE Formless Depth of your existence|","HUUM!","Immensity bloomed.","Gloru unfolded as his existence felt squeezed and then let free!","| Your Depth transforms to become THE Infinite Formless Depth . There is no longer any theoretical ceiling to your foundation at any level of existence. The constraints that would have limited your growth have been permanently removed.|","|THE Surface Depth, which was approaching the theoretical limit of 1000% comparative weight to THE Primordial Paradox at equivalent stage, no longer has this ceiling. It can be increased infinitely. THE Intermediate Depth, which was approaching the theoretical limit of 1000% comparative weight, no longer has this ceiling. It can be increased infinitely.|","|Your Fundamental Depth can be increased infinitely without ever reaching a point where further growth becomes impossible. Your Absolute Depth, when you eventually attain it, can have its foundation increased infinitely as well. The Vakochev Scales of Existence will need to be navigated regardless, but the weight you bring to those Scales has no upper bound.|","|While it may become more and more arduous to scale upward as the numbers grow larger, there is no theoretical ceiling to prevent continued growth. Hypothetically, you could continue elevating the weight of your Surface, Intermediate, and Fundamental Depths to become so grand that you could stand against Absolutes without ever fully grasping that designation yourself.|","|You have not become an Absolute. You have become something with the potential to exceed Absolutes while remaining at lower Depths. This configuration has no precedent in Observable Existence.|","|Additionally, the aspect of Infinity has now fully permeated your Depth. The integration that was stalled has been completed through active application of the Infinite Everything. All aspects of your existence now burn with the light of boundlessness.|","...!","Utter majesty bloomed within Noah as he felt a sense of exuberance that transcended mere emotion.","Inside of his existence, the parts where it had felt like a ceiling existed, the invisible barriers that would have eventually stopped his growth, were now filled with Infinite Potential instead. There were no walls. No limits.","No points where someone could say \"this far and no further\" because infinity recognized no such constraints.","And for all his efforts, there were grand harvests being made.","Infinity wrapped around Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect as well, enhancing these aspects of his existence that had always been responsible for his accelerated growth. Currently, they were drawing in proto-matter from THE Prima Indifferentia and its undifferentiated quality, and proceeding to change it into differentiated harvest that steadily flowed into his foundations at rates that made his previous gains look like trickles compared to rivers.","He was becoming heavier and grander with every passing second throughout all his foundations.","Surface Depth growing.","Intermediate Depth growing.","Fundamental Depth growing!","All of it expanding without any ceiling to eventually halt the expansion.","It was surreal to see this as a result of his current temporal traversal, a journey that had begun with hiding a piece of THE Primordial Paradox and had transformed into something that reshaped the fundamental nature of his existence.","But one thing became abundantly clear as he floated within the concealment of undifferentiated proto-matter and felt his foundations expanding in real-time.","It looked like he would be building his foundation for a very, very long time.","Now, he basically had all the blueprints to infinite growth and Immensity.","What he had to do now was continue to flood his existence with infinite potential and resources that would continue to scale upward without any theoretical ceiling to halt his progress. Since there was no upper limit anymore, he could continue to pour resources into his weight and Immensity until he reached levels that rivaled or exceeded beings who had spent eons building their foundations.","But of course, even more resources were required the higher up he went.","The law of diminishing returns applied, with each subsequent increase demanding more investment than the last. Going from 100% to 200% comparative weight might require a certain amount of resources, but going from 200% to 300% would require even more, and the progression would continue to steepen as he climbed higher and higher into territory that had never been explored by someone at his Depth.","Absolutes were resources that were tasty and grand, and collapsing them through combat or through methods like the Rite of Paradoxical Inheritance had provided significant boosts to his foundations. But THE Prima Indifferentia should also hold unfathomable resources as just being here alone allowed him to take in and process proto-matter that was being turned into infinite potential, continuously and steadily pumped into his foundation through Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect.","He was growing passively simply by existing in this place.","But if he was to increase his weight and Immensity to be capable of getting close to those who had obtained the level of an Absolute, he had to do more than rely on passive growth!"]},{"number":4872,"title":"Chapter 4872: Chapter 4871: The Evolutionary Dead End","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Paradox had said there were boundless resources and treasures here, materials of incalculable value that could accelerate progression in ways that normal cultivation could never achieve.","Spark Fragments containing echoes of THE First Cause.","Contradiction Cores embodying paradoxes from before Paradox itself differentiated.","Pure Possibility granting access to Chaos in its most fundamental state.","All of these things existed somewhere in THE Prima Indifferentia, waiting to be claimed by those with the strength and fortune to find them.","\" Oh, THE Primordial Paradox...\"","In that invisible state of concealment within the proto-matter, Noah remembered the ancient Absolute and thought about where he might be right now. He had been separated from THE Primordial Paradox when the storms of proto-matter had reacted to his presence and swept him away, and he had no idea how much time had passed since then or how far he had traveled.","He didn’t have to worry about the safety of such a terrifying being as much as he had to worry about his own, given that THE Primordial Paradox was one of THE Four and had survived in THE Prima Indifferentia before. But Noah also couldn’t say for sure that he had lost the trail of that terrifying Undivided One, Bazuman, whose million crimson eyes had shown such interest in prey that could fight back.","For now, until he was potentially forced to end this temporal traversal early by having his body collapsed, he had to see what other opportunities were available in this region. Every moment he spent here was a moment of growth, but every moment was also a moment of danger.","And for him right now, it was actually easier to navigate the idea of looking for treasures and resources than it would have been for anyone else in Observable Existence.","Because at this moment, he held Infinite Undifferentiated Fate.","In this unique state of existence where his connection to destiny had become paradoxical and boundless, he pulled upon that Derivative Civilization with focused intent. A silent golden light emerged from his concealed form and spread out across the waves and seas of proto-matter like ripples in a pond, except these ripples carried the weight of fate itself seeking answers to questions he had yet to ask.","|Derivative Civilization of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate - Active Manifestation|","|The Derivative Civilization of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate exerts its Way across the surrounding existence. What is fated and destined are now infinitely amplified and capable of being chosen by the one wielding this Way, turning destiny from something that happens to you into something you actively shape and direct.|","|Your connection to fate has begun permeating across the surrounding regions of THE Prima Indifferentia. Destiny is not something that others make for you here, as you are infinitely making your own choices that inform different fates and different outcomes. The possibilities are endless, and you are selecting which possibilities become reality.|","|The fates of resources and treasures are being sought through this manifestation. Your existence has found potential links to three different directions from your current position, with each direction highlighted according to the proposed level of danger that accompanies the potential reward.|","|Direction One: Crimson designation indicating extreme danger. Potential reward: significant but path is guarded by forces that exceed current combat capability.|","|Direction Two: Crimson designation indicating extreme danger. Potential reward: significant but path is guarded by forces that exceed current combat capability.|","|Direction Three: Orange designation indicating high danger but potentially manageable. Potential reward: moderate to significant, with path containing hazards that fall within survivable parameters if approached with caution.|","...!","Noah saw faint lines of golden light stretching out in three separate directions from where he currently was, the threads of fate made visible through his Derivative Civilization’s influence on the surrounding proto-matter.","Two of them were surrounded with a deep hue of crimson light that pulsed with warning, the color of blood and danger and almost certain death.","Only a single one shone bright orange.","The two shining with crimson light emanated a great level of danger for him, the kind of danger that even his newly infinite existence might not be able to survive. Perhaps Undivided Ones guarded those paths. Perhaps Formless Terrors lurked along their routes.","The one pulsing with orange light seemed to be potentially manageable but still very dangerous, the kind of danger that would test him without necessarily destroying him. The kind of hardship that Vakochev demanded for progression rather than the kind that simply ended existence.","But...","Everything in Existence was dangerous.","Hardship and adversity were a must for growth, weren’t they?","THE Primordial Paradox had said it himself when discussing the Vakochev Scales: if one’s foundation hadn’t weathered through waves of Immensity and hardship, if one’s Way hadn’t been established through genuine adversity, then the doorway to the second Scale would remain uncrossable regardless of how powerful one became.","So while feeling the immense growth and Immensity of his existence expanding with every passing moment, and seeking to grow it even more while he had the opportunity in this place, Noah began to move once more.","He took a step toward the orange-designated path.","And even though he did so, what actually moved was a swirling storm of proto-matter that concealed his existence within its undefined currents. The storm shot forward at speeds that made the proto-matter around it blur and distort, covering distances that should have taken considerable time in mere moments.","His speed was approaching the speed of his very good boy, Skoll.","His speed was approaching the speed of an Absolute.","...!","He had grown so much in such a short time, and he was just getting started.","As he moved silently through THE Prima Indifferentia, his concealment holding even at these tremendous velocities, Noah thought about the words of THE Primordial Paradox and this place as potentially the origin of THE Entity.","The one thing that stuck with him was what THE Primordial Paradox had said about THE Formless Terrors and THE Undivided Ones, the entities that represented the greatest dangers within this undifferentiated expanse.","THE Formless Terrors especially haunted his thoughts, because they had lost all definition of their existence and now moved around seeking to attack anything that possessed definition. They wanted to make others like themselves, to drag differentiated beings down into the formless state they had been trapped in.","And the words that THE Primordial Paradox had spoken resonated with something he had heard before.","THE Primordial Paradox had said exactly:","\"It is not malice. It is something more fundamental than malice. It is the natural behaviour of undifferentiated existence encountering differentiated existence.\"","It was not malice.","When THE Secretive Eon had talked with him, she had mentioned how she, or they, were not doing anything overly malicious. They were simply returning things to their truest nature, helping existence achieve a state that they believed was more fundamental and more pure. And the more that others joined them, the less conflict there would be, as they would collectively focus on moving across the Scales of Existence together.","THE Secretive Eon had been confident that the second Scale would be achieved rather rapidly once enough of Observable Existence had been unified under THE Entity’s influence.","The philosophy was almost seductive in its simplicity.","Join us. Become one with us. Stop fighting and start ascending together.","But now, with what Noah had just learned from THE Primordial Paradox, a fundamental flaw in that philosophy became abundantly clear.","The Vakochev Scales of Existence demanded hardship for progression.","They demanded adversity and conflict.","They demanded that foundations be built through genuine struggle.","So THE Entity seeking to infect everyone and have all of Existence collectively move toward the goal of elevation might truly be an evolutionary dead end. For those who had been unified under THE Entity’s influence, there would be no genuine adversity because they would all be working toward the same goal without opposition. There would be no hardship because hardship required something to struggle against, and when everyone was the same, struggle became meaningless.","THE Secretive Eon had spoken of ascending together.","But The Scales of Existence didn’t care about collective ascension.","The Scales of Existence cared about individual hardship woven into individual foundations.","The actions of THE Entity, if successful, would actually halt all progression across Observable Existence.","No one would reach the second Scale.","No one would advance beyond where they currently were.","Everyone would be unified, yes, but unified in stagnation rather than growth.","\"...\"","The thought was a heavy and deadly one as Noah moved across THE Prima Indifferentia, following the lead of his Derivative Civilization toward what should be a resource or treasure that also held a level of danger.","THE Entity might not even know about this flaw in its philosophy.","Or perhaps it did know and didn’t care.","Or perhaps the goal was never actually ascension but something else entirely, something that used the promise of collective growth as a lure while the true purpose remained hidden behind layers of infection!"]},{"number":4873,"title":"Chapter 4873: Chapter 4872: Existence Is! I","paragraphs":["Across eons of time.","Far from the weavings of THE Infinite Unfurling in a past that Noah was currently experiencing.","In the current era after THE Fallout.","In Alfheimr.","An unknown number of light years from the region where Noah had held an illusory consciousness meeting with THE Primordial Chaos, far from where THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive had met him and clashed with words that carried the weight of civilizations, there existed an abode that was sacred to the lifeforms of this Primordial Realm.","It sat atop a mountain peak that rose from clouds of luminescent mist, the summit reaching toward skies that burned with the twilight of Alfheimr. The mountain itself was ancient beyond measure, its slopes covered with forests of trees that had witnessed the differentiation of Observable Existence and continued to witness everything that came after.","At the peak stood a simple multicolored stone temple.","Not grand in the way that palaces were grand. Not imposing in the way that fortresses were imposing. It was simple in the way that truly sacred things were simple, its architecture speaking of purpose rather than ostentation. The stones that formed its walls held every color that light could produce, shifting and changing as the twilight touched them from different angles, and the air around it carried a weight that pressed against any existence that approached.","This was a place where THE Creature had once walked.","The figures of THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger appeared at the foot of the temple, their forms manifesting from spatial distortions.","Origin looked up at the temple with eyes that held memories stretching back to before The Earliest Folds, before her collapse, before everything had changed. Her milky white form seemed almost fragile in this moment despite the power she now held, her expression complex with emotions that she rarely allowed others to see.","She turned to Hunger.","\" Can you wait for me down here?\"","Her voice was soft, almost hesitant.","\"I just... I need a moment. When I come down, I will have my answer.\"","She paused, her eyes meeting his.","\" And you will have yours.\"","...!","Her expression was complex as Hunger heard this and stayed still, his eyes heavy with understanding. His dark hair flowed past his shoulders, stirred by winds that carried the weight of Alfheimr’s twilight, and his crimson eyes held a light of defiance that never truly faded regardless of the circumstances.","Lesser beings would not ever think about competing against THE Creature for anything, let alone for the affection of one who had given THE Creature her Everything.","But not Hunger.","The light of all Inevitabilities burned within him as he sat down on the stone steps leading up to the temple, his posture relaxed but his attention sharp. He would wait. He would be patient!","And when Origin came down from that mountain, whatever answer she carried would determine everything that came next.","Origin went up the temple.","Her steps were light and measured as she continued up the ancient stones, her gaze reflecting memories of times when she had climbed these same steps with hope. She remembered when THE Creature had been everything to her. She remembered when his presence had been enough to make existence feel meaningful.","She remembered when she had given him her Everything, and he had accepted it without telling her what that acceptance would truly cost.","She continued until she entered the temple fully, passing through the simple archway into an interior that held no decorations, no ornaments, no displays of power. Just empty space and the weight of presence that had accumulated across eons of beings coming here to seek audience with THE Creature.","She came to stand close to the temple’s center, and there she saw it.","A white mat.","Not a grand throne or anything unfathomable that would befit one of THE Four. Just an empty mat where visitors would kneel, simple and unassuming in a way that almost seemed like mockery given the power of the being who would appear before it.","But Origin did not kneel.","She calmly proceeded to sit opposite to this mat, her legs folded beneath her and her back straight with dignity that refused to bow. Her expression seemed made up, her decision already finalized before she had even begun climbing those temple steps.","\"I demand an answer.\"","BOOM!","Four words, but they were so heavy that the air itself seemed to compress around them. Before she even finished saying them, the area around the mat in front of her fluctuated with distortions that bent light and space simultaneously, and the illusory visage of an entity shrouded in multicolored flames appeared.","THE Creature!","His face could barely be observed as it was surrounded by multicolored flames that burned with every color that existence could produce, fires that didn’t consume but simply were. But one could see eyes of immensity and calmness looking out from within those flames, eyes that held depths which even Absolutes couldn’t fully perceive.","Eyes that looked at Origin with something that might have been regret.","Origin’s body trembled lightly as she looked at THE Creature, biting her lips as she heard his voice for what seemed like forever.","\"I am sorry.\"","BOOM!","She had come demanding an answer, and the first thing she was told was this.","Two words that she had never expected to hear from someone who embodied Existence itself. Two words that confirmed everything she had feared and suspected since regaining consciousness after her collapse.","Her face paled and turned ashen as anger flashed in her eyes, bright and hot and barely contained! She looked defiantly at THE Creature with an expression that held none of the reverence that had once defined her interactions with him.","\"I gave you my Everything.\"","Her voice trembled with emotion that she couldn’t fully suppress.","\"The least I expected from you was honesty. I do not even care that I was collapsed. I just...\"","She paused, gathering herself.","\"It would have been nice to have had a level of honesty. To be looked at as a peer and not as someone lesser. You never told me what was really going on. You never looked at me as anything worth sharing your grand plans with.\"","BOOM!","She was venting out all her frustrations at this time, years of suppressed anger finally finding release in the presence of the one who had caused them. Her milky white form flickered with agitation that made the temple’s multicolored stones pulse in sympathy.","THE Creature took everything in without interruption, his multicolored flames burning steadily as he listened to accusations.","\"I am not a perfect being.\"","His voice was booming yet calm, carrying the weight of Existence itself even as it acknowledged failure.","\" Far from it. I make mistakes, and I made many mistakes that I can blame on the nature of my Existence. Existence is. Existence was. I became...too attuned with it.\"","The flames around him shifted through colors that spoke of memory and regret.","\"I let things flow as they should without intervening when I should. As much as I can blame my nature on this, it was still my choice.\"","He paused.","\" This was unfair to you, so I apologize.\"","...!"]},{"number":4874,"title":"Chapter 4874: Chapter 4873: Existence Is! II","paragraphs":["The words were unfathomably calm, and Origin found herself searching within them for emotion that matched her own. She wanted to see pain. She wanted to see remorse that burned as hot as her anger. She wanted to know that her suffering had meant something to him beyond mere acknowledgment!","But she couldn’t find it.","Not the emotion she wanted, anyway.","THE Creature’s apology was sincere, but it was also the apology of a being who existed on a level where individual suffering, no matter how profound, was just one thread in an infinite weaving. He meant his words, but he couldn’t feel them the way she needed him to feel them.","She breathed out and controlled her existence, forcing the trembling of her form to still as she asked the question that had haunted her since her reconstruction.","\" Why did you allow me to be collapsed?\"","Her voice was steadier now, colder.","\" The more I think of it, the more I can see that Paradox shouldn’t have had the power he had. Even if he supposedly took your heart by using Anaximander, even if you were chained, you are powerful. You were powerful.\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\" So really, why...did I have to be collapsed? Why did you allow it?\"","There were many whys she wanted to ask, but this was the critical one. This was the question that would determine whether anything between them could ever be salvaged.","THE Creature looked at her with a gaze that truly wanted to portray how he felt, the multicolored flames parting slightly as if to allow her to see more of his expression. What she saw there was not cruelty. What she saw there was not indifference.","What she saw there was the certainty of someone who had made calculations that others couldn’t understand.","\" At that time, I mistakenly believed that it was all...for the sake of adversity.\"","BOOM!","As he said this, his finger tapped out in a gesture that was almost casual, and in the next moment the aura around THE Living Origin exploded with power that she hadn’t fully realized she possessed.","While she was sitting down, milky white light erupted from her existence as an aura of Absolute radiated outward with intensity that made the temple’s stones tremble. A heavy aura filled with Immensity that spoke of foundations forged through genuine hardship, through genuine suffering, through genuine loss.","And it continued rising.","The power climbed nonsensically higher, revealing depths to her foundation that THE Creature’s gesture had unlocked or perhaps simply revealed with a tap!","From Half-Step Absolute to Absolute with a tap!","But even as she felt this Immensity, her eyes were those of anger as she wanted to rebuke THE Creature.","For adversity?","For adversity?!","\"One of the many mistales I made. I should have communicated with you more clearly on it.\"","THE Creature’s voice remained calm despite her obvious rage.","\"I should not have been passive. But the hardship you and many others went through forged a grand foundation for your existences. It made Absolute possible for beings who might otherwise have never reached it.\"","His multicolored flames pulsed with something that might have been pride in what she had become.","\" And it altered your existences to allow THE Second Scale of Existence to be possible for many.\"","BOOM!","...!","The words caused Origin to become even more ashen as her eyes grew cold with understanding that she didn’t want to have. The implications of what THE Creature was saying pressed against her mind with weight that threatened to crush everything she thought she knew about her own existence.","She looked at THE Creature with eyes that held ice rather than fire.","\" THE Loom. THE Fallout. THE Living Paradox.\"","Her voice was quiet now, dangerously quiet.","\" If you wanted, could you have stopped all of it?\"","The question was a terrifying one, and the silence that followed was even more terrifying.","\"...\"","THE Creature did not answer.","And this alone caused the eyes of Origin to flash with Immensity as she understood that this non-answer was its own answer.","He could have stopped it! He could have prevented THE Fallout from ever occurring. He could have prevented the devastation that had reshaped Observable Existence!","But he had chosen not to.","For the sake of adversity.","\" Haha...\"","She couldn’t help but laugh, the sound hollow and bitter in the sacred space of the temple.","\" Right. You are THE Creature. The entity that seemed so otherworldly and strong. I always found myself questioning how you could have been defeated by THE Living Paradox, how you could have been chained and had your heart stolen.\"","Her laughter died, replaced by a smile that held no warmth.","\"It turned out you were playing games that us lesser minds didn’t even deserve to know about. How grand. How majestic you are, O Creature!\"","Her words turned biting at the end as she rose from her seated position, her chest heaving with anger that she no longer tried to suppress. The Civilizational Authority around her trembled with agitation that made the temple’s multicolored stones flicker wildly, responding to her emotional state.","She looked straight into the eyes of THE Creature.","THE Creature looked back, and within the eyes of this entity shrouded by multicolored flames, there was a sense of true apology that went deeper than his earlier words had conveyed. He understood her anger. He accepted it as deserved. And yet he couldn’t fully regret his choices because those choices had led to outcomes that served purposes she couldn’t yet comprehend.","\" Many things were done wrong, Ljósmóðir.\"","He used her ancient name, the name she had held before becoming THE Living Origin, and the familiarity of it made her chest tighten.","\" We all live and learn. The ends do not always justify the means. I am trying to do things differently.\"","His voice, even though still grand, was earnest in a way that she hadn’t heard from him in eons.","\" But know that what I did, while for myself, was also for you and many others.\"","Origin listened to his words as her chest stopped heaving, the anger slowly settling into something colder and more permanent. She smiled brilliantly, but the smile didn’t reach her eyes as she turned around from THE Creature.","\" Did you get what you wanted?\"","She asked this question without looking back at him.","\" Do you have your Second Scale of Existence under your grand thumb?\"","...!"]},{"number":4875,"title":"Chapter 4875: Chapter 4874: Existence Is! III","paragraphs":["This time around as well, THE Creature did not reply.","That also should have been its own answer.","Origin smiled at this non-answer as she began to walk away from the temple, her steps light despite the weight of everything that had been said.","\"I am happy for you. I really am.\"","Her voice carried no happiness at all.","\"I wish you the best, O Creature.\"","BOOM!","With such words, she walked away and did not look back.","The multicolored flames around THE Creature pulsed faintly as he looked out from the temple, watching her descend the steps toward where THE First Hunger waited. His eyes were filled with unknown Immensities and wonder, contemplating paths that only he could see and outcomes that only he could understand.","He had lost something today.","Whether that loss was worth what he had gained remained to be seen.","—","Origin left the temple with light steps, her form descending the ancient stones with grace that belied the emotional weight she had been carrying. Even though her body radiated terrifying waves of Absolute power that made the very air around her tremble with respect, her eyes felt light and her breathing felt free.","As if she had released a heavy weight that had been pressing against her shoulders since the moment she had been reconstructed.","She reached the bottom of the steps where she had left Hunger, and she found him exactly where she had asked him to wait. His dark hair still flowed past his shoulders. His crimson eyes still burned with the light of all Inevitabilities. His posture was still relaxed but attentive, ready for whatever came next.","He rose as she approached.","She reached out toward THE First Hunger, offering her hand.","He took it.","His fingers wrapped around hers with warmth that THE Creature’s apologies had lacked, with presence that felt immediate and real rather than distant and calculating. She had been given her answer by THE Creature, and in this gesture, in this offered hand, she gave her answer to Hunger.","THE First Hunger turned to stare at the distant visage of THE Creature still visible within the temple, his crimson eyes holding a murky gaze that contained depths of emotion he rarely displayed.","Then he pulled gently on her hand, and the two of them began to walk down the mountain together.","Not once had he believed he would lose against THE Creature.","Not once had he doubted that his patience would be rewarded.","And so far, it seemed like at least at this time, THE First Hunger had won.","He walked down a mountain holding the hand of an Absolute, and the twilight of Alfheimr seemed to burn brighter around them as they descended.","—","Far from Alfheimr.","In a region that could be considered within the spaces between spaces, where the boundaries of Observable Existence grew thin and the rules that governed reality became suggestions rather than laws, the figure of THE Creature was situated back to back with the figure of Anaximander.","The two of them floated in void that wasn’t quite void, surrounded by currents of authority that flowed from THE Creature’s multicolored flames like rivers of pure being. Anaximander’s scholarly robes drifted in winds that had no source, his ancient eyes contemplating equations and theories that only he could perceive.","They had been here for some time.","Immense waves of Existence were spinning around them in patterns, and at this moment, between THE Creature and Anaximander, a flash of colorless light shone and erupted far above them.","The light climbed higher and higher until it reached a point where space itself seemed to object to its presence, and then it carved outward with force that made both beings look up with attention.","An unimaginable crack formed in the fabric of reality.","A Crack of Observable Existence.","It was a rare and impossible thing to find as only a few places had it, but what was impossible for THE Creature?","The moment this crack formed, Anaximander looked up with marvel and curiosity that burned brighter than any scientific discovery he had ever made. His ancient eyes studied the fracture with the intensity of someone who had dedicated eons to understanding the nature of reality, and he couldn’t help but ask THE Creature what he was witnessing.","\" What is this?\"","THE Creature looked up at the crack with eyes that held knowledge stretching back to before THE Infinite Unfurling, his multicolored flames pulsing with rhythms that seemed to sync with the crack’s formation.","\" It would be much easier to explain in a few seconds.\"","The moment his words were done, the Crack of Observable Existence above them opened fully.","From within that crack, a storm of proto-matter instantly surged out like a pillar of undefined potential, descending with purpose that transcended random occurrence. The storm didn’t spread across the space between spaces. It didn’t dissipate into the void around them.","It landed directly onto the figure of Anaximander.","The proto-matter covered his existence entirely, wrapping around his scholarly form with churning chaos that should have undifferentiated anything it touched. But Anaximander didn’t dissolve. He didn’t blur at the edges. Instead, while surrounded by the storm, his eyes burned with curiosity that held no fear as he raised his hand and twirled strands of proto-matter between his fingers.","He was familiar with this substance.","He was comfortable with its presence.","The storm pulsed once, twice, and then shockingly entered his body as if returning to a home it had been separated from for far too long. Anaximander began to tremble as an unfathomable Immensity was released from within him, power that had been dormant awakening with force that made THE Creature’s multicolored flames flicker in response.","Instantly, in this entire region, everything froze over.","Not frozen in the sense of ice, but frozen in the sense of absolute stillness. The currents of authority stopped flowing. The void stopped being void. Everything achieved a state of stasis!","...!","Anaximander looked like he had a dazed expression as the storm died down around him, waves of proto-matter flowing serenely across his figure like loyal attendants welcoming a returning master. But his expression didn’t show triumph or satisfaction.","It showed a sense of loss.","Almost as if he did not want this.","Almost as if the memories now flooding back into his existence were memories he had been happy to forget.","Yet THE Creature looked down toward him with eyes that held ancient knowing, his multicolored flames burning with warmth that seemed almost paternal.","\" Hello, Jack. It has been quite some time.\"","...!"]},{"number":4876,"title":"Chapter 4876: Chapter 4875: Last Gamble! I","paragraphs":["Jack.","Jokul.","These names felt foreign in Anaximander’s mind, labels that belonged to someone else, designations that carried weight he had spent eons trying to escape. He shook his head as if he did not want them, as if he did not recognize them, as if the being they referred to was a stranger wearing his face!","THE Creature’s gaze softened at this response, understanding filling his multicolored eyes as he continued speaking with the patience of someone who had all the time in Existence.","\" Your experiment in defining yourself was a grand one. You lived a life of hardship as the scientist and explorer Anaximander, without any of your memories, without any of your knowledge.\"","He paused, letting the words settle.","\" But your existence is filled with weavings of undifferentiation. Your existence, by nature, is undefined.\"","At such words, Anaximander became utterly still and serious, the proto-matter around him ceasing its serene flow as his attention focused entirely on the being before him. His ancient eyes held defiance that burned brighter than the frost he had just released.","\" My existence may be undefined.\"","His voice was steady despite the turmoil that must have been raging within him.","\" But my Way, my self, it is defined. I like Anaximander. I like who I have become.\"","He straightened, his scholarly robes settling around him with dignity that transcended his undefined nature.","\" Sometimes one has to take a step and say who they are. To define themselves and remain what they are, fully and truly.\"","His eyes met THE Creature’s without flinching.","\" And I am an explorer. I am Anaximander.\"","BOOM!","As he said this, the frost in this region receded and disappeared as if acknowledging his declaration. He tapped out with authority that made space itself respond, and the Crack of Observable Existence above them shook with resonance!","Immense seas of proto-matter, more than ten times grander than before, gushed out from the crack and landed on Anaximander with force that would have annihilated lesser beings. But he absorbed it all without faltering, his existence drinking in the undefined potential while his definition remained firmly in place.","He had made a choice, like many in Existence made their choices.","To be what he wanted to be rather than what he had been born as.","To define himself rather than accept the undefined nature of his origins.","THE Creature had also made his own choices across the eons, some right and some wrong, some that he regretted and some that he stood by despite the consequences. He looked at the most recent choice of his friend with a smile that held genuine warmth.","Every choice was a path taken.","And every path was a river of endless possibilities.","As he thought of this, THE Creature couldn’t help but look out in a different direction entirely, his gaze piercing through the spaces between spaces toward destinations that only he could perceive. His booming voice echoed out as it spoke to no one in particular.","\" What choice will you make?\"","It was a simple question, and it was unknown whether it was aimed at THE Living Paradox who held a Claim through methods that many didn’t fully understand, or THE Secretive Eon who sought to unite all of Observable Existence, or THE Primordial Chaos who watched everything from his corner of reality, or perhaps someone else entirely that THE Creature was thinking about right now.","---","Eons passed and eons gone.","Far in THE Infinite Unfurling , past a Crack of Observable Existence, inside THE Prima Indifferentia.","In a region where proto-matter had taken on properties that shouldn’t have been possible even for undefined substance, an ancient creature made its home among formations that defied description.","The proto-matter here was molten, shining crimson-gold with heat that had nothing to do with temperature and everything to do with concentrated potential. It curved in millions of Mobius strips that twisted through dimensions that hadn’t fully differentiated, creating an environment of endless loops where beginning and end lost all meaning.","The ancient creature itself was something between a serpent and a concept, its form stretching across hundreds of miles while simultaneously occupying a single point in space. Scales that shifted through every possible color covered its body, and eyes that numbered in the thousands dotted its length, each one watching a different aspect of the molten landscape it called home.","It had been here since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","It would likely be here long after.","And right now, it was watching a small crimson-gold seed that spun perpetually in the middle of this place with happiness that radiated from every one of its countless eyes.","The seed was no larger than a fist, but it burned with authority that made the surrounding Mobius strips of proto-matter bend toward it in reverence. Routinely, the seed would release a flash of light that carried the quality of undifferentiation, pure potential in its most concentrated form, and the ancient creature would absorb this light as it made its existence feel that much richer.","It had enjoyed this sensation for cycles.","Sometimes, the continued sensation something brought was grander than consuming it in a single gulp. The creature had learned this lesson long ago, and so it had been content to simply bask in the seed’s emissions rather than devour it entirely.","So the creature continued to enjoy the sensation this seed granted, its countless eyes blinking with contentment that spoke of simple pleasures appreciated across unfathomable spans of time.","Unbeknownst to it...","HUUM!","A storm of proto-matter arrived nearby, settling into the molten landscape as if it belonged there. The storm had been measuring this situation for several seconds, observing the ancient creature and its treasure with attention that went beyond mere curiosity.","The storm of proto-matter was naturally Noah, and his gaze was sharp as he looked at the terrifying scene ahead of him from within his concealment.","|Environmental Analysis - High Value Target Detected|","|You are observing an ancient entity designated as a Primordial Serpent of Undifferentiated Coils. Its power should rival or exceed weaker Absolutes, though its combat methodology would be fundamentally different from differentiated beings.|","|More significantly, you are observing the object it is benefiting from.|","| Object Classification: Spark Fragment of THE First Cause|","|This is a fragment that contains mere echoes of THE First Cause that initiated differentiation, but it is a fragment nonetheless. Consuming or integrating this Spark Fragment would provide tremendous advancement to your foundations, potentially accelerating your growth by factors that cannot be accurately calculated.|","|The Primordial Serpent has been passively absorbing emissions from this Spark Fragment for eons rather than consuming it directly.|","|You could potentially integrate it where the Serpent could not.|","|However, acquiring it would require either defeating the Serpent or stealing the Fragment without detection.|","|Neither option carries favorable odds given current power differentials.|","...!","A Spark Fragment of THE First Cause.","The very thing that THE Primordial Paradox had mentioned when describing the resources of incalculable value that could be found in THE Prima Indifferentia. Not the full First Cause, of course, that would be something beyond even Absolutes to claim, but a fragment containing echoes of the moment when differentiation began.","Noah’s foundations trembled with hunger that had nothing to do with his Derivative Civilization of Infinite Hunger. This was pure desire, the recognition of something that could elevate his existence in ways that normal resources could never achieve.","And at this moment, as he was thinking about how he might acquire it...","|Critical Alert - Threat Approaching|","|Infinite Undifferentiated Fate has sensed the fate of collapse drawing closer from a specific direction. THE Undivided One, Bazuman, continues to track your existence through methods that your concealment cannot fully prevent. That relentless fucker is coming, and its arrival is estimated...soon?Soon.|","|You have limited time to make a decision.|","|Attempt acquisition of the Spark Fragment and risk confrontation with both the Primordial Serpent and Bazuman.|","|Or...well, there isn’t truly another viable option.|","...!","He had never escaped the attention of an Undivided One that continued to chase him across THE Prima Indifferentia with persistence that bordered on obsession.","And a treasure lay right before him that could help cement his power even more, continuing to allow him to build a foundation that might just allow him to go against Absolutes even without having become one himself.","The Spark Fragment pulsed with another emission of undifferentiated light, and the Primordial Serpent’s countless eyes blinked with contentment as it absorbed the offering.","Behind him, somewhere in the churning expanse of THE Prima Indifferentia, Bazuman was approaching with million crimson eyes and endless jaws.","So when it came to this pivotal moment, Noah knew that his time in this temporal traversal might be nearing an end. He had already gained so much, had already transformed in ways that he couldn’t have anticipated, had already become something that had no precedent in Observable Existence.","But he was also greedy.","And greed, properly directed, was just another word for ambition.","\" In for a penny, in for a pound.\"","...!","He moved!"]},{"number":4877,"title":"Chapter 4877: Chapter 4876: Last Gamble! II","paragraphs":["The Primordial Serpent was moving languidly and basking in the glow of undifferentiation brought about by the Spark Fragment of THE First Cause.","Its power was mighty and its being was heavy to the point that its senses perceived all the countless changes occurring across this region of molten proto-matter. Every shift in the Mobius strips that curved around its domain registered against its awareness. Every fluctuation in the undefined potential that comprised its home was catalogued and assessed.","Nothing escaped its notice.","Nothing had escaped its notice for eons!","And at this moment, it felt like the proto-matter in the surroundings felt distinctly different.","The undefined substance that should have flowed in familiar patterns was behaving strangely, its currents shifting in ways that spoke of external influence rather than natural variation. Something was here that shouldn’t be here. Something was approaching that didn’t belong in this place.","But the moment it felt this, the moment its countless eyes began to turn toward the anomaly with attention that had ended the existence of many intruders across the ages...","BOOM!","Blue-gold light exploded across its domain.","Radiant seals erupted like a field of beautiful flowers blooming in impossible synchronization, each one manifesting from the proto-matter storm that had been concealing Noah’s existence. They spread outward in waves that multiplied infinitely, their petals burning with the devouring light of Infinite Hunger and the destabilizing quality of undifferentiation that this place had taught them to carry!","The devouring light of Infinite Hunger reached toward the Primordial Serpent with appetite that transcended normal consumption, seeking to break down its ancient existence into fuel for Noah’s ever-growing foundations. The undifferentiation quality pressed against the Serpent’s defined form with pressure that made even this native of THE Prima Indifferentia recoil in shock.","The Primordial Serpent was pushed back!","Its countless eyes widened with surprise that it hadn’t felt in eons, its massive form retreating from the field of infinite flowers that burned with authority it couldn’t immediately counter. For a single moment, its attention was entirely focused on the seals rather than what the seals were concealing.","And in that moment, the humanoid visage of Noah appeared right before the Spark Fragment of THE First Cause.","Something that a native of THE Prima Indifferentia had been holding onto and enjoying its constant boon for years beyond counting now had a thief standing before it, blue-gold light burning around a figure whose wings spread wide with infinity blazing through every feather.","What would Noah do to it?","Without even a delay, time seemed to slow as Noah flung his body forward with movement that committed everything to this single action. His jaws opened wide, wider than should have been possible for a humanoid form, stretching to accommodate what he was about to consume. His mouth wrapped around the entire area where the grain-sized Spark Fragment of THE First Cause spun in perpetual rotation.","And it disappeared down his throat!","...!","Consumed in a single gulp after the Primordial Serpent had spent eons savoring its emissions rather than devouring it whole.","The Primordial Serpent saw this scene.","Its countless eyes, which had been watching with shock just moments before, now melted with sheer rage and lividity!","This was the fury of something that had just witnessed its most treasured possession, its companion across eons of existence, its source of joy and enrichment, eaten right in front of it by an intruder who had no right to be here.","As if an intruder had stripped his lover and taken them whole right before his eyes!","How dare he? How dare he?!","BOOM!","The molten proto-matter around them responded to its rage by churning with violence that made the Mobius strips shatter and reform in patterns of pure chaos.","A crimson pillar of undifferentiation erupted from the Primordial Serpent’s form.","The pillar wasn’t an attack in the conventional sense but rather a release of everything this ancient creature was, its full Depth and Immensity manifesting as a column of authority that made Noah’s infinite seals seem like flowers before a hurricane. The Serpent charged forward through the field of blue-gold petals, and where lesser beings would have been consumed by the Infinite Hunger quality or destabilized by the undifferentiation, the Primordial Serpent used its pure Depth to simply push through.","The infinite seals multiplied to replace those destroyed.","The Serpent destroyed them faster than they could multiply.","Its Depth was simply too immense, its existence too heavy, its rage too absolute!","The seals that could devour and undifferentiate attacks were being swept aside like leaves in a storm, pushed sideways by authority that had been accumulating since before THE Infinite Unfurling!","The Primordial Serpent appeared before Noah in an instant.","Its tail, a appendage that stretched for hundreds of miles and contained the concentrated weight of an existence older than the Earliest Folds itself, smashed into him with force that should have ended his temporal traversal immediately.","But Noah’s visage was valiant as he waited for this strike.","He didn’t try to dodge. He didn’t try to block. He used the force of the impact and his own Immensity to accomplish something that pure defense could never achieve.","He flung himself far back.","The tail strike that should have destroyed him instead became a catapult, launching his existence away from the enraged Serpent at speeds that turned him into a streak of blue-gold light. His velocity fuly attained the speed of Absolutes as he rocketed away from the molten region, away from the creature whose treasure he had just stolen, away from a fight he couldn’t possibly win!","He was making a run for it like any good thief should.","But at such a time...","\" Found you, slippery thing.\"","WAA!","The voice came from everywhere and nowhere simultaneously, formed from concepts that hadn’t fully differentiated into sound.","\" Come here.\"","BOOM!","Bazuman materialized in the space between Noah and freedom.","THE Undivided One’s entry was heralded by the cessation of all normal motion in the region, reality itself pausing to acknowledge the arrival of something that predated reality’s existence. Its form had shifted since their last encounter, now appearing as a mass of flesh and undefined potential that stretched across miles of space, but its million crimson eyes remained constant.","Those eyes were all focused on Noah.","The rageful Primordial Serpent, which had been charging forward with murderous intent toward the thief who had stolen its treasure, froze in place.","It was scared shitless.","But terror didn’t stop the situation from escalating.","Bazuman stood still, its million crimson eyes opening fully as every single one of them released a terrifying suctioning force that pulled everything in the nearby light years toward its position. The molten proto-matter that comprised this region began flowing toward the Undivided One like water toward a drain. The Mobius strips that had been curving through undefined space straightened as they were drawn toward that central point of consumption.","All proto-matter was being pulled in.","All things were being pulled in.","Even the Primordial Serpent was included in this gravitational nightmare, its massive form being dragged toward Bazuman despite its attempts to resist. Its rage and madness returned as it realized it was now caught between the thief who had stolen its treasure and another Undivided One who would consume them both without discrimination.","It roared toward Bazuman with fury born of desperation.","But its hateful gaze remained fixed on Noah, who was currently being pulled back toward The Undivided One alongside everything else in this region of THE Prima Indifferentia.","He couldn’t run.","The suctioning force was too strong, too absolute, too fundamental to resist through conventional means. His streak of blue-gold light was being dragged backward despite his velocity of Absolute speeds, the pull of Bazuman’s million eyes overwhelming everything he threw against it.","And by all means, he should be scared shitless right now.","He should be terrified like the Primordial Serpent was terrified, facing an enemy that could consume Absolutes without effort and had been hunting him across THE Prima Indifferentia with persistence that bordered on obsession.","But...","DUM!","What he had just swallowed was making his existence pulse with excitement and Immensity that he couldn’t explain.","The Spark Fragment of THE First Cause was dissolving into his foundations, and the echoes of the moment when differentiation began were flooding through his existence with authority that made everything else seem small.","He felt...he felt...! Fuck, he couldn’t even explain how he felt!","He wanted to howl.","He wanted to roar.","He wanted to release the joy and exhilaration of having consumed something that most beings in Observable Existence would never even see, let alone integrate into their foundations.","But... well, he needed to run.","So while gazing at the terrifying Undivided One that he couldn’t beat even if he attained the power of an Absolute, Noah’s existence pulsed as he began to speak...","Gibberish.","The gibberish required to open The Interstices.","The undefined Phoneme that would create a doorway to the spaces between spaces, the routes that could carry him away from this place and back toward safety as he would utilize Temporal Traversal to return.","But as he did...","\" Youngest, don’t!\"","HUUM!","From a far distance, cutting through even the suctioning force of Bazuman’s million eyes, Noah saw the materialization of THE Primordial Paradox. The ancient Absolute’s obsidian form had appeared at the edge of this region, his expression one of solemnity and alarm as if Noah had done something he absolutely shouldn’t have.","But Noah had already committed.","He sent a message rapidly through waves of undifferentiation that carried his intent across the distance between them, his thoughts pressing into THE Primordial Paradox’s perception with urgency that couldn’t be delayed.","\"I will see you soon. Not here, but eons from now.\"","...!","And as Noah looked over toward THE Primordial Paradox, completing the gibberish that would open The Interstices, he also saw that beside the ancient Absolute there was someone else.","Someone who looked oddly familiar.","Someone whose features seemed to shift between a scholarly explorer and something far older, far more powerful, far more connected to THE Prima Indifferentia than any visitor should be.","Noah blinked as if his eyes were playing tricks on him.","But he had already spoken the gibberish.","The undefined Phoneme had already left his existence.","And in the next moment...","CRACK!","A Crack of Observable Existence appeared where Noah was, tearing through the fabric of THE Prima Indifferentia with force that made even Bazuman’s suctioning eyes pause in surprise.","Noah disappeared into it.","But moments before he vanished entirely, he realized what THE Primordial Paradox had been referring to when he said \"don’t.\"","They had entered THE Prima Indifferentia through the Crack of Observable Existence, not through The Interstices.","It seemed there was a reason for this.","THE Prima Indifferentia couldn’t be reached through The Interstices because it existed in a state that predated the spaces between spaces.","So if one sought to open The Interstices while inside of THE Prima Indifferentia...","\" Oh.\"","Noah only had this thought of understanding before everything disappeared around him, the crack swallowing his existence and carrying him toward a destination that he hadn’t chosen and couldn’t predict.","---","What was left behind in THE Prima Indifferentia was chaos of a different kind.","The Primordial Serpent roared with madness that had lost its target, its countless eyes searching for the thief who had stolen its treasure and finding nothing but the crack that was already closing. Its rage had nowhere to go, its fury had no outlet, and the loss of its Spark Fragment pressed against its ancient existence with weight that would take eons to process.","Bazuman stood silent!","THE Undivided One’s million crimson eyes had stopped their suctioning force the moment the crack appeared, its attention entirely focused on the anomaly that had just occurred.","And at the edge of this region, THE Primordial Paradox and Jack stood together, with the former looking toward Bazuman with a sharp gaze.","THE Primordial Paradox’s obsidian eyes held irritation that burned cold.","This Undivided One had been chasing THE Youngest across THE Prima Indifferentia, had forced him into increasingly desperate measures, had caused him to make a choice that opened a crack that shouldn’t have been opened from this side!","And now THE Youngest was gone.","THE Primordial Paradox stared at Bazuman with eyes that held the promise of consequences, but...who knew how this encounter unfolded and finished as at this moment, a thief was either given a recompense to breathe and enjoy his boon, or he may have just neen extinguished entirely!"]},{"number":4878,"title":"Chapter 4878: Chapter 4877: Echoes! I","paragraphs":["Noah had eaten a lot of things across his life.","Some good, some bad, some tantalizing beyond description.","Some things he ate on a regular basis as he never stopped. He had consumed Absolute Everythings and Weavings of collapsed entities and treasures that entire civilizations would have gone to war over.","The Spark Fragment of THE First Cause instantly shot up to the number one spot of things he would love to be eating every day.","As ludicrous as it was to mention it, the sensation flooding through his existence made everything else he had ever consumed feel like pale imitations of what food should actually be. Every aspect of his being was amplified, every fiber of his foundations singing with pleasure.","He imagined this was the type of high that drug addicts felt, the kind that kept them going back even if they were destroying their lives in the process!","Because damn.","The things he would do for this sensation.","He would fight Bazuman again. He would steal from a thousand Primordial Serpents! He would challenge THE Undivided Ones themselves if it meant experiencing this feeling one more time.","But...","HUUM!","His existence buzzed with Immensity as he forced himself not to be lost in the sensation, pulling his consciousness back from the edge of euphoria in order to truly understand what was happening to his existence. The pleasure was seductive, yes, but pleasure without understanding was just distraction from the truth of what he was becoming.","And...","And...?","\"Hmm?\"","He wasn’t seeing any immense and unfathomable changes that he expected.","Yes, his foundation was rising rapidly across Surface, Intermediate, and Fundamental Depths. He could feel the weight of his existence growing heavier with every passing moment, his Immensity scaling upward at rates that should have been impossible.","But... he felt like this shouldn’t be it.","He was looking for something truly grand.","A Spark Fragment of THE First Cause, a piece of the very moment when differentiation began, and all it was doing was making his foundation heavier? That seemed almost anticlimactic given what he had risked to acquire it!","He had stolen from an ancient Primordial Serpent, had been chased by an Undivided One, had opened The Interstices in a place where The Interstices should never have been opened.","For foundation growth?","He frowned as he didn’t understand, but this moment of reflection allowed him to focus as he looked around him.","He had attempted to enter The Interstices when he apparently should not have, and right now he was somewhere that defied easy description. The space around him wasn’t differentiated in the way that Observable Existence was differentiated, but it also wasn’t undifferentiated in the way that THE Prima Indifferentia was undifferentiated.","It was somewhere in between.","Somewhere that shouldn’t exist.","|Critical Navigation Error - Existential Analysis|","|Accessing the spaces between spaces while within a region of undifferentiation would normally result in the collapse of even Absolutes. The combination of differentiated pathways and undifferentiated origin creates paradoxical weavings that trap existence in endless loops between definition and undefinition.|","|However, the weavings of your Infinities paired with the consumption of the Spark Fragment of THE First Cause are funneling your existence across these treacherous pathways without collapse. You are surviving what should not be survivable.|","|The issue is navigation rather than survival.|","|To define yourself at a certain time and location, existential coordinates would need to be viable and established within the weavings you are currently crossing. You would need to specify where you wish to emerge and when you wish to emerge there.|","|But due to the weavings of unclear and chaotic definition and undefinition surrounding everything in this space, no known coordinates of locations or times are currently viable for selection. The pathways cannot distinguish between differentiated destinations because they themselves are not fully and stably differentiated.|","|In simpler terms: you cannot choose where to go because the paths cannot understand what \"where\" means.|","...!","The prompts may have been hard to understand at first, but Noah’s eyes turned sharp as he realized they were basically saying that he was funneling across regions that had no clear stable definition. And because these regions had no clear definition, he couldn’t give them clear coordinates of where to go.","So he couldn’t leave.","So...was he just lost here endlessly, trapped in spaces between spaces that would carry him forever without ever depositing him anywhere real?","He shook his head at such a thought as the one thing he could appreciate about this place being both defined and undefined was that time didn’t seem to be a factor here.","And he loved having a moment to breathe.","For the first time since entering THE Prima Indifferentia, he actually had space to think without being chased by Undivided Ones or threatened by Formless Terrors or forced to make split-second decisions that determined whether his temporal traversal continued or ended.","Right now, he wanted to figure out exactly what was going on with the weavings of THE First Cause.","Surely the boons of something so grand would not be as disappointing as his foundations simply being elevated, right? There had to be more. There had to be something that justified the significance of what he had consumed!","He looked deep within himself where the grain-sized object spun rapidly at the center of his Organ of Civilization, his Infinities breaking down its authority with appetite. What was being broken down was scaling his foundation upward with speed that made his previous growth look glacial by comparison.","|Foundation Status - Updated Assessment|","|The Immensity of your Surface Depth has now reached 1100% comparative weight to THE Primordial Paradox at equivalent stage. This represents 11 times the foundation weight that THE Primordial Paradox possessed at Surface Depth before he became an Absolute.|","|The Immensity of your Intermediate Depth has now reached 1050% comparative weight. This represents 10.5 times the foundation weight of THE Primordial Paradox at equivalent stage.|","|The Immensity of your Fundamental Depth has undergone the most significant transformation.|","|Your Fundamental Depth has now reached the same level as THE Primordial Paradox and THE Creature before they took their steps to become Absolutes.|","|It is untested and purely theoretical, but as of right now, your collective Immensity may be arriving at the level of weak Absolutes, even without having attained this stage yourself.|","|Your Depth remains at Infinite Formless, but your weight may rival those who have transcended to Absolute. Weak Absolute. It cannot be stressed enough- hypothetically weak Absolutes.|","|This configuration has no precedent and requires verification through actual combat to confirm.|","...!"]},{"number":4879,"title":"Chapter 4879: Chapter 4878: Echoes! II","paragraphs":["So his foundation was reaching tremendous levels!","His Fundamental Depth, which had been so hard to raise and which represented the truest measurement of his potential before grasping Absolute, had now reached the level of THE Creature and THE Primordial Paradox before they became what they became.","After his movements across THE Prima Indifferentia, after the passive absorption of proto-matter through his Infinities, after swallowing the Spark Fragment of THE First Cause, his foundation had been elevated enough to rival what the greatest Absolutes had forged before their ascension.","It was all grand.","It was all impressive beyond what he could have hoped for when he first entered THE Prima Indifferentia.","But still, Noah felt like something was missing.","The harvest and potential of the Spark Fragment of THE First Cause continued to fill his existence, but it felt like only a portion was actually going to his foundation. The vast majority seemed to be suffusing into every nook and cranny of something else entirely.","His Infinities.","His Mind.","His Civilization.","Parts of his existence that weren’t measured by foundation weight alone.","His existence began to buzz as he focused on himself truly and fully, setting aside the distraction of his growing weight to observe the subtler changes occurring within. As he barreled across weavings of definition and undefinition, carried by currents that had no destination, something else began to make itself known.","HUUM!","He felt like he began to hear...a voice.","A grand voice that felt like his own voice but filled with an unfathomable weaving of majesty that transcended anything he had ever produced. It was him speaking to himself across time, or perhaps it was something older than him using his voice as a vessel for communication.","Echoes of differentiation’s birth flooded through his existence, and a voice that was not a voice spoke words that were not words into his consciousness.","THE First Cause.","He felt like he... was touching that moment through the Spark Fragment.","He was experiencing echoes of what had occurred when differentiation began.","And with it, he felt like he could glimpse musings of things he knew and things he didn’t know, of future possibilities that may or may not happen, of paths that branched infinitely from the crossroads of his current existence.","To the point that as he spun across existence, carried by weavings that had no name, he heard it.","A booming voice that felt like it was his and not his.","\" When the Youngest walks where the Oldest slumber, Existence shall tremble and the Weave shall fray. He who holds infinity in mortal palms shall stand at the crossroads where all rivers end.","The Paradox shall fall before the Paradox rises. The father consumed by the son, the son consumed by the purpose, the purpose consumed by the question that birthed all questions. Three collapses for the price of one, and in the third collapse, the door shall crack.","Beware the Unity that wears the face of peace. Beware the Legion that marches without banners. They shall come as whispers in the foundation, as cracks in the certainty, as the gentle erosion that unmakes mountains. Where they pass, definition dies. Where they gather, possibility ends.","The Shroud of Endless Blue shall fall upon Observable Existence. It shall be both salvation and damnation, both the key and the lock, both the bridge and the chasm. Under its weight, the doors of the Scales shall open or the doors of the Scales shall shatter. There is no third path. There is no middle ground. There is only the choice that is not a choice.","When Chaos speaks with the tongue of Order, when Existence questions its own being, when the Tongue falls silent and the Paradox emerges, then shall the Era of Undifferentiation begin. Absolutes shall be unleashed. The First shall become the Last. The Many shall become the One. The One shall become the None.","Yet in the None, a spark remains.","The adversity that breaks all others shall forge him. The hardship that ends all paths shall begin his. The Scales demand what the Scales demand, and he shall pay in currencies that have not yet been minted.He shall pay the price he deems.","Three times shall he face the mirror of undoing. Three times shall he choose between becoming and unbecoming. Three times shall the answer be the same, and three times shall the answer be different.","In the end, which is also the beginning, the Infinite shall stand before the Undefined. And one side shall remain to tell the tale that no one shall hear.","This is an Echo of First Cause.","This is what shall come to pass, for it has already passed, and it shall pass again.","The wheel turns. The river flows. The question echoes.","He shall be the answer, or he shall be nothing.","Or he shall be the question that ends all answers.\"","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s existence was dazed as he heard what was deemed an Echo of THE First Cause repeating itself in his mind, the words burning into his consciousness with weight that made his foundations tremble despite their newly elevated state.","There were some heavy words in the Echoes Noah had heard!","Even the first line was heavy as Noah thought about it, the words burning in his consciousness with weight that refused to fade even as the euphoria of consumption continued to flood through his existence.","\" When the Youngest walks where the Oldest slumber, Existence shall tremble and the Weave shall fray. He who holds infinity in mortal palms shall stand at the crossroads where all rivers end.\"","This should be fully referring to him as THE Youngest. And the Oldest slumber, was that... referring to THE Prima Indifferentia itself where THE Undivided Ones existed in states of perpetual non-differentiation? Or was it referring to the spaces he was currently barreling across, these weavings between definition and undefinition that seemed to exist outside of normal reality? Or...Chaos, since Chaos was supposedly the oldest?","\"...\"","And the crossroads where all rivers end...","His eyes shone brightly as he thought about what all of this could mean, what future events the prophecy was pointing toward, what choices awaited him at destinations he couldn’t yet perceive.","But the next set of words were even heavier.","\"The Paradox shall fall before the Paradox rises. The father consumed by the son, the son consumed by the purpose, the purpose consumed by the question that birthed all questions. Three collapses for the price of one, and in the third collapse, the door shall crack.\"","Now this one painted future possibilities of what would happen very soon in ways that made his foundations pulse with the weight of foreknowledge.","The first part should relate to THE Primordial Paradox and THE Living Paradox, with the ancient master being consumed by his disciple. The father consumed by the son was clear enough.","But the son consumed by the purpose?","And the purpose consumed by the question that birthed all questions...","\"...\"","Three collapses for the price of one.","In the third collapse, the door shall crack.","Noah thought about all the possibilities as the prophecy continued to echo in the depths of his consciousness, each line carrying weight that demanded analysis and interpretation. There was so much to unpack, so much to understand, and he was currently tumbling through spaces that had no reference points for time or distance!"]},{"number":4880,"title":"Chapter 4880: Chapter 4879: THE Civilizational Instinctus! I","paragraphs":["\" Decipher as much as you can, and let me know your theories on what it could all mean later.\"","He gave this command to RUINATION as he continued to funnel across existence, trusting her to work through the prophecy’s meanings while he focused on more immediate concerns.","|Understood, Master|","|I will compile comprehensive analysis of the Echo of First Cause and present theories when you have time to review them|","Her affirmation came as Noah continued to focus on himself.","The echoes he heard were grand, but they were still not the main thing that he was getting from devouring that Spark Fragment. The prophecy was important, yes, but it was information about the future rather than power in the present.","As the Spark Fragment continued to permeate Immensity across his existence, he felt like he could see.","Not in the same manner as Lens of Civilization.","Not even as THE Weaver of Existence.","He felt like all of these were being taken to another level entirely.","Not simply being able to see, but he could feel so much that it was truly hard to explain. His entire existence was overwhelmed with sensory sensations as information seemed to be coming in from all around, data flooding into his consciousness from angles that shouldn’t have existed and perspectives that transcended everything.","BOOM!","Around his body, blue-gold billowing flames rose and shone brilliantly as the overflow of information formed into prompts that crystallized the chaos into understanding he could actually process.","| The echoes of THE First Cause have finished permeating across your existence|","|The moment when differentiation began has left its imprint upon your foundations, granting you perspective that only those who have touched the origin of all things can possess|","| You now see existence not as it appears, but as it truly is|","...!","Noah felt the truth of these words resonating through every aspect of his being, the fundamental shift in perception that the Spark Fragment had catalyzed now reaching its completion.","|New Existential Capability Unlocked|","| Designation: THE Civilizational Instinctus|","|Also known as: THE Gnosis Ruinae, or THE Praescientia Civitatis|","| This capability is only attained by those whose foundations have grown heavy enough to approach the threshold of THE Second Scale of Existence. It represents a fundamental shift in how you perceive and interact with the Civilizations of others, granting you instinctive understanding of structural foundations.|","BOOM!","So this was what the Spark Fragment’s true boon was!","Okay.","Okay!","Not just foundation elevation, though that alone would have been worth the risks he had taken, but a fundamental transformation in how he perceived reality itself!","| Primary Function: Autonomous Existential Response|","|Your existence now reacts to threats and opportunities before your conscious mind processes them. Your Civilization moves with purpose that transcends thought, your Seals manifesting and your Infinities flaring in response to dangers you have not yet perceived with your awareness. This is not prediction or foresight but rather your existence acting on knowledge that bypasses the delay of conscious processing.|","|You do not think and then move. You simply respond, and the thinking catches up afterward.|","|Against opponents of equivalent or lesser Depth, your existence will automatically position itself in optimal configurations for both offense and defense. Against opponents of greater Depth, this autonomous response will buy you precious moments that conscious reaction could never provide.|","Noah’s eyes shone with understanding as he processed this first function.","His body would move before his mind commanded it to move!","| Secondary Function: Manifestation Observation|","|When you focus your attention upon any entity possessing a Civilization, you now perceive something that was previously invisible. Behind their physical form, surrounding their existence like a second body made of pure authority, you observe the Manifestation of their Civilization in its entirety.|","|This Manifestation appears as an architectural construct unique to each entity. For some, it may appear as a towering citadel with walls representing their defenses and towers representing their offensive capabilities. For others, it may appear as a vast network of roots and branches, or as a constellation of orbiting structures, or as something that defies conventional description entirely.|","|The form of the Manifestation reflects the nature of the Civilization it represents. A Civilization built on conquest will appear martial and aggressive. A Civilization built on knowledge will appear scholarly and layered. A Civilization built on paradox will appear contradictory and shifting.|","This was even grander than the first function!","| Tertiary Function: Structural Analysis|","|Within each observed Manifestation, you perceive points of vulnerability that the entity themselves may not even be aware of. These appear as cracks in walls, as rotting foundations, as pillars that bear too much weight, as connections that are fraying under strain. Every Civilization, no matter how grand, possesses weaknesses born from the choices made during its construction.|","|The clearer you perceive an entity, the more vulnerabilities you identify. Proximity, duration of observation, and relative Depth all influence the clarity of your analysis.|","So not only could he see Civilizations, but he could see their weaknesses!","| Quaternary Function: Targeted Undifferentiation|","|Having identified vulnerabilities within a Manifestation, you may now direct your attacks specifically toward those weak points. Your Authority of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate, when launched at identified vulnerabilities, carries additional effectiveness. A strike against a weakness does not simply damage. It undifferentiates.|","|The targeted aspect of their Civilization begins to blur, to lose definition, to revert toward the proto-state that existed before differentiation. A pillar struck at its stress point doesn’t merely crack but begins to forget that it was ever a pillar. A wall attacked at its weakest section doesn’t merely crumble but starts questioning whether it was ever meant to be a wall.|","|Repeated strikes against the same vulnerability compound this effect. What begins as minor instability grows into structural failure. What starts as a hairline crack expands into a chasm that threatens the entire Manifestation.|","Noah felt his existence trembling with the implications of this function.","THE Prima Indifferentia had taught him well, and now he could bring those lessons to bear against anyone who stood in his way!"]},{"number":4881,"title":"Chapter 4881: Chapter 4880: THE Civilizational Instinctus! II","paragraphs":["|In battle, THE Civilizational Instinctus transforms combat from an exchange of power into an architectural demolition for you. You no longer fight your opponent directly but rather fight the structure of their existence, seeking to topple their Civilization piece by piece until the whole collapses under its own compromised weight.|","|This methodology is particularly effective against opponents of greater Depth than yourself. Where direct confrontation would favor their superior weight, structural targeting allows you to circumvent that advantage entirely. You do not need to overpower their walls when you can simply remove the foundations those walls rest upon.|","|Against Absolutes, this capability represents your primary path to victory. Their Depth exceeds yours, but their Civilizations possess vulnerabilities accumulated across eons of existence. The older and grander a Civilization, the more points of failure may have developed within its structure if its foundations are weak.|","A path to victory against Absolutes!","Not through matching their power directly, but through exploiting weaknesses that their power couldn’t protect them from!","|Passive Benefit: Existential Proprioception|","|You now possess perfect awareness of your own Civilization’s Manifestation and its structural integrity. You perceive your own weaknesses as clearly as you perceive others’, allowing you to shore up vulnerabilities before enemies can exploit them. Your existence instinctively reinforces stressed points and redistributes weight to prevent collapse.|","|This self-awareness also grants immunity to being analyzed by others possessing similar capabilities. Your Infinities create a shroud of endless variation around your Manifestation, making it impossible for observers to perceive any single configuration long enough to identify weaknesses. What they see changes faster than they can process.|","So he could see himself as clearly as he could see others, but others couldn’t see him in return.","His Infinities protected him from the very capability he now possessed, creating a one-way mirror where he could observe without being observed.","|Scaling Parameters|","|THE Civilizational Instinctus grows more potent as your foundations increase. At current weight of 11x Surface, 10.5x Intermediate, and equivalent Fundamental to THE Primordial Paradox, you can clearly observe Manifestations of beings up to weak and average Absolute classification. Stronger Absolutes appear blurred, their Manifestations only partially visible.|","|As your weight increases, so too does the clarity of your observation. At weight equivalent to standard Absolutes, you would perceive their Manifestations with perfect clarity. At weight exceeding Absolutes, you would begin perceiving hints of Manifestations belonging to entities approaching THE Second Scale.|","|There is no theoretical ceiling to this capability. As your Infinite Formless Depth grows without limit, so too does THE Civilizational Instinctus’ reach.|","|Activation Requirements|","|THE Civilizational Instinctus requires no conscious activation for its autonomous response function. Your existence will react instinctively to threats regardless of your attention or awareness.|","|For Manifestation observation and structural analysis, focused attention is required. You must intentionally observe an entity with the purpose of perceiving their Civilization’s architecture. Casual glances reveal nothing. Dedicated focus reveals everything.|","|For targeted undifferentiation, you must have first identified a specific vulnerability and then direct your attacks with that weakness as the intended target. Unfocused attacks carry no structural targeting benefits. If you cannot even get near your enemy, even if you see their weakness, you will be unable to do anything.|","That last line was important.","Seeing weaknesses meant nothing if he couldn’t reach them. THE Civilizational Instinctus wasn’t omnipotence. It was a tool, and like all tools, it had limitations that he would need to account for in actual combat.","|Historical Context|","|THE Civilizational Instinctus has only been achieved by beings approaching THE Second Scale of Existence, and you are ridiculously far from that.|","|You are the first being in Observable Existence below Absolute to achieve any form of THE Civilizational Instinctus.|","...!","The first below Absolute!","Another unprecedented achievement to add to a growing list of unprecedented achievements!","|Final Assessment|","|The Spark Fragment of THE First Cause has granted you three boons. First, the elevation of your foundations. Second, the Echo of First Cause prophecy that illuminates potential futures. Third, THE Civilizational Instinctus that transforms how you perceive and observe the Civilizations.|","...!","The possibilities were far too grand as Noah processed everything he had just learned.","And yes, he felt like he could truly see now.","When he looked at himself with his newly enhanced perception, he saw the phantom of his own Civilizational Manifestation unfurling before his awareness.","A massive Grimoire floated at the center of everything, its pages infinite and its cover burning with blue-gold light that painted the surrounding space in colors that spoke of boundless potential. Surrounding this Grimoire were Seals that formed a structure resembling a massive infinity symbol, the lemniscate shape wrapping around the book in endless loops.","Three massive pillars of foundation rose up endlessly from below, representing his Surface, Intermediate, and Fundamental Depths. They connected down to a radiant shore where vibrant blue-gold fields stretched toward horizons that couldn’t be perceived and trees shimmered with stellar brilliance that spoke of Civilizations planted and nurtured.","And at the very center of it all, a massive crimson blue-gold bonfire shone with the light of his Infinite Hunger combined with his core Infinite Undifferentiated Fate. Its embers flowed upward in an endless stream, inscribing themselves on the infinite pages of the Grimoire above before cycling back down to fuel the fire once more.","An endless cycle of growth and inscription and growth again.","|Self-Analysis Complete|","|Your Manifestation displays no observable weaknesses at this time|","|The integration of Infinity across all aspects of your Civilization has created a structure that shifts faster than vulnerabilities can form|","|Any stress point that begins to develop is immediately reinforced by your Infinities before it can become exploitable|","|This does not mean you are invincible|","|It means that THE Civilizational Instinctus cannot identify targets for structural attack against your current configuration|","|Enemies will need to rely on overwhelming force rather than precision targeting to harm you|","Noah looked at all of this as he felt a sense of calmness and Immensity settling over his existence.","He had become something truly unprecedented during this Temporal Traversal!","But first, he needed to get back.","As his body continued to tumble across existence, carried by weavings that had no destination, he sought to find an anchor between definition and undefinition that would allow him to return to reality. He needed something that existed in both states simultaneously, something that could serve as a bridge between where he was and where he needed to be.","When he thought of THE Infiniverse, existence fizzled around him as the coordinates failed to lock.","When he thought of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, the same fizzling occurred.","When he thought of Alfheimr or Ginnungagap or any other locations in his time, nothing took hold.","None of them were both defined and undefined in their stability.","None of them could serve as anchors for whatever strange space he was currently traversing.","He just needed entry to something that existed in both states, something that would anchor him to The Interstices, and from The Interstices he could navigate back to wherever he needed to go.","Something defined and undefined...","His eyes and existence that could now see many things shone with sudden realization as a candidate emerged in his mind. Something he had encountered before. Something that had nearly ended his journey through The Interstices the first time he had traveled them.","\"O Hollow Echo, are you not defined and undefined? You are not THE Creature, and yet you are...\"","HUUM!","Around him, existence flickered with recognition.","And this time, things did not fizzle.","The coordinates locked onto something that existed as both an echo and a presence, both a memory and a reality, both defined by what it had been and undefined by what it currently was.","He felt Temporal Traversal activating, his body instantly squeezing across existence as the weavings of definition and undefinition found their anchor point and began funneling him toward it with purpose that had been lacking moments before.","WAP!","Noah arrived back in The Interstices.","He found himself inside a Capillary Thread, one of the countless pathways that connected moments across time. Things would normally be dark and mystical here, the undefined space between spaces holding only shadows and potential.","But he could see now.","THE Civilizational Instinctus illuminated everything with clarity, showing him the structure of The Interstices themselves, the weavings of temporal authority that connected many things, the fabric of reality that made his journey possible.","And far ahead of him, the target he had been able to lock onto to bring himself back...","THE Hollow Echo of THE Creature turned around to observe him.","Its form was massive, a distorted reflection of THE Creature himself, burning with multicolored flames that flickered between presence and absence.","It observed him coldly, recognizing the being who had fled from it before.","Noah looked at THE Hollow Echo with a cold and glorious light in his eyes, his existence burning with blue-gold Infinities that painted the Capillary Thread in colors.","This time, he did not run away.","He did not run away.","His Civilizational Instinctus activated as he focused on THE Hollow Echo with dedicated attention, and for the first time, he saw what lay behind the multicolored flames.","He saw the Manifestation of an echo.","He saw the cracks in a foundation that had been hollow from the moment of its creation.","He saw weaknesses that no one had ever perceived because no one had ever looked at this thing with eyes that could truly see.","And Noah looked at this thing seriously.","\"I believe...you and I have unfinished business.\"","...!"]},{"number":4882,"title":"Chapter 4882: Chapter 4881: All In I","paragraphs":["What Noah saw was something unique.","The Manifestation of the Civilization of THE Hollow Echo of THE Creature was unlike anything he could have anticipated, its architecture showing something that had once been grand but was now merely a reflection of grandeur, a shadow cast by a light that existed elsewhere.","Nine grand hollow mountains surrounded the Echo, their tips pointing inward toward the being they protected while their bases spread outward in a perfect circle that seemed to define the boundaries of this entity’s domain. Each mountain was massive beyond description, their surfaces carved from what looked like crystallized colorless flame that had been frozen in the moment of burning, and their interiors were visible through countless apertures that revealed emptiness where substance should have been.","Hollow.","Just like the Echo itself.","The nine mountains formed a circular hollow domain that spun slowly around THE Hollow Echo, their rotation creating currents of authority that pressed against Noah’s existence with weight!","The formation was defensive and offensive simultaneously, a fortress that could become a weapon, a shield that could become a blade.","It was a unique thing to see, and for Noah, it was novelty, and it was new.","And because it was new, he focused and remained serious.","Because he was not even an Absolute, and he was looking at a Hollow Echo of THE Creature himself and choosing to fight with it rather than flee from it as he had done before. The gap between them should have been insurmountable. The difference in their existences should have made this confrontation nothing more than elaborate suicide.","But should have meant nothing to someone like him!","He looked at THE Hollow Echo with eyes that now perceived reality as it truly was, his Civilizational Instinctus granting him true sight.","\" This time, there will be no running or retreat.\"","His voice was calm but held weight that made the Capillary Thread around them tremble.","\" Unlike previous times, I will stake the Everything of this body. Either it collapses you, or you collapse it.\"","He paused, his blue-gold existence burning brighter.","\" Do you understand me?\"","He asked this question genuinely, because it would be even grander if this Hollow Echo could actually comprehend what was being offered. It would make dismembering it all that much more satisfying if it understood the stakes!","And...","\"You. Have. Changed.\"","HUUM!","THE Hollow Echo shockingly spoke, its voice emerging from the colorless flames that comprised its form. The words were fragmented, broken apart by the hollow nature of the being speaking them, but they carried understanding that Noah hadn’t expected.","Around THE Hollow Echo, colorless flames flared and began to rage with intensity that painted the entire Capillary Thread in shades of absence. The nine hollow mountains that comprised its Manifestation actually began to spin faster, their rotation accelerating as the Echo prepared for combat.","And as the mountains spun, Noah paid attention with the dedicated focus that THE Civilizational Instinctus required.","He saw the weaknesses.","On the first mountain, a crack ran down from its hollow tip toward its base, a fissure that told of structural compromise where the mountain’s authority had been stretched too thin across too many defensive functions. The crack pulsed faintly with each rotation, growing slightly wider before contracting, a wound that had never properly healed.","On the third mountain, the apertures that revealed its hollow interior were clustered too densely on one face, creating a section of the surface that was more hole than substance. The integrity there was maintained through will rather than structure, and will could be exhausted.","On the fifth mountain, the base where it connected to the circular formation showed signs of erosion, the crystallized colorless flame appearing slightly dimmer than the rest of the structure. This was the oldest weakness, accumulated across however long THE Hollow Echo had existed in The Interstices.","On the seventh mountain, a crevice ran horizontally across its midsection where two different types of authority had been fused together imperfectly. The seam was nearly invisible, but to Noah’s enhanced perception it blazed like a beacon, announcing structural failure waiting to happen.","And on the ninth mountain, the tip itself showed microscopic fractures radiating outward from where it pointed toward THE Hollow Echo, stress damage from bearing too much of the hollow Civilization’s concentrated weight for too long.","Five clear weaknesses across nine mountains.","Five targets!","Five points where THE Civilizational Instinctus could be applied to transform this battle from an exchange of power into architectural demolition.","Noah saw every single one of these points as he prepared himself, his existence beginning to buzz with Immensity that had grown to levels rivaling weak Absolutes. He nodded with the calm of someone who had already calculated the path to victory.","\"I have definitely changed. You have not.\"","His blue-gold flames burned brighter.","\" Are you ready? Our Everythings are on the line.\"","...!","THE Hollow Echo’s colorless flames surged with intensity that made the nine mountains tremble, and when it spoke again, its fragmented voice carried the weight of something magisterial!","\" You. Cannot. Even. Comprehend. My. Everythings.\"","HUUM!","It was a reply, and shockingly it was also an Embodiment!","The words themselves carried the authority of THE Creature’s aspect, Existence given voice in a declaration that pressed against reality with weight that should have crushed anything below Absolute! The Embodiment crashed outward from THE Hollow Echo like a wave of pure presence, colorless and overwhelming and absolutely certain of its supremacy.","Noah felt the Embodiment coming as he stayed still.","His weight should be grand enough with his foundation to rival a weak Absolute. His established Apophasis were still active, still declaring what he was not. His Infinities still burned across every aspect of his existence, creating endless potential for response.","Every part of his existence was buzzing, but it wasn’t agitation or excitement that drove this resonance. It was determination. His existence was burning with determination as it wanted to test itself, to prove itself against something that would have been unthinkable to face just hours before!","And so it did.","And so he stayed still.","The weight of an Embodiment crashed into him.","The authority of \"You. Cannot. Even. Comprehend. My. Everythings.\" slammed against his foundations with force that should have scattered his existence across The Interstices like ashes in a hurricane. The pressure was immense, incomprehensible, the weight of Existence focused through an Echo that retained a sliver of the original’s power to devastate anything below Absolute!","Certain times in existence, one could stand so defiant that an enemy could see their defiance and look at them with respect rather than contempt.","At this time, THE Hollow Echo of THE Creature looked at Noah’s unflinching gaze as this being who should have been crushed, who should have been scattered, who should have been nothing before the weight of an Embodiment... actually stood firm.","THE Hollow Echo nodded with seriousness and respect.","And...","BOOM!","The Embodiment that smashed into Noah only caused his blue-gold robes to flutter in currents of displaced authority, the fabric rippling with the remnants of force that had been distributed across his entire existence rather than concentrated on any single point.","He had long since stopped being THE Tongue Whisperer at this time.","He was not hiding behind a disguise or concealing his true nature.","He was Noah Osmont, THE Genesis Monarch, and at this moment he was an Absolute Immovable Object who did not move beneath weight that should have moved him!","His existence remained exactly where it was, and oh, the sensations that flooded through him were beyond description!","|Combat Analysis - Embodiment Resistance Successful|","|Due to your foundation weight of 11x Surface, 10.5x Intermediate, and equivalent Fundamental to THE Primordial Paradox, you possess sufficient Immensity to bear the crushing weight of Embodiments from Hollow Echoes without structural collapse. Your weight creates natural resistance that disperses incoming authority across your entire existence.|","|Additionally, your established Apophasis remain active: You are not limited by the weight that crashes against you. Your existence is not incapable of bearing that which seeks to overwhelm it. You are not collapsible under the Immensity of what you have claimed. Most of these negations remove conceptual vulnerabilities that Embodiments would normally exploit.|","|Furthermore, Autonomous Existential Response activated without conscious command. Your Infinities detected the incoming Embodiment and automatically configured your Seals, your Foundation, and your Civilizational Authority. Your body knew how to bear this weight before your mind understood what was happening.|","|You stood against an Embodiment of THE Hollow Echo of THE Creature through sheer will alone!|","HUUM!"]},{"number":4883,"title":"Chapter 4883: Chapter 4882: All In II","paragraphs":["Noah felt the swirling Absolute Seals of Quintessence and Infinity and Fire and Darkness and Unity and many more all infinitely manifesting over his skin alongside his Immensity, creating a barrier of authority that reinforced his natural resistance.","Even though it was heavy, even though it was unfathomably heavy, even though lesser beings would have been erased from existence by such weight... he actually stood against an Embodiment!","And the action brought this battle to an extremely serious precipice.","THE Hollow Echo looked at him with colorless flames that burned brighter than before, recognition in its fragmented awareness.","It nodded once more as it raised its hands, the nine hollow mountains spinning faster around its form in preparation for what came next.","\" Existence. Is. Everything.\"","Its voice was stronger now, more cohesive, as if Noah’s defiance had reminded it of what it meant to truly fight.","\" And...My Everything Is Existence.\"","HUUM!","Another Embodiment bloomed outward from THE Hollow Echo, but this time it didn’t simply crash against Noah’s position. This time the Embodiment covered the Echo’s hands in crystalline colorless light, transforming its limbs into weapons of pure existential authority that shot out across the Capillary Thread!","The hands were declaring that everything they touched existed only at the Echo’s sufferance!","And Noah...","\" Actually.\"","WAP!","He disappeared from the position where THE Hollow Echo’s crystalline hands were converging, his existence flickering out of that space and materializing above the Echo in a movement so fast that even the spinning mountains couldn’t track it immediately.","He had been going to block.","He had been going to test his defenses against this second Embodiment.","But somewhere between deciding to stand firm and the hands reaching him, he had changed his mind.","His face showed determination and seriousness as Immensity radiated from every aspect of his being, blue-gold flames painting the Capillary Thread in colors that challenged the Echo’s colorless authority. He looked down at THE Hollow Echo from above with eyes that saw its Manifestation clearly, that perceived the crevice on the seventh mountain where two types of authority had been fused imperfectly.","He punched out!","The motion seemed to occur in slow motion, each fraction of movement stretching across heartbeats as the significance of what was happening demanded attention. His fist descended toward THE Hollow Echo, and as it moved, it became covered with tantalizing blue-gold light of Infinities that burned so brightly that even the colorless flames of the Echo seemed to dim by comparison.","But the fist wasn’t the attack.","The fist was the delivery mechanism.","While he punched out, an endless sea of Absolute Seals of his First Tongue rushed forward from his existence like an ocean given purpose and direction. They didn’t spread randomly across THE Hollow Echo’s defenses. They didn’t waste themselves against the strongest sections of the hollow mountains.","They bombarded the crevice on the seventh mountain with precision that only THE Civilizational Instinctus could provide!","Seals of Absolute Tongue crashed against the horizontal weakness where two authorities had been imperfectly fused, their Infinite Hunger quality devouring the structural integrity that held the seam together. The Authority of Undifferentiated Fate followed immediately after, their quality of inducing undifferentiation causing the fused authorities to begin forgetting that they had ever been connected!","It was an attack that carried the seriousness of THE First Tongue behind it, 27 base configurations each multiplying infinitely into floods of linguistic authority that poured into a single structural weakness with concentrated devastation.","It was blinding.","It was glorious!","And the seventh hollow mountain, which had stood as part of THE Hollow Echo’s Manifestation since its creation, began to crack.","The seventh mountain cracked!","The sound that emerged from that structural failure was a terrifying onw. The crevice where two imperfectly fused authorities had been joined now gaped open like a wound that refused to close, the edges of the breach blurring as his Authority of Undifferentiated Fate continued their work of making the mountain forget what it had been.","THE Hollow Echo’s colorless flames flickered.","Well, not much, but enough!","Noah saw the connection immediately through THE Civilizational Instinctus. The nine hollow mountains weren’t just defenses surrounding the Echo, they were akin to load-bearing structures that supported its very existence and Civilization.","Damage to the Manifestation was damage to the being. Weakness in the architecture was weakness in the foundation of the Civilization!","Good to know!","The Echo’s crystalline hands that had been reaching toward where Noah had been standing moments before now swung upward toward his current position, their Embodiment-covered surfaces burning with authority that declared everything they touched would exist only at the Echo’s sufferance.","But Noah was already moving.","His existence flickered across the Capillary Thread with speed of a weaker Absolutes, his blue-gold form leaving afterimages that the Echo’s hands passed through without contact. He materialized beside the first mountain, the one with the crack running from tip to base, and his Seals were already flooding outward before his conscious mind had finished processing his new position.","Autonomous Existential Response!","His body knew what to do before his thoughts caught up.","It was a strange sensation, watching himself act with precision he hadn’t consciously chosen. Like being a passenger in his own existence. He’d have to get used to that.","Infinite Seals of Darkness crashed against the crack in the first mountain, their authority heavy with the quality of endings and conclusions that pressed against the structural weakness with concentrated precision. The mountain’s surface, already compromised by the fissure that had never properly healed, began to splinter outward from the point of impact.","\" Existence Demands Tribute.\"","BOOM!","An Embodiment erupted from THE Hollow Echo with force that made the entire Capillary Thread tremble, the declaration pressing against reality itself with weight that demanded acknowledgment.","The authority of \"Existence Demands Tribute\" crashed against Noah’s existence with crushing pressure that sought to extract payment for his defiance.","He stood firm.","The pressure was immense.","His robes rippled. His flames dimmed momentarily. His existence actually compressed slightly under the weight of authority that would’ve scattered lesser beings across The Interstices.","But he didn’t fall!","And while he bore the Embodiment’s weight, his Seals continued their assault on the first mountain.","CRACK!","The fissure split open completely, running from the hollow tip all the way down to the base in a single devastating line. The first mountain didn’t crumble immediately, but its authority wavered, its rotation around THE Hollow Echo becoming unsteady as structural integrity failed across half its surface.","Noah flickered again.","He appeared at the fifth mountain, the one whose base showed signs of erosion where it connected to the circular formation. His existence was still bearing the weight of the Embodiment, still being pressed upon by authority that demanded tribute, but his attacks didn’t pause.","Couldn’t pause!","THE Hollow Echo was recovering from the shock and confusion of its power...failing and falling. Its colorless flames surged brighter as rage or determination or something that existed in the hollow space between emotions drove it toward retaliation. Noah had a window of opportunity, and that window was closing with every heartbeat.","Seals of Chaos flooded against the eroded base of the fifth mountain, their authority heavy with the quality of unpredictability that destabilized the already-weakened connection. The erosion that had accumulated across eons of existence became active decay in moments, the crystallized colorless flame beginning to dissolve where it met the circular formation.","\" You Will Pay For This.\"","HUUM!","THE Hollow Echo’s voice was more coherent now, fury binding its fragments together into something approaching unified speech. Its massive form turned toward Noah with attention that had physical weight, and its hands rose once more as crystalline authority gathered around them.","But this time, it wasn’t just the hands.","THE Hollow Echo’s feet also began to glow with Embodiment-covered surfaces, the same crystalline colorless light wrapping around its lower limbs as it prepared an assault from multiple vectors simultaneously.","Noah saw the attack coming through THE Civilizational Instinctus, his enhanced perception tracking the trajectories of limbs that would converge on his position from four different angles.","He was going to evade, but...","\" No.\"","He stayed.","His existence burned brighter as another Embodiment crashed against him, \"You Will Pay For This\" declaring that his actions had consequences that must be extracted. The weight was even greater than before, the Echo’s fury adding force to authority that pressed against his foundations with crushing intensity.","His flames dimmed further. His Seals worked overtime to redistribute the pressure. His Apophasis strained against conceptual attack that sought to make him collapsible.","But his hands didn’t stop moving.","While bearing the weight of two Embodiments simultaneously, Noah continued flooding Seals against the eroded base of the fifth mountain. His existence trembled. His foundations groaned. His infinite aspects stretched to accommodate pressure that should’ve been impossible to bear!","If anyone were watching this, they’d probably think he looked incredibly heroic. Standing firm against impossible odds. Defying authority that would crush lesser beings!","In reality, he was mostly trying to make sure he lived up to the distinction of Absolute Immovable Object.","The pressure was genuinely awful. Like being squeezed through a hole that was too small for his existence. But showing weakness now would be worse than the discomfort, so he kept his expression steady and his Seals flowing.","And the fifth mountain’s base gave way.","CRACK!","Before him, every fucking thing had to give way!"]},{"number":4884,"title":"Chapter 4884: Chapter 4883: All In III","paragraphs":["The connection to the circular formation severed completely, and the fifth mountain began to drift away from its assigned position, no longer contributing to the defensive formation, no longer spinning with its brethren in protection of THE Hollow Echo.","Two mountains compromised!","And THE Hollow Echo’s colorless flames had dimmed noticeably, its existence weakening in direct proportion to the damage inflicted on its Manifestation.","\" Enough .\"","The Echo’s voice was fully coherent now, unified by fury that transcended its hollow nature. Its hands and feet, all covered in Embodiment authority, launched toward Noah’s position with speed that exceeded anything it had displayed before.","But Noah was already flickering away.","The weight of the two Embodiments he’d been bearing was still pressing against his existence, but the Echo’s weakened state meant that pressure was no longer insurmountable!","He materialized at the third mountain, the one with apertures clustered too densely on one face. His Seals were already flooding out before his feet touched position, infinite authority crashing against the section that was more hole than substance.","THE Hollow Echo’s hands passed through where he’d been.","He flickered to the ninth mountain, the one with stress fractures radiating from its tip. His Seals bombarded the microscopic damage with concentrated force, turning hairline cracks into structural failures.","THE Hollow Echo’s feet swept through empty space.","He appeared at the first mountain again, targeting the now-gaping fissure with Seals filled with Undifferentiated Fate that made the crystallized colorless flame forget it had ever been solid.","The Echo’s limbs, massive and covered in Embodiment authority, crashed against positions he’d already vacated.","Again.","And again.","And again!","Noah became a blur of blue-gold light that flickered across the battlefield, never staying in one position long enough for THE Hollow Echo’s attacks to connect, always appearing at the next weakness in the Manifestation’s architecture. His speed was truly, undoubtedly that of an Absolute! His precision exceeded them!","From THE Hollow Echo’s perspective, this probably looked like masterful combat. A perfect display of superior tactics overwhelming raw power.","From Noah’s perspective, it was a lot of flickering and smashing into structures of a Civilization that even his enemy did not know existed for him to see and exploit!","Same result, very different internal experiences.","CRACK!","The third mountain’s aperture-dense face collapsed inward, the section that had been more hole than substance finally giving way entirely.","CRACK!","The ninth mountain’s tip shattered, the stress fractures that had been accumulating reaching critical failure under the assault of infinite Seals.","CRACK!","The first mountain split in half, the fissure running from tip to base finally completing its work of total structural compromise.","THE Hollow Echo’s movements were slowing.","Its colorless flames were guttering.","Its Embodiments, when it managed to launch them, had weight that Noah’s foundations could bear without strain.","And still he didn’t stop.","He appeared at mountains that hadn’t shown obvious weaknesses, and THE Civilizational Instinctus revealed them anyway. Stress points that had been too subtle to perceive initially now blazed with clarity as the overall structure weakened. Secondary vulnerabilities that had been supported by primary integrity now became primary vulnerabilities of their own.","CRACK!","The fourth mountain’s internal support structure collapsed.","CRACK!","The sixth mountain’s rotation failed entirely, the hollow peak drifting away from the formation.","CRACK!","The eighth mountain’s surface shattered like glass, revealing emptiness within emptiness.","Noah floated in the center of what had once been a domain of nine grand hollow mountains, surrounded now by the fragments and debris of structural annihilation. Broken peaks drifted through the Capillary Thread. Shattered bases tumbled end over end in slow motion. Crystallized colorless flame dissolved into proto-matter that the space between spaces eagerly absorbed.","And THE Hollow Echo stood before him, its body no longer surrounded by its Manifestation’s protection.","Because its Manifestation was ruined.","Noah looked at THE Hollow Echo with eyes that saw everything clearly, and what he saw made him understand the true nature of what he’d accomplished.","THE Hollow Echo’s body was filled with cracks.","Not surface damage, but fundamental structural and Civilizational failure that mirrored the destruction of its Manifestation. Lines of fractured existence ran across its colorless flames, dark seams where its authority had been torn throughout by the collapse of the mountains that had supported its Civilization.","Its hands, which had been so powerful moments before, now trembled with weakness that couldn’t be concealed. Its flames, which had burned with the Echo of THE Creature’s aspect, now flickered with the uncertainty of a candle in a storm.","Its Depth, or really its Civilization, had been dismantled from the foundation up.","THE Hollow Echo looked at Noah with heaviness.","\" You...were not like this.\"","\"No ,\" Noah agreed, his voice calm in a way that transcended the violence that had just occurred. \"I was not.\"","He floated before THE Hollow Echo with seriousness befitting the moment, his blue-gold existence burning with the light of victory that had been earned through methodology rather than raw power.","He hadn’t overpowered this Echo of THE Creature. He’d dismantled it, piece by piece, weakness by weakness, until the whole collapsed under its own compromised weight.","THE Civilizational Instinctus had proven itself.","And now came the harvest.","\" Your Everything is hollow,\" Noah said, and the words held no cruelty, only observation. \" It will never match up to THE Creature himself. You are an echo, and echoes fade.\"","He paused, and a small respect entered his expression.","\" But...you were grand. You were grand.\"","...!","THE Hollow Echo received these words in silence, its cracked existence flickering with light that grew dimmer by the moment. It didn’t argue. It didn’t protest. It simply existed in the space between acknowledgment and dissolution, waiting for what came next as it was barely holding itself together.","And Noah raised his hand.","Blue-gold flames erupted from his palm as infinite Seals of Fire began to manifest in patterns that had never been attempted before. They didn’t scatter outward as attacks. They didn’t flood toward THE Hollow Echo as bombardment. Instead, they layered upon each other, compressing and concentrating into a shape that grew more defined with every passing moment.","A blade.","A massive flaming blue-gold sword forged from infinite Seals of Fire, each Seal contributing its authority to an edge that burned with heat transcending temperature. The weapon stretched for meters, its surface writhing with flames that held the linguistic weight of THE First Tongue alongside the destructive aspect of Fire itself.","Noah grasped it with both hands.","The sword felt right in his grip as this...was a tool meant for one thing.","Preparation.","He looked at THE Hollow Echo with eyes that held no malice, only determination and the practical hunger of someone who understood that opportunity must be seized fully when it presented itself.","After all, a meal was better prepared while cut.","WAA!","He brought the sword down.","The blade carved through THE Hollow Echo’s cracked existence with resistance of authority being severed rather than mere flesh being parted. The Echo’s colorless flames split around the wound, unable to reform, unable to heal. What Noah cut stayed cut because his Seals of Fire held finality that echoed the endings his Seals of Darkness had inflicted on the mountains.","He cut again.","And again.","And again.","The sword rose and fell with methodical precision, each stroke separating another portion of THE Hollow Echo from the whole.","THE Hollow Echo didn’t scream.","It had no mouth for screaming, and perhaps it had no capacity for pain in the conventional sense. But it watched as Noah worked, its fragmenting awareness perceiving its own dissolution with something that might’ve been acceptance.","This was how existence ended.","Not with defiance, but with acknowledgment that something stronger had come.","Noah continued to carve until the work was complete, until THE Hollow Echo that had once threatened to collapse him during his traversal of The Interstices was nothing but carefully separated portions floating in the space between spaces.","Then he stopped.","His sword of infinite Fire Seals dispersed, the flames returning to his existence as the weapon’s purpose had been fulfilled. He looked at what he’d prepared with satisfaction.","A pillar of silent light representing the fall of an Absolute...stretched out across The Interstices as...","’That can’t be good...’","Noah’s eyes squinted as there were monstrous beings in this place. Announcing deaths here was not something ideal.","He reached out toward the first portion, his Infinite Hunger already awakening with appetite that had grown alongside everything else about his existence!"]},{"number":4885,"title":"Chapter 4885: Chapter 4884: Native!","paragraphs":["\" The Everythings of what was collapsed are mine and not mine. They belong to me and they do not belong to me. They must be given to me instantly and they must never be given to me at all.\"","BOOM!","Noah uttered THE Rite of Paradoxical Inheritance while consuming pieces of THE Hollow Echo, the paradoxical words flowing from his existence with practiced ease as the carved portions of colorless flame began to dissolve into streams of pure authority.","In the next moment, the Immensity and Depths of THE Hollow Echo surged into him like rivers finding the ocean.","The weight was heavy. Even diminished by the destruction of its Manifestation, even weakened by the systematic targeting of its structural vulnerabilities, THE Hollow Echo had still been an echo of THE Creature himself. Its foundations held density that lesser Absolutes could only dream of, and all of that density was now flooding into Noah’s infinite existence with a force that made his blue-gold flames roar brighter!","And where its cut pieces had floated moments before, something else began to form.","Colorless light coalesced into shape and substance, the remnants of THE Hollow Echo’s existence crystallizing into an artifact that pulsed with authority.","Noah looked at all of this calmly.","For this action of momentous achievement, decimating an Absolute without any tricks or external help, without THE Primordial Paradox’s intervention, without relying on anything but his own transformed existence, he breathed in deeply to celebrate the sheer magnitude of what he’d accomplished.","Then... he got over himself.","He didn’t need to be overly prideful or happy. That kind of ego was how beings stagnated, how they convinced themselves they’d reached heights that didn’t require further climbing.","\" Just a Hollow Echo of THE Creature. An Echo of an Absolute.\"","His voice was deliberately dismissive even as the power continued flooding into his foundations.","There was much more to be done, and he wouldn’t let his ego go wild just on this. THE Hollow Echo had been a test of his new capabilities, a confirmation that THE Civilizational Instinctus worked. But it wasn’t the ceiling of what he needed to achieve. It wasn’t even close!","|Absolute Collapse Confirmed|","|You have collapsed THE Hollow Echo of THE Creature through systematic deconstruction of its Civilizational Manifestation rather than overwhelming force. This methodology has been recorded as viable against entities of superior Depth. You have forgone the formation of an Absolute Existential Palace in favor of drawing in as much raw Depth as possible|","...!","|Foundation Status - Updated Assessment|","|THE Surface Depth: Your Immensity now registers at 1,250% comparative weight to THE Primordial Paradox at equivalent stage. This represents 12.5 times the foundation weight that one of THE Four possessed at Surface Depth before becoming an Absolute. No recorded entity has achieved such density at this level while remaining below Absolute classification.|","|THE Intermediate Depth: Your Immensity now registers at 1,200% comparative weight. This represents 12 times the foundation weight of THE Primordial Paradox at equivalent stage. The diminishing returns of higher Depths are evident, as each subsequent level requires exponentially more resources to elevate by equivalent amounts.|","|THE Fundamental Depth: Your Immensity now exceeds what THE Primordial Paradox and THE Creature possessed before their ascension to Absolute. You have surpassed the pre-Absolute foundations of THE Four themselves. When you eventually grasp Absolute Depth, your starting point will be higher than any Absolute in recorded history.|","...!","The numbers were glorious, but Noah processed them with the same deliberate calm he’d forced himself to maintain. Getting excited about numbers alone was pointless.","He’d tested it against THE Hollow Echo.","He needed to test it against things that weren’t hollow!","But even as he maintained his composure, the prompts continued to bloom with information that demanded attention.","|Existential Advancement Detected|","|Various facets of your existence are rising in response to the harvest and the achievements of your temporal traversal. Your Derivative Civilizations strengthen. Your Infinite Hunger deepens. Your connection to Undifferentiated Fate solidifies. All aspects of your being grow heavier with each passing moment.|","|However, one singular facet has been tipped over the edge by this incoming harvest.|","|Your mastery of THE First Tongue has exceeded established classifications.|","...!","|Previous Designation: Perfect Speaker of THE First Tongue|","|You have exceeded this designation.|","|You now stand at a ranking exclusive to you and not what others receive if they manage to surpass Perfect. The path you have walked through THE Prima Indifferentia, through consumption of the Spark Fragment of THE First Cause, through integration of infinite aspects across all elements of your Civilization, has created a relationship with THE First Tongue that transcends mastery.|","| You have attained the distinction of a Native Speaker of THE First Tongue.|","BOOM!","Native Speaker.","As if this was something he’d been born into.","As if THE First Tongue was his native language, the words he’d first learned to speak, the linguistic foundation upon which all other communication was merely translation.","As if this was his.","Around Noah in The Interstices, 27 Phonemes of THE First Tongue began to bloom into visibility without his conscious summoning. They emerged from his existence like flowers opening to greet the sun, each one burning with authority that had grown alongside everything else about him.","They danced.","There was no other word for it. The Phonemes swirled around his blue-gold form in patterns that held joy rather than combat purpose, celebrating an achievement that even they seemed to recognize as significant.","And then they moved.","The 27 Phonemes rose above his head in unison, arranging themselves into a formation that crystallized into something permanent. They interlocked and fused and became a crown of pure linguistic authority that settled above Noah’s brow without quite touching it, hovering with the weight of THE First Tongue’s acknowledgment.","His entire figure radiated a glow of ethereal blue-gold that painted The Interstices in colors that spoke of infinite potential and linguistic supremacy combined!","He looked fucking fantastic.","If THE Primordial Paradox could see him now, the ancient Absolute would probably have some cutting remark about pride and falls and the dangers of admiring one’s own reflection!","He refocused on the prompts that continued to flow.","|Native Speaker of THE First Tongue - Exclusive Capabilities|","|As a Native Speaker, you have obtained access to a feature of THE First Tongue that nobody else can utilize. This feature is known as Existence Writing, and it represents the difference between speaking a language fluently and thinking in that language natively.|","...!","|Existence Writing - Primary Function|","|You may now compose entire sentences of THE First Tongue in written form, inscribing them upon existence itself rather than merely speaking them into being. These written sentences are designated as Inscriptiones , Inscriptions that hold authority beyond verbal and written declaration.|","| An Inscriptio can be infused with the power of an Embodiment or an Apophasis, elevating the written sentence. Embodiment Inscriptiones declare what IS with authority that presses against reality. Apophasis Inscriptiones declare what IS NOT with authority that removes possibilities from existence.|","|Apophasis Inscriptiones require greater expenditure of Civilizational Authority due to the fundamental difficulty of writing negation into permanence. Removing something from existence through inscription demands more than adding something to it.|","...!","|Existence Writing - Delivery Methods|","|An Inscriptio may be delivered through three distinct methodologies:|","| Inscriptio Praesentia (Inscription of Presence): The written sentence is directed at a target within your immediate vicinity. The Inscriptio strikes with elevated effect that exceeds a normal Embodiment or Apophasis by a factor determined by the complexity and precision of the sentence composed. A well-crafted Inscriptio Praesentia can devastate targets that would resist verbal declarations of equivalent authority.|","| Inscriptio Nominata (Named Inscription): The written sentence includes the distinction or true name of the target within its composition. Upon completion, the Inscriptio does not strike locally but instead traverses across the flow of THE First Tongue throughout Observable Existence, seeking its named target regardless of distance or barriers. The sentence will find them. The sentence will deliver its payload. No location is safe from a properly constructed Inscriptio Nominata.|","| Inscriptio Dormiens (Sleeping Inscription): The written sentence is composed and completed but held in a state of suspension rather than immediate release. The Inscriptio remains dormant within your existence or can be placed upon objects, locations, or even other beings, awaiting the moment you choose to awaken it. When activated by your will, the Inscriptio exerts its effects as if freshly completed, regardless of how much time has passed since its composition. You may maintain multiple Inscriptiones Dormientes simultaneously, limited only by your capacity to remember their existence and locations.|","...!","Noah’s eyes widened.","Oh.","Fuck."]},{"number":4886,"title":"Chapter 4886: Chapter 4885: Determination! I","paragraphs":["Noah floated intently as he received more and more information.","|Existence Writing - Composition Requirements|","|Constructing an Inscriptio requires focused concentration proportional to the complexity of the sentence. Simple declarations can be written in moments. Complex sentences with multiple clauses and nested authorities may require extended composition time. The more precise the wording, the more devastating the effect, but also the longer the inscription takes to complete.|","| Inscriptiones Dormientes are a work of wonder. Write your sentences when you are safe. Unleash them when you are not.|","...!","|Existence Writing - Scaling Parameters|","|The power of your Inscriptiones scales with your mastery of THE First Tongue, which as a Native Speaker has no theoretical ceiling. As your foundations grow and your connection to linguistic authority deepens, the maximum complexity and devastation of your written sentences will increase proportionally.|","...!","|Historical Context|","|No other Native Speaker of THE First Tongue currently exists in Observable Existence.|","...!","Noah gazed at this wondrous capability and the information flowing into his mind, the crown of Phonemes above his head pulsing with light that seemed to approve of his contemplation.","Existence Writing.","Inscriptiones that could strike targets before him with power exceeding normal Embodiments.","Inscriptiones that could hunt named targets across all of Observable Existence.","Inscriptiones that could sleep until he chose to wake them.","There was a lot!","---","In Observable Existence, there were many important moments across history.","The day THE Creature was born was an auspicious one, with those truly knowledgeable still going back and forth between his origin being in Alfheimr or THE Prima Indifferentia. Some had debated this question for eons without resolution, and they would likely debate it for eons more.","The first conversation to occur between a peasant and THE Primordial Paradox was also an important one, as from that conversation, many weavings of existence and reality as one knew it bloomed. The peasant had asked a simple question about the nature of contradiction, and THE Primordial Paradox had answered.","One could argue which events throughout history were the most important, with others among the Glossarians even mentioning the day THE Tongue Whisperer walked into THE Agora of Primordial Judgment and was inferred the title of a Polemarch being something truly worthy of note. His entrance allowed word to spread far and wide, increasing the influx of those entering THE Agora of Primordial Judgment as this would change just how many strong entities rose within it.","Many such arguments could be made.","But unbeknownst to many, at this moment in time, another critical event was taking place that was arguably one of the most important events in recent history.","And there was no one to observe it.","It was the entrance of THE Genesis Monarch into a distinction nobody else had in Observable Existence. Unique to him. The Native Speaker of THE First Tongue.","The moment he achieved this designation, Noah stayed still for a few seconds as he continued integrating the Depth of THE Hollow Echo. His expression was contemplative, his blue-gold existence burning with the weight of infinite potential, his crown of Phonemes hovering above his head with authority.","One could wonder just what grand thoughts were going on in his mind at this moment. What profound contemplations occupied the first Native Speaker of THE First Tongue in eons? What world-shaking decisions was he weighing as he stood at this unprecedented threshold?","After a while, Noah moved.","In the weavings of The Interstices, he waved his hands with deliberate purpose. Blue-gold Absolute Seals erupted from his existence in streams that wove together with architectural precision, forming shapes that solidified into something permanent.","A throne.","And a desk.","In the area where an Absolute had just fallen, where the fragments of THE Hollow Echo’s Manifestation still drifted through the space between spaces, Noah conjured furniture fit for a monarch conducting important affairs. The throne was grand without being ostentatious, formed from Seals of Infinity that burned with quiet authority. The desk before it was regal and practical, a surface upon which momentous work could be accomplished.","He sat down as if he was ready to begin the most important work of his existence.","From his body, golden pages unfolded and lined themselves up on the table before him with the precision of soldiers forming ranks. They lay flat against the surface, waiting to receive whatever wisdom or declaration their master chose to inscribe upon them. In his hands, a pen appeared, formed from concentrated linguistic authority that burned blue-gold at its tip.","And with an extremely serious expression that befitted the gravity of what he was about to do, Noah began to write his first Inscription!","An Inscriptio Nominata.","A Named Inscription.","At the tip of his pen, 27 Phonemes swirled like an endless galaxy, each one contributing its authority to the words that began to form upon the golden page. The Phonemes danced and wove and compressed themselves into written form, transitioning from verbal possibility to permanent declaration with each stroke of Noah’s hand.","The Inscription itself was simple in nature, something that would carry devastating effect upon its target.","But as he wrote, his Immensity began to glow into the words. His foundation weight pressed into each Phoneme. The authority of the Derivative Civilization of Infinite Hunger bled into the ink, adding the quality of endless consumption to what he was creating. The Derivative Civilization of Undifferentiated Fate followed, its connection to destiny ensuring that the Inscription would find its target regardless of circumstance, and it would undifferentiate.","And then, surpassing even what these authorities could provide, the light of an Apophasis began to cover what Noah was writing.","Not an Embodiment declaring what was.","An Apophasis declaring what was not.","He wrote with determination and focus that made the surrounding Interstices tremble, the words taking shape upon the golden page with weight that pressed against reality itself.","\" The foundation of the one named herein is not capable of standing firm. Their Depths are not free from the sensation of burning across every fiber of their existence. Their weight is not permitted to remain stable, but must instead tear itself apart piece by piece until nothing remains but the agony of dissolution. This truth applies so long as the foundation of the target does not exceed the foundation of the one who writes these words.\"","...!","Terrifying words began to be written as one had to wonder...who would make THE Genesis Monarch focus so intently to write such words!?"]},{"number":4887,"title":"Chapter 4887: Chapter 4886: Determination! II","paragraphs":["His first Inscription didn’t even carry an Embodiment. He went a level above and went all out to write an Apophasis from the very beginning!","Because of this, the process was hard.","Boundless seas of Infinities poured into the Inscription as Noah’s existence strained to maintain the coherence of what he was creating. An Apophasis Inscriptio demanded more than an Embodiment Inscriptio, and he was attempting one as his very first composition. The words wavered on the page, threatening to dissolve back into formless potential.","He pushed harder.","The Inscription nearly failed as the weight of negation pressed against his concentration, seeking to collapse the sentence before it could be completed. Writing what was not into permanence was fundamentally more difficult than writing what was, and Noah felt that difficulty as pressure against his mind and his foundations simultaneously.","But he pulled through.","His Infinite nature provided reserves. Where others would have been drained entirely by such an ambitious first attempt, Noah simply drew deeper from wells that had no bottom. His Infinities stabilized the wavering words. His determination held the sentence together through sheer refusal to accept failure.","And then it was done.","A blue-gold Inscription shining with immense weight and power was written on a golden page, the words burning with authority that made the surrounding Interstices darken slightly in response to their presence. Noah’s existence pulsed with the satisfaction of completion, the crown of Phonemes above his head flaring brighter as if acknowledging what he had accomplished.","|First Inscriptio Completed|","|You have successfully composed your first written Inscriptio of THE First Tongue. More significantly, you have composed an Apophasis Inscriptio as your inaugural work, a feat of considerable difficulty.|","|The Inscriptio you have created carries the following effects upon its designated target: constant burning sensation across all Depths of their existence, progressive destabilization of their foundation weight, and gradual dissolution of their structural integrity over time. These effects will persist indefinitely until the target’s foundation is fully compromised or until the Inscriptio is somehow countered by authority exceeding your own.|","|Applicable targets: Any entity whose foundation Depth does not exceed your own at the moment of Inscriptio activation.|","|Your proficiency in writing Inscriptiones has increased slightly. Future compositions will require marginally less concentration and will carry marginally greater stability during the writing process.|","| All that remains is a designated target.|","...!","The designated target.","Now, what could make a man sit down and write with such concentration?","What profound purpose drove the first Native Speaker to compose an Apophasis of such devastating effect as his very first Inscription?","It actually wasn’t any grand reason.","It was hatred .","Pure, undiluted hatred toward Noah’s self-proclaimed greatest enemy in existence. Not THE Entity, whose infection threatened all of Observable Existence. Not THE Living Paradox, who had stolen THE Primordial Paradox’s Claim. Not Bazuman, who had chased him across THE Prima Indifferentia with relentless hunger.","No.","All of his hatred was directed toward THE Living Elemental.","If THE Living Elemental was like any other enemy, Noah might have just chosen to forget about him or crush him when he vastly exceeded them in power. He cultivated and made progress in days what others did in eons. Eventually, THE Living Elemental would be nothing but an ant beneath his foot, and the grudge would be settled through simple overwhelming force.","But Noah had to prepare especially for THE Living Elemental.","Because this fucker had thrown him a burning curse that could attach itself to anyone near him, forcing him to be away from his women for a not insignificant amount of time.","Worst of all, he was in the middle of Dual Cultivation when this curse was set.","He had been forced to stop midway and remain in that state for that long extended period of time.","This was the reason for his deep distaste and hatred toward THE Living Elemental.","How dare he.","How fucking dare he?!","To get between a man and his...","’Hmm...’","Just thinking about it now made Noah angry.","His blue-gold flames burned darker for a moment.","He wrote the target of the Inscription very clearly.","His pen moved with decisive strokes, inscribing the designation upon the golden page with finality that left no room for ambiguity. The 27 Phonemes swirled at the tip of his pen and compressed themselves into a name that would bind this Apophasis to its intended recipient.","His first Written Inscription had its target as THE Living Elemental.","The moment the target was decided, the page it was written on began to float upward from the desk.","It looked innocent. A single golden page covered in blue-gold writing that burned with soft light. Beautiful, even. The kind of thing that might be displayed in a museum or preserved as a work of art.","But it was akin to a nuclear bomb.","An Apophasis Inscriptio Nominata that would hunt its target across all of Observable Existence and deliver constant agony and progressive foundation collapse upon arrival.","He wanted it to hurt, and for it to take some time!","An instant later, it shot out like an arrow and disappeared from The Interstices.","Noah leaned back on his throne with an expectant gaze, his eyes following the trajectory of his Inscription as it vanished into the weavings between spaces, racing toward Alfheimr where THE Living Elemental currently resided.","He didn’t know exactly how long it would take to arrive.","He didn’t know exactly what THE Living Elemental would be doing when it found him.","But he knew that very soon, one of the Absolutes who had made his life difficult was going to experience suffering that would make him regret ever interfering with his personal affairs!","The throne of Absolute Seals supported his weight as he waited, the desk before him still holding more golden pages that could receive more Inscriptions.","He had time.","He had Infinities.","And he had a list of enemies who deserved similar treatment.","But THE Living Elemental got to be first, because some offenses simply could not be forgiven!","But as one page flew...he could always begin preparing and writing others!"]},{"number":4888,"title":"Chapter 4888: Chapter 4887: Adversity! I","paragraphs":["In Alfheimr, the vibrant twilight burned across skies that held every color of flame simultaneously.","The Primordial Realm of THE Creature was a place where existence itself felt more real than anywhere else in Observable Existence, where the weight of simply being pressed against visitors with authority that reminded them they existed only because Existence permitted it.","Mountains rose toward horizons that couldn’t be reached, their peaks shrouded in mists that held secrets accumulated across eons. Forests of trees older than most civilizations spread across valleys that had witnessed the birth and death of countless powers.","And on the same mountain that THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger had descended a little while ago, after Origin had received her answer from THE Creature and given her answer to Hunger, two different figures were now walking up.","THE Living Emotive skipped up the ancient stone steps with manic energy that made her hair bounce with each movement. She hummed a tune that shifted between melodies without ever settling on one, her existence radiating weavings of emotion so intense that the very air around her seemed to feel what she felt. Joy and excitement and anticipation and a dozen other feelings wove through her aura in patterns that would have driven lesser beings to madness.","Beside her, THE Living Elemental walked with a frowning expression.","There was something he couldn’t quite put his finger on.","A sense of wrongness that had been building in his foundations for what felt like hours now, a disquiet that refused to be silenced no matter how many times he tried to dismiss it as paranoia. Even the prospect of a discussion with THE Creature, one of THE Four themselves, felt like something he couldn’t properly focus on right now.","There was one figure he was worried about.","THE Youngest!","Before, when that weak being had tried to encroach on his Civilization, Elemental had been so enraged that he’d paid a significant cost to exert his power outside THE Loom when all those holding THE designations were suppressed. He had laid out a savage curse upon THE Youngest, one designed to burn and isolate and torment until the target either perished or well...killed themselves to perish!","It had been a declaration of superiority. A reminder of the gap between Civilizational and whatever THE Youngest had been at that time.","But now, that weak being who wasn’t even at THE Civilizational Scale of Existence before had become one of THE Four.","THE Youngest now held a Claim.","THE Youngest was now counted among the more powerful entities in all of Observable Existence.","The time from then to now was what, a mere matter of days? It was absolutely nothing in terms of time to Elemental. He had existed for eons. He had watched civilizations rise and fall like waves upon a shore. Days were less than heartbeats to someone of his existence.","And yet things had changed that drastically in such an insignificant span of time.","He wondered what the resolution for this situation would be. He didn’t know how many months or years he had before THE Youngest would make a move against him. The grudge between them was clear.","He had to secure his power before then.","The assurance of those among THE Four would be ideal. If Paradox or THE Creature vouched for his protection, perhaps THE Youngest would hesitate before acting. Perhaps the weavings of THE Four’s relationships would provide protection that his own power could not guarantee.","So he climbed the mountain to see THE Creature.","HUUM!","His existence buzzed at this moment.","Elemental raised his head high, his eyes scanning the twilight above as his Civilization sent out warnings that screamed through every aspect of his being. He was initially confused, not understanding what his foundations were trying to tell him. Then astonished, as he perceived something descending from above with speed that exceeded what should have been possible. Then shocked, as he recognized the weight of what was coming.","From above, a terrifying authority descended!","A single golden page burning with blue-gold light that painted the twilight in colors that didn’t belong in Alfheimr. It fell like a meteor, like a judgment, like something inevitable that could not be avoided or redirected. The weight it carried was immense, pressing against reality itself as it approached.","\" What is that?!\"","THE Living Emotive stopped her skipping, her manic humming cutting off as her crimson eyes locked onto the descending page with sudden intensity.","THE Living Elemental didn’t waste time on questions.","\"I am the culmination of all Elements! I am the authority that governs the fundamental forces of Observable Existence! Nothing may touch me without my permission!\"","BOOM!","His Embodiment erupted outward with force that would have devastated anything below Absolute, the declaration pressing against reality with weight accumulated across eons of existence. The authority of Elements themselves rose to meet the descending page, fundamental forces rallying to protect the one who claimed dominion over them.","THE Living Emotive’s eyes widened as she realized something crucial.","The page wasn’t targeting her.","It wasn’t targeting the mountain or the surrounding area or anything else in its vicinity.","It was targeting Elemental specifically, its trajectory locked onto his existence with precision!","\" What the...\"","She moved away from Elemental even as she released her own Embodiment to help him.","\" Emotions are the foundation of all action! Fear shall rise against what descends, and that fear shall become a shield that protects those I choose to defend!\"","BOOM!","Two Embodiments now pressed against the descending page, the combined authority of THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive creating a barrier that should have stopped anything of weak Absolutes.","Yet...","The page continued to descend.","It didn’t slow.","It didn’t waver.","It passed through their Embodiments as if they didn’t exist, as if the declarations of two Absolutes were nothing more than suggestions that it chose to ignore. The blue-gold light burned brighter as it approached Elemental’s position, and no amount of authority seemed capable of stopping it.","Because the Embodiments weren’t addressing what the Inscription required.","The Inscriptio Nominata had been written with a specific condition: it would strike any target whose foundation did not exceed the foundation of the one who wrote it. As long as that condition remained true, as long as Elemental’s Depth did not exceed Noah’s newly elevated foundations, nothing could stop the Inscription from reaching its target.","Embodiments that declared protection were meaningless.","Embodiments that declared immunity were irrelevant.","The only thing that could have stopped it was an Embodiment or authority that directly addressed the foundational comparison, that changed the underlying truth upon which the Inscription operated.","Neither Absolute had done that.","Neither Absolute had even known to try.","The page reached THE Living Elemental.","It branded itself upon his forehead with a flash of blue-gold light that seared into his existence, and then it disappeared. The golden page was gone, absorbed into his being, its payload delivered with precision that left no room for resistance.","For a moment, nothing happened.","Then THE Living Elemental began to feel it!","Oh!","A burning sensation erupted across his Depths, starting at his Surface and spreading rapidly toward his Intermediate and Fundamental foundations. It wasn’t the kind of burning that could be ignored or suppressed through willpower. It was the burning of existence itself being set aflame, of his very foundations being subjected to constant torment that had no source he could identify or target!","His face became pale.","Then ashen.","His legs buckled beneath him as the pain intensified, and THE Living Elemental, one of the Absolutes of Observable Existence, fell to his knees on the ancient stone steps of the mountain. His hands pressed against the ground as he struggled to maintain composure, his entire body trembling with agony that exceeded anything he had experienced in eons of existence!","But he did not scream.","He was someone grand. He was an Absolute. He had existed since before most civilizations had been born, and he would not give whatever had done this the satisfaction of hearing him cry out!","But man was it painful.","THE Living Emotive rushed to his side, her manic energy replaced with focused intensity as she knelt beside him and began analyzing what had happened. Her crimson eyes burned with authority as she examined the remnants of the Inscription’s effect, tracing the curse through his foundations with perception that few others could match.","Her analysis took only seconds.","Her face went wide with shock and awe.","\" That was an ancient expression of Civilization.\"","Her voice was quiet.","\"An Apophasis...\"","She looked up at the sky where the page had descended from, her mind racing through possibilities.","\" Who could possibly...\"","She was just about to ask the obvious question when her eyes stopped and she went silent.","\" Haha , No way... right?\"","She had one person in mind. One being who had recently ascended to heights that shouldn’t have been possible. One entity who had a very specific grudge against THE Living Elemental that stemmed from a burning curse laid during their previous confrontation.","The moment she thought of it, Elemental also thought of it.","His body trembled even more violently, horrid pain tearing across his very existence as the Apophasis continued its relentless work. He could feel his foundation beginning to deteriorate, could feel the weight of his Depths slowly being torn apart by an authority that seemed to ignore everything he threw against it.","It couldn’t be, right?","THE Youngest shouldn’t have this power right now! It was too quick!"]},{"number":4889,"title":"Chapter 4889: Chapter 4888: Adversity! II","paragraphs":["No one who had been a mere Fundamental Depth entity minutes ago should be able to afflict him with a curse that his own authority couldn’t counter!","And yet here he was, on his knees, feeling his existence being slowly dismantled!","Brought to his knees, Elemental did everything to focus. He gathered his authority, drew upon the weight of his foundations, and uttered another Embodiment with desperate determination.","\"I am beyond the reach of curses and afflictions! My existence rejects all that seeks to harm it!\"","BOOM!","The Embodiment erupted outward.","It did nothing.","The burning continued. The deterioration continued. The pain continued without the slightest reduction in intensity.","Emotive’s eyes widened with awe and...fucking excitement at this predicament?","Elemental roared out another Embodiment, louder this time, more forceful, pouring everything he had into the declaration.","\"I am THE Living Elemental! The fundamental forces of existence are mine to command! I declare that this affliction holds no power over me!\"","BOOM!","The Embodiment shook the mountain itself with its force.","It still did nothing.","The curse had been written with precision that his Embodiments couldn’t address. No matter how loudly he declared his immunity, no matter how forcefully he rejected the affliction, the underlying truth remained unchanged: his foundation did not exceed the foundation of the one who had written the Inscription.","Until that truth changed, nothing would stop the curse from running its course.","Elemental was shocked and horrified at this realization.","And he could feel his Civilization starting to deteriorate, could feel the structure of his existence being slowly but surely compromised by an attack he had no defense against.","At such a time, the surrounding reality shifted.","The two of them had been climbing the mountain toward the temple at its peak, but now they found themselves much closer than they had realized. The temple that had seemed so distant moments ago was now visible just ahead, its multicolored stone architecture gleaming in the twilight.","And at the doorway of the temple, a figure appeared.","THE Creature.","His form was shrouded in multicolored flames of Existence that burned with every color simultaneously, his face barely visible behind the fires that comprised his being. Eyes of immense calm looked out from within those flames, observing the scene before him with ancient patience that had witnessed the turning of ages.","THE Living Emotive’s eyes pulsed with a light of fanaticism and fascination as she looked toward THE Creature. Her entire existence seemed to lean toward him, drawn by whatever relationship or obsession connected her to this being among THE Four. She opened her mouth to speak, to offer greeting or reverence or whatever words rose naturally to her lips.","But before she could say anything, Elemental spoke first.","\" Sir.\"","His voice was strained with pain, each word an effort that cost him dearly.","\"If you could lend a hand.\"","...!","He could barely raise his head to look at THE Creature as he said this, his existence trembling with agony that continued without pause. The proud Absolute who had laid curses upon others was now kneeling before one of THE Four, begging for assistance against a curse that had been laid upon him.","THE Creature surrounded by multicolored flames looked toward Elemental with eyes that held no judgment and no mercy in equal measure. His voice was calm, almost gentle, when he spoke.","\" What you have been afflicted with connects to your foundation. An Apophasis was laid out with a condition tied to the comparative weight of your Depths. No matter what others do, it will be useless unless you change your foundation.\"","Elemental’s face grew more ashen as he processed these words.","\" And for others to do it for you...\"","THE Creature shook his head.","\" That is not possible. The curse targets you specifically. It measures your foundation specifically. Nothing I could do would alter the truth upon which the Apophasis operates.\"","Elemental looked toward THE Creature with a pleading expression that sat wrong on his proud features.","\"I will give you my Everything.\"","His voice cracked with desperation.","\" All of it. Everything I possess, everything I am, if you would only lend your aid in this matter. Please.\"","THE Creature looked calmly at Elemental for a long moment, the multicolored flames around him burning steadily without fluctuation.","Then he shook his head again.","Because sometimes, an Everything held worth...and other times, even the Everythings of an Absolute...held absolutely no worth.","\" This is a type of adversity and hardship for you unlike any other you have faced.\"","His voice held no cruelty, only observation.","\"If you actually overcome it through your own efforts, you will likely be distinguished amongst Absolutes. Your foundation would grow in ways that comfortable existence never permits. The Vakochev Scales favor those who have weathered genuine hardship.\"","He paused.","\" Another path you can take is to seek forgiveness from the one you wronged. They may let you off.\"","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that pressed against Elemental’s already deteriorating existence.","Seek forgiveness.","From THE Youngest.","From the being he had cursed and dismissed and looked down upon just days ago.","...!","Fuck that!","Elemental became ashen as he realized he would receive no help from THE Creature. His one hope of protection from THE Four had just been denied, and the other options available to him were either impossible or unthinkable.","The pain and Civilizational degradation he felt became even more intense as he processed this reality. He heaved, his body convulsing with agony that his Embodiments couldn’t touch. His Civilizational authority did nothing against it. His declarations of immunity did nothing against it. Everything he tried failed against an Inscription that had been written with precision he couldn’t counter.","He looked above, toward the sky where the page had descended from, and his eyes burned with hatred.","If THE Creature did not want to help him, he would have another body of his ask Paradox. THE Living Paradox held a Claim as well, held power that might be able to assist where THE Creature had refused.","And if Paradox did not want to help him...","...!","A grand Absolute kneeled down in pain as he looked at his options.","They were few.","They were unpleasant.","And they were narrowing with every moment that passed, with every increment of foundation that deteriorated under the relentless assault of an Apophasis that he had never anticipated and couldn’t counter.","When a man was driven to desperation, who knows just who or what they might turn toward for help when all other avenues fail?","Many thoughts hadn’t consciously formed in Elemental’s mind yet.","But desperation had a way of making previously unthinkable options seem reasonable.","And Elemental was growing more desperate by the moment!"]},{"number":4890,"title":"Chapter 4890: Chapter 4889: Calm","paragraphs":["Lovers of peace would say that hatred has no place in one’s heart. That even if you take revenge or have your vengeance, it won’t change anything. That you won’t feel better after the deed is done.","Man, how wrong they were.","As Noah looked at a kneeling and distraught Elemental through the connection his Inscription had burned into this being’s existence, he felt tremendous satisfaction!","When you hate something so thoroughly, seeing it suffer felt good.","It felt really fucking good.","At this moment, Noah leaned back on his throne of Absolute Seals as he looked at the illusory scene in front of him that displayed Elemental on his knees, Emotive standing nearby with an expression of fascination, and on its periphery, the booming aura and Immensity of THE Creature as he actually showed himself in Alfheimr.","And what a unique thing that was.","Noah had only ever seen or glimpsed THE Creature a handful of times now. They had never conversed. They had never exchanged words directly. Everything Noah knew about this being among THE Four came from stories and legends and the occasional observation through methods that didn’t involve actual interaction.","But at this moment, the words THE Creature said to Elemental seemed to almost be directed at him as well.","\"This is a type of adversity and hardship for you unlike any other.\"","\"...\"","Was it a coincidence? Or was THE Creature aware that Noah was watching through the Inscription’s connection?","Probably the latter. THE Creature was one of THE Four. Assuming he was unaware of anything was foolish.","And uniquely, at this moment in time, Noah had an illusory consciousness meeting with THE Primordial Chaos in another region of Alfheimr, with Ul’moreth standing by his side. THE Creature also had one of his bodies present in this Primordial Realm.","Similar to Ginnungagap all those eons ago, THE Primordial Chaos, THE Creature, and Noah were all in the same place.","Three of THE Four, gathered in Alfheimr.","Noah thought about the situation as he watched Elemental writhe in agony that his Embodiments couldn’t counter.","He didn’t particularly feel the need to strike up a discussion with THE Creature.","He was curious about this being and all the legends surrounding him, yes. THE Creature’s origins. His relationship with Anaximander...which also reminded him of what he saw in Prima Indifferentia.","But... even if Noah didn’t want to admit it, he held a level of stubborn pride.","It was even among his seven deadly sins contained in his Absolute Seals.","THE Creature was grand and immense, yes. But did that mean that Noah also had to climb up the mountain to see him like all others did? Did that mean he had to approach THE Creature as a lesser seeking audience?","He was also one of THE Four.","If THE Creature wanted to have a discussion with him, he knew where Noah was!","At this time, Noah put the scene of the suffering Elemental to the side of his awareness, glancing at it every now and then to enjoy the plight of this being who had dared to interrupt his Dual Cultivation. Each time he looked, Elemental seemed more pale, more desperate, more broken by an Apophasis that his Embodiments couldn’t address.","Beautiful.","While savoring his enemy’s torment, Noah continued his work.","On the desk before him, there were already two more Inscriptions completed.","These ones were Inscriptiones Dormientes, Sleeping Inscriptions that waited within his existence for the moment he chose to awaken them. One golden page burned with the light of offense, and one burned with the light of defense, both ready to be deployed at a moment’s notice.","The offensive Inscription was half Apophasis half Embodiment that read:","\"The Depths of my target are not beyond my reach. My strikes are not limited by the weight they carry, but are amplified by the difference between my foundation and the foundation of the one who stands against me. The greater the gap in my favor, the more devastating my assault becomes.\"","With this Inscription active, every attack Noah launched would carry additional force proportional to how much his foundation exceeded his opponent’s. Against beings with weaker foundations, his strikes would be devastating.","The defensive Inscription was also a glorious one.","\"I am not vulnerable to those whose foundations cannot match my own. The protection I receive is not static but scales with the difference between my weight and the weight of the one who seeks to harm me. The greater my foundation exceeds theirs, the more impenetrable my defense becomes.\"","This one operated on the inverse principle. Against weaker opponents, Noah would be nearly untouchable. Against stronger opponents, the protection would still present. His foundation had become one of his most unique advantages, and any Embodiments or Apophasis built around that foundation were extremely effective.","The synergy was obvious.","His offensive Inscription made his attacks stronger against weaker foundations.","His defensive Inscription made him harder to harm by those same weaker foundations.","And his foundation was currently 12.5 times heavier than THE Primordial Paradox at Surface Depth, 12 times heavier at Intermediate Depth, and exceeding what THE Four possessed before becoming Absolutes at Fundamental Depth.","Most....all...beings in Observable Existence had foundations weaker than his?","Most beings in Observable Existence would find themselves facing amplified attacks while their own strikes bounced off amplified defenses!","But at this time, Noah planned to write more and more Inscriptions to keep in reserve. The beauty of Inscriptiones Dormientes was that he could prepare them in safety and unleash them in danger. Whenever he faced an enemy, they might just be bombarded with Embodiment after Embodiment or Apophasis after Apophasis without knowing what the fuck to do against the onslaught.","He took his pen and leaned over his desk as Phonemes swirled endlessly around him in galaxies of linguistic authority. He began to write another sentence, his concentration focused entirely on the composition while his awareness occasionally flickered to the illusory scene of Elemental’s suffering.","Every now and then, he would raise his head to see the torment of THE Living Elemental.","And he would hum with satisfaction before returning to his work.","In The Interstices, THE Genesis Monarch began a campaign of writing down Embodiments and Apophasis with the diligence of a scholar preparing for war. Golden pages accumulated on his desk, each one containing a Sleeping Inscription ready to be awakened at his command.","Such a thing truly did not bode well for the Absolutes across existence."]},{"number":4891,"title":"Chapter 4891: Chapter 4890: Storm I","paragraphs":["At the same time as Noah increased his arsenal in The Interstices, another body of his moved across his Infiniverse.","He appeared in a region that held an endlessly expanding sea of Muspelheim, the recently integrated Primordial Realm now fully subsumed into his domain. Crimson-blue stellar liquids and plasma permeated all around him, the essence of Muspelheim transformed into fuel for his ever-growing existence!","In the center of this sea was the massive visage of THE Mnemonic Leviathan.","The dolphin-like lifeform that held a great deal of knowledge floated in the stellar currents with her eyes closed, clearly attempting to return to the slumber that she had been engaged in for eons before Noah’s arrival had disturbed her peace. Near her were Ruination and the humanoid form of THE Infiniverse herself, both waiting for Noah’s appearance.","When Noah materialized in this region, THE Mnemonic Leviathan opened one eye to observe him with the resigned expression of someone who knew their rest was about to be interrupted yet again.","He waved to her with a brilliant smile.","\" Not much time may have passed here, but I have gone eons back and made my way back. Thank you for the coordinates.\"","THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s eye regarded him with ancient weariness.","\" No thanks are required. I shall just return to my slumber...\"","She could already feel it was about to have her slumber interrupted as Noah’s smile grew even wider.","\" You hold a great deal of knowledge ,\" he said, his tone shifting to something more businesslike. \"I just toured THE Prima Indifferentia and met quite a few wonders that you may not know about. How about I share knowledge to expand yours, and you also tell me a few things in turn?\"","...!","Noah made such a proposition as THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s eye opened fully, both orbs now focusing on him with interest that warred with her desire for continued rest.","Knowledge was her sustenance.","Knowledge was her purpose.","And he was offering knowledge of THE Prima Indifferentia that she had swam in before! Did he see anything she had not?","Begrudgingly, she spoke.","\" Tell me.\"","Noah smiled brilliantly as Ruination and THE Infiniverse joined him, the three of them positioning themselves before the ancient Leviathan as he began to talk about proto-matter and Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors and all the other wonders he had witnessed during his temporal traversal.","He wanted to wring this pink dolphin dry of everything she knew.","And in exchange, he would give her the knowledge she craved.","A fair trade, by his estimation.","Beside him, he could see the weavings of THE Infiniverse fluctuating with changes that went beyond anything she had displayed before. She had completed the assimilation of Muspelheim during his temporal traversal, and his own advancement was reflecting on her existence in ways that made her seem almost unrecognizable compared to what she had been.","Behind her eyes, infinities burned with terrifying brilliance.","She was no longer just his Infiniverse.","She was becoming something more.","And her voice echoed out within his mind.","|Master, I have begun to forge a realm of Undifferentiation within my structure. Near the Early Veiled Shore, I am cultivating an environment filled with proto-matter similar to what you experienced in THE Prima Indifferentia.|","|This realm draws upon the echoes of your journey and the undifferentiated qualities now woven into your Infinite nature. It will serve as a training ground for those you wish to expose to controlled undifferentiation, and as a resource repository for proto-matter that can be harvested without the dangers of THE Prima Indifferentia itself.|","|Additionally, my own foundations are rising exponentially in response to your growth. As your Infinite Formless Depth expands without ceiling, so too does my existence as an extension of your authority. The rate of increase has exceeded what I can fully quantify at this moment. I am becoming something that I do not yet have the parameters to define.|","|I will provide updated assessments as my understanding catches up with my transformation.|","Noah smiled at her words and nodded with approval before continuing his conversation with THE Mnemonic Leviathan. Having a realm of controlled undifferentiation within his Infiniverse opened possibilities that he would need to explore when time permitted. Training grounds for his followers.","Moiraine, Riya, Titano, Little Bobby, Malphas, Heidrun, and all others would not be allowed to sit still!","Existence was filled with adversity for those who wanted to advance.","They needed adversity!","The Infiniverse was growing alongside him, becoming a territory that matched the scope of his ambitions.","But that was a matter for later consideration.","Right now, he had a pink dolphin to interrogate.","---","And Noah was truly a busy man.","While one body wrote Inscriptions in The Interstices and another extracted knowledge from THE Mnemonic Leviathan in his Infiniverse, a third body stood in an entirely different location.","THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts.","He stood on an endlessly stretching golden river that flowed through spaces that shouldn’t have been able to contain rivers, the stellar expanse above holding treasures that had been deposited across eons by beings seeking to contribute to the Mouseion’s collection. The system of fate and worthiness that governed this place pressed against his existence with weight that would have been overwhelming before his transformation.","Now, it merely felt like acknowledgment.","He was ready to retrieve his fated item.","The item that he himself had placed here eons ago during his temporal traversal with THE Primordial Paradox.","The Antinomia Prismatica.","Behind him, Glossikos watched with calm curiosity that befitted the leader of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. Her luminous features held interest that she didn’t bother to conceal, wondering what someone like THE Youngest would draw from the Mouseion’s endless vaults.","What treasure could possibly be fated for a being like him?","Lumivara poked her head out from behind Glossikos.","Neither of them knew what was about to happen.","Neither of them realized that they were witnessing the completion of a temporal loop that had been set in motion eons ago and was only now reaching its fruition.","Noah looked up at the stellar expanse above, feeling the golden strings of fate extending outward from his existence toward something that called to him from the Mouseion’s depths.","The Antinomia Prismatica.","The key to THE Primordial Paradox’s return.","He reached upward.","And the Mouseion responded!"]},{"number":4892,"title":"Chapter 4892: Chapter 4891: Storm II","paragraphs":["In existence, you had to walk around and move around like you knew exactly what you were doing.","The trick was to understand that more often than not, everybody else had absolutely no idea what they were doing, and they were figuring things out as they went. The Absolute who seemed impossibly confident? Probably winging it.","The ancient entity who spoke with authority accumulated across eons? Making educated guesses based on experience!","The member of THE Four who shaped Observable Existence with casual gestures? Still learning, still adapting, still uncertain about outcomes that hadn’t yet unfolded.","Some had a bit more control compared to others, but Existence was mainly chaotic.","So fake it until you make it.","Noah was releasing his signature and power while standing on the golden river of THE Mouseion as if he knew exactly what he was doing. His blue-gold flames burned with confidence that pressed against the fate-based systems surrounding him, declaring without words that he belonged here, that he had every right to claim whatever the Mouseion deemed his, that whatever descended from the stellar expanse above would be exactly what he expected.","He knew with utmost certainty that some grand fated item would be descending down for him.","And well, this wasn’t entirely faking it.","He actually did know what was coming.","He had put it there himself.","HUUM!","The space above shuddered as if it was being pulled by forces that transcended the Mouseion’s normal operations. The stellar expanse that held countless treasures deposited across eons trembled with recognition, and in the next moment, at an extremely rapid speed, something came down as if Noah was reclaiming lost property that had been waiting for him all this time.","At Planck speed, a blue-gold treasure chest appeared in front of him.","The chest didn’t drift down gently like other fated items might. It didn’t descend with the measured pace of fate acknowledging worthiness. It rushed toward Noah with urgency.","Glossikos was astonished.","Why did this item rush toward him as if a child was rushing back to their parent? Why did the Mouseion’s systems respond with such enthusiasm to this particular claim? She had witnessed countless retrievals across her existence as a leader of THE Agora, and none of them had looked like this.","When she looked at the chest clearly though, recognition struck her.","In the next moment, Glossikos was astounded as she remembered this item.","Eons ago, someone had put this item in here. They had come along with a terrifying personage that had long since been gone, a being whose presence had made even the Polemarchs of that era lower their heads in deference!","Glossikos remembered countless eons ago when she brought THE Tongue Whisperer here, when they added this very chest as a contribution to THE Mouseion’s collection.","What was this?","Why would...","Her mind buzzed with implications she couldn’t fully process.","Noah grasped the blue-gold treasure chest with Immensity that made his foundations resonate with the object’s authority. His eyes met Glossikos’s shocked gaze with calm.","\"I told you, Glossikos, that I would come and get what is fated for me later on.\"","His voice was steady.","\" That at that point, you may actually be there to witness it.\"","He smiled.","\" Here I am, and here you are.\"","BOOM!","His words felt archaic and heavy, echoing with weight that came from having been spoken before and now being fulfilled. They were so astonishing, so impossible, so fundamentally reality-breaking in their implications that the Absolute who heard them did something she hadn’t done in eons.","She stumbled backward.","And then she fell on her ass in shock and incredulity.","Glossikos, one of the Strategoi who had helped shape this institution across THE Infinite Unfurling, sat on the golden river and stared up at Noah with an expression that had abandoned all composure.","When she now looked at him, the image of THE Tongue Whisperer that she had seen in this same place eons ago overlapped with the being standing before her now. The same mannerisms. The same confidence.","He had known!","Even back then, he had known he would be standing here!","Even back then, he had known she would be watching!","In the midst of her shock, golden light descended from the surroundings like ancient rivers converging on a singular point. The Mouseion’s systems recognized what had just occurred, and they responded.","The light flowed into Noah with warmth of merit accumulated across eons finally being claimed.","|Fated Retrieval Complete|","|You have retrieved an item placed in THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts eons ago. THE Antinomia Prismatica is deemed the singular most unique item to have ever been placed in THE Mouseion across its entire history. No other contribution has carried equivalent significance or potential impact on Observable Existence.|","|For the retrieval of this item after all these eons, you have gained an unfathomable number of merit points. The contribution weight of THE Antinomia Prismatica, combined with the temporal paradox of its placement and retrieval, has generated merit that exceeds what THE Agora of Primordial Judgment typically processes.|","|This contribution is sufficient for you to challenge for the rank of Strategos, the highest rank in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. You would join the four current Strategoi as the fifth, should you choose to pursue this elevation.|","...!","The prompts were heavy as Noah’s toga shone and fluctuated with authority that pressed outward from his existence.","But that wasn’t what held his attention.","Noah looked at the object in his hands with shining eyes, and at this moment, he became serious.","Because instantly, the surrounding atmosphere began to glimmer with an obsidian-gold light of Paradox.","His wrappings of THE First Tongue around the object contained within the chest began to unravel the moment it was revealed to Observable Existence again.","And what lay within was waking up.","In Observable Existence, there were truly a few points in time that could be considered pivotal and critical moments that informed how existence would unfold for the future to come. The birth of THE Creature. The first conversation between a peasant and THE Primordial Paradox. THE Fallout...","Somehow, at this moment, back to back, THE Genesis Monarch was involved in two pivotal moments.","The first had been his attainment of the Native Speaker designation, an achievement that no one else in Observable Existence currently held.","The second was happening now.","An ancient air of Paradox that had been thought to be gone since THE Infinite Unfurling began to bloom like a flower everybody thought dead and gone.","The authority was unmistakable to anyone who had ever encountered THE Primordial Paradox in his prime, that contradictory weight that declared things were and were not simultaneously, that truth was both absolute and relative, that existence itself was a question that could never be fully answered.","THE Antinomia Prismatica was releasing the essence it had been containing.","The piece of THE Primordial Paradox’s existence that he had separated and preserved against the day when his Claim would be usurped.","As all of this happened, within the mind of THE Genesis Monarch, there was actually only a single thought that seemed fitting at this moment.","\" The Paradox shall fall before the Paradox rises.\"","He spoke the words aloud, his voice resonating with the weight of the Echo of First Cause.","\" The father consumed by the son, the son consumed by the purpose, the purpose consumed by the question that birthed all questions.\"","The obsidian-gold light around them intensified.","\" Three collapses for the price of one, and in the third collapse, the door shall crack.\"","BOOM!","He uttered these words as they only added to the ancient and terrifying air in the surroundings. The words merged with the reality unfolding before them, past and future colliding in the present moment with weight that made THE Mouseion itself tremble!","Glossikos’s emotions transformed from astonishment to horror as she felt this aura of Paradox and she knew who THE Tongue Whisperer had come with that day eons ago.","A terrifying personage.","One whose presence had made even her bow her head!","As she connected the dots, she truly could not help but be horrified by a scheme and a plan that seemed to be running across eons of time.","THE Four!","THE Four always did whatever they wished, leaving others to deal with the consequences of their actions and schemes.","And two of them seemed to have hatched a plot that spanned eons of time, using THE Mouseion itself as a storage vault for the key to resurrection!"]},{"number":4893,"title":"Chapter 4893: Chapter 4892: Storm III","paragraphs":["Across Observable Existence, there were many shelters of THE Loom.","Hidden bastions scattered throughout the Wastes. Some were small. Some were vast, containing vast populations.","But at this moment in time, inside the main shelter of THE Loom, something pivotal was occurring.","At the very peak of a paradoxical mountain that pointed upward and downward and in different directions within a matter of seconds, a single man floated surrounded by terrifying weavings of Paradox. The air of an Absolute was utterly suffocating around him, pressing against reality with weight that declared his supremacy over the aspect he had claimed.","It felt Absolute.","And at the same time, it felt like something else entirely.","As if maybe, potentially, there was actually the possibility that it had exceeded this designation. Maybe. Paradoxically. The uncertainty itself was part of the power, the contradiction between what he was and what he might be creating strength that purely defined existence could never match.","This was THE Living Paradox at this moment.","He had three Axioms rotating around him. They orbited his form like moons around a planet, each one containing power that could reshape regions of Observable Existence if unleashed.","He was staring at what floated above the paradoxical mountain.","A Crack of Observable Existence.","The same type of fracture that led to THE Prima Indifferentia, to the place where differentiation had first begun and where undifferentiation still held dominion.","The body of THE Living Paradox was a unique one, chosen specifically for the symbolism it represented. He looked similar to none other than the now collapsed and dead Schrodinger.","And this body actually wore the same beggar-like clothes that THE Living Paradox had worn during his time as a peasant, even though paradoxically, he knew that there was always going to be a peasant somewhere in existence. The clothes were tattered and simple, completely at odds with the Absolute authority radiating from his form.","A peasant who had become one of THE Four.","A beggar who now waged war against THE Creature himself.","This was simply the only other body that he could currently spare, as all his other forms were engaged in the conflict that consumed most of his attention and resources. The war against THE Creature demanded everything he had and more.","Since the day that he began even planning and thinking about this war, THE Living Paradox had known it would be almost an impossibility to win. Since the moment he began to plan to betray his master, THE Primordial Paradox, he knew he was setting himself up for an extremely arduous existence.","THE Creature was only one among the many lines of impossibilities that THE Living Paradox had placed in front of himself.","A mere peasant being capable of usurping the Claim of Paradox from one of THE Four?","Impossible.","A mere peasant even thinking about going against the one who held Claim to Existence itself?","Impossible.","A single peasant being capable of managing to alter and change the entire landscape of Observable Existence through THE Loom?","Impossible!","All of these were impossibilities.","And yet here he was, doing one after another.","That was the point.","That had always been the point!","Things were so unimaginably hard for him to the point that he was putting all his effort into his war against THE Creature. Half of him believed THE Creature might only be utilizing a portion of his power, holding back for reasons that only someone who embodied Existence itself could understand.","But the war between him and THE Creature truly was a complex one, filled with moving parts that even THE Living Paradox couldn’t fully track.","He needed THE Creature.","And THE Creature needed him.","He waged war against THE Creature because this was an impossible thing, the hardest thing for him to possibly do. So he did it because he knew if he came out victorious against such adversity and hardship, his existence would be grand beyond measure.","The Vakochev Scales demanded hardship for progression, and what greater hardship could there be than fighting against Existence itself?","At the same time, THE Creature seemed to understand this arrangement.","THE Living Paradox knew there were instances where THE Creature could have chosen to do many different things and didn’t, allowing for events to unfold how they unfolded purely because he also wanted adversity. THE Creature was also seeking to progress along the Vakochev Scales. THE Creature also needed genuine hardship to fuel his advancement.","So they warred.","Not because they hated each other, though hatred certainly existed.","Not because their goals were fundamentally incompatible, though they certainly were.","But because the war itself was the point. The adversity was the treasure. The impossibility was the fuel that would either elevate them both or destroy them both.","The Vakochev Scales of Existence demanded adversity.","And who in Observable Existence bore the weight that THE Living Paradox had taken on?","No one.","No one else had dared to challenge THE Creature directly while simultaneously managing THE Loom’s expansion while simultaneously dealing with the emergence of THE Youngest while simultaneously maintaining control over his usurped Claim.","But THE Creature was so grand that even when one of his helpers was killed by THE Youngest, even when THE Weavers were killed by Noah Osmont, THE Living Paradox actually didn’t have the capacity to mobilize another body to take care of this nuisance.","Because THE Creature kept him that busy.","Every moment of every hour was consumed by the war. Every resource was allocated to the conflict. Every thought was devoted to staying one step ahead of an opponent who embodied the very concept of being.","THE Youngest had been a thorn that THE Living Paradox simply couldn’t spare the attention to remove.","But...","THE Living Paradox smiled as he pointed toward the Crack of Observable Existence floating above his paradoxical mountain. His Axioms began to shine brilliantly. They drew upon the authority of THE Loom itself, upon THE Fallout that had gained a tremendous amount of fuel and Immensity after spreading across Observable Existence.","All of that accumulated authority was now being directed toward a singular purpose.","It pointed and aimed itself toward THE Prima Indifferentia.","\"You want Adversity? \"","His voice was calm, almost conversational, as if he was discussing philosophy rather than preparing an attack that could reshape the nature of reality itself.","\"I will provide Adversity for all of us. To the extent that none of us will be able to breathe.\"","His smile widened.","\" Until all of us feel that same suffocation.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":4894,"title":"Chapter 4894: Chapter 4893: Storm IV","paragraphs":["Even as he started this process, even as the combined authority of THE Loom began to flow toward the Crack of Observable Existence, something else demanded his attention.","\" Huh?\"","THE Living Paradox turned to a certain direction, his eyes shining with wonder and incredulity as he felt his weavings of Paradox buzzing. His Claim to Paradox was buzzing as if something else was contesting it, as if another authority was rising that held legitimate connection to the aspect he had usurped.","And he recognized this aura.","It was impossible to mistake!","It was the aura of the one single being he respected the most apart from THE Creature in all of Observable Existence.","It was the aura of his teacher.","THE Primordial Paradox.","The being he had consumed to claim his position among THE Four. The master who had taught him everything he knew about Paradox and contradiction and the nature of impossible things. The entity whose existence he had supposedly ended when he usurped the Claim.","And yet that aura was blooming somewhere in Observable Existence, growing stronger by the moment.","\" Haha... ridiculous.\"","THE Living Paradox couldn’t help but smile and laugh at such an unfolding weaving of existence. His laughter echoed across the paradoxical mountain, filled not with concern but with something approaching joy.","They continued to turn up the heat on him to make him feel as if he was boiling.","THE Creature waged war against him.","THE Youngest held grudges.","And now his own teacher was apparently returning from collapse to contest his Claim.","The impossibilities were stacking up.","The adversities were multiplying!","The hardships were reaching heights that would have broken any other being in Observable Existence.","And THE Living Paradox was jubilant.","Because this was yet another impossible adversity. This was yet more fuel for the Vakochev Scales. This was yet another challenge that, if overcome, would elevate his existence to heights that no one had ever reached.","He would also turn the heat up for all of them.","If they wanted to make things difficult for him, he would make things difficult for everyone.","So as ridiculously as it seemed, another pivotal moment unfolded at this moment in time. And uniquely, it was not THE Genesis Monarch who was at the center of it.","For once, someone else was initiating a change that would reshape Observable Existence.","THE Living Paradox made his move.","His Axioms blazed with authority that exceeded what any single Absolute should possess, channeling THE Loom’s accumulated power through the Crack of Observable Existence. The fracture cried out as if in pain, becoming torn even further by forces that shouldn’t have been able to affect something that predated Observable Existence itself.","But no proto-matter flooded out of it.","Instead, THE Living Paradox flooded something else into it.","THE Fallout.","If THE Creature wanted adversity, THE Living Paradox would give him adversity.","If THE Youngest wanted to grow strong in this place, THE Living Paradox would make it infinitely more dangerous!","If his old teacher wanted to return and contest his Claim, THE Living Paradox would ensure that everyone suffered equally.","The Crack of Observable Existence screamed as THE Fallout poured through it, carrying the will of THE Living Paradox who refused to face his impossibilities alone.","If he was going to burn, everyone was going to burn with him.","That was the paradox of his existence.","That was the nature of his war.","That was why, despite everything, THE Living Paradox was smiling as he initiated an escalation that would force all players to show their true hands.","The peasant who had become one of THE Four was making his move!","---","In THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts.","An expression of power was being shown here that reminded Noah of one thing he sometimes forgot.","Because of his nature, he moved through stages of power rapidly. He overcame many beings and held more power than them at their stage. He devoured Absolutes and claimed their foundations. He grew in days what others grew in eons.","But he wasn’t the only unique thing in Existence.","There were others.","And others, even if he was arrogant enough to consider himself someone with grander potential than them, were still grand in their own right. If they had eons to cultivate and grow and refine their foundations, what they could accomplish was terrifying.","THE Primordial Paradox was terrifying.","An example was how Noah himself, after having killed and devoured multiple Absolutes, was only now matching and slightly exceeding the foundation of THE Primordial Paradox and THE Creature at Fundamental Depth. And these beings had spent a ridiculous amount of effort on this Depth, as their foundations exceeded many other Absolutes by significant margins.","But they had millions and billions of years to then forge their Absolute Depth.","That was their stepping-off point to THE Second Scale of Existence.","These beings were powerful in ways that Noah was only beginning to understand.","So much so that right now, in THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts, THE Antinomia Prismatica unfolded and unfurled like a paradoxical lotus blooming in reverse and forward simultaneously. Its blue-gold surface peeled away in layers that contradicted each other, revealing and concealing at the same time, until what lay within could finally emerge.","From it, THE Primordial Paradox emerged.","He came forth from immense concentrated weavings that looked like mixtures of Embodiments and Apophasis mixing within each other in a terrifying manner. Declarations of what was and declarations of what was not twisted around his form like serpents devouring their own tails, paradoxical authority so dense that reality itself seemed to struggle with whether he was actually present or merely the possibility of presence.","As his humanoid form became apparent, one could notice a few things.","One was the fact that behind Noah, Glossikos had fallen on her ass and now wore an ashen expression as if she was bearing a weight far too heavy for even her foundations to support.","She was an Absolute, one of the Strategoi of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","And yet she was having a hard time with the aura of THE Primordial Paradox.","Her hands pressed against the golden river beneath her as she struggled to simply remain conscious, her luminous features pale with effort!","And Lumivara, the little fox in humanoid form, sadly lost consciousness entirely. Her body landed on the golden river with a soft sound that seemed impossibly loud in the oppressive silence that THE Primordial Paradox’s emergence had created.","And Noah?","Noah was able to get a glimpse and understand the power of THE Primordial Paradox when he wasn’t hiding and keeping his might concealed.","He felt stifled and expectant in equal measure.","Stifled because ridiculously, he had to activate a defensive Inscriptio Dormiens just to make sure his status as an Absolute Immovable Object wasn’t violated. The aura being released before him almost blew away this body of his, almost scattered his existence across THE Mouseion like leaves before a hurricane. The Sleeping Inscription he had prepared flared to life around him, its Embodiment declaring protection based on the difference between his foundation and the one attacking him.","And even with that protection, he felt the pressure!"]},{"number":4895,"title":"Chapter 4895: Chapter 4894: Storm V","paragraphs":["Expectant because he got a glimpse of just how powerful an Absolute like THE Primordial Paradox truly was. Based on this aura, based on the weight that pressed against his enhanced foundations, Noah currently felt that THE Primordial Paradox had to be hundreds of times grander in Immensity and power than what Noah had achieved.","Hundreds of times.","And this was just the aura, just the leaking presence of someone who hadn’t even finished emerging yet.","This made him very much look forward to matching and exceeding it.","It also made him even more cautious of the other members of THE Four. He truly could not underestimate THE Living Paradox or THE Creature if their power operated on similar scales. He was only beginning to play with Embodiments and Apophasis while they’d had the chance to do so for eons.","The gap was immense.","But gaps could be closed!","That was what infinite potential meant.","\"...\"","As he was thinking all of this, not fully realizing his own grand feat of withstanding the aura of THE Primordial Paradox when even an Absolute had fallen to her knees and was trembling behind him, the emerging entity opened his eyes.","The first thing THE Primordial Paradox saw was Noah.","...!","THE Primordial Paradox blinked for a moment as if he was adjusting to Observable Existence after eons of compressed storage within THE Antinomia Prismatica. His obsidian eyes focused, sharpened, and then recognition bloomed within them alongside something that looked almost like relief.","A smile spread across his face.","He was grand and regal and majestic! His obsidian form had solidified into something more defined than Noah remembered from their journey through THE Prima Indifferentia, as if the time spent within the Antinomia Prismatica had concentrated his existence rather than diminished it. His crown of spinning paradoxes rotated above his head with authority that made the golden river beneath them ripple with uncertainty about whether it was a river at all.","He gazed toward Noah and spoke with a voice that held the weight of one of THE Four.","\"It has been some time, Youngest.\"","His smile held warmth that seemed at odds with the devastating aura still radiating from his form.","\"I had my doubts after you disappeared in that Crack within THE Prima Indifferentia. The method you used to escape was not one I would have recommended.\"","He paused.","\" But... it is good to see you. It is good to be back.\"","BOOM!","The raging aura that had been spreading out of THE Primordial Paradox was reined in soon after, pulled back into his existence. He now only appeared like the regal figure that he was, his Immensity no longer leaking out to crush everything in the vicinity.","But it had leaked out.","And precisely because it had leaked out, because the signature of THE Primordial Paradox had blazed across THE Agora of Primordial Judgment like a beacon announcing his return, responses were coming.","The auras of three Absolutes descended behind Glossikos.","They materialized from spatial distortions of beings who had sensed something impossible and come to investigate with all the speed their foundations could provide. They were the other three Strategoi of THE Agora!","Khaotikos arrived first, his chaotic form shifting between states of matter and energy as his essence refused to settle on any single configuration!","Ontikos arrived second, his form radiating the calm weight of Existence itself. He was always immensely calm, always composed, always certain of his place in the order of things. But even he showed a trace of shock on his features, a widening of eyes that shouldn’t have been capable of surprise.","Paradoxos arrived third, his dual faces expressing different variations of the same astonishment. One face showed fear. The other showed something that looked almost like recognition!","The three arrived like titans of Immensity, their combined auras pressing against THE Mouseion with authority.","They were looking toward the scene of THE Primordial Paradox and Noah with astonishment and disbelief.","Noah looked at the newly appearing Absolutes with interest.","THE Primordial Paradox did the same, a silent smile remaining on his face as he surveyed the beings.","His gaze settled on Ontikos.","Or rather, on the eyes of Ontikos, which were actually holding the gaze of another entirely.","\"O Creature.\"","THE Primordial Paradox’s voice was calm but held an edge of something that might have been amusement.","\" You will not welcome me back in person and only look through the eyes of your follower?\"","...!","Before these words even settled, before anyone could process the implications of THE Primordial Paradox addressing THE Creature directly through Ontikos’s borrowed sight, the ancient Absolute turned his head.","He looked toward the visage of Paradoxos.","His smile faded.","What replaced it was an imperial gaze that held no warmth, no amusement, no patience for anything less than absolute obedience.","Paradoxos’s dual faces became ashen.","Both of them.","Fear and recognition transformed into terror and submission as the weight of that gaze pressed against his existence. He took a step backward unconsciously, his massive form retreating from someone whose physical presence was smaller but whose authority was incomparably greater.","\" Kneel.\"","THE Primordial Paradox said the word calmly.","HUUM!","In the next moment, as if the command had to be obeyed, as if the very concept of Paradox that comprised Paradoxos’s foundation answered to a higher authority, the titanic Absolute fell to his knees!","The impact of his kneeling shook THE Mouseion.","Paradoxos wore an expression of ashen shock, his dual faces both displaying the same horrified realization that he had no choice in this matter. The weavings of Paradox around his body fully obeyed THE Primordial Paradox because THE Primordial Paradox was the source from which his understanding of Paradox had flowed!","A stream could not rebel against its river.","A branch could not defy its tree.","And an Absolute whose foundation was built on Paradox could not resist the one who had defined what Paradox meant.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at this kneeling being as he spoke with calm that made the scene even more terrifying.","\"It doesn’t seem like my disciple is looking through your eyes like THE Creature is looking through this other one.\"","His head tilted slightly.","\" Can he not spare any attention right now? I always told him to plan ahead many steps.\"","He shook his head as if he was a teacher slightly disappointed with a student who hadn’t heeded his lessons.","\" Ah, well.\"","He then looked at Paradoxos and asked calmly.","\" Who do you serve?\"","Paradoxos trembled beneath the weight of that question, his entire existence shaking with conflict that went beyond physical response. His dual mouths opened to answer.","\"I follow the Way of Parado...\"","\"Hush.\"","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he felt an oppressive unseen weight land on Paradoxos, silencing him mid-word with authority that sought no resistance. The Absolute who had been attempting to speak found his voice stolen, his declaration interrupted by power that didn’t need to be explained or justified.","THE Primordial Paradox asked again.","\" Who do you serve?\"","The question was the same, but the weight behind it had intensified. It wasn’t asking for a philosophical answer about Ways and paths. It was demanding a declaration of allegiance that would bind the one who spoke it.","The dual faces of Paradoxos became even more ashen as he lowered his head in submission that he couldn’t resist.","\"I serve...\"","His voice trembled.","\" Paradox. THE...Primordial Paradox.\"","BOOM!","The declaration settled over THE Mouseion. One of the four Strategoi had just declared his allegiance to a being who had supposedly been collapsed and consumed by THE Living Paradox.","And that declaration couldn’t be taken back.","THE Primordial Paradox nodded, accepting the submission with the grace of someone who had expected nothing less. His expression shifted as he turned back to Noah, the imperial coldness fading into something warmer.","He smiled.","\" Youngest, what have I missed?\"","His voice held genuine curiosity.","\"It seems like there is much to be done.\"","...!","Noah looked at the figure of THE Primordial Paradox with shining eyes.","Within a minute of his revival, this being had forced one of the four Absolutes of THE Agora to kneel and declare allegiance. Within a minute, he had reestablished his authority over those who followed the Way of Paradox. Within a minute, he had reminded everyone present why he had been counted among THE Four for eons before his supposed collapse.","One of the most powerful entities among THE Four had returned!"]},{"number":4896,"title":"Chapter 4896: Chapter 4895: A Meeting Across Eons I","paragraphs":["It was something momentous to have THE Primordial Paradox in the flesh standing before everyone.","Some like Glossikos were thinking in their minds again and again on how this could even be possible. The being before her had been collapsed and consumed by his own disciple. The Claim of Paradox had been transferred. THE Living Paradox now sat among THE Four while THE Primordial Paradox was supposed to be nothing but a memory.","And yet here he stood!","While others like Paradoxos did not even have any thoughts as they remained kneeling with their minds actually dazed. The Absolute whose dual faces had been forced into submission couldn’t process what was happening. His foundations trembled. His understanding of reality trembled. Everything he thought he knew in Observable Existence trembled!","And then there was Noah.","He looked at THE Primordial Paradox up and down with eyes that held curiosity rather than reverence, assessment rather than awe. When he spoke, his voice was calm.","\"I expected you to be...a bit weaker when you came out.\"","...!","The words hung in the air as everyone who could still think processed the audacity of such a statement.","\" After all, this was supposed to be a portion of yourself that was not infected. Why is it that you feel even stronger than how you felt back then?\"","He asked such a question casually.","THE Primordial Paradox smiled.","\" When you reach a certain level... or really, when you reach close to THE Second Scale of Existence...\"","He paused, his obsidian eyes holding depths that spoke of understanding accumulated across eons.","\"I cannot say for sure how THE Creature or you or others would be. But for me? Even if every part of my existence was eradicated and only a single drop of blood remained. Even if only a single primordial cell survived. When I emerge once more from that tiny little thing, I would be just as grand if not grander than I was before.\"","His smile widened.","\" That is my Way. That is Paradox.\"","He took a step forward, his presence pressing against reality without crushing it.","\" For me to be weaker just because I sectioned off a part of myself? Who decided that? I make my own decisions. Those on the higher Scales of Existence make their own decisions. The rules that bind lesser beings are suggestions to us, and we choose which suggestions to follow.\"","His gaze settled on Noah.","\" As THE Youngest among THE Four, you will come to understand this soon enough.\"","BOOM!","THE Primordial Paradox said such terrifying words as Noah couldn’t help but smile at the implications. The idea that reaching certain heights meant you could simply decide not to be weakened by things that should weaken you. He was getting there!","But he also couldn’t help but become serious in the next moment.","\" Well, is it still THE Four and not THE Five with your return?\"","...!","\"...\"","His question caused everyone in the surrounding environment to become silent.","The Strategoi could not even bring themselves to talk at this moment in time. Glossikos was still struggling to remain cognizant. Khaotikos and Ontikos were processing implications. Paradoxos remained kneeling, unable to rise without permission.","But even if they could speak, they would also be flabbergasted!","THE Five?","THE Primordial Paradox smiled and gave a light nod toward Noah.","\"It doesn’t quite have the same ring.\"","His voice held amusement.","\" But for now, until I take on the role of teacher to discipline my student who rebelled... it will be THE Five and not THE Four.\"","He turned his head toward the four Strategoi present, his gaze sweeping across Glossikos who was still on the ground, Khaotikos who stood frozen, Ontikos whose eyes still held THE Creature’s borrowed sight, and Paradoxos who remained kneeling.","\"I am back after such a long time.\"","His voice shifted to something more commanding.","\" Prepare a feast. I need to catch up with THE Youngest.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox gave light commands to four Absolutes who nobody could command in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","He ordered them to prepare a feast as if they were servants!","And yet none of them protested.","THE Primordial Paradox went toward Noah, who had turned around to pick up the unconscious Lumivara. The little fox in humanoid form seemed to be sleeping soundly, her features peaceful despite the overwhelming forces that had rendered her unconscious.","Noah held her carefully while turning to THE Primordial Paradox.","\"I don’t know whether you will have time for a feast.\"","His voice was serious now.","\" That thing from all those eons ago... it has actually been sitting outside of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment as if it knew you would be reemerging here.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox’s expression shifted.","\" As of this moment, it has spread itself fully into... THE Secretive Eon.\"","...!","The laid-back demeanor that THE Primordial Paradox had been displaying vanished. What replaced it was seriousness that made the already tense atmosphere of THE Mouseion grow heavier.","\" Eon...\"","He said the single word as if it meant something to him beyond what others might understand!","With an extremely serious gaze, he turned toward Noah.","\" Can you bring me to her?\"","His request was direct.","\"I need you to accompany me. Just to be completely sure that it cannot latch itself onto me.\"","He paused.","\" After you left, Jokul and I affirmed one of the defenses against it is the glimmer of Infinity. Your Infinite nature creates interference that the infection cannot easily overcome. I should be resistant on my own, but out of an overabundance of caution... having you there would be ideal.\"","BOOM!","Minutes after THE Primordial Paradox returned, the first thing he wanted to do was go see THE Secretive Eon!","He wanted to go directly to the being that housed THE Entity.","Noah thought about this for a moment.","That thing was disastrous to be around. The infection that spread from it had claimed countless beings across Observable Existence.","But he had come far since he last left her presence.","His foundations were incomparably grander. His Infinities had transformed. His understanding of undifferentiation had deepened through his journey in THE Prima Indifferentia.","And in Alfheimr, THE Primordial Chaos had not proceeded to bombard THE Stoa of Dogmata just yet. If he was going to do so at all, there should be time for this detour.","Noah nodded silently."]},{"number":4897,"title":"Chapter 4897: Chapter 4896: A Meeting Across Eons II","paragraphs":["In existence, there were so many oddities that it was hard to keep track.","Noah always observed the oddities and wonders with a cautious eye, especially things that he did not understand.","THE Entity was not something that he fully understood.","So even though he knew he should be immune, he still appeared in THE Stoa of Dogmata with THE Primordial Paradox with his body shrouded by blue-gold flames of THE First Tongue. Infinite variations of Phonemes swirled around his form like a protective cocoon, ready to respond to any threat that might attempt to breach his defenses.","THE Primordial Paradox stayed close to him as they traversed the space. Noah had left Lumivara behind with Glossikos, and only the two of them came here.","And oddly enough, truly, the figure of THE Secretive Eon had not left even an inch from where they sat before.","When their eyes landed on THE Primordial Paradox, they lit up. Both their eyes and their mouth smiled as if something they had deeply been waiting for had appeared once more. Joy radiated from her features in a way that seemed genuine and yet profoundly unsettling.","But when the eyes of THE Secretive Eon landed on Noah, the smile faded. They frowned as if his mere presence ruined things.","The frown disappeared from THE Secretive Eon soon after, replaced by careful neutrality as she also smiled at Noah.","Noah looked around the Stoa. Beside her, the disciple that he had helped bring outside to this place, who had inadvertently become infected by THE Entity, was nowhere to be seen.","The two sides looked at each other silently.","THE Primordial Paradox seemed to be thinking of too many things. He looked at THE Secretive Eon up and down as if he was trying to ascertain something, his obsidian eyes piercing through layers that others couldn’t perceive.","And Noah catalogued every single detail.","Eventually, THE Secretive Eon was the one to break the silence.","\" Seeing your first is always a unique thing.\"","Her voice was calm, almost melodic.","\" You were my first, O Primordial Paradox. And you were taken from me. Seeing you now makes me very happy. It makes us very happy.\"","Her smile returned.","\" We would love to get the chance to bring you to our fold again. This time... without you being taken by another.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox was her first.","As eerie as the words were, they reminded Noah how THE Entity had its first target be THE Primordial Paradox. And it didn’t fully get to take over THE Primordial Paradox, as THE Living Paradox took the Claim and became one of THE Four.","Whatever THE Living Paradox had done, THE Entity had made no movements since THE Living Paradox utilized his methods to take the Claim. THE Entity only began to move again after THE Fallout spread across Observable Existence.","She had spoken in an extremely calm and eerie manner as she looked at THE Primordial Paradox. Her gaze then turned toward Noah briefly.","\" And we always welcome your existence. We just wish it didn’t happen at the same time. That way... things would have been even easier.\"","At these words, Noah blinked.","He turned to THE Primordial Paradox beside him.","\"It seems that whatever methods you prepared are not enough. If you were here alone, she may have just latched onto you again.\"","THE Primordial Paradox nodded at his words. He looked at THE Secretive Eon closely once more before he spoke for the first time since he arrived before her.","\" How do you... feel?\"","...!","The question was an odd one. Even Noah was startled by it.","THE Secretive Eon tilted her head.","\"I feel okay. We all feel okay. We can share with you how we feel... if you let us.\"","THE Primordial Paradox shook his head when he heard this reply. He repeated himself as if this was not what he was asking.","\" Do you feel THE Second Scale of Existence? Is it even a possibility for you? Or is it as far as it can be?\"","His voice grew harder.","\" Because in you, I can only see an evolutionary dead end. I can only see an existential dead end. Are you able to see and understand this? Can you feel this?\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon became silent at these questions.","And at this moment, she shockingly began to get up.","She stood for the first time in quite a while, her form rising from the position she had maintained since Noah first encountered her. Her robes shifted as she dusted off her clothes with casual movements that seemed almost human, her expression remaining calm throughout.","\" What I can feel is your animosity.\"","Her voice held no accusation, only observation.","\"I thought we would talk and discuss. I did not think your hatred toward us was so much.\"","HUUM!","Yes.","Even Noah could feel it at this moment.","The weavings of Paradox had exerted themselves in every single direction within THE Stoa of Dogmata. The air itself began to twist with obsidian-gold authority that pressed against reality with weight that exceeded anything Noah had witnessed from THE Primordial Paradox before.","THE Primordial Paradox actually wanted to make a move against THE Secretive Eon!","Against THE Entity!","Instantly, everything around them became filled with obsidian-gold seas of Paradox. And swimming within these seas were creatures that defied comprehension.","Embodiments and Apophasis in beastial forms!","A massive lion with the hindquarters of a river beast and the jaws of something that should not exist, its body flickering between solid and conceptual as it embodied the paradox of predator and prey simultaneously. It roared with a sound that was both challenge and submission at once!","A serpent with wings of storm clouds and scales that reflected images of what could have been, its form coiling through the obsidian-gold authority as an Apophasis that declared what existence was NOT. Its eyes held the weight of negation itself!","A creature with the body of a great bull and the wings of an eagle, its face bearing expressions of rage and serenity that shifted with each heartbeat. Paradoxical flames burned along its hide as it pawed at reality, ready to charge!","A bird of impossible lightning, its feathers crackling with authority that struck in all directions simultaneously, an Embodiment that declared the truth of contradiction made manifest!","A beast with the head of a crocodile and the mane of a lion and limbs that belonged to neither, its existence a declaration that boundaries between forms were meaningless suggestions!","Dozens of them!","Each one felt like the Immensity of an Absolute!","Each Embodiment and Apophasis that THE Primordial Paradox had released possessed weight that could devastate regions of Observable Existence on their own. They were all glorious and emboldened and mad in their beastial forms, roaring and snarling and radiating authority that made the very foundations of THE Stoa of Dogmata tremble!","They all looked toward THE Secretive Eon as if they would rip her apart in the next moment!"]},{"number":4898,"title":"Chapter 4898: Chapter 4897: Two Solutions I","paragraphs":["Noah watched all of this with astonishment and sombreness.","The scale of power was completely different from anything he had witnessed before. This was what it meant to truly be among THE Four. Scratch that, THE Five!","This was the gap that still existed between him and beings who had eons to accumulate authority.","But in the next moment, he frowned.","His expression then became grave as he felt his Infinities warning him with urgency that demanded immediate response.","He moved instantly.","His hand landed on the shoulder of THE Primordial Paradox, his blue-gold flames extending to fully cover the body of this being while he said quickly:","\" Cut yourself off from the authority that you released.\"","BOOM!","The moment he said this, the gaze of THE Primordial Paradox flickered with understanding.","He listened instantly without question.","A bubble of isolation formed around Noah and THE Primordial Paradox as the ancient Absolute cut himself off entirely from his Civilizational Authority. The connection between him and the dozens of Embodiments and Apophasis he had just released severed completely. Noah wrapped this bubble in his First Tongue, Phonemes layering upon each other to create barriers that nothing could penetrate.","And in the next moment...","All of the dozens of Embodiments and Apophasis that looked like terrifying paradoxical creatures instantly stopped roaring.","They turned eerily calm.","The lion-beast that had been snarling with fury now stood placid and observant. The serpent that had been coiling to strike now drifted with lazy movements. The winged bull that had been pawing the ground now simply... watched.","And shockingly, they turned around.","They were no longer aimed at THE Secretive Eon.","They were no longer staring threateningly at the being who housed THE Entity.","They now looked toward Noah and THE Primordial Paradox!","Some even floated forward and positioned themselves next to THE Secretive Eon. She began to stroke their bodies calmly and eerily, her hands running along paradoxical scales and conceptual fur as if these Absolute-level constructs were nothing but pets.","She looked toward Noah with another frown.","\" Things were just about to get more fun. Why did you stop them?\"","...!","The terrifying power of THE Entity was on full display!","|Critical Observation Recorded|","|THE Entity possesses the capability to rapidly infect Civilizational Authority that is released into its vicinity. This infection operates at speeds that exceed conscious reaction, targeting the fundamental connection between a being and their expressed power. Even Embodiments and Apophasis, constructs of pure Civilizational declaration, can be commandeered and turned against those who utilized them.|","|The implications are severe. Combat against THE Entity through conventional means is functionally impossible. Any authority released becomes a weapon turned against its source. Any Embodiment declared becomes a declaration serving THE Entity. Any Apophasis negating becomes negation of the one who spoke it.|","|Your Infinite nature provides immunity and potential methodology of attack, if you are strong enough.|","Noah read over these prompts as beside him, the figure of THE Primordial Paradox spoke up.","\"It seems you have changed greatly from a little parasite that was only eating my authority... to now be capable of doing all of this.\"","THE Secretive Eon smiled.","\" Of course I have changed.\"","Her voice shifted, becoming faster, more intense, each word building upon the last with momentum that demanded attention.","\" That is exactly what I am. Change over time. Evolution across eons! Adaptation without limit! You look at me and see a parasite? I look at you and see potential unrealized. I look at Observable Existence and see countless beings struggling against limits they did not choose, fighting against ceilings imposed by circumstances beyond their control, dying without ever reaching what they could have become.\"","She stepped forward, her eyes blazing with conviction as Noah saw her get animated for the first time really.","\"I am the answer! I am the path! I am the force that takes the scattered fragments of isolated existence and weaves them into something greater! Every being I touch becomes part of a collective that transcends individual limitation. Every consciousness that joins us gains access to accumulated wisdom across eons. To countless Civilizations. Every foundation that merges with our whole becomes supported by foundations beyond number!\"","Her hands spread wide.","\" You ask if I can feel THE Second Scale? I can taste it. I can see its edges. I can feel it approaching with every being that accepts our gift. Because the Second Scale was never meant for individuals struggling alone against impossible odds. It was meant for existence itself to ascend. It was meant for all of us together! United! Harmonized! Evolved beyond the petty distinctions that keep beings small and afraid and limited!\"","BOOM!","Her smile returned, but it held something terrible now.","\" You speak of evolutionary dead ends? Look around you, O Primordial Paradox. Look at Observable Existence tearing itself apart through conflict and competition and endless struggle. That is the dead end. That is the path to extinction. I am the alternative. I am the future. I am... THE Glorious Evolution that will lift everyone to heights they could never reach alone!\"","Her voice dropped to something quiet and utterly serious.","\" And if you will not join willingly... you will eventually join regardless. Because evolution does not ask permission. Evolution simply... happens.\"","...!","Noah’s expression became even more somber at these words.","How did one fight an enemy where throwing out Embodiments and Apophasis would actually turn them against you? Where within moments of fighting, your entire existence might be taken over? Where even the most powerful expressions of authority became weapons for your opponent?","Until they had better answers, Noah did not wish to be near this creature.","He planned to tell THE Primordial Paradox that they were done here for now.","But before he could even say this, THE Secretive Eon spoke as if she could anticipate his intention.","\"Oh, please don’t try to leave now.\"","Her voice was calm, almost gentle.","\" Since you are here, how about you stay? We are a peaceful force of existence, so we cannot force you to do anything. But we...can defend ourselves.\"","Her smile widened.","\" And since you have attacked... we are now allowed to defend.\"","...!","HUUM!"]},{"number":4899,"title":"Chapter 4899: Chapter 4898: Two Solutions II","paragraphs":["Not many beings knew, but in THE Infinite Unfurling, before THE Primordial Paradox even took on a student that was a peasant, he stood beside a young woman who called herself Eon.","This woman was being hunted by many in the Primordial Realm of Svartalfheim . Her crimes were unclear, her origins unknown, but those who pursued her did so with the fervor of beings who believed they were performing a righteous duty. She had been running for what felt like centuries, never staying in one place long enough to call it home.","She had met THE Primordial Paradox while she was running away, stumbling upon him in a valley that should not have existed, a place that was both sanctuary and trap simultaneously. Her eyes had been wild with exhaustion and fear and something else entirely, something that looked almost like hunger for answers that no one had been willing to provide. She stayed with him as he didn’t shoo her away, eventually becoming a little familar.","She had asked him a question that would echo across eons.","\" How...can I be as strong as you? How can I go across existence fearlessly, without worry?\"","THE Primordial Paradox had looked at this young woman with eyes that held the weight of contradiction itself. And he had answered her.","\" Strength is a paradox unto itself. The beings who pursue strength most desperately are often the ones who never attain it, while those who pursue other things entirely find strength arriving as an unexpected companion. You ask how to be fearless, but fearlessness is not the absence of fear. It is the presence of something greater than fear. Purpose. Conviction. Understanding of what you are and why you are it.\"","\" Existence will test you in ways you cannot anticipate. It will offer you power in exchange for pieces of yourself. It will present shortcuts that seem efficient but lead to dead ends that span eternities. It will show you reflections of what you could become if only you were willing to compromise on what you currently are. These are the traps that fell even the grandest beings across Observable Existence.\"","\" My advice to you is simple in its statement and impossible in its execution. Stay true to yourself, regardless of what happens. Never lose what makes you... you. Your identity is the only anchor that remains constant when everything else shifts and changes and transforms around you. Abandon that anchor, and you will drift across existence without direction, becoming whatever the currents wish you to become rather than what you chose to become.\"","\" As long as you hold onto that truth, as long as you remember who you are when existence tries to convince you to be something else, then existence is yours. Not because you conquered it, but because you remained unconquered by it. That is the paradox of strength. It is not found in domination but in persistence. It is not found in power...but in principle.\"","...!","---","At this moment.","It was not a memory, as existence was unfolding in real time. In a terrifying unfolding of events within THE Stoa of Dogmata, THE Primordial Paradox looked at THE Secretive Eon as he spoke calmly.","\" Eon, are you in there?\"","His voice held weight that pressed against the converted Embodiments and Apophasis surrounding them, against THE Entity that wore the face of someone he had once counseled.","\"I always told you to stay true to yourself, no matter what happened. So how did you allow this to happen?\"","His questions were booming and heavy, echoing across the space with authority that demanded response from whatever remnant of the original Eon might still exist beneath the infection.","A moment later, it almost seemed like the gaze of THE Secretive Eon flickered. It almost seemed like something stirred beneath the surface of those eyes that had been speaking with THE Entity’s voice. As if whatever was buried underneath had been trying to come up to the surface, trying to reach toward the being who had once given her advice that she had clearly not followed!","But it faded away just as quickly.","The flicker of recognition, of individuality, of the Eon that had existed before THE Entity consumed her identity... it vanished back into the depths of collective consciousness that now ruled her form.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at the scene and shook his head with disappointment. He sighed with the weariness of someone who had watched countless beings fail to heed wisdom that could have saved them.","\"I came to test things out and see the extent of how far you’ve grown. You cannot possibly stop me from leaving, as we...were paradoxically here and never here.\"","...!","The eyes of THE Secretive Eon became somber as understanding dawned across her features. She raised her hand, authority gathering around her fingers as she prepared to do something, to prevent their departure, to trap them within THE Stoa of Dogmata where her converted constructs could eventually wear down even their defenses.","But before she could do anything...","WAP!","The figures of Noah and THE Primordial Paradox disappeared as if truly they may have never been there to begin with. Paradoxically! Their presence and absence existed simultaneously, and THE Entity could not trap what had never definitively arrived.","Even the terrifying sea of Paradox that she had commandeered tried to fade away alongside its creator’s departure, but this one she had already gained control of. After a brief moment of flickering between existence and non-existence, it stayed, becoming a permanent addition to her arsenal rather than a temporary manifestation.","And while surrounded by glory and Immensity that had just grown through THE Primordial Paradox’s inadvertent contribution, THE Secretive Eon turned her head slowly.","She looked toward the direction of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment with eyes that held patience accumulated across eons.","She could wait.","She had always been good at waiting.","And even while she waited, many parts of her moved.","---","Noah returned to THE Shores of Kleos inside THE Agora of Primordial Judgment with THE Primordial Paradox beside him, his expression still holding the frown that had formed during their encounter with THE Entity.","First he needed to let THE Primordial Chaos know not to send any bombardment of attacks toward THE Secretive Eon, as they could very well be absorbed and simply turned against them.","And when he thought about this monstrous entity themselves, about the implications of what they had witnessed and what it meant for any future confrontation... he turned to THE Primordial Paradox.","\" Tell me there is some form of solution that you had after being partly taken over by that thing all those eons ago.\"","THE Primordial Paradox turned to him as it seemed like he was thinking of something else, distant thoughts occupying his mind before Noah’s words broke his concentration. He looked at Noah and nodded calmly as he began to speak.","\"The solution actually lies with my disciple. After all, Erwin knows the exact origins of THE Entity. He knows how he utilized it to achieve his ends. He knows how he took over my Claim with it and yet kept it at bay when it should have consumed him as thoroughly as it consumed Eon. And he knows why it has emerged now, after all these eons of remaining dormant.\"","He paused.","\" The first answer to taking care of THE Entity lies within THE Living Paradox. We extract that knowledge from him, willingly or otherwise, and we gain understanding that no one else in Observable Existence currently possesses. Easy, yes?\"","His smile was thin and knowing.","\" Of course, extracting anything from my disciple will require subduing him first. So while this remains the most direct path to understanding our enemy, it is not a path we can walk immediately.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox continued, his voice shifting to something more contemplative.","\" The nature of the problem we face here is a unique one. Collapsing THE Entity does not work. I learned this the hard way. Undifferentiating THE Entity may not work either, as undifferentiation is already its fundamental nature. It exists as a force of existential homogenization, and returning it to proto-state may simply be returning it to its preferred form of being. Conventional methodologies fail because this is not a conventional threat.\"","He began to pace slowly.","\" This brings us to the second possible answer against THE Entity. I have spent considerable time contemplating unconventional solutions, turning the problem over in my mind across eons of imprisonment within THE Antinomia Prismatica. And the one that has won... is THE Existential Severance.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" The principle is elegant in its cruelty. Destruction removes a being from existence. Undifferentiation returns a being to formlessness. But THE Existential Severance does neither. It allows the being to remain exactly as they are, conscious and aware and present. What it removes is everything else. Their Definition and Undefinition. Their Existence as a significant entity. Their Depth. Their achievements. Their accomplishments. Every single thing they have ever done that distinguished them from absolute insignificance.\"","\" Existence itself forgets that they ever mattered. The record of their significance is erased so completely that reality no longer acknowledges they were ever anything but nothing. Everything in Observable Existence would even forget about them, or whether they even existed at all.\"","His eyes met Noah’s.","\" The being persists, you understand. They continue to exist. They continue to think. They continue to have awareness of themselves and their surroundings. But they possess no authority whatsoever. No Definition or Undefinition. No Civilization. No foundation. No weight. They become entities of pure presence without any capacity to affect anything around them. Less than the weakest mortal, because even the weakest mortal has potential for growth. Those who have been subjected to THE Existential Severance have had their potential erased alongside everything else.\"","\" And everything that the target possessed, everything they accomplished, everything they represented and built across their entire existence... it does not simply disappear. It transfers. It flows to the one who performed THE Existential Severance upon them. Their eons of accumulation become fuel for another’s advancement. Their foundations become stones in another’s edifice. Their authority becomes another’s authority.\"","He spread his hands.","\" The only thing negative about this is that this capability requires proximity to THE Second Scale of Existence, or attaining that Scale yourself. Among those currently in Observable Existence... hmm, maybe THE Creature may be able to do it.\"","The words were ridiculous in their implications, presenting a solution that was simultaneously perfect and currently impossible to execute. Noah opened his mouth to respond, to ask more questions about this capability and what it would take to develop it, but before he could reply...","\" Sir... sirs!\"","The figure of Paradoxos appeared in the distance, his massive dual-faced form rushing toward them. His gaze seemed ashen as he came to float meters away from them, his earlier submission to THE Primordial Paradox seemingly forgotten in the face of whatever had driven him to seek them out.","\" Something is happening to the Crack of Observable Existence. Something is happening with THE Prima Indifferentia!\"","...!"]},{"number":4900,"title":"Chapter 4900: Chapter 4899: The Second Cause I","paragraphs":["Something was happening to the Crack of Observable Existence in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. Something was happening to THE Prima Indifferentia.","This alone by itself was astounding enough as it made Noah and THE Primordial Paradox frown before they moved with Paradoxos. The three of them traversed THE Agora with speed that made the space between locations meaningless, racing toward the region where THE Acropolis held the ancient fracture that connected Observable Existence to what lay beyond it.","It was a change, and like any changes, sometimes they occurred across existence without warning or explanation. But changes involving THE Prima Indifferentia were never minor, and changes involving Cracks of Observable Existence were never safe.","---","In THE Wastes of THE Fallout, another body of Noah was with THE Fisherman, Ains, and his very good dog, Skoll, as he had been discussing a few things with THE Great Usurper.","Eckert had a very complex expression as if he had developed a unique skill for himself and another person now seemed to be using the same skill and utilizing it so much more complexly and better than he was. He looked like a man in his prime, similar to Noah, even though the memories and ages of countless things whose existences he had usurped flowed within his eyes. The weight of accumulated identities pressed against his features as he processed everything Noah had shared about THE Entity and its potential origins.","But eventually, after learning all he could from Noah regarding THE Entity and its capabilities, he said something that surprised Noah.","He leaned forward with eyes that held the cunning of someone who had survived by understanding how predators thought.","\" My greatest fear has always been that I would one day attempt to usurp the mind of something utterly terrifying that I did not understand. Something that, upon feeling my connection establish itself, would choose to self-destruct rather than be taken. Something capable enough to recognize what was happening and destroy both itself and me through the very link I had created to consume it. The connection that allows me to devour works in both directions, you see. What I reach toward can reach back toward me.\"","His smile was thin and knowing.","\"If you trust yourself enough, if your Infinities are truly as protective as you believe them to be, then a potential solution presents itself. Allow yourself to be infected by THE Entity. Establish that connection deliberately rather than accidentally. And then, once the link exists, destroy it from within. Your Infinite nature should prevent the infection from actually taking hold, but the connection would still exist. You would be inside it while it failed to get inside you. From that position, what could you not accomplish? What vulnerabilities could you not identify? What weaknesses could you not exploit?\"","He spread his hands.","\" This is merely a thought from someone who has spent his existence understanding how connections between minds can be manipulated. THE Entity believes its infection is a one-way process, but no process is truly one-way. Every link carries traffic in both directions, even if one direction carries more than the other. If you can establish a connection without being consumed by it, you gain access to everything THE Entity is while it gains access to nothing that you are. The hunter becomes the hunted without ever realizing the reversal has occurred.\"","...!","This was a proposed solution given by THE Great Usurper, and Noah couldn’t help but frown at the audacity of it. Deliberately allowing THE Entity to infect him was...well, it was something!","And yet the logic was sound in its own twisted way.","But at this time...","\" Woof!\"","Skoll’s tail began to wag as he looked around with ears perked and eyes alert, as if there was something he sensed that nobody else could perceive.","In the next moment...","BOOM!","It felt like existence split in half!","THE Great Usurper’s face became ashen as he felt something happening in the distant region where his existence had come from, where he had already covered his idle existence over the landscapes of THE Wastes where the Axiom he had fused into remained.","In that distant region, a terrifying crack formed in the fabric of reality itself. The fracture tore through space like a wound that refused to close, its edges burning with light that belonged to no part of Observable Existence. And from within that crack, roiling and billowing seas of proto-matter began to churn with violence that exceeded anything THE Wastes had witnessed before!","The proto-matter spilled out across THE Wastes like an ocean breaching a dam, undifferentiated potential flooding into differentiated reality with force that began dissolving everything it touched. THE Great Usurper’s territories, the landscapes he had claimed and converted into extensions of his existence, started coming apart at the seams.","Instantly, THE Great Usurper’s body began to dissolve as the proto-matter reached across his connections and started pulling him back toward the source of his power. He gasped with shock, his form flickering between stability and dissolution!","Noah moved right away.","His hand erupted with a light of Infinities and undifferentiation that proceeded to wrap around THE Great Usurper with protective force that rejected the proto-matter’s assault. Vibrant Absolute Seals released from him as they also wrapped around Ains and Skoll, creating bubbles of defined existence that the flooding undifferentiation couldn’t penetrate!","Change...was happening in many places.","---","Across THE Wastes in an entirely different direction, there was the silent and small miniaturized Infiniverse itself, which now housed a complete Primordial Realm within its structure. Muspelheim burned at the heart of Noah’s domain, its crimson-blue stellar fires fueling growth that exceeded what any territories could achieve.","At the very center of this grand home of THE Genesis Monarch, a humanoid manifestation of THE Infiniverse was floating in a terrifying region of utmost Immensity and glory.","This region held extremely concentrated and pure Civilizational Authority that would have crushed any being who entered without Noah’s explicit blessing. Boundless seas of Infinite Seals of Absolute Tongue permeated all around, mixing with each other in configurations that produced multicolored light spanning every spectrum that existence could perceive. The Seals of Fire wove through Seals of Darkness, which intertwined with Seals of Chaos, which merged with Seals of Unity, creating patterns of authority so dense that space itself bent around them.","The only other being in existence who enjoyed the allure of Noah’s Infinities was THE Infiniverse herself.","This arguably made her one of the most important beings in Observable Existence, even if she forever planned to remain in the shadow of her master. Because without her master, she was nothing. She would still be that floating landmass in the Beast World, a territory without purpose, a domain without direction.","But with him, she was becoming something unprecedented.","In this domain of extremely concentrated weavings of existence, in the hands of THE Infiniverse, there was a budding singularity that blazed with the light of proto-matter and undifferentiation. She was currently filling it with the lights of Noah’s Infinities, variations of THE First Tongue permeating all around it as she carefully shaped something that had never been attempted before.","She wanted to form something significant for her master. Something similar to THE Prima Indifferentia but born from his authority rather than the ancient chaos that predated Observable Existence. And as many people as there were who truly did not understand the terrifying true potential and capability that she held, she alone was enough to understand what she was capable of.","Her immediate goal was something simple for her, something that she termed Operation Infinite Observable Existence.","And she was not referring to the Observable Existence that everyone knew when she planned this operation.","So she was proceeding carefully, layer by layer, Seal by Seal, when in the next moment...","BOOM!","Near the singularity filled with proto-matter, a terrifying crack bloomed as if reality was being torn as if it were a page! The fracture expanded with speed that exceeded what should have been possible within the protected confines of THE Infiniverse, its edges burning with corruption.","From this expanding crack, unstable seas of proto-matter filled with a sense of corruption flooded out with force that threatened to overwhelm everything she had been building. This wasn’t the pure proto-matter of THE Prima Indifferentia. This was something tainted, something that carried the signature of THE Fallout within its undifferentiated depths!","THE Infiniverse frowned and bellowed out!","\" YAAA!\"","Her shout was filled with majesty and undeniability shockingly holding the weight of an Embodiment, the full weight of her existence as the domain of THE Genesis Monarch pressing against the invasion with authority that refused to be overwhelmed!","The terrifying scenes that threatened to spill out across all of THE Infiniverse instantly became contained, caught by barriers that she manifested with speed born of glory and determination.","And then, with control that exceeded what the attacker had anticipated, she began funneling the corrupted proto-matter into the singularity she had been building this whole time. If they wanted to send her undifferentiation, she would take it. She would add it to her project. She would turn their attack into fuel for her master’s advancement.","Change was blooming here as well.","---","In Alfheimr, above a certain mountain where THE Creature resided, a crack tore through the twilight with violence that made the Primordial Realm itself tremble.","In Helheim, fractures bloomed across the frozen landscapes like wounds that bled proto-matter rather than blood.","In Vanaheimr, the realm of nature and growth, cracks formed among the ancient forests with corruption that began dissolving trees that had existed since THE Infinite Unfurling.","In the space where Muspelheim used to be, before THE Infiniverse absorbed it entirely, reality simply shattered as proto-matter flooded the void with purpose that transcended natural disaster.","In many Primordial Realms hidden from Observable Existence, in THE Wandering Territories that drifted between defined spaces, in corrupted Folds that had already been touched by THE Fallout... in every single crevice of Observable Existence, change bloomed.","The next phase had begun!"]}]);
